			<h1>rīnan<span class="pron"> | riː.nɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:rignan" class="xref-target">rignan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="hand-wundor" d:title="hand-wundor">
		<body>
			<h1>hand-wundor<span class="pron"> | xɑnd.wun.dor |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>neuter noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A wondrous thing wrought by hand</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-cilcan" d:title="ge-cilcan">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-cilcan<span class="pron"> | je.Kil.kɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">to whitewash</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">similes estis sepulchris dealbatis</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gelīco giē sint byrgennum oferhīudum ł ūta gecǣlcad</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. L. 23, 27)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:nīw-cilct" class="xref-target">nīw-cilct</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="middel" d:title="middel">
		<body>
			<h1>middel<span class="pron"> | mid.del |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Middle, middlemost</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="Cynewulf" d:title="Cynewulf">
		<body>
			<h1>Cynewulf<span class="pron"> | Ky.ne.wulf |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">An Anglo-Saxon poet, who has preserved his name in Runes, in his poem on Elene's Recovery of the Cross</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">Ever was contest till then, with waves of sorrow tossed C [the torch] sinking, though he, in meadhall treasures, handled appled gold, Y [sorrow] he mourned, N [need] his consort, narrow sorrow he suffered, a close rune, where E [the horse] before him measured the mile paths, proudly hastened with wires adorned. W [hope] is overpowered, my joy in my old age, youth is turned back my old pride. U I was of old a gleam of youth, now are the days of my life after the appointed space departed, the joy of life flowed away, as L [lake or water] glideth, the floods that hasten. F [wealth] will be for every man failing under the heaven, the ornament of the land will depart under the welkin.</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ā wæs sæc ōþ-ðæt, cnyssed cearwelmum &amp;c-rune; [cēn] drūsende, ðeāh he, in medoheallelīfe māþmas, þege æplede gold, &amp;y-rune; [yr] gnornode, &amp;n-rune; [nȳd] gefēra, nearu sorge dreāh, enge rūne, ðær him &amp;e-rune; [ēh] fōre mīlpaðas mæt, mōdig þrægde wīrum gewlenced. &amp;w-rune; [wēn] is geswīþrad, gomen æfter gearum, geōgoþ is gecyrred ald onmedla. &amp;u-rune; [ūr] wæs geāra geōgoþhādes glǣm, nū synt geārdagas æfter fyrstmearce forþgewitene, līfwynne geliden, swā &amp;l-rune; [lagu] toglīdeþ, flōdas gefȳsde. &amp;f-rune; [feoh] ǣghwam biþ lǣne under lyfte, landes frætwe gewītaþ under wolcnum.</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Elen. Kmbl. 2512-2541; El. 1257-1272)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:Cyneweard" class="xref-target">Cyneweard</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ribbe" d:title="ribbe">
		<body>
			<h1>ribbe<span class="pron"> | rib.be |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -an</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">The herb hounds-tongue</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. cynogiossum officinale)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ribbe cinoglosa</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. i. 286, 23 : ii. 104, 2)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">canes linga</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ribbe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (102, 51)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">quinquenerbia</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ribbe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (i. 68, 33)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðās wyrte ðe man cynoglossam and ōðrum naman ribbe nemneþ, and hȳ eāc sume men linguam canis hāteþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lchdm. i. 210, 16-19)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ribban seāw</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (ii. 40, 29)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Genim ribban</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (36, 23)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-risnian" d:title="ge-risnian">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-risnian<span class="pron"> | je.ri.sni.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">convenire</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Gerisnian</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 15, 65)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">congruentes</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Gerisniende</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (24, 46)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="þeaca" d:title="þeaca">
