			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:crāwan" class="xref-target">crāwan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="wrǣstlere" d:title="wrǣstlere">
		<body>
			<h1>wrǣstlere<span class="pron"> | wræːst.le.re |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A wrestler</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. luctator)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Wrǣstlere luctator (- ur, MS. )</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 50, 37)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:wraxlere" class="xref-target">wraxlere</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="þanc-weorþ" d:title="þanc-weorþ">
		<body>
			<h1>þanc-weorþ<span class="pron"> | θɑnk.we͜orθ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Worthy of thanks, acceptable, pleasing</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="orweg-stig" d:title="orweg-stig">
		
		<body>
			<h1>orweg-stig<span class="pron"> | or.weG.stiG |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A path difficult of access</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. devia callis)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Orwegstig devia callis (-us, MS. )</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 139, 57)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Horwegstīg (but cf. horu-weg)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (25, 25)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:horu-weg" class="xref-target">horu-weg</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="folc-mǣgþ" d:title="folc-mǣgþ">
		<body>
			<h1>folc-mǣgþ<span class="pron"> | folk.mæːɣθ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A nation-tribe, tribe</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. nātio, trībus)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Folc-mægþa of nation-tribes</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. 64; Th. 77, 18; Gen. 1277)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="hlædel" d:title="hlædel">
		<body>
			<h1>hlædel<span class="pron"> | xlæ.del |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">An instrument for drawing water, a ladle</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. antlia)</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:hladan" class="xref-target">hladan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="for-sceādan" d:title="for-sceādan">
		<body>
			<h1>for-sceādan<span class="pron"> | for.ʃæ͜ɑː.dɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<ol class="sub-senses">
						<li>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Gif hēr ðegna hwelc ðyrelne kylle brōhte tō ðȳs burnan, bēte hine georne, ðȳlǣs hē forsceāde scīrost wætra</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 469, 11)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="coorta" d:title="coorta">
		<body>
			<h1>coorta<span class="pron"> | ko.or.tɑ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -an</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A band of soldiers, cohort</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. cohors)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">he had eighty-eight cohorts, which we now call bands, each of which was, in those days, one thousand five hundred men</span>
							<span class="q-oe">He hæfde eahta ond hund-eahtatig coortena [MS. coortana], ðæt we nū truman hātaþ, ðæt wæs, on ðām dagum, fīf hund manna, and ān þūsend</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 5, 12; Bos. 111, 14, 17)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="hearpe" d:title="hearpe">
		
		<body>
			<h1>hearpe<span class="pron"> | xæ͜ɑr.pe |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -an</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A harp</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. cithara)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hearpe cithara</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. 73, 56: Ps. Th. 56, 10)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Psalm æfter hærpan sang canticum: ǣr hærpan sang psalmus</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. Gl. 34; Som. 62, 57, 58; Wrt. Voc. 28, 37, 38)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">there was the sound of the harp</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðǣr was hearpan swēg</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Beo. Th. 179; B. 89: 4908; B. 2458: 6039; B. 3023: 4517; B. 2262: 4221; B. 2107)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">he first awaked with his hands the sound of the harp</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Se hearpan ǣrest handum sīnum hlyn āwehte</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. 52; Th. 66, 5; Gen. 1079)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">cum esset lætitiæ causa ut omnes per ordinem cantare deberent ille ubi adpropinquare sibi citharam cernebat surgebat</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðonne ðǣr wæs blisse intingan gedēmed ðæt hī ealle sceoldan þurh endebyrdnesse be hearpan singan ðonne he geseah ða hearpan him neālǣcean ðonne ārās hē</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 4, 24; S. 597. 6)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">psallam tibi in cithara</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic ðē on sealmfatum singe he hearpan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 70, 20: Exon. 86 b; Th. 325, 1; Vīd. 105)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">he has no mind to the harp ... who on the ocean puts forth</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ne biþ him tō hearpan hyge ... se ðe on lagu fundaþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (82 a; Th. 308, 23; Seef. 44)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">one shall at his lord's feet sit with the harp and receive treasure</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Sum sceal mid hearpan æt his hlāfordes fōtum sittan feoh þicgan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (88 a; Th. 332, 4; Vy. 80)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">one with his hands can touch the harp</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Sum mid hondum mæg hearpan grētan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (79 a; Th. 296, 11; Cri; 49: 91 b; Th. 344, 10; Gn. Ex. 171: 17 b; Th. 42, 8; Cri. 669)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="morgen-wlǣtung" d:title="morgen-wlǣtung">
		<body>
			<h1>morgen-wlǣtung<span class="pron"> | mor.Gen.wlæː.tung |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Nausea in the morning</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Wið morgen-wlǣtunga</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lch. iii. 44, 19)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="Baningas" d:title="Baningas">
		<body>
			<h1>Baningas<span class="pron"> | bɑ.nin.gɑs |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">The Banings, people mentioned in the Gleeman's tale</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">Becca ruled the Banings</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Becca weōld Baningum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Scōp Th. 39; Wīd. 19)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-hȳdan" d:title="ge-hȳdan">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-hȳdan<span class="pron"> | je.xyː.dɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Condit, i. abscondit, reservat vel sell vel gehȳt</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 135, 56)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gehȳdde occulit</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (65, 23)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gehȳddum abditis</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (98, 34)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(1)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">to hide, put out of sight, bury in the ground</span>
								<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. abscondit)</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Dætste ꝥ wīf gehȳdeð (abscondit) in meolo mitto</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Lk. L. R. 13, 21)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ic gehȳdde (abscondi) cræft ðīn on eorðo</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. L. 25, 25)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Gehȳdde l̄ dēgelde</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (13, 33)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(2)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">to hide an object in order that it may not be found</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Striōn monn gehȳdde</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. L. 13, 44)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Þām þe unrihte inne gehȳdde wrǣte under wealle</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (B. 3059)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(3)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">to hide in order to shield</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Gewint se iil tō ānum cliēwene, and tīhð his fēt suā hē inmest mæg, and gehȳt his heāfod (caput abscondit)</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 241, 12)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hiē biddaþ ꝥ seō eorþe hiē forswelge and gehȳde . . . hiē cweþaþ tō; þǣm dūnum : ' Feallaþ ofer ūs, and ūs bewreōþ and gehȳdaþ, '</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Bl. H. 93, 27-33)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(4)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">reflex.</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">Jesus fugit in montem ipse solus</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Se Hǣlend becierde hiē and gehȳdde hiene</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 33, 15: Jn. L. 12, 36)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(5)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">to keep a matter from the knowledge of others</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ðu gehȳddest (abscondisti) ðās from snottrum and ædeānades ðā ðām lytlum</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Lk. L. 10, 21)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ne is gehȳded ꝥne oncnāuen biþ</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (8, 17: 12, 2: 19, 42)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Nǣnig is gehȳded (occultum) ꝥ ne sē gewitten</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. L. 10, 26)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hiē ðeahtigaþ on hiera mōdes rinde monig gōd weorc tō wyrcanne, ac on ðām piðan biþ ōðer gehȳded (aliud in imis intentio supprimit)</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 55, 23)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hē þā oðēwde openlīce ꝥ hē ǣr diēgellīce gehȳd hæfde</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 6, 34; S. 388, 32)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(6)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">to hide from sight, prevent from being seen, cover up</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ne mæg burug gehȳda ofer mōr geseted</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. L. 5, 14)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ongunnun sume gehȳdæ (uelare) onsiōne his</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Mk. L. 14, 65)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Þeōs lǣine gesceaft longe stōðe heolstre gehȳded</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Hy. II, 13)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
							<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
								<li>
									<p>
										<span class="sense-label">(6 a)</span>
										<span class="meaning-en">fig.</span>
									</p>
									<ul class="quotes">
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Þā dysegan sint swā hlince, þæt hī ne magon oncnāwan hwǣr þā ēcan gōd sindon gehȳdde</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Met. 19, 32)</span>
										</li>
									</ul>
								</li>
							</ol>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge-hēdan" class="xref-target">ge-hēdan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-leāfa" d:title="ge-leāfa">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-leāfa<span class="pron"> | je.læ͜ɑː.fɑ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -an</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Belief, faith, confidence, trust</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. fides, fiducia)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the right faith teaches us that we should believe in the Holy Ghost</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Se rihta geleāfa us tǣcþ, ðæt we sceolon gelȳfan on ðone Hālgan Gāst</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. i. 280, 22 : Elen. Kmbl. 2070; El. 1036)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">fides</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Geleāfa</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. Gr. 12; Som. 15, 54)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the dayspring of bright belief awoke</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Dæges ōr onwōc leōhtes geleāfan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Apstls. Kmbl. 131; Ap. 66 : Elen. Kmbl. 1928; El. 966)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">in right faith</span>
							<span class="q-oe">On rihtum geleāfan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 6; Fox 14, 31)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">multos in brevi ab idolatria ad fidem converterent Christi</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hī monige hrǣdlīce fram deōfolgyldum to Cristes geleāfan gecyrdon</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 5, 10; S. 624, 9 : Chr. 565; Erl. 17, 21)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">thou hast the belief</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðū ðone geleāfan hæfst</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 5, 3; Fox 12, 11)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">we will now declare to you the faith which stands in the creed</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Nū we wyllaþ secgan eōw ðone geleāfan ðe on ðam crēdan stent</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. i. 274, 23 : 292, 9, 10 : 294, 8)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">habete fiduciam</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Habbaþ geleāfan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. Bos. 14, 27)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">I have firm trust in the Almighty God above</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic hæbbe me fæstne geleāfan up to ðam ælmihtegan Gode</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. 26; Th. 34, 26; Gen. 543 : 205; Th. 256, 19; Dan. 643 : Andr. Kmbl. 670; An. 335)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">I am fairly filled with bright belief</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Eom ic leōhte geleāfan fægre gefylled</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 42 a; Th. 141, 8; Gū. 624 : 62 b; Th. 230, 28; Ph. 479 : 75 a; Th. 281, 28; Jul. 653)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ǣdre" d:title="ǣdre">
		
		<body>
			<h1>ǣdre<span class="pron"> | æː.dre |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -an</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">a channel for liquids, An artery, a vein, fountain, river</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. arteria, vena, fons, rivus)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">they let life forth through the fountain of their veins</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Feorh alēton þurh ǣdra wylm</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 72b; Th. 271, 6; Jul. 478)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the veins shall bleed</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Blēdaþ ǣdran</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Salm. Kmbl. 290; Sal. 144)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">blood sprang from the veins</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Swāt ǣdrum sprong</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Beo. Th. 5925; B. 2966)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">a nerve, sinew, kidney</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. nervus, ren)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">renes mei resoluti sunt</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Wǣron mīne ǣdra ealle tolȳsde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 72, 17)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">tu possedisti omnes renes meos</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðū canst mīne ǣdre ealle</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (138, 11)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">then all his sinews shrank because of the cold</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðā for ðam cȳle him gescuncan ealle ǣdra</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 3, 9; Bos. 64, 39)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:wæter-ǣdre" class="xref-target">wæter-ǣdre</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="sprott" d:title="sprott">
		<body>
			<h1>sprott<span class="pron"> | sprott |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A sprat</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ða myclan hwælas and ða lytlan sprottas and eall fisckynn</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Anglia viii. 310, 18)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="hyll" d:title="hyll">
		<body>
			<h1>hyll<span class="pron"> | xyll |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Hyl oððe beorh collis</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. i. 80, 43)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">On ða rūgan hylle</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (C. D. iii. 454, 1)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Dena ł hylla colles</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. L. 113, 4)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:æmett-hyll" class="xref-target">æmett-hyll</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:ciric-hyll" class="xref-target">ciric-hyll</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:eāg-hyll" class="xref-target">eāg-hyll</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-met-fæst" d:title="ge-met-fæst">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-met-fæst<span class="pron"> | je.met.fæst |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Moderate, modest</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. moderatus, modestus)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">neither do they always dwell with the patient and moderate</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ne hie ðām geþyldegum and ðām gemetfæstum simble ne wuniaþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 11, 1; Fox 34, 3)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">she is very modest</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Siō is swīðe gemetfæst</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (10; Fox 28, 20)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">vir modestus</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Man gemetfæst</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 1, 16; S. 484, 18: 4, 28; S. 606, 33: Exon. 48 b; Th. 168, 19; Gū. 1080: 95 b; Th. 357, 19; Pa. 31)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="hege-rife" d:title="hege-rife">
		<body>
			<h1>hege-rife<span class="pron"> | xe.Ge.ri.fe |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Wiþ cneōwwærc, wuduweaxe and hegerife,</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Lch. ii. 66, 11 : 140, 3)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Wyl æscrinde, . . . hegerife, marubian . . . and jī līc gnid mid þǣre hegerifan, Wyrc sealfe of marubian, . . . hegerifan,</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (78, 11-16)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Hegerifan corn,</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (344, ii)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Genim hegerifan,</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (76, II : iii. 16, 16)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Wyl hegerifan,</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (ii. 342, 2)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Wyl hegerifan ufewearde,</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (iii. 38, 25)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="sprǣce" d:title="sprǣce">
		<body>
			<h1>sprǣce<span class="pron"> | spræː.Ke |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -an</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A talk, discourse</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">jamne igitur vides, quid haec omnia, quae diximus, consequatur</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hwæðer ðū nū ongite hwider þiōs sprǣce wille?</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 40, 1; F. 234, 32)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Apollonius hyre ārehte ealle his gelymp, and æt þāre sprǣcan ende him feōllon teāras of ðām eāgum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ap. Th. 15, 26)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="spreōt" d:title="spreōt">
		<body>
			<h1>spreōt<span class="pron"> | spre͜oːt |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Spreōt palus</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (An. Ox. 30, 1)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="bȳrgan" d:title="bȳrgan">
		<body>
			<h1>bȳrgan<span class="pron"> | byːr.ɣɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">to taste</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:birgan" class="xref-target">birgan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ā-werian" d:title="ā-werian">
		<body>
			<h1>ā-werian<span class="pron"> | ɑː.we.ri.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ā-wersian" class="xref-target">ā-wersian</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="be-nǣman" d:title="be-nǣman">
		
		<body>
			<h1>be-nǣman<span class="pron"> | be.næː.mɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -nǣmde, sg: -nēmde</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -nǣmed, past participle sg: -nēmed</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To deprive, take away</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. auferre, privare)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">he could not deprive them of their land</span>
							<span class="q-oe">He ne meahte hī ðæs landes benǣman</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 1, 10; Bos. 33, 35 : Cd. 98; Th. 129, 32; Gen. 2152)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">to deprive of life</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ealdre benǣman</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Judth. 10; Thw. 22, 24; Jud. 76)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">deprived of glory</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Wuldre benēmed</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. 215; Th. 272, 18; Sat. 121)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="on dōmes dæg" d:title="on dōmes dæg">
		<body>
			<h1>on dōmes dæg<span class="pron"> | on, doː.mes, dæj |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:for-gifenlīc" class="xref-target">for-gifenlīc</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="mēðe" d:title="mēðe">
		<body>
			<h1>mēðe<span class="pron"> | meː.θe |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">weary, exhausted (with labour, hunger, disease, etc.)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē hine ðǣr hwīle reste, mēðe æfter ðam miclan gewinne</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Rood Kmbl. 129; Kr. 65)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Mēðe and meteleās</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Elen. Kmbl. 1220; El. 612: 1392; El. 698: Exon. 90 b; Th. 340, 15; Gn. Ex. 111)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">exhausted by disease</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Mēðe for ðām miclan bysgum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (49 a; Th. 168, 25; Gū. 1083)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">exhausted from want of food</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Mē swā mēðum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Elen. Kmbl. 1620; El. 812)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Mēðne fessum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 38, 26: Exon. 47 b; Th. 163, 3; Gū. 988: 49 b; Th. 171, 23; Gū. 1131)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Mēðe stōdon, hungre gehæfte</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Andr. Kmbl. 2316; An. 1159: 78; An. 39)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hiē slǣp ofereode mēðe be mæste</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (929; An. 465)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">weary in mind, troubled, sad</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðē unrōtne, mēðne, mōdseōcne</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 51 a; Th. 177, 30; Gū. 1235)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hyge geōmurne, mēðne mōdsefan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (52 a; Th. 182, 16; Gū. 1311)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ongunnon sorhleōþ galan, ðā hiē woldon sīðian mēðe fram ðam mǣran þeōdne</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Rood Kmbl. 137; Kr. 69)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">comforter of the weary-hearted</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Mēðra frēfrend</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 62 a; Th. 227, 13; Ph. 422)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">III.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">troublesome, causing weariness</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">noli mihi molestus esse</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Nelle ðū mē moeðe ł hefig wosa</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lk. Skt. Rush. 11, 7)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ā-giēta" d:title="ā-giēta">
		<body>
			<h1>ā-giēta<span class="pron"> | ɑː.Gi͜yː.tɑ |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ā-gīta" class="xref-target">ā-gīta</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-lǣt" d:title="ge-lǣt">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-lǣt<span class="pron"> | je.læːt |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:wæter-gelǣt" class="xref-target">wæter-gelǣt</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="un-fracod-līce" d:title="un-fracod-līce">
		
		<body>
			<h1>un-fracod-līce<span class="pron"> | un.frɑ.kod.liː.tʃe |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adverb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Not dishonourably, honourably, virtuously</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">materiam gerendis rebus optavimus, quo ne virtus tacita consenesceret</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic wilnode andweorces tō ðam weorce ðe mē beboden wæs tō wyrcanne, ðæt wæs, ðæt is unfracoðlīce and gerisenlīce mihte steōran and reccan ðone anweald ðe mē befæst wæs</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 17; Fox 58, 27)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="geōmor-mōd" d:title="geōmor-mōd">
		<body>
			<h1>geōmor-mōd<span class="pron"> | Ge͜oː.mor.moːd |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">of persons.</span>
					</p>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(1)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">sad-hearted, sad of soul, sorrowful</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Þā wearð Esau swīðe sārig and geōmormōd (consternatus)</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Gen. 27, 34)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Cain gewāt gongan geōmormōd, wineleās wrecca</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Gen. 1050)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ic teāras sceal geōtan geōmormōd</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Cri. 173)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Geōmormōd, . . . earg and unrōt</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (1407: Hy. 10, 29)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-en">if a young man must ever be sad of soul, brave heart's thought, also cheery bearing must he have</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Ā scyle geong mon wesan geōmormōd, heard heortan geþoht, swylce habban sceal blīþe gebǣro</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Kl. 42)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Geōmormōdes drūsendne hyge</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Gū. 1033)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Gewitan him (the apostles after the ascension) gongan . . . geōmormōde</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Cri. 535: An. 406)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(2)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">gloomy from a sense of evil fortune or danger</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Eald æscwiga, se þe eall geman gārcwealm gumena (him bið grim sefa), onginneð geōmormōd geongum cempan . . . higes cunnian</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (B. 2044)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Þām folce geōmormōdum (the people threatened by Holofernes' army)</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Jud. 144)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">of birds</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Fugelas cyrrað from þām gūþfrecan geōmormōde eft tō earde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ph. 353)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="hæn-fugul" d:title="hæn-fugul">
		
		<body>
			<h1>hæn-fugul<span class="pron"> | xæn.fu.ɣul |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A hen</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. gallina)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">gallina</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Henfugel gallina</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. Ecg. C. 40; Th. ii. 164, 21)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">throw it to a hen</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gewurp tō sumum hen [hæn, MS. B.] fugule</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Herb. 4, 10; Lchdm. i. 92, 16)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">iiii hænfugulas four hens</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Th. Chart. 509, 18)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">after that the hens died</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðǣr æfter swulten ða henne fugeles</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 1130; Erl. 259, 25)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="wiþ-meting" d:title="wiþ-meting">
		<body>
			<h1>wiþ-meting<span class="pron"> | wiθ.me.ting |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Comparison</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. comparatio)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Wiðmetincg comparatio</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Scint. 194, 13)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Of wiðmetincge ex comparatione</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (103, 9)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="fȳr-bryne" d:title="fȳr-bryne">
		<body>
			<h1>fȳr-bryne<span class="pron"> | fyːr.bry.ne |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A fire burning</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. incendium)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">an immense fire happened among the Romans</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Wearþ ungemetlīc fȳrbryne mid Rōmānum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 4, 7; Bos. 87, 18)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="clīða" d:title="clīða">
		
		<body>
			<h1>clīða<span class="pron"> | kliː.θɑ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -an</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A plaster, salve, poultice</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. emplastrum, malagma)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the prophet Isaiah made for king Hezekiah a plaster for his sore</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Se wītega Isaias worhte ðam cyninge Ezechie clīðan to his dolge</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. i. 476, 1)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Clīða malagma</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. 74, 9: Ælfc. Gr. 9, 1; Som. 8, 22)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">one must make him a poultice for his forehead</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Man sceal him wyrcean clīðan tofōran his heāfde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lchdm. iii. 8, 13, 16)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">as if a poultice were laid there</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Swylce ðǣr clȳða togelǣd wǣre</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Herb. 51, 2; Lchdm. i. 154, 18)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">take the lesser of these herbs, make it into a poultice</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðyssa wyrta genim ða læssan, wyrc to clȳðan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (143, 5; Lchdm. i. 266, 15: 173, 4; Lchdm. i. 304, 15)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">take roots of these herbs, pounded with oil, and with wheaten meal, and with soap, in the manner in which thou wouldst make a poultice</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Genim ðyssa wyrta wyrtruman, gecnucude mid ele, and mid hwǣtenan meluwe, and mid sāpan, ðam gemete ðe ðū clȳðan wyrce</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (184, 4; Lchdm. i. 322, 14: 130, 1; Lchdm. i. 240, 21: 125; Lchdm. i. 236, 21)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="be-seten" d:title="be-seten">
		<body>
			<h1>be-seten<span class="pron"> | be.se.ten |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>participle</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">beset; circumdatus</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:be-sittan" class="xref-target">be-sittan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-dafenian" d:title="ge-dafenian">
		
		<body>
			<h1>ge-dafenian<span class="pron"> | je.dɑ.fe.ni.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -ode</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -od</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To be becoming or fit, to behove</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. decere, convenīre)</span>
					</p>
					<ol class="sub-senses">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sub-heading">chiefly used impersonally, it behoves, it is becoming or fit, ought</span>
								<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. decet, oportet)</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-en">I will ask whether it was becoming to Abraham</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Ic axige hwæðer hit mihte gedafnian Abrahame</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Boutr. Scrd. 21, 47)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-en">it befits teachers that they salt the minds of believing men with the salt of wisdom</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Lāreōwum gedafenaþ ðæt hī mid wīsdōmes sealte geleāffulra manna mōd sylton</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. ii. 536, 16 : L. E. I. 24; Th. ii. 420, 32)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">me oportet</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Me gedæfnaþ</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Jn. Skt. Lind. 9, 4)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">te oportet</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Ðē gedæfneþ</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (3, 7)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">te decet</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Ðē gedafenaþ</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 64, 1 : 92, 7 : Ælfc. Gr. 33; Som. 37, 20 : Andr. Kmbl. 633; An. 317)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">aliis civitātibus oportet me evangelizāre regnum Dei</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Me gedafenaþ ōðrum ceastrum Godes rīce bodian</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Lk. Bos. 4, 43 : Ælfc. Gr. 33; Som. 37, 21)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">decuit</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Gedafenode</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (33; Som. 37, 21 : Bd. 4, 11; S. 579. 11)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-en">it was becoming that the Almighty first created the temporary light</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Hit gedafnode ðæt se Ælmihtiga ǣrest ðæt hwīlendlīce leōht geworhte</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Boutr. Scrd. 19, 4 : 21, 39)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">decet nos</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Gedæfnad is ūs</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. Kmbl. Lind. 3, 15)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-hādod" d:title="ge-hādod">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-hādod<span class="pron"> | je.xɑː.dod |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">In holy orders, ordained</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="āhreōsan" d:title="āhreōsan">
		<body>
			<h1>āhreōsan<span class="pron"> | ɑː.xre͜oː.sɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -hreās, pl: -hruron</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -hroren</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To rush, fall, fall down</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. irruere, mere, corruere, decidere)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">flaverunt venti et irruerunt in domum illam</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Bleōwun windas and ahruron on ðæt hūs</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. Bos. 7, 25)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">in God's name let this temple fall down</span>
							<span class="q-oe">On Godes naman ahreōse ðīs tempel</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. i. 72, 2, 5)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">he fell</span>
							<span class="q-oe">He ahreās</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. i. 192, 20)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="fōran-to" d:title="fōran-to">
		<body>
			<h1>fōran-to<span class="pron"> | foː.rɑn.to |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>preposition</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Before</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. ante)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">before Easter</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Fōran-to Eāstron before Easter</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 921; Erl. 104, 37)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">before midsummer</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Fōran-to middum sumera before midsummer</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (920; Erl. 104, 31)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">antelūcānum tempus</span>
							<span class="q-oe">fōran-to uhtes</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Nar. 15, 31)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:to-fōran" class="xref-target">to-fōran</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="un-seþe" d:title="un-seþe">
		<body>
			<h1>un-seþe<span class="pron"> | un.se.θe |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:un-sōþ" class="xref-target">un-sōþ</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ed-wist" d:title="ed-wist">
		<body>
			<h1>ed-wist<span class="pron"> | ed.wist |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Crīst is on twām edwistum, on Godcundnysse and on menniscnyise</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. Th. ii. 292, 15)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="car-least" d:title="car-least">
		<body>
			<h1>car-least<span class="pron"> | kɑr.læ͜ɑst |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Freedom from care, security, carelessness</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. securitas)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">to receive a ring in dreams betokens freedom from care</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ring on swefoum underfōn carleāste getācnaþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lchdm. iii. 198, 21, 29: 210, 5)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ārfæstnes" d:title="ārfæstnes">
		<body>
			<h1>ārfæstnes<span class="pron"> | ɑːr.fæst.nes |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">piety</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. Pietas)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Pietas ārfæstnys</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Angl. xi. 107, 8)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ǣrfastness</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wülck. Gl. 251, 18)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">mercy, clemency, kindness</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">per pietatis viscera</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðurh ðā mildheortnesse his ārfæsðnesse</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 99, 1)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">sinum pietatis expandit</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðone greādan his ārfæstnesse and his frōfre hē gebrǣt</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (407, 11: Gr. D. 146, 28)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē bæd ðone ælmihtigan for his ārfæstnysse ꝥ hē þām preōste gemiltsode</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. S. 6, 167: 30, 350)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ongeān þǣre ārfæstnysse hē sylð ārleāsnysse, þæt hē ne ārige his underþeōddum ne his gelīcum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wlfst. 59, 16)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="leāctūn-weard" d:title="leāctūn-weard">
