<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="wracu" d:title="wracu">
		<body>
			<h1>wracu<span class="pron"> | wrɑ.ku |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">Adversam fortunam videas sobriam, succintamque, et ipsius adversitatis exercitatione prudentem.</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Siō wiþerweardnes biþ simle untǣlu and wracu (wæru, v. l.) āscirred (-scirped?) mid ðære styringe hire āgenre frecennesse.</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 20; Fox 72, 6)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:wacor" class="xref-target">wacor</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="giscian" d:title="giscian">
		<body>
			<h1>giscian<span class="pron"> | Gi.ʃi.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">to sob</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic nū wēpende and gisciende misfō</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 2; F. 4, 8)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:gesca" class="xref-target">gesca</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="lǣnan" d:title="lǣnan">
		<body>
			<h1>lǣnan<span class="pron"> | læː.nɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to lend, grant temporary possession of a thing on the condition of the return of the same or its equivalent</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Be ðām monnum ðe heora wǣpna tō monslyhte lǣnað. Gif hwā his wǣpnes ōðrum onlǣne (lǣne, v. l.)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ll. Th. i. 74, 1-3)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">I a.</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">to lend for a consideration, lend (money) at interest</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">pecuniam suam injusto foenore mutuam dederit</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Gif bisceop . . . oððe hwylc Godes þeōw lǣnð his feoh tō unrihtun gafole</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Ll. Th. ii. 198, 14)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Be þām gehādodum mannum þe hyra feoh lǣnað tō hȳre</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (194, 31)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ys forboden ꝥ hē his feoh, ne his ǣhta (pecuniam suam vel possessiones) tō nānum unrihtum gafole ne lǣne; ꝥ is ꝥ hē hine māran ne bidde tō āgyfanne þonne hē him ǣr lǣnde; ac for lufe lǣne gehwā ōðrum his feoh and his ǣhta</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (194, 15-19)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to grant</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Se gōda līchama þancode Gode ealre þǣre āre . . . þe hē him lǣnde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wlfst. 237, 6)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">sapientiam praestans</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Wīsdōm lǣnende ł tȳðiende</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. L. 18, 8)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="telgor" d:title="telgor">
		
		<body>
			<h1>telgor<span class="pron"> | tel.ɣor |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A plant, shoot, twig</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">omne virgultum agri</span>
							<span class="q-oe">On ðam dæge ðe God geworhte ǣlcne telgor on eorðan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Gen. 2, 5)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Telgre vimen</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Engl. Stud. xi. 67, 95)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gif hwā mid him ðysse wyrte (verbascum) āne tealgre byrþ, ne biþ hē brēged mid ǣnigum ōgan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lchdm. ii. 176, 3)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Tealgras propagines</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Blickl. Gl.)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðeōs wyrt (wild gourd) wið ða eorðan hyre telgra tōbrǣdeþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lchdm. i. 324, 3 note)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A plant, shoot, twig</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:next word" class="xref-target">next word</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="mirce" d:title="mirce">
		<body>
			<h1>mirce<span class="pron"> | mir.Ke |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>neuter noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">For another rendering of An. 1315 see ge-scirdan</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge-scirdan" class="xref-target">ge-scirdan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-hwemman" d:title="ge-hwemman">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-hwemman<span class="pron"> | je.xwem.mɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -ed</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To slope</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Næs þæt hūs æfter manna gewunan getimbrod, ac mid mislicum torrum gehwemmed (the walls were not smooth and vertical but of varying inclination on account of projecting rocks) tō gelīcnysse sumes scræfes</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. Th. i. 508, 17)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:hwem-dragen" class="xref-target">hwem-dragen</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-scrence" d:title="ge-scrence">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-scrence<span class="pron"> | je.ʃren.Ke |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Withered, dry</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">habebat manum aridam</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē hæfde hond gescrengce ł drȳge</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lk. L. 6, 8)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:mis-scrence" class="xref-target">mis-scrence</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-winfullīc" d:title="ge-winfullīc">
		
		<body>
			<h1>ge-winfullīc<span class="pron"> | je.win.ful.liːK |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Laborious, toilsome</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. laboriōsus)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">ne tam periculōsam, tam incertam peregrinātionem adīre debērent</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt hī ne þorftan in swā frǣcne sīþfætt, and on swā gewinfullīcne, and on swā uncūþe ællþeōdignysse fēran</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 1, 23; S. 485, 37)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">non se ultra tam laboriōsis expedītiōnibus posse fatīgārī</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt hī nō mā ne mihton swā gewinnfullīcum fyrdum swencte beōn</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (1, 12; S. 481, 4)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-merce" d:title="ge-merce">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-merce<span class="pron"> | je.mer.Ke |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge-mirce" class="xref-target">ge-mirce</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="lītan" d:title="lītan">
		<body>
			<h1>lītan<span class="pron"> | liː.tɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">to cause to bow, to bend, incline</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the mind of every man inclines the body whither it will</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt ingeþonc ǣlces monnes ðone līchoman līt ðider hit wile</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. Met. Fox 26, 237; Met. 26, 119)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="glēsan" d:title="glēsan">
		<body>
			<h1>glēsan<span class="pron"> | gleː.sɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Hē ðās bōc gloesde</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Jn. p. 188, 15)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ofer-glēsan" class="xref-target">ofer-glēsan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="rihtan" d:title="rihtan">
		<body>
			<h1>rihtan<span class="pron"> | rix.tɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -te</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to right, to restore to a proper position that which is displaced, erect, direct</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">he (God) with his hands again in the heavenly kingdom restored the celestial seats (after the expulsion of the rebellious angels)</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē mid handum eft on heofonrīce rihte rodorstōlas</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. Th. 46, 24; Gen. 749)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">ad dirigendos pedes nostros in uia pacis</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Tō rehtanne foet ūsra in woege sibbe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lk. Skt. Rush. 1, 79)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to right a person, to replace a person in the rights of which he is wrongfully deprived</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Heō smeādan hū heō mehton monige men ryhtan, ge godcundra hāda ge weorldcundra, ge on londum ge on mā ðara þinga ðe heō on forhaldne wēran</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Chart. Th. 139, 25)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">III.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to make right that which is faulty, set right, rectify, correct, amend</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">that I may set thy mind thoroughly right</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ne sēce ic nō ða bēc, ac ðæt ðæt ða bēc forstent, ðæt ic ðīn gewit swīðe rihte</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 5, 1; Fox 10, 20)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Sume dēman myccle swīðor rihtaþ Godes folc ðonne hiē reāfan earme. Ða dēman beōþ ǣghwǣr ge ðæt hiē him selfum heora synna bebeorgaþ ge eāc ōðre syngiende rihtaþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Blickl. Homl. 63, 16-25)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">corrigimus</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Wē boetas ł wē hrihð</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. Kmbl. p. 2, 2)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Se wīsdōm hine rēte and rihte mid his andsworum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. tit. 5; Fox x, 9)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">let weights and measures be made correct with all diligence</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gemeta and gewihta rihte man georne</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. C. S. 9; Th. i. 380, 24)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ælþeōdige mæn, gif hiō hiora hǣmed rihtan (amend) nyllaþ, of lande gewīten</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. Wih. 4; Th. i. 38, 1)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">emendasse</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Tō rihtanne ł tō boetanne</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. Kmbl. p. 2, 12)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">IV.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to keep right, direct, rule</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">gens Anglorum quam regebat</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Angelþeōde ðe hē rihte</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 3, 3; S. 525, 29)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">rexit ecclesiam</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē ða circan heōld and rihte</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (3, 20; S. 550, 32 : 1, 23; S. 485, 23)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ða sylfan stōwe ðe Eata mid abbudes onwalde heōld and rihte (regebat)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (4, 27; S. 604, 41)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðys eōwde stȳran and rihtan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Blickl. Homl. 191, 28)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge-rihtan" class="xref-target">ge-rihtan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="heāh-beorg" d:title="heāh-beorg">
		<body>
			<h1>heāh-beorg<span class="pron"> | xæ͜ɑːx.be͜orɣ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A high mountain</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">et altitudines montium ipse conspicit</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē ðās heāhbeorgas healdeþ swylce</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 94, 4)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="eorþ-hele" d:title="eorþ-hele">
		<body>
			<h1>eorþ-hele<span class="pron"> | e͜orθ.xe.le |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A heap</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. tumulus)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the dew was about the camp, as it were a heap of hail</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Wæs ðæt deāw abūtan ða fyrdwīc, swilce hit hagoles eorþhele wǣre</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ex. 10, 14)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="lim-nacod" d:title="lim-nacod">
		<body>
			<h1>lim-nacod<span class="pron"> | lim.nɑ.kod |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">With uncovered limbs, naked</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Se eādega wer [Noah] him selfa sceāf reāf of līce; læg ðū limnacod</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. 76; Th. 94, 23; Gen. 1566)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="gearo-wita" d:title="gearo-wita">
		<body>
			<h1>gearo-wita<span class="pron"> | Gæ͜ɑ.ro.wi.tɑ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">uti est ad intellectum ratiocinatio</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Swilce siō smeāung and siō gesceādwīsnes is tō metanne wiþ þone gearowitan</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. F. 224, 4)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ofen" d:title="ofen">
		<body>
			<h1>ofen<span class="pron"> | o.fen |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Hē sceolde beōn forbærned on hātum ofne</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. Th. ii. 18, 26)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Þā forlēt hē þone lǣmnan ofn ðæs mænniscan līchornan</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Shrn. 50, 33)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ālamp" d:title="ālamp">
		<body>
			<h1>ālamp<span class="pron"> | ɑː.lɑmp |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>participle</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">happened, occurred</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ālimpan" class="xref-target">ālimpan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="āgeara" d:title="āgeara">
		
		<body>
			<h1>āgeara<span class="pron"> | ɑː.Gæ͜ɑ.rɑ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">prepared</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. paratus)</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:gearwa in gearo" class="xref-target">gearwa in gearo</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="scendþ(u)" d:title="scendþ(u)">
		<body>
			<h1>scendþ(u)<span class="pron"> | ʃendθ, u |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge-scendþ(u)" class="xref-target">ge-scendþ(u)</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="un-geheāfdod" d:title="un-geheāfdod">
		<body>
			<h1>un-geheāfdod<span class="pron"> | un.Ge.xæ͜ɑːf.dod |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Not come to a head</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gif se slyte blind bið and mid ðam geswelle ungeheāfdud, ðonne lege ðū ða wyrte ðǣrtō, sōna hit sceal openian</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lchdm. i. 92, 26)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="dæges" d:title="dæges">
		<body>
			<h1>dæges<span class="pron"> | dæ.Ges |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adverb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Daily</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. die)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">die ac nocte</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Dæges and nihtes</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 1, 2: Bt. 35, 6; Fox 168, 7: Chr. 894; Erl. 93. 5)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ig-dæges" class="xref-target">ig-dæges</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:y-dæges" class="xref-target">y-dæges</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="caucetung" d:title="caucetung">
		<body>
			<h1>caucetung<span class="pron"> | kɑ.u.Ke.tung |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A laughing in a cackling manner</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. cachinnus)</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ceahhetung" class="xref-target">ceahhetung</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="marm-stān" d:title="marm-stān">
		<body>
			<h1>marm-stān<span class="pron"> | mɑrm.stɑːn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Se marmstān sceolde beōn onwænded, sē wæs āseted ofer his byrgene. Þā þā se marmstān āweg genumen wæs</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Gr. D. 302, 15-16)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Hī gemētton āne mǣre þrūh geworht of marmstāne</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. S. 20, 80)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Godes encgel sette ēnne marmstān æt þæs mǣdenes heāfde</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (8, 201)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="āhwettan" d:title="āhwettan">
		<body>
			<h1>āhwettan<span class="pron"> | ɑː.xwet.tɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -hwette</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -hwetted</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to whet, excite</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. excitare, accendere)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">that I may excite thy desire</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt ic ðē mǣge lust ahwettan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Andr. Kmbl. 606; An. 303)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to provide</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. adhibere, subministrare)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">I will provide you the favour [liberal supply] of every good</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic eōw gōda gehwæs ēst ahwette</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Andr. Kmbl. 678; An. 339)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">III.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to cast away, drive away</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. abigere, repudiare)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">God will cast them away from his favour</span>
							<span class="q-oe">God ahwet hie from his hyldo</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. 21; Th. 26, 13)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="heall-ærn" d:title="heall-ærn">
		<body>
			<h1>heall-ærn<span class="pron"> | xæ͜ɑll.ærn |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:heal-ærn" class="xref-target">heal-ærn</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="fird" d:title="fird">
		
		
		<body>
			<h1>fird<span class="pron"> | fird |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">in glosses or referring to other than English forces</span>
					</p>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(1)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">an expedition, campaign</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Faerd (fertd, Erf. ) expeditio</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Txts. 61, 790)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Fird</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 29, 69)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Fird expeditio, i. praeparatio</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (145, 41)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Fyrda expeditionum</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (76, 62 : 29, 70)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Firdum expeditionibus</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (30, 8)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ðā gesægdon Rōmāne Bryttum ꝥ hī nō mā ne mihton for heora gescyldnysse swā gewinnfullicum fyrdum swencte beōn</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. I. 12; Sch. 33, 17)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(2)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">an army</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ferd exercitus</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 145, 41)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">venerunt ad Moysen et ad omnem coetum</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Hi cōmon tō Mōise þǣr hē mid þǣre firde wæs</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Num. 13, 27)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">cum exercitibus suis</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Cōmon þā fīf cynegas mid firde</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Jos. 10, 5)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Eneas mid his firde fōr in Italiam</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. ii; S. 50, 24)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Mid lytelre firde</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (3, 7; S. 118)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hē mid firde wæs farende þǣr Constantinus wæs mid ōþerre fierde</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (6, 31; S. 284, 32)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Philippus gelǣdde fird on Læcedemonie</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (3, 7; S. 118, 24)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">bellum parans</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Hē gegaderade fierd</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (6, 31; S. 286, 9)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Eōde Porrus mē on houd mid ealle his ferde and dugoþe</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Nar. 19, 17)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Swylce man fyrde trymme and samnige</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Bl. H. 01, 31)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Fyrdum exercitibus</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 145, 42)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(3)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">a camp</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ær þǣm gefeohte, þā hiē on firde wǣron</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 4, l; S. 156, 34)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-en">where he was encamped</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Hannibal bestæl on þone consul, ðǣr hō on firde sætt</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (4, 10; S. 198, 12)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">used in reference to the English militia</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Besæt siō fierd hiē þǣr ūtan þī hwīle þe hiē þǣr lengest mete hæfdon. Ac hiē hæfdon þā heora stemn gesetenne and hiora mete genotudne . . . fÞā se cyng wæs þiderweardes mid þǣre scīre þe mid him fierdedon . . . , siō ōþeru fierd wæs hāmweardes</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 894 ; P. 85, 22-86, 4)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Seō fird</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (P. 88, 7, 20)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gesomnode man ormǣte fyrde Defenisces folces and Sumorsǣtisces . . . beāh seō Englisce fyrd</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (looi; P. 133, 23)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Wæs þæs cynges fyrde hindan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (948; P. 112, 30)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Cōm seō Centisce fyrde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (999 ; P. 131, 21)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē hēt ōðre fyrde ābannan, . . . and his fyrde tōscyfte . . . , seō fyrde eall tōgædre cōm</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (1095; P. 231, 21)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Sende hē his sunu of þǣre fierde micle werede</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (823; P. 60, 12)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Mid West-Seaxna fierde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (851; P. 64, 21)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Of þǣre fierde, ge eāc of þǣm burgum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (894; P. 84, 30)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Cōm Byrhtnðð ealdorman mid his fyrde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (993 ; P. 126, 5 : 1001 ; P. 133, 22)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Sceōc hē on niht fram þǣre fyrde him sylfum tō mycelum bismore</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (992 ; P. 127, 16)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ecgbryht lǣdde fierd</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (827; P. 60, 32)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ferde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (605; P. 23, 5)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gegaderode Ælfrēd cyning his fierd</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (894 ; P. 84, 23)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Fird</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (905 ; P. 94, I)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hēt hē beōdan ofer ealle þā fird</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (94, 4)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē sende firde ge of West-Seaxum ge of Mercum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (910; P. 94, 28)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Fyrde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (993; P. 127, 27)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gif þisses hwæt gelimpe þenden fyrd ūte siē, hit siē twybōte</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ll. Th. i. 88, ii)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gif hwā būtan leāfe of fyrde gewende þe se cyning sylf on sȳ, plihte him sylfum . . . , and sē þe elles of fyrde gewende, beo sē, cxx. scill. scyldig</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (310, 28-30)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gif hwā on fyrde griðbryce fulwyrce, þolige</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="trum-līce" d:title="trum-līce">
		
		<body>
			<h1>trum-līce<span class="pron"> | trum.liː.tʃe |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adverb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">firmly, strongly, steadfastly</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. firmiter)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Trumlīce firmiter</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. Gr. 38; Zup. 236, 8)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">etiam quae humanis oculis fortia videntur</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ða gōdan weorc, ðeāh ðe hiē beforan monna eāgum ðyncen trumlīce gedōn</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 34; Swt. 237, 2)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ð æt leōd and lagu trumlīce stande</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wulfst. 74, 8)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Eahta sweras syndon ðe rihtlīcne cynedom trum—līce up wegaþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L.I. P. 3 ; Th. ii. 306, 19)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Trumlīcor firmius</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Rtl. 34, 26)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Freōndscype trumlīcust (firmissimē) wunaþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Sciut. 197, 18)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">in a way that encourages (?)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ungeleāffullnise trumlīce- strongly (?); but the Latin is clementer geðreāð bið</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Mk. Skt. p. 5, 13)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="mirgan" d:title="mirgan">
		<body>
			<h1>mirgan<span class="pron"> | mir.ɣɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:myrgan" class="xref-target">myrgan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="neāhfeald-lic" d:title="neāhfeald-lic">
		<body>
			<h1>neāhfeald-lic<span class="pron"> | næ͜ɑːx.fæ͜ɑld.liːtʃ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Intimate</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">þurh þā hālgan sprǣcu þæs gāstlican līfes.</span>
							<span class="q-la">vicaria relalione</span>
							<span class="q-oe">H gereordon hī sylfe mid neāh-fealdlicre gesægne</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Gr. D. 168. 17.)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="mynster-līc" d:title="mynster-līc">
		<body>
			<h1>mynster-līc<span class="pron"> | myn.ster.liːtʃ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Monastic</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">monastic institutions</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Man ārǣrde cyrcan on his rīce geond eall and mynsterlīce gesetnyssa</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Swt. A. S. Rdr. 97, 71)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ā-stīflan" d:title="ā-stīflan">
		<body>
			<h1>ā-stīflan<span class="pron"> | ɑː.stiː.flɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Āstīfode obrigesceret, āstīfedan obriguerunt</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 63, 62, 65)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(1)</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">lit. to become incapable of motion</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hē āstīfode and se earm stōd ungebīgendlic</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Gr. D. 254, 36)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Heora handa āstīfedon</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. Th. i. 598, 11)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Þā mūlas āstīfodon</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. S. 31, 985)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hē āstīfod lǣge</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Bl. H. 193, 8)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hī stōdon swilce hī āstīfode wǣron</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. S. 31, 375)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Āstīfode on stāna gelīcnysse</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (1001)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(2)</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">fig. to become incapable of action from fear, wonder</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Āstifedon (obriguerunt) ealle þā būendan</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. L. fol. 187 b, 12 ( = Ex. 15, 15))</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">stupet attonito impia turba timore</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Þǣr stænt āstīfad stāne gelīcast eal ārleās heāp</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Dōm. L. 173)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="eāgan beorht" d:title="eāgan beorht">
