						<span class="meaning-en">Recompense, compensation</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Wiðerriht vel edleān hostimentum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. i. 22, 24)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-hōfod" d:title="ge-hōfod">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-hōfod<span class="pron"> | je.xoː.fod |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Hoofed, having a hoof</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Þā þe synd gehōfode on horses gelīcnysse wǣron unclǣne</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. S. 25, 44)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="for-ðam" d:title="for-ðam">
		
		
		
		
		<body>
			<h1>for-ðam<span class="pron"> | for.θɑm |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>conjunction</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">For that, for that reason which, for, because</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. nam, quia)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">blessed are the poor in spirit, for theirs is the kingdom of heaven</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Eādige synd ða gāstlīcan þearfan, forðam hyra ys heofena rīce</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. Bos. 5, 3: Ps. Spl. 24, 22: Beo. Th. 301; B. 149: Cd. 167; Th. 209, 30; Exod. 507: Runic pm. 20; Kmbl. 343, 15; Hick. Thes. i. 135, 40)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">he went there chiefly for the walruses, because they have very good bone in their teeth</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Swīðost he fōr ðyder for ðǣm horshwælum, forðæm hī habbaþ swȳðe æðele bān on hyra tōþum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 1, 1; Bos. 20, 16, 28: Bt. Met. Fox 5, 76; Met. 5, 38)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">my people counselled me that I should seek thee, because they knew my capacity of strength</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Me ðæt gelǣrdon leōde mīne ðæt ic ðē sōhte, forðan hie mægenes cræft mīnne cūðon</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Beo. Th. 840; B. 418: Ps. Spl. 6, 2: Apstls. Kmbl. 93; Ap. 47: Menol. Fox 42; Men. 21)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">they suffer torment because they neglected the service of God</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hī wīte þoliaþ forðon hie þegnscipe Godes forgȳmdon</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. 18; Th. 21, 19; Gen. 326: Exon. 10 a; Th. 11, 11; Cri. 169: Beo. Th. 4688; B. 2349: Ps. Spl. 11, 1: Bd. 4, 19; S. 587, 30)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">blessed are they who weep now, for they shall be comforted</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Eādige synd ða ðe nū wēpaþ, forðamðe hī beōþ gefrēfrede</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. Bos. 5, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9, 10, 12: Cd. 184; Th. 230, 1; Dan. 226: Bt. Met. Fox 20, 73; Met. 20, 37)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">this verb [to will] has no imperative, for the will must always be free</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Næfþ ðys word [willan] nǣnne imperātīvum, forðanðe se willa sceall beōn ǣfre frig</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. Gr. 32; Som. 36, 11: Homl. Th. ii. 290, 1, 3, 25)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">because the sun in its setting goes nearer there than in any other land, there are milder weathers than in Britain</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Forðonðe siō sunne ðǣr gǣþ neār on setl, ðonne on ōðrum lande, ðǣr syndon lȳðran wedera ðonne on Brittannia</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 1, 1; Bos. 24, 20, 32: Mt. Bos. 7, 13: Ps. Spl. 1, 7: Exon. 25 b; Th. 74, 7, Cri. 1203: Beo. Th. 1010; B. 503)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="hālettan" d:title="hālettan">
		
		<body>
			<h1>hālettan<span class="pron"> | xɑː.let.tɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Gif gē hālettaþ (salutaveritis) eōwre brōþer</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. R. 5, 47)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">salutate domum</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Hǣleteþ þæt hūs</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (10, 12)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">cum me more rituque salutaret</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Þā se biscop tō mē cwōm, ðā grētte hē mē sōna and [h]ālette his leōdþeāwe</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Nar. 27, 17)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">gloriosissimo regi Ceoluulfo Baeda famulus Christi et Presbyter</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Ic, Bēda, Crīstes ðeōw and mæssepreōst, sende grētan þone leōfastan cyning and hālettan Ceōlwulf</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. praef.; Sch. 1. 3)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge-hālettan" class="xref-target">ge-hālettan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="aclian" d:title="aclian">
		<body>
			<h1>aclian<span class="pron"> | ɑ.kli.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:āclian" class="xref-target">āclian</a>
			</p>
		</body>
