			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Forlǣtan wē leāsunga and līcettunga, tǣlnessa and twysprǣcnessa</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Verc. Först. 94, 3)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="āweorpan" d:title="āweorpan">
		
		<body>
			<h1>āweorpan<span class="pron"> | ɑː.we͜or.pɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">present: 2sg: -wyrpst, 3sg: -wyrpþ</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: 1sg: -wearp, 3sg: -wearp, 2sg: -wurpe, pl: -wurpon</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -worpen</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">imperative: sg: -weorp, sg: -wurp, sg: -wyrp ðū</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To throw or cast from or down, to cast away or off, cast out, to degrade, reject, divorce</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. abjicere, dejicere, projicere, ejicere, propellere, repellere, reprobare, repudiare)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">that he shall cast thee from thy worldly kingdom</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt he ðec aweorpe of woruldrīce</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. 203; Th. 253, 1; Dan. 589)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">dejecisti eos, dum allevarentur</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðū awurpe hī, ðā hī wǣron upahafen</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Spl. 72, 18 : 79, 9: Ps. Th. 72, 14)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the curse is cast off</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Is wærgðu [wærgða MS.] aworpen</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 9 a ; Th. 7, 8 ; Cri. 98 : Bt. Met. Fox 23, 12; Met. 23, 6 : Bd. 3, 24; S. 557, 44 : Mt. Bos. 12, 28)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">then would the senate degrade him</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðā woldon senatus hine aweorpan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 3, 10; Bos. 70, 36: Bt. 37, 4; Fox 192, 10)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">ne projicias me</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ne aweorp ðū me</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Spl. 70, 10)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">oportet filium hominis reprobari</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Mannes sunu gebyreþ beōn aworpen</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Mk. Bos. 8, 31)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">a divorced wife</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Aworpen wīf</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. Æ1f. C. 7 ; Th. ii. 346, 6)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">homo apostata, vir inutilis</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Aworpen man biþ ā unnyt</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 47, 1; Hat. MS. 68 a, 23)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">to cast into</span>
							<span class="q-oe">awurpan on</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. Foxe 13, 50)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="swēr" d:title="swēr">
