			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:sæltna" class="xref-target">sæltna</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="folc-gefeoht" d:title="folc-gefeoht">
		<body>
			<h1>folc-gefeoht<span class="pron"> | folk.Ge.fe͜oxt |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>neuter noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Folk-battle, a great battle, pitched battle</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. publīca pugna, plēnum prælium)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the Scythians would not attack him in a pitched battle</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ða Sciððie noldon hine gesēcan to folcgefeohte</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 2, 5; Bos. 46, 5)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">nine great battles were fought</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Wurdon ix folcgefeoht gefohten</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 871; Erl. 77, 7: 887; Erl. 87, 9)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">in three pitched battles</span>
							<span class="q-oe">On þrīm folcgefeohtum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 3, 9; Bos. 66, 11)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-wǣtan" d:title="ge-wǣtan">
		
		<body>
			<h1>ge-wǣtan<span class="pron"> | je.wæː.tɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -wǣtte</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -wǣted, past participle sg: -wǣtt</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To wet, to make wet</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">send Lazarus, that he may wet the tip of his finger in water</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Onsend Ladzarus ðætte he gewǣte his ȳtemestan finger on wættre</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 43, 1; Swt. 309, 6; Hat. MS.)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the ropes creaked wet with the waters</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Strengas gurron wædo gewǣtte</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Andr. Kmbl. 749; An. 375)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="beorm-teāg" d:title="beorm-teāg">
		<body>
			<h1>beorm-teāg<span class="pron"> | be͜orm.tæ͜ɑːG |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A yeast-box</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Man sceal habban . . . bearmteāge</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Angl. ix. 264, 20)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="gat" d:title="gat">
		<body>
			<h1>gat<span class="pron"> | gɑt |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>neuter noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es, nominative pl: -u, nominative pl: -a, nominative pl: -o, accusative pl: -u, accusative pl: -a, accusative pl: -o</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A GATE</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. porta)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">when the Saviour approached the gate of the city</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðā se Hǣlend geneālǣhte ðære ceastre gate</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lk. Bos. 7, 12 : Exon. 12 b; Th, 20, 15; Cri. 318 : Ps. Spl. 117, 19 : Ps. Th. 126, 6)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:geat" class="xref-target">geat</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="un-ārweorþlic" d:title="un-ārweorþlic">
		<body>
			<h1>un-ārweorþlic<span class="pron"> | un.ɑːr.we͜orθ.liK |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Dishonourable, disgraceful</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Swā hit is eāc unārwurðlic (inhonestus) and bysmerlic ꝥ hig ōðres hādes reāf werian</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Chrd. 63, 24)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="mūþ-bana" d:title="mūþ-bana">
		<body>
			<h1>mūþ-bana<span class="pron"> | muːθ.bɑ.nɑ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -an</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">One who destroys with the mouth</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Him Grendel wearþ tō mūþbonan, leōfes mannes līc eall forswealg</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Beo. Th. 4165; B. 2079)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="twædding" d:title="twædding">
		<body>
			<h1>twædding<span class="pron"> | twæd.ding |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Adulation</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. adulatio)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Twaddung adulatio</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Chrd. 40, 28)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">eos adulationibus decipere</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hig mid twæddingum beswīcan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (62, 23)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="fliōn" d:title="fliōn">
		<body>
			<h1>fliōn<span class="pron"> | fli͜oːn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To flee</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. fugere)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">he must flee this world's splendour</span>
							<span class="q-oe">He sceal fliōn ðisse worulde wlite</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. Met. Fox 7, 60; Met. 7, 30)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:fleōn" class="xref-target">fleōn</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="æmtegian" d:title="æmtegian">
		<body>
			<h1>æmtegian<span class="pron"> | æm.te.Gi.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">to be at leisure</span>
					</p>
