			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:sam-tinges" class="xref-target">sam-tinges</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="burh-sittende" d:title="burh-sittende">
		
		<body>
			<h1>burh-sittende<span class="pron"> | burx.sit.ten.de |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>participle</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">City-dwelling, inhabiting a city</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. urbem incolens)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">adhœsit uni civium regionis illius</span>
							<span class="q-oe">He folgode ānum burhsittendum men ðæs rīces</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lk. Bos. 15, 15)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the sons of men dwelling in cities</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Folca bearn burgsittende</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. 52; Th. 66, 24; Gen. 1089: Exon. 12b; Th. 21, 20; Cri. 337)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Burgsittendra, gen. pl.</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (106b; Th. 407, 10; Rä. 26, 3)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="dwol-līc" d:title="dwol-līc">
		<body>
			<h1>dwol-līc<span class="pron"> | dwol.liːtʃ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Foolish, erring, heretical</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. stultus, hæreticus)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">this is not a foolish saying</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Nis ðis nān dwollīc sagu</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Jud. 15, 19)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">they extinguished the heretical doctrines</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hȳ adwæsedon ða dwollīcan lāra</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. Ælf. C. 33; Th. ii. 356, 11)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="merece" d:title="merece">
		<body>
			<h1>merece<span class="pron"> | me.re.Ke |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -an</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">smallage, wild celery</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-bennian" d:title="ge-bennian">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-bennian<span class="pron"> | je.ben.ni.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -ode</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -od</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To wound</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. vulnerare)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">wounded with a sword</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Bille gebennad</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 102 b; Th. 388, 3; Rä. 6, 2)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ben" class="xref-target">ben</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:benn" class="xref-target">benn</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="āfȳrd" d:title="āfȳrd">
		<body>
			<h1>āfȳrd<span class="pron"> | ɑː.fyːrd |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A eunuch</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. spado)</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:āfȳrida" class="xref-target">āfȳrida</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-sundfullīc" d:title="ge-sundfullīc">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-sundfullīc<span class="pron"> | je.sund.ful.liːK |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Safe, sound</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">there is never aught sound in the devil</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ne biþ ǣfre ōwiht gesundfullīces in ðam deōfle</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Shrn. 38, 35)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="bræsen" d:title="bræsen">
		
		<body>
			<h1>bræsen<span class="pron"> | bræ.sen |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">BRAZEN, made of brass</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. æreus, æneus)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Bræsen oððe ǣren æneus</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. Gr. 5; Som. 4, 59)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">posuisti ut arcum æreum brachia mea</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðū gesettest swā swā bogan bræsenne earmas mīne</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Lamb. 17, 35)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">strong, powerful, bold, daring</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. validus, fortis, potens, procax)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">then the bold lord of Babylon proclaimed</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gebeād ðā se bræsna Babilōne weard</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. 196; Th. 244, 16; Dan. 449)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="eāw-brǣce" d:title="eāw-brǣce">
		<body>
			<h1>eāw-brǣce<span class="pron"> | æ͜ɑːw.bræː.Ke |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ǣ-brǣce" class="xref-target">ǣ-brǣce</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="seōd" d:title="seōd">
		<body>
			<h1>seōd<span class="pron"> | se͜oːd |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A money-bag, purse, pouch</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Seōd marsupium vel marsippa (cf. marsupium a purse, 197, 16)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. i. 40, 65: 83, 12)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Kyninga seōd fiscus</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (ii. 39, 80)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðā ic eōw sende būtan seōde (sacculo) and codde . . . Se ðe hæfþ seōd gelīce nime codd.</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lk. Skt. 22, 35, 36)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Seōdas marsupia</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hpt. Gl. 500, 40 : Wrt. Voc. ii. 55, 9)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Siōdas</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (84, 37)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt feoh ðæt hī hæfdon on heora seōdurn</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Skt. i. 23, 262)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Seōdas loculos</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 52, 22 : 74, 18)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Wyrcaþ seōdas (seādas, Rush. : seādo, Lind. sacculos) ða ðe ne forealdigeaþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lk. Skt. 12, 33)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Seādo loculos</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Jn. Skt. Lind. 12, 6)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Seōdas</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Blickl. Homl. 69, 11)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="lǣta" d:title="lǣta">
		<body>
			<h1>lǣta<span class="pron"> | læː.tɑ |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:lǣtan" class="xref-target">lǣtan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-gladian" d:title="ge-gladian">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-gladian<span class="pron"> | je.glɑ.di.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">trans.</span>
					</p>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(1)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">to make glad, gladden</span>
							</p>
							<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
								<li>
									<p>
										<span class="sense-label">(a)</span>
										<span class="meaning-en">of a physical effect</span>
									</p>
									<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
										<li>
											<p>
												<span class="sense-label">(α)</span>
												<span class="meaning-en">of cheerful appearance</span>
											</p>
											<ul class="quotes">
												<li>
													<span class="q-la">exilaret (cor gaudens exhilarat faciem)</span>
													<span class="q-oe">Gegladað</span>
													<span class="q-cite"> (Kent. Gl. 516)</span>
												</li>
											</ul>
										</li>
										<li>
											<p>
												<span class="sense-label">(β)</span>
												<span class="meaning-en">of the reviving effects of a medicine</span>
											</p>
											<ul class="quotes">
												<li>
													<span class="q-oe">Hyt þone innoð wið þæs geallan tōgotennysse gegladað</span>
													<span class="q-cite"> (Lch. i. 270, 5)</span>
												</li>
											</ul>
										</li>
									</ol>
								</li>
							</ol>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(2)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">of a mental effect</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">nos laetificas</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Ðū ūsig gigladas</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Rtl. 31, 32)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Giglædas</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (21)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">nec pax nec pietas immo spes nulla quietis flentibus arrident</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Ne þǣr ārfæstnes sib ne hopa ne swige gegladað</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Dōm. L. 220)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">dedit requiem universis provinciis</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Hē his folc gegladode</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. A. 95, 107)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">laetificet</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Gegladiga</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Rtl. 18, 15)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">exhilaror</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Ic beō gegladod</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 145, 3)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(2)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">to please</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Sē sē þe þæt dēð þæt his þearfa beōð, sē gegladað God; and sē þe dēð ǣnig unnyt, . . . hē ābelhð his Drihtne</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Wlfst. 279, 1)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Gif hī mid gōdum weorcum hine gegladiað</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. T. Grn. 6, 16)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ꝥ hig God gegladian</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Ll. Th. ii. 256, 8)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(3)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">to make propitious, propitiate</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Se cāsere . . . offrigende his lāc his ārleāsum godum wolde hī gegladian . . . ꝥ hī him fylstan sceoldon</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. S. 28, 38)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(4)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">to appease, reconcile, make gentle what is hard</span>
							</p>
							<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
								<li>
									<p>
										<span class="sense-label">(a)</span>
										<span class="meaning-en">the object a person</span>
									</p>
									<ul class="quotes">
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Hē mid gebedum gegladað God</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. S. 3, 562)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-la">demulcet</span>
											<span class="q-oe">Gegladode</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (An. Ox. 2, 137)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Ꝥ hī þone rēðan cāsere mid sceattum gegladodon</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. S. 3, 231)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-la">repropitiarent, i. mitigarent</span>
											<span class="q-oe">Gegladedon</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (An. Ox. 4724: 2, 374)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-la">reconciliarent</span>
											<span class="q-oe">Gegladudon</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (7, 328)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Þæt hē him God gegladode</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. Th. ii. 30, 33)</span>
										</li>
									</ul>
								</li>
								<li>
									<p>
										<span class="sense-label">(b)</span>
										<span class="meaning-en">the object a feeling (anger, &amp;c.)</span>
									</p>
									<ul class="quotes">
										<li>
											<span class="q-la">placabit (indignationem)</span>
											<span class="q-oe">Gegladað</span>
										</li>
									</ul>
								</li>
							</ol>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-frēdan" d:title="ge-frēdan">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-frēdan<span class="pron"> | je.freː.dɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(i)</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">absolute</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">To have sensation</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Seō sāwul is sensus, ꝥ is andgit oððe fēlnyss, þonne heō gefrēt</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. S. I. 184)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(2)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">to be sensible of an object that touches the body</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Se lǣce wile ðæt se untruma his lǣceseax gefrēde, ǣr hē hit geseō</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 187, 10: 331, 21)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Gefrēdan hiere feōnda speru</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (277, 22)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ðon mā ðe mon his, feax mæg gefrēdan būtan ðām felle</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (139, 21)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Sē þe bær līc gefrēddan wolde, hē hyt scolde myd barum handum gefrēdan</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Solil. H. 43, 14)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
							<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
								<li>
									<p>
										<span class="sense-label">(2 a)</span>
										<span class="meaning-en">to feel a blow, heat, cold, &amp; c.</span>
									</p>
									<ul class="quotes">
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Ðū þās dyntas nāht ne gefrētst</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. S. 4, 147)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Hē þæs fȳres bryne gefrēdde him onbūtan</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (31, 884)</span>
										</li>
									</ul>
								</li>
							</ol>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(3)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">to be sensible of an action (gen.)</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">capilli super cerebrum insensibiliter oriuntur</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Ðæt feax grēwð ofer ðǣm brægene and his (the growing] mon ðeāh ne gefrēd (-frēt, v.l.)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">quasi nobis non sentientibus procedunt</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Suā giēmeleāslīce oft sceacað ūre geðōhtas from ūs, ðæt wē his (the careless escape of the thoughts) furðum ne gefrēdað</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 139, 16-20)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(4)</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">of the sense of easte</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ðȳ lǣs hē ðā bieternesse ðǣre wyrte gefrēde</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 303, 15)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(5)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">to be sensible of a state or condition</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hē swilces nān þing ofer ꝥ on him sylfum ne gefrēdde (ongæt, v.l.)</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Gr. D. 102, 4)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">ita ut gravius scissuram sentiat, si hanc immoderatius ligamenta constringant</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Him bið ðæt sār ðe gefrēdre, gif siō wund bið tō ungemetlīce fæste gewriðen</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 123, 19)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
							<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
								<li>
									<p>
										<span class="sense-label">(a)</span>
										<span class="sub-heading">with acc. and complement</span>
										<span class="meaning-en">to feel a thing so and so</span>
									</p>
									<ul class="quotes">
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Hē hine selfne untrumran gefrēd on his līcho-man</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 407, 25)</span>
										</li>
									</ul>
								</li>
								<li>
									<p>
										<span class="sense-label">(b)</span>
										<span class="sub-heading">with clause</span>
									</p>
									<ul class="quotes">
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Þǣr þǣr hit gefrēt ꝥ hit hraþost weaxan mæg</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 34, 10; F. 148, 21)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Ðonne gefrēd (-frēt, v.l.) hē ǣresð hwelc heō tô habbanne wæs</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 249, 7)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Ðæt hiē ongieton and gefrêden ðæt hiē suā micle mā beōð Godes bearn</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (251, 21)</span>
										</li>
									</ul>
								</li>
							</ol>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="of-wundrod" d:title="of-wundrod">
		<body>
			<h1>of-wundrod<span class="pron"> | of.wun.drod |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Þā cwæð eall seō meniu þe ðǣr mid stōd ofwundrod</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. S. 12, 228)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Dionysius þā āxode þone ǣrendracan ofwundrod, 'Eart þū, lā, se blinda þe swā geboren wǣre?'</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (29, 64)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="brǣr" d:title="brǣr">
		<body>
			<h1>brǣr<span class="pron"> | bræːr |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">a brier</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. tribulus)</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:brēr" class="xref-target">brēr</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="slǣp-drenc" d:title="slǣp-drenc">
		<body>
			<h1>slǣp-drenc<span class="pron"> | slæːp.drenk |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A sleeping-draught</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Slǣpdrenc; rædic, hymlic, wermōd, belone, cnuca ealle þā wyrte, dō in ealað</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lch. iii. 22, 27)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="un-āmeten-lic" d:title="un-āmeten-lic">
		
		<body>
			<h1>un-āmeten-lic<span class="pron"> | un.ɑː.me.ten.liːtʃ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Unmeasured</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. immensus)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Unāmetenlic immensus (Pater)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Rdr. 298, 9)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="hāl-wendlīc" d:title="hāl-wendlīc">
		<body>
			<h1>hāl-wendlīc<span class="pron"> | xɑːl.wend.liːK |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Salutary, healthful</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the Saviour's advent was salutary for both men and angels</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæs Hǣlendes tōcyme wæs hālwendlīc ǣgðer ge mannum ge englum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. i. 214, 22: ii. 220, 20: 564, 7)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the bishop proposed to them salutary counsel</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Him se bisceop hālwendlīce geþeaht forþbrohte</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Blickl. Homl. 205, 18)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="an-fōn" d:title="an-fōn">
		<body>
			<h1>an-fōn<span class="pron"> | ɑn.foːn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -fēng</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -fangen</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To take, take to one's self, receive, perceive, comprehend</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. accipere, suscipere, sumere, percipere, recipere)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">thou shouldest have taken to thyself shame from me</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðū sceonde æt me anfēnge</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. 42; Th. 54, 10; Gen. 875 : Exon. 112 a; Th. 429, 12; Rä. 43, 3: Ps. C. 50, 135; Ps. Grn. ii. 280, 135)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">to receive</span>
							<span class="q-oe">To anfōnne</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 3, 6; S. 528, 4)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:on-fōn" class="xref-target">on-fōn</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="galg-mōd" d:title="galg-mōd">
		<body>
			<h1>galg-mōd<span class="pron"> | gɑlɣ.moːd |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Sad in mind, gloomy</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. tristis anĭmo)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">his mother, greedy and gloomy, would go a sorrowful journey</span>
							<span class="q-oe">His mōdor, gīfre and galg-mōd, gegān wolde sorhfulne sīþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Beo. Th. 2558; B. 1277)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:gealg-mōd" class="xref-target">gealg-mōd</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="BRYNE" d:title="BRYNE">
		<body>
			<h1>BRYNE<span class="pron"> | bry.ne |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:BEYTNIAN" class="xref-target">BEYTNIAN</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="æ-bylgan" d:title="æ-bylgan">
		
		<body>
			<h1>æ-bylgan<span class="pron"> | æ.byl.ɣɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To make angry</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. exasperare)</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ābelgan" class="xref-target">ābelgan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="rēsung" d:title="rēsung">
