			<h1>rēsung<span class="pron"> | reː.sung |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:rǣswung" class="xref-target">rǣswung</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="hīw-cūþ" d:title="hīw-cūþ">
		<body>
			<h1>hīw-cūþ<span class="pron"> | xiːw.kuːθ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">of a house or family, domestic</span>
					</p>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(1)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">of persons</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">domesticis (sodalibus)</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Hīwcūþum</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (An. Ox. 5132)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Se cyngc betwux his hīwcūðum mannum blissode</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Ap. Th. 3, 4)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
							<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
								<li>
									<p>
										<span class="sense-label">(1 a)</span>
										<span class="sub-heading">figuratively</span>
									</p>
									<ul class="quotes">
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Hwæt is ꝥ þǣm men sȳ māre þearf tō þencenne þonne embe his sāuwle þearfe, ... and hwylce lātteōwas hē hæbbe, and hwyder hē gelǣded sȳ ... Sweotollīce wē magon ongeotan ꝥ þā syndon heōwcūðe (there are those belonging to the household, i. e. good or evil spirits?) þe wē geseōn ne magon</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Bl. H. 97, 23)</span>
										</li>
									</ul>
								</li>
							</ol>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(2)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">of things</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">domestica sollicitudo</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Hīwcūþ carfulnys</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (An. Ox. 4183)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">domesticę (sodalitatis)</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Hīwcūþre</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (2808)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">familiar</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">familiarissimum</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Þone hīwcūþestan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 147, 33)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(1)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">of persons</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ic ne eom him swǣ hiēwcūð</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 62, 6)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">hujus viri familiarissimus fuit Julianus</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Ðyses weres hīwcūðesta wæs Julianus</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Gr. D. 71, 11)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(2)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">of things</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ðeōs wyrt ys culfran swīðe hīwcūð (doves are very fond of this plant), þanon hȳ sum þeōdscipe columbinam hāteð</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Lch. i. 170, 13)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Þone deōfol þe sit on þīnum hneccan ic þē of ābleōw, and se deōfol his hīwcūðe setl sōna forlēt</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. S. 31, 1191)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:hīw-cūþ" class="xref-target">hīw-cūþ</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ell-þeōd" d:title="ell-þeōd">
		
		<body>
			<h1>ell-þeōd<span class="pron"> | ell.θe͜oːd |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A strange people, foreign nation</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. peregrina gens)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">they went into a foreign land</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hȳ fōron on ellþiēde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 4, 4; Bos. 81, 6)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:el-þeōd" class="xref-target">el-þeōd</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="feaxede" d:title="feaxede">
		<body>
			<h1>feaxede<span class="pron"> | fæ͜ɑk.se.de |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(1)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">having hair</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-en">this plant is with thick boughs and very narrow leaves, it looks rather as if furnished with hair</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Ðeōs wyrt is greāton bōgum and swȳþe smælon leāfon swylce heō mā fexede gesewen sȳ</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Lch. i. 250, 20)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(2)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">bushy, full of foliage (?), cf. feax ; ¶</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">de spinetis nascentibus</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Of ācynnendlicum ł fexedum (wexendum? The gloss to the passage in An. Ox. 2420 is: Of ācennendlicum, wexendum) þyrnetum</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Hpt. Gl. 463, 35)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:sceacgede" class="xref-target">sceacgede</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="on-spreca" d:title="on-spreca">
		<body>
			<h1>on-spreca<span class="pron"> | on.spre.kɑ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">One who brings a claim or charge</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðone āþ funde ðe se onspeca (claimant) on gehealden wǣre</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. Ed. 1; Th. i. 158, 20)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:sprecan" class="xref-target">sprecan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="leger-fæst" d:title="leger-fæst">
		<body>
			<h1>leger-fæst<span class="pron"> | le.Ger.fæst |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Sick, ill</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="gristbātian" d:title="gristbātian">
		<body>
			<h1>gristbātian<span class="pron"> | grist.bɑː.ti.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">to rage</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Fremit, i. perstrepit, furit, indignabatur gristbātaþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 150, 58)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:gristbitian" class="xref-target">gristbitian</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="āswunden" d:title="āswunden">
