			<h1>āswunden<span class="pron"> | ɑː.swun.den |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>participle</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">weakened, slothful</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:āswindan" class="xref-target">āswindan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="faber ferrarius" d:title="faber ferrarius">
		<body>
			<h1>faber ferrarius<span class="pron"> | fɑ.ber, fer.rɑ.ri.us |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:īsen-wyrhta" class="xref-target">īsen-wyrhta</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:isern-wyrhta" class="xref-target">isern-wyrhta</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="geofian" d:title="geofian">
		<body>
			<h1>geofian<span class="pron"> | Ge͜o.fi.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -ode</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -od</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To give, to endow</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. dare, donare)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">he can endow me with every good</span>
							<span class="q-oe">He mæg me geofian mid gōda gehwilcum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. 26; Th. 34, 31; Gen. 546)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:gifian" class="xref-target">gifian</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="-hīwe" d:title="-hīwe">
		<body>
			<h1>-hīwe<span class="pron"> | xiː.we |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:heard-hīwe" class="xref-target">heard-hīwe</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="nearu-ness" d:title="nearu-ness">
		<body>
			<h1>nearu-ness<span class="pron"> | næ͜ɑ.ru.ness |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
					</p>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">I a.</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">a narrow space, a place of small extent</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">ergastulo (e corporis ergastulo emigrare)</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Nearenesse</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (An. Ox. 979)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Þām men bið þurst getenge and nearones.</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lch. ii. 194, 2)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">crebris angustiis ad exitum propinquans</span>
							<span class="q-oe">For manegum nearonessum ic neālǣhte mīnum ende</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Gr. D. 243, 19)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">II a.</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">physical inconvenience, difficulty, troublesome action</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">factam sibi difficultatem videbant</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Hī gesāwon þā nearonessa and þā uneāðnesse þe him sylfum gedōn wæs</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Gr. D. 226, 17)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">III.</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Geseah hē frēfrende gesyhðe, seō him ealle þā nearonesse (neara-, v.l.) þǣre gemyngedan sorge (omnem anxietatem memoratae sollicitudinis) āfyrde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 4, II; Sch, 406, 9)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gif ealle wītegan wītegodon þæt Crist sceolde ðurh nearunysse his ðrowunge intō his heofonlican wuldre faran, hūmeta mæg sē beōn crīsten, sē ðe nele . . . ðurh nānre earfoðnysse þæt ēce wuldor mid Crīste geearnian ?</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. Th. ii. 284, 27)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">redime ex omnibus angustiis meis</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gefriða mē of eallum mīnum nearonessum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 24, 20)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">IV.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">scantiness</span>
					</p>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(l)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">of space</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">propter angustiam loci, in quo monasterium constructum est</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Fore nearonesse (nearwnesse, v.l.) þǣre stōwe þe þæt mynster on getimbred is</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 4, 10; Sch. 400, 6)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(2)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">of means</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ðeāh wē þisse worulde wlenca tilian swīðe . . . ; þeāh wē ūs mid þām deōrwyrþestan gimmum ūton ymbehōn, hwæðere wē sceolon on nearonysse ende gebīdan</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Wlfst. 263, 1)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="brūn-ecg" d:title="brūn-ecg">
		<body>
			<h1>brūn-ecg<span class="pron"> | bruːn.edʒː |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Brown-edged</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. nigra acie præditus)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">Byrhtnoth drew his battle-axe from its sheath, broad and brown of edge</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Byrhtnōþ bræd bill of scēðe, brād and brūnecg</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Byrht. Th. 136, 38; By. 163: Beo. Th. 3096; B. 1546)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="mæhe" d:title="mæhe">
		
