<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="mægen" d:title="mægen">
		<body>
			<h1>mægen<span class="pron"> | mæ.Gen |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">quidquid necessario victui superest ex operibus manuum</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Swā hwæt swā tōforan þām neādbehēfum belifen byþ on heora mægenes tilunge</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (R. Ben. 138, 17)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic sylle Wulfsige mīnum gerēfan wið his holdum mægene ( for his loyal and able service) ānes hīdes lond</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cht. E. 161, 27)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Be sāre þæs magan. Gif se man ꝥ mægen hæbbe lǣt him blōd</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lch. ii. 180, 31)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē (Aidan) munuclīce leofode . . . mid sōþum mægnum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. S. 26, 82)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">a virtuous action</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Þæt wē beōn gōdum mannum gelīce in ðām mægenum þē wē dōn magon</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Verc. Först. 169, 3)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">III.</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Þæt eorðlice mægn þe þū hēr samnast. . . eall þis mægn wāt, þe hēr tō gemōte cōm, þæt bīn heāhsetl is þrymmes āfylled</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wlfst. 254, 13-18)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:full-mægen" class="xref-target">full-mægen</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:god-mægen" class="xref-target">god-mægen</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:heāfod-mægen" class="xref-target">heāfod-mægen</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:helle-mægen" class="xref-target">helle-mægen</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:nīd-mægen" class="xref-target">nīd-mægen</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:stīþ-mægen" class="xref-target">stīþ-mægen</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="freōls-tīd" d:title="freōls-tīd">
		<body>
			<h1>freōls-tīd<span class="pron"> | fre͜oːls.tiːd |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A feast-tide</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. festīvum tempus)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">at this feast-tide</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Æt ðissere freōlstīde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. ii. 264, 17)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">let all St. Mary's feast-tides be strictly honoured</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Sce. Marian freōlstīda ealle weorþie man georne</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. Eth. v. 14; Th. i. 308, 13)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">at festival-tides and fast-tides</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Freōlstīdan and fæstentīdan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. C. S. 38; Th. i. 398, 17)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:heāh-freōlstīd" class="xref-target">heāh-freōlstīd</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="cwealm-bǣrnes" d:title="cwealm-bǣrnes">
		
		<body>
			<h1>cwealm-bǣrnes<span class="pron"> | kwæ͜ɑlm.bæːr.nes |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Heō heōld þā līc oþ ꝥ seō ēhtnys geswāc, and se crīstendōm ācucode æfter þǣre cwealmbǣrnysse</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. S. 29, 330)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="on-herian" d:title="on-herian">
		<body>
			<h1>on-herian<span class="pron"> | on.xe.ri.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:on-hyrian" class="xref-target">on-hyrian</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="grunnian" d:title="grunnian">
		<body>
			<h1>grunnian<span class="pron"> | grun.ni.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:grunian" class="xref-target">grunian</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-niþerian" d:title="ge-niþerian">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-niþerian<span class="pron"> | je.ni.θe.ri.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to bring down, cast down, degrade, humiliate</span>
					</p>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(1)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">a person or place occupying an exalted position</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Oft ðis andwearde līf ūp āhefeð ðā yfelan, ac se tōcyme ðǣre ēcan eādignesse hiē geniðrað</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 389, 27)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hierusalem āhēned bið ł gehniðrad bið (calcabitur) from hǣdnum</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Lk. L. 21, 24)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
							<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
								<li>
									<p>
										<span class="sense-label">(1 a)</span>
										<span class="meaning-en">used of a thing</span>
									</p>
									<ul class="quotes">
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Gif h byð gesett þǣr hē standan ne mæg, þonne sceal man hine þus genyðerian</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Angl. viii. 333, 39)</span>
										</li>
									</ul>
								</li>
							</ol>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(2)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">a person who exalts himself</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">dejecisti eos, dum allevarentur</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Ðū hiē geniðrades, ðā hī hī selfe ūp āhōfon</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 391, 9)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">ex virtutum decore te elevas, ipsa tua pulchritudine impelleris, ut cadas</span>
									<span class="q-oe">For ðǣm wlite ðīnra cræfta ðū wurde ūp āhæfen, and ðonan ðū wyrst geniððrad</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (463, 22)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ēghuelc sē ðe hine āhebbað gehniðrad bið (humiliabitur)</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Lk. L. 14, 11)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
							<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
								<li>
									<p>
										<span class="sense-label">(2 a)</span>
										<span class="meaning-en">the pride of a person</span>
									</p>
									<ul class="quotes">
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Hū God þā mǣstan ofermētto geniðerade</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 2, 5; S. 84, 12)</span>
										</li>
									</ul>
								</li>
							</ol>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to condemn</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Nællað giē gehniðra (condemnare) ꝥte giē ne se gehniðrad</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lk. L. 6, 37)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">condemnari</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Beōn genyðered</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (An. Ox. 2916)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">damnatur</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Wæs geneþorod</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (3769)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Manega unrihtlīce fram yflum dēmum genyþrode wǣron</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. S. 30, 8)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">II a.</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">to condemn to a punishment</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">condemnabunt eum morte</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Hig genyðeriað (geniðredon, L.) hyne tō deāðe</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. 20, 18)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">damnabunt eum morte</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Hī hine deāþe genyþeriað (geniðriað tō deāðe, L. R.)</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Mk. 10, 33)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">II b.</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">to pass sentence(?)</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-en">that I fall under the sentence passed on the slothful servant</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Ꝥ ic on gefealle on þone genyðredan (-endan?) cwyde þæs slāwan þeōwes (þeawas, MS.)</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. S. 23 b, 14)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">III.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to accuse</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Mið ðȳ (wæs) gewroeged ł geniðrad (accusaretur)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. L. 27, 12)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ǣrend-bōc" d:title="ǣrend-bōc">
