						<span class="meaning-en">To put under, support</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="Lǣden-word" d:title="Lǣden-word">
		<body>
			<h1>Lǣden-word<span class="pron"> | læː.den.word |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>neuter noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A Latin word</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðās word ne beōþ nā lēdenword gif se r byþ āweg gedōn</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. Gr. 19; Som. 22, 54)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="sām-cwic" d:title="sām-cwic">
		<body>
			<h1>sām-cwic<span class="pron"> | sɑːm.kwiK |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Hē Smaragdum forðfērendne geseah, and Pafnuntium sāmcwicne on eorðan licgan</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. S. 33, 302)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Mid flānum ofscotene, mid wǣpnum ofsette, hī heora burh sāmcuce (cf. healfcwice, Bl. H. 203, 19) gesōhton</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. Th. i. 506, 2)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="æt-wītan" d:title="æt-wītan">
		<body>
			<h1>æt-wītan<span class="pron"> | æt.wiː.tɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -wāt, pl: -witon</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -witen</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To reproach, blame, upbraid</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. imputare, improperare, exprobrare)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the thanes of this people shall not reproach me</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ne sceolon me on ðære þeōde þegenas ætwītan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Byrht. Th. 138, 15; By. 220)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">since Guthlaf and Oslaf reproached him for a part of their woes</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Siððan Gūþlāf and ōslāf ætwiton weāna dǣl</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Beo. Th. 2304; B. 1150: Ps. Th. 88, 44: 73, 17: Ps. Spl. 31, 2)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:edwitan" class="xref-target">edwitan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="-īþian" d:title="-īþian">
		<body>
			<h1>-īþian<span class="pron"> | iː.θi.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:un-īþian" class="xref-target">un-īþian</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="feormung" d:title="feormung">
		<body>
			<h1>feormung<span class="pron"> | fe͜or.mung |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">a harbouring, an entertaining</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. susceptio, hospitium)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">by the harbouring of exiles</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Þurh wreccena feormunge</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. Alf. Pol. 4; Th. i, 62, 16)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">a cleansing, polishing</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. purgatio, politio)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">if a sword polisher receive another man's weapon for polishing</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gif sweordhwīta ōðres monnes wǣpn to feormunge onfō</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. Alf. pol. 19; Th. i. 74, 9)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:āfeormung" class="xref-target">āfeormung</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:niht-" class="xref-target">niht-</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="gāl-mōd" d:title="gāl-mōd">
		<body>
			<h1>gāl-mōd<span class="pron"> | gɑːl.moːd |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Light-minded, licentious</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. libīdinōsæ mentis, lascīvus)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the licentious [Holofernes]</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Se galmōda</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Judth. 12; Thw. 25, 12; Jud. 256)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="heāh-mæsse" d:title="heāh-mæsse">
