			<h1>hyse-cild<span class="pron"> | xy.se.Kild |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">occidit omnes pueros</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Hēofslōh ealle þā hysecild</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. Th. i. 80, 15)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="scūr-heard" d:title="scūr-heard">
		<body>
			<h1>scūr-heard<span class="pron"> | ʃuːr.xæ͜ɑrd |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Made hard by blows</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Sweordes ecg, scerp and scūrheard</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Andr. Kmbl. 2267; An. 1135)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt him fēla lāf (the sword) ne meahte scūrheard sceþþan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Beo. Th. 2070; B. 1033)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ā-blāwan" d:title="ā-blāwan">
		<body>
			<h1>ā-blāwan<span class="pron"> | ɑː.blɑː.wɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to breathe (trans.)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Crīst ābleōw ðone Hālgan Gāst upon ðā apostolas</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. Th. i. 324, 31)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">illud lumen quod mentibus aspirasti</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt lēht. . . ðætte ðencum ðū ābleāwe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Rtl. 2, 15)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to blow away</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Sume cwǣdon ðæt ðæt heāfod sceolde āblāwan Herodiaden, swā ðæt heō fērde mid windum geond ealle woruld</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. Th. i. 486, 5)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">III.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to blow up, swell</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðā mettas ðe āblāwan monnan mægen</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lch. ii. 254, 24)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Tācn āblāwenre lifre</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (160, 24)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="rūm-gāl" d:title="rūm-gāl">
		<body>
			<h1>rūm-gāl<span class="pron"> | ruːm.gɑːl |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Rejoicing in ample space in which to move (applied to the dove when sent from the ark)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">far the dove flew, in flight unconfined rejoicing, until a place of rest she found (cf. heō rūme fleāh, 87, 29; Gen. 1456)</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Seō culufre wīde fleāh ōþ ðæt heō rūmgāl reste stōwe funde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. Th. 88, 16; Gen. 1466)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="-teāw" d:title="-teāw">
		<body>
			<h1>-teāw<span class="pron"> | tæ͜ɑːw |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:manig-teāw" class="xref-target">manig-teāw</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-þohte" d:title="ge-þohte">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-þohte<span class="pron"> | je.θox.te |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>participle</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">thought; p. of ge-þencean</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">thought</span>
							<span class="q-oe">ge-þohte</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. 217; Th. 276, 11; Sat. 187)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge-þencean" class="xref-target">ge-þencean</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="cniht-līc" d:title="cniht-līc">
		<body>
			<h1>cniht-līc<span class="pron"> | knixt.liːtʃ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Boyish, childish</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. puerilis)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">nor was he [Guthlac] addicted to boyish levity</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ne he cnihtlīce gālnysse næs begangende</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Guthl. 2; Gdwin. 12, 16)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">as childish age is often wont</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Swā oft swā cnihtlīcu yldo begǣþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (2; Gdwin. 12, 19)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="slūpan" d:title="slūpan">
		<body>
			<h1>slūpan<span class="pron"> | sluː.pɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:on-slūpan" class="xref-target">on-slūpan</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:un-slopen" class="xref-target">un-slopen</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="waru" d:title="waru">
		<body>
			<h1>waru<span class="pron"> | wɑ.ru |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(5)</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ne synd āwritene ealle Iūdan gefeoht for his freōnda ware</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. S. 25, 677 : 26, 147)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:in-waru" class="xref-target">in-waru</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:waru a weir" class="xref-target">waru a weir</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="BREŌWAN" d:title="BREŌWAN">
		<body>
			<h1>BREŌWAN<span class="pron"> | bre͜oː.wɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">present: 1sg: -breōwe, 2sg: -breōwest, 2sg: -brȳwst, 3sg: -breōweþ, 3sg: -brȳwþ, pl: -breōwaþ</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -breāw, pl: -bruwon</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -browen, past participle sg: -ge-browen</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To BREW</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. cerevisiam coquere)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">there is no ale brewed by the Esthonians</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ne biþ ðǣr nǣnig ealo gebrowen mid Estum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 1. 1; Bos. 22, 17)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">he drank not of any mixed or brewed fluid</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ne dranc he nānes gemencgedes wǣtan, ne gebrowenes</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. i. 352, 7)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:twy-browen" class="xref-target">twy-browen</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="bodan" d:title="bodan">
		<body>
			<h1>bodan<span class="pron"> | bo.dɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:botm" class="xref-target">botm</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ufan-cund" d:title="ufan-cund">
		<body>
			<h1>ufan-cund<span class="pron"> | u.fɑn.kund |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Heavenly, celestial</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. supernus)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Segnbora ðæs ufancundan kyninges</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Blickl. Homl. 163, 22)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ufancundes eagles word</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. Th. 169, 19; Gū. 1097)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Engel ufancundne</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (176, 26; Gū. 1216)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">fear from heaven</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ufancundne ege</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (143, 8; Gū. 658)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">cum superna voluntas agnoscitur</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðonne hē ongiete ðone ufancundan willan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 7; Swt. 51, 8)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">celestial messengers</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Āras ufancunde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. Th. 31, 29; Cri. 503)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="lār-spell" d:title="lār-spell">
		<body>
			<h1>lār-spell<span class="pron"> | lɑːr.spell |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Lārspell (as heading to a homily)</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Wlfst. 232, 11 : 242, 22: 250, 14: 266, 1)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">predicare</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Mid lārspelle bodian</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Chrd. 50, 7)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Marcus, þe wæs mid Petre on lāre, wrāt þā ōðre bōc (the second gospel) be Petres bodunge be þām þe hē geleornode on his lārspellum (the discourses in which he (Peter) instructed Mark)</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. T. Grn. 12, 35)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Se mæssepreōst sceal mannum mid rihte bodian þone sōðan geleāfan and him lārspel secgan</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Ll. Th. ii. 384, 25)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ā-bilgan" d:title="ā-bilgan">
		<body>
			<h1>ā-bilgan<span class="pron"> | ɑː.bil.ɣɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge-ābiligan" class="xref-target">ge-ābiligan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="wīn-sæl" d:title="wīn-sæl">
		<body>
			<h1>wīn-sæl<span class="pron"> | wiːn.sæl |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>neuter noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A wine-hall, a hall where there is feasting</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Wōriaþ ða wīnsalo</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. Th. 291, 6 ; Wand. 78)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:next word" class="xref-target">next word</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="scyld" d:title="scyld">
		
		<body>
			<h1>scyld<span class="pron"> | ʃyld |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">guilt, sin, crime, fault</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">sceleris aliquid commiserat, quod commissum, ubi ad cor suum rediit, gravissime exhorruit</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē sume māndǣde gefremede ðā seō scyld ðā tō his heortan hwearf ðā onscunode hē hī hefelīce</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 4, 25; S. 599, 34)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Sitte siō scyld (the killing of a slave) on him</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. Alf. 17; Th. i. 48, 15)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">On eōw scyld siteþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. Th. 131, 2; Gū. 449)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Is Euan scyld eal forpyuded</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (7, 6; Cri. 97)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">veniam reatus postulans</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē his scylde forgyfenysse bæd</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 3, 22; S. 553, 33)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">tanti reatus pondera</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ða byrðenne suā micelre scylde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 2, 2; Swt. 31, 14)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">sine culpa</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Būtan scylde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (3, 1; Swt. 33, 16: L. H. E. 12; Th. i. 32, 9)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hī būton ǣlcere scylde (without being guilty of any crime) wurdon fordōne</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 29, 2; Fox 104, 30)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">flagrante delicto</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Æt openre scylde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. In. 37; Th. i. 124, 23)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">habet animus aliquem reatum</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hafaþ ðæt mōd hwylcehugu scyldo</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. l, 27; S. 496, 42)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">piacula</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Synna, scylda</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 66, 78)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">delicta mea</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Mīne scylde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 68, 6: Ps. Surt. 58, 13)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Scylða</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 32, 2; Swt. 211, 20)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Scelda</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. C. 45)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">fratris vitia</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Brōðres schyldo</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. Kmbl. p. 15, 5)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Āscyred scylda gehwylcre, deōpra firena</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Elen. Kmbl. 2624; El. 1313: 937; El. 470)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hwīlum biþ gōd wærlīce tō mīðanne his hiēremonna scylda (vitia)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 21, 1; Swt. 151, 9)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">a debt, awe</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">justitiae debitum potius solvimus, quam misericordiae opera implemus</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ryhtlīcor cweðan ðæt wē him gielden scylde ðonne wē him mildheortnesse dōn</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (45, 1; Swt. 335, 19)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">reddi debitum</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Āgefnæ beōn ða scylde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. Kmbl. Rush. 28, 25)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">debitum dimisit ei</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē ða scyld forlēt wið hine</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (27: 30)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:deāþ-scyld" class="xref-target">deāþ-scyld</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:frum-scyld" class="xref-target">frum-scyld</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge-scyld" class="xref-target">ge-scyld</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:god-scyld" class="xref-target">god-scyld</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:mān-scyld" class="xref-target">mān-scyld</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:nīd-scyld" class="xref-target">nīd-scyld</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="un-wemness" d:title="un-wemness">
		<body>
			<h1>un-wemness<span class="pron"> | un.wem.ness |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Purity</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt ða clǣnan and ða unwemman hira clǣnnysse and hiora unwemnysse forð gehiōldan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Ass. 207, 422)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="EAL" d:title="EAL">
		
		<body>
			<h1>EAL<span class="pron"> | æ͜ɑl |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">ALL</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. tōtus, omnis, cunctus, unĭversus)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Eal ða earfeðu all the pains</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 25 b; Th. 74, 5; Cri. 1202: 118 a; Th. 452, 25; Hy. 4, 7: Andr. Kmbl. 1889; An. 947)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Eal here the whole host</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. 114; Th. 150, 12; Gen. 2490: Salm. Kmbl. 645; Sal. 322)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Eal ic I all</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 115 a; Th. 443, 13; Kl. 29)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ealles ðæs gafoles of all the tribute</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 16 a; Th. 35, 16; Cri. 559)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ealre worlde of all the world</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hy. 7, 57: 11, 20)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ealles ðæs of all that</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 119 a; Th. 456, 19; Hy. 4, 69)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ealne ðisne ymbhwyrft all this orb</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (110 b; Th. 423, 1; Rä. 41, 14)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ealne ðone egesan all the terror</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. 202; Th. 250, 3; Dan. 541)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">tōto orbe</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Geond ealne middangeard</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 2, 4; S. 505, 26)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ealne weg always</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 38, 4; Fox 204, 10, 11)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ealle ðā gesceaft all the creation</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. Met. Fox 20, 37; Met. 20, 19)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">unĭversam legem</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ealle ǣ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Deut. 4, 8)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">omnia mandāta tua</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðīne ealle gebann</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 118, 86)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ealle gesceafte all creatures</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Andr. Kmbl. 2997; An. 1501)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">omnia</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ealle ða þing</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Gen. 1, 31: Deut. 4, 3)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">cuncta</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ealle þing</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 1, 26; S. 487, 34: Mk. Bos. 9, 23)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">plūres vĭri doctissĭmi</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ealle ða gelǣredestan men</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 2, 2; S. 502, 38)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">omnes cultōres ejus</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ealle his bigengan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Deut. 4, 3)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ealla gesceafta all creatures</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. Met. Fox 13, 14; Met. 13, 7: 20, 105; Met. 20, 53: Bt. 39, 13; Fox 234, 24)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ealle mægne with all power</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. Met. Fox 26, 128; Met. 26, 64)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">omni mŏdo</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ealle gemete</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 1, 27; S. 496, 39)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ealra ðara gifena for all the gifts</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 41 b; Th. 138, 18; Gū. 578)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Earmost ealra wihta poorest of all creatures</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (110 a; Th. 421, 7; Rä. 40, 14)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">On eallum biþ ðærn līchoman it is in</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="oftrǣd-līce" d:title="oftrǣd-līce">
		
		<body>
			<h1>oftrǣd-līce<span class="pron"> | of.træːd.liː.tʃe |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adverb</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">qui minimis, sed crebris noxis immerguntur . . . qui licet minima, crebro tamen illicita faciunt</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Ðā ðe oftrǣdlīce lytla scylda wyrceað. . . ðā ðe oftrǣdlīce syngiað, and ðeāh lytlum scyldum</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 437, 1-6)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Hī oftrǣdlīce on ðā burh fuhton</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 1016; P. 149, 7)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Deōfol hine oftrǣdlīce mid mænigfealdum costnungum costnode</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. A. 195, 18)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-strod" d:title="ge-strod">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-strod<span class="pron"> | je.strod |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>neuter noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Plunder[?], wealth</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">flagitiosum facinus ad efficiendum præmiis incitari</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt hī ðȳ ēþ mǣgen heora unriht gewitt forþbringan hī sind mid gifum and mid gestreōnum [Cot. gestrodum] gefyrðrode</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 3, 4; Fox 6, note 7)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge-strūdan" class="xref-target">ge-strūdan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-þweorod" d:title="ge-þweorod">
		
		<body>
			<h1>ge-þweorod<span class="pron"> | je.θwe͜o.rod |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>participle</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">tu numeris elementa ligas, ut frigora flammis, arida conveniant liquidis</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Þeāh ānra hwilc siē gebunden gesiblīce tōgædre, ꝥte heora ǣnig ōðres ne dorste mearce ofergangan, ac geþweorod sint ðegnas tōgædre, cele wið hǣto, hǣt wið drȳgum; winnað hwæðre</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Met. 20, 72)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge-þrowian" class="xref-target">ge-þrowian</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge-þwǣrian" class="xref-target">ge-þwǣrian</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="gladian" d:title="gladian">
		<body>
			<h1>gladian<span class="pron"> | glɑ.di.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">intrans.</span>
					</p>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(1)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">to be bright, shine, gleam (of polished metal)</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">On him gladiað gomelra lāfe</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (B. 2036)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(2)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">to be glad, rejoice</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hwīlon heō besārgað hyre līchoman sārnissa, hwīlon heō gladað on gōdum gelimpum</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. S. 1, 221)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
							<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
								<li>
									<p>
										<span class="sense-label">(2 a)</span>
										<span class="meaning-en">to rejoice in something possessed</span>
									</p>
									<ul class="quotes">
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Februarius and Martius gladiað on fīfum</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Angl. viii. 302, 1)</span>
										</li>
									</ul>
								</li>
							</ol>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">trans.</span>
					</p>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(1)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">to make glad.</span>
							</p>
							<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
								<li>
									<p>
										<span class="sense-label">(a)</span>
										<span class="meaning-en">of physical effect, to make of cheerful appearance</span>
									</p>
									<ul class="quotes">
										<li>
											<span class="q-la">ut exhiberet faciem in oleo</span>
											<span class="q-oe">Ðæt hē gleadie onsiēne in ele</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Srt. 103, 15)</span>
										</li>
									</ul>
								</li>
								<li>
									<p>
										<span class="sense-label">(b)</span>
										<span class="meaning-en">of mental effect, to gladden, cheer</span>
									</p>
									<ul class="quotes">
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Ꝥ hī widuwan and steōpcild georne gladian</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Ll. Th. i. 326, 26)</span>
										</li>
									</ul>
								</li>
							</ol>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(2)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">to please</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Þā þe mid clǣnnysse him gecwēmað on līfe and mid gōdum weorcum hine gladiað nū</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. A. 15, 54)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Utan gladian georne God</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Wlfst. 112, 12)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(3)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">to make gentle, soften, appease</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Mildode mansuescit, gladode mitigat</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Germ. 399, 436)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">pro demulcebat (mentem . . . nec blandimentorum lenitas demulcet, Ald. 40, 36)</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Gladode demulcet</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (An. Ox. 3004)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge-gladian" class="xref-target">ge-gladian</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="æfen-hrepsung" d:title="æfen-hrepsung">
		<body>
			<h1>æfen-hrepsung<span class="pron"> | æ.fen.xrep.sung |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:æfen-repsung" class="xref-target">æfen-repsung</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="bærs" d:title="bærs">
		
		<body>
			<h1>bærs<span class="pron"> | bærs |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A perch</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. perca, lupus)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Bærs lupus vel scardo</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. Gl. 101; Som. 77, 58; Wrt. Voc. 55, 63)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="līcham-līce" d:title="līcham-līce">
		
		<body>
			<h1>līcham-līce<span class="pron"> | liːk.xɑm.liː.tʃe |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adverb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Bodily, in the body</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">though he was not present in the body at their slaughter</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðeāh ðe hē līchamlīce on heora slege andwerd nǣre</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. i. 82, 33)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">corporaliter</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Līchamlīce</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. Gr. 38; Sam. 41, 6)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Seō stōw ðe Drihten līchomlīce nēhst on stōd on middangearde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Blickl. Homl. 125, 15)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">they saw him with their bodily eyes</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hiē hine līchomlīce gesāwon</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (135, 19)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">quamvis corporaliter absens</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðeāh ðe hē līcumlīce æfward wære</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 3, 15; S. 542, 6)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="-sigefæstnian" d:title="-sigefæstnian">
		<body>
			<h1>-sigefæstnian<span class="pron"> | si.Ge.fæst.ni.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge-sigefæstnian" class="xref-target">ge-sigefæstnian</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="teart" d:title="teart">
		<body>
			<h1>teart<span class="pron"> | tæ͜ɑrt |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">of material objects, sharp, piercing</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Tearte acra (testularum fragmina)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (An. Ox. 8, 218)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">of pain, &amp;c.</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">acerrimo, i. asperrimo tormento</span>
							<span class="q-oe">On þǣre teartestan tintregun</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (1946)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="fremed-līce" d:title="fremed-līce">
		
		<body>
			<h1>fremed-līce<span class="pron"> | fre.med.liː.tʃe |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adverb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Perfectly</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. perfecte)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Þurh þæt fremedlīce (perfecte) ys ge-herud</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Scint. 129, 3)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:full-fremedlīce" class="xref-target">full-fremedlīce</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="efn-eald" d:title="efn-eald">
		<body>
			<h1>efn-eald<span class="pron"> | efn.æ͜ɑld |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">co-eval</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. æquævus vel coætāneus)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Efneald æquævus vel coætāneus</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. Gl. 9; Som. 56, 119; Wrt. Voc. 19, 3)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:efen-eald" class="xref-target">efen-eald</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="fioh" d:title="fioh">
		<body>
			<h1>fioh<span class="pron"> | fi͜ox |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>neuter noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -fiōs, dative sg: -fiō</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Cattle, property, a portion</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. pecus, opes, dos)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gif ðē becume ōðres monnes giēmeleās fioh on hand if the stray cattle of another man come to thy hand</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. Alf. 42; Th. i. 54, 9: L. Ethb. 81; Th. i. 24, 1)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:feoh" class="xref-target">feoh</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="sibsumness" d:title="sibsumness">
		<body>
			<h1>sibsumness<span class="pron"> | sib.sum.ness |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:un-sibsumness" class="xref-target">un-sibsumness</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="sirwung" d:title="sirwung">
		<body>
			<h1>sirwung<span class="pron"> | sir.wung |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Plotting, machination, contrivance</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Beō āīdlod Amanes sirwung ongeān ðām Judēiscum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. As. 101, 308)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">of plotting against a lord. If any man plot against king or lord</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Be hlāfordes syrwunge. Gif hwā embe cynincg oððe hlāford syrwie</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. C. S. 58 ; Th. i. 408, 1)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">with guile, Exod. 21, 14</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gif hwā ofsleā his ðone nēhstan þurh syrwunge</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. Alf. 13 ; Th. i. 48, 1, note)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē cȳdde his fācenfulle syrewunge</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. i. 82, 18)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Mid syrewungum hē becom tō ðære cynelīcan geþincþe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (80, 34)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">God heōld hine wið ðæs deōfles syrwungum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (ii. 454, 3)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">machinamentis</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Serewungum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hpt. Gl. 478, 54)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">insidias</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Syrwunga</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hymn. Surt. 47, 26)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Samson heora syrwunga undergeat</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Jud. 16, 3)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:searwung" class="xref-target">searwung</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="þrym-wealdend" d:title="þrym-wealdend">
		<body>
			<h1>þrym-wealdend<span class="pron"> | θrym.wæ͜ɑl.dend |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Glory-ruling, ruling heaven</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Seō Hālige Ðrynnys ðe is þrymwealdend God</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. ii. 316, 4)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Þrimwealdend</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Skt. ii. 27, 156)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Se ðrimwealdenda Scyppend</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. i. 112, 10)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">We sceolon biddan ða hālgan ðæt hī ūs þingion tō ðam þrymwealdendum Gode</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Skt. i. 21, 288)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="līhting" d:title="līhting">
		<body>
			<h1>līhting<span class="pron"> | liːx.ting |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">shining</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">quantum hora permittit</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Swā micel swā þæs dæges līhting geþafige</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (R. Ben. 67, 8)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">haec omnia per hanc lucis viam (has vitani been read?)</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ealle þās þing þurh līfes līht-incge gefyllan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (5, 8)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:rodor-līhting" class="xref-target">rodor-līhting</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="heard-sǣlig" d:title="heard-sǣlig">
		<body>
			<h1>heard-sǣlig<span class="pron"> | xæ͜ɑrd.sæː.liG |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Having hard fortune, unfortunate, unhappy</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">one is indigent, an unfortunate man</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Sum biþ wonspēdig heardsǣlig hæle</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 78 b; Th. 295, 12; Crä. 32: Bt. 31, 1; Fox 112, 20: Exon. 115 a; Th. 442, 27; Kl. 19)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="wirpan" d:title="wirpan">
		<body>
			<h1>wirpan<span class="pron"> | wir.pɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -de</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To recover</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Wyrpton hiē wērige, wiste genǣgdon mōdige meteþegnas, hyra mægen bēton</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. Th. 185, 29; Exod. 130)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">statim melius habere incipio</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Sōna ic wæs wyrpende and mē sēl wæs</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 5, 3; S. 616, 34)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">confestim me melius habere sentirem</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðā sōna gefēlde ic mē b[e]ōtiende and wyrpende (batiende and werpende, Bd. M. 404, 1)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (5, 6; S. 620, 12)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ā-wirpan" class="xref-target">ā-wirpan</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge-wirpan" class="xref-target">ge-wirpan</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:-wyrpan" class="xref-target">-wyrpan</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge edwyrpan" class="xref-target">ge edwyrpan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="woruld" d:title="woruld">
		<body>
			<h1>woruld<span class="pron"> | wo.ruld |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:weorold" class="xref-target">weorold</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="fædren-cnōsl" d:title="fædren-cnōsl">
		<body>
			<h1>fædren-cnōsl<span class="pron"> | fæ.dren.knoːsl |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">father's kin</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:fæderen-cnōsl" class="xref-target">fæderen-cnōsl</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="of-setting" d:title="of-setting">
		<body>
			<h1>of-setting<span class="pron"> | of.set.ting |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Pressure</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ofsettincge oppressum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Scint. 143, 5)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="on-bēn" d:title="on-bēn">
		<body>
			<h1>on-bēn<span class="pron"> | on.beːn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A prayer asking for something (evil) to come upon a person, an imprecation</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">qui adversis nos imprecationibus persequuntur</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hī ūs mid heora wiðerwordum onbēnum and wyrinessum ēhtaþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 2, 2; S. 504, 4)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="þideres" d:title="þideres">
		<body>
			<h1>þideres<span class="pron"> | θi.de.res |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adverb</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Hider and þyderes ultro cilroque, i. hinc et inde.</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (An. Ox. 1040)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="bād" d:title="bād">
		<body>
			<h1>bād<span class="pron"> | bɑːd |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A pledge, stake, a thing distrained</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. pignus)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">if a pledge be taken, then shall he obtain the pledge home again, or back</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gif bād genumen sȳ, ðonne begyte ða bāde hām</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. O. D. 3; Th. i. 354, 6, 7)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:wed" class="xref-target">wed</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:wedd" class="xref-target">wedd</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="hūs-bonda" d:title="hūs-bonda">
		
		<body>
			<h1>hūs-bonda<span class="pron"> | xuːs.bon.dɑ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -an</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">The master of a house</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">one of his men wanted to stop at a man's house against his will, and wounded the man of the house, and the man of the house slew the other. Then Eustace got on his horse and his companions on theirs, and went to the man of the house and slew him, in his own home</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ān his manna wolde wīcian æt ānes bundan hūse his unþances and gewundode ðone hūsbundon and se hūsbunda ofslōh ðone ōðerne. Ðā wearþ Eustatius uppon his horse and his gefeoran uppon heora and fērdon tō ðam hūsbundon and ofslōgon hine binnan his āgenan heorþa</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 1048; Erl. 177, 35-40)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="drepe" d:title="drepe">
		
		<body>
			<h1>drepe<span class="pron"> | dre.pe |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A slaying, stroke, violent death</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. occīsio)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">he suffered the stroke [death-stroke]</span>
							<span class="q-oe">He drepe þrōwade</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Beo. Th. 3183; B. 1589)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:deāþ-drepe" class="xref-target">deāþ-drepe</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
