						<span class="meaning-en">Wise-minded</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Him ðā wīshȳdig Abraham gewāt</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. Th. 109, 2; Gen. 1816)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ongan his brȳd wīshȳdig wer wordum lǣran</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (109, 15; Gen. 1823)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-frēfrian" d:title="ge-frēfrian">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-frēfrian<span class="pron"> | je.freː.fri.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">present: 1sg: -ge-frēfrige</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -ode</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -od</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To comfort, console</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. consolari)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">consolor</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic ge-frēfrige consolor</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. Gr. 25; Som. 26, 64)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">nunc hic consolatur</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Nū ys ðes gefrēfrod</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lk. Bos. 16, 25)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:frēfrian" class="xref-target">frēfrian</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-ondettan" d:title="ge-ondettan">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-ondettan<span class="pron"> | je.on.det.tɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -te</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -ed</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To confess</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. confitēri)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">that confess</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðe geondettaþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Blickl. Homl. 57, 27)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">if he confess it</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gif he hit geondette</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. In. 71; Th. i. 148, 3)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge-andettan" class="xref-target">ge-andettan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="fulteman" d:title="fulteman">
		
		<body>
			<h1>fulteman<span class="pron"> | ful.te.mɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">to assist, help, support</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. juvāre, auxiliāri)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the belly must support the hands</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Siō womb sceal fulteman ðǣm hondum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 34, 3; Hat. MS. 44 a, 21)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">through the power which each one supports</span>
							<span class="q-oe">For ðæm ānwalde ðe ānra gehwilc fultemaþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. Met. Fox 25, 42; Met. 25, 21)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:fultuman" class="xref-target">fultuman</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="-hlēta" d:title="-hlēta">
