			<h1>in-burh<span class="pron"> | in.burx |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Inbirig uestibule, i. atrii</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (An. Ox. 3828)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">In[byrig?] atria</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (8, 214)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="plegan" d:title="plegan">
		
		
		<body>
			<h1>plegan<span class="pron"> | ple.ɣɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -de, sg: -ede, sg: -ode</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To play</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. ludere)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">ludo</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic plege</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. Gr. 28, 4; Som. 31, 23 : Wrt. Voc. ii. 53, 29)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">lusit</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Plegade</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (53, 28)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">ludens</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Plegende</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Kent. Gl. 279 : 995)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">to play, move about sportively, frolic, dance</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Horufisc plegode, glād geond gārsecg</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Andr. Kmbl. 740; An. 370)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">H1ōh ðā and plegode boda bitre gehugad</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. Th. 45, 10; Gen. 724)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">saltasset</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Plægede</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Mk. Skt. Lind. Rush. 6, 22)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">saltavit</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Pleagade</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. Kmbl. Rush. 14, 6)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">non saltastis</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Ne plægde gē, Lind., gē ne plagadun, Rush.</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (11, 17)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ðæt folc sæt and æt and dranc, and ārison and plegedon</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Ex. 32, 6)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ðæt folc ... eodon him plegean</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 43 ; Swt. 309, 14)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Men willaþ binnan Godes hūse bysmorlīce plegian</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (L. Ælfc. C. 35; Th. ii. 357, 2 note)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Gesiōn sǣmearh plegan</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Elen. Kmbl. 490; El. 245)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ðæt wīf geseah Ismael plegan</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. Th. 168, 6; Gen. 2778)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ðā geseah hē plegan micel cnihta weorod be ðæs sǣs waroþe</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Shrn. 78, 27)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ān plegende cild arn under wǣnes hweowol</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (32, 11)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">quasi agnus lasciviens</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Swā plegende lamp</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Kent. Gl. 214)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Seofon nacode wīmmen urnon plegende on heora gesihþum</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. ii. 162, 32)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">to play, to divert or amuse one's self</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ða ðe dwollīce plegaþ æt deādra manna līce, and ǣlce fūlnysse ðǣr forþteōþ mid plegan</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Skt. i. 21, 308)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-en">the Tarentines were taking their amusement at the theatre</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Tarentīne ðæt folc plegedon binnan heora byrg æt heora þeatra</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 4, 1 ; Swt. 154, 2)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-en">we enjoin that a priest be neither a hunter nor a hawker nor a gamester, but let him find his amusement in his books</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Wē lǣraþ ðæt preōst ne beō hunta ne hafecere ne tæflere ac plege on his bōcum</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (L. Edg. C. 64; Th. ii. 258, 8)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
							<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
								<li>
									<p>
										<span class="sense-label">II a.</span>
										<span class="meaning-en">to play (a game), exercise one's self in any way for the sake of amusement</span>
									</p>
									<ul class="quotes">
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Ða cild rīdaþ on heora stafum, and manigfealdne plegan plegiaþ</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 36, 5 ; Fox 180, 9)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-la">ludens Samson</span>
											<span class="q-oe">Samson plegode him ætforan</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Jud. 16, 27)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">On ðæm dæge plegedon hiē of horsum</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 3, 7 ; Swt, 118, 29)</span>
										</li>
									</ul>
								</li>
								<li>
									<p>
										<span class="sense-label">II b.</span>
										<span class="meaning-en">to play (with anything)</span>
									</p>
									<ul class="quotes">
										<li>
											<span class="q-en">he waved both hands aloft</span>
											<span class="q-oe">Hē mid bǣm handum upweard plegade</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Elen. Kmbl. 1609; El. 805)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Ðā pleogede hē mid his wordum</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 2, 1; S. 501, 25)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Wē wiernaþ ūrum cildum ūrra peninga mid tō plegianne</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 50; S. 361, 27)</span>
										</li>
									</ul>
								</li>
								<li>
									<p>
										<span class="sense-label">II c.</span>
										<span class="meaning-en">to play with a person, toy; in a bad sense, to make sport of</span>
									</p>
									<ul class="quotes">
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Sarra beheōld, hū Agares sunu wið Isaac plegode</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Gen. 21, 9)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Ðære helle hund ongan fægenian mid his steorte and plegian wið hine (Orpheus)</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 35, 6; Fox 168, 17)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Plegan</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. Th. 429, 10; Rä. 43, 2)</span>
										</li>
									</ul>
								</li>
								<li>
									<p>
										<span class="sense-label">II d.</span>
										<span class="meaning-en">to play (for something), strive after</span>
									</p>
									<ul class="quotes">
										<li>
											<span class="q-en">this is the same for whose death thou hast long played</span>
											<span class="q-oe">Ðis is se ilca ðe ðū longe for his deāþe plegodest</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Blickl. Homl. 85, 19)</span>
										</li>
									</ul>
								</li>
							</ol>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">III.</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">to play on an instrument</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">tympanistriarum</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Plægiendra (plegiyndra, Ps. Spl. C.) timpanan</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Surt. 67, 26)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">IV.</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">to clap the hands in applause</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">flumina plaudent</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Flōdas plægiaþ (plegiaþ, Ps. Spl. C.)</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Surt. 97, 8)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">plaudite</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Plagiaþ (plegaþ, Ps. Spl. C.)</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (46, 2)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:plega" class="xref-target">plega</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="þeōd-scipe" d:title="þeōd-scipe">
		<body>
			<h1>þeōd-scipe<span class="pron"> | θe͜oːd.ʃi.pe |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Connexion, association, fellowship</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">it is entitled to be connected with arithmetic</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Uton witan hwā hine ðæs wurðscipes cūðe ðe hē sceolde gestandan on ðam rīmcræfte. Ic wāt gere, ðæt hē ys þeōdscipes wyrðe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Anglia viii. 308, 23)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">that we lack not fellowship with God, the Maker's mercies</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt wē gēsine ne sȳn Godes þeōdscipes, metodes miltsa</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. Th. 211, 19; Exod. 528)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Nǣfre ðū geþreātast ðīnum beōtum, ðæt ic þeōdscype ðīnne lufie</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. Th. 253, 10; Jul. 178)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:þeōd-ness" class="xref-target">þeōd-ness</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:þeōdan" class="xref-target">þeōdan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="deōg" d:title="deōg">
		<body>
			<h1>deōg<span class="pron"> | de͜oːG |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:dīgan" class="xref-target">dīgan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-dohtra" d:title="ge-dohtra">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-dohtra<span class="pron"> | je.dox.trɑ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">nominative pl: -pl. (dual ?)</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">[Two] daughters</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Heora (Jupiter and Juno) gedohtra wǣron Minerua and Uenus (cf. heora twā dohtra wǣron Minerua and Uenus, Wlfst. 106, 15)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Sal. K. p. 121, 33)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="acolitus" d:title="acolitus">
		<body>
			<h1>acolitus<span class="pron"> | ɑ.ko.li.tus |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A light-bearer</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. lucifer)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">acolite is he who bears the light at God's services</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Acolitus is se ðe leōht berþ æt Godes þēnungum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L.Ælf.P.34; Th.ii.378,7: L.Ælf.C.14; Th.ii.348,4)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:hādll" class="xref-target">hādll</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-tȳdan" d:title="ge-tȳdan">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-tȳdan<span class="pron"> | je.tyː.dɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge-tīdan" class="xref-target">ge-tīdan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="scyndan" d:title="scyndan">
		
		<body>
			<h1>scyndan<span class="pron"> | ʃyn.dɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -de</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">intrans. To hurry, hasten</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Swā ðeōs woruld fareþ, scūrum scyndeþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. Th. 469, 24; Hy. 11, 7)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Brimwudu scynde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (182, 5; Gū. 1305)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Scynde Gregorius in Godes wære</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Menol. Fox 77; Men. 38)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Scynde beaduþreāta mǣst tō hilde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Elen. Kmbl. 60; El. 30)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Fǣge scyndan (of death by violence)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. Th. 271, 29; Jul. 489)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hī ǣghwonon tō him ēfston and scyndon</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Guthl. 15; Gdwin. 66, 10: Bd. 4, 27; S. 604, 8)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">coepere plures ad audiendum verbum confluere</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðā ongunnan monige ēfstan and scyndan tō gehȳranne Godes word</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (1, 26; S. 488, 11: Guthl. 2; Gdwin. 14, 25)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē gewāt scrīðan, tō gesceape scyndan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Beo. Th. 5133; B. 2570)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Manna freōndscipe biþ swīðe hwīlwendlīc and swīðe scendende (cf. gnornscendende)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Blickl. Homl. 195, 26)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">trans.</span>
					</p>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(1)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">To cause to hasten, to hurry</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ðā wæs morgenleōht scofen and scynded</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Beo. Th. 1840; B. 918)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(2)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">to urge, incite, exhort</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Se feōnd his (Judas) heortan tō ðan lǣrde and scynde, ðæt hē Drihten tō deāðe belǣwde</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. As. 153, 55)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hū mon monige scyndan scyle (de exhortatione multis exhibenda) tō ðæm ðætte his gōdan dǣda ne weorðen tō yflum dǣdum</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 60; Swt. 453, 6)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ā-scyndan" class="xref-target">ā-scyndan</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge-scyndan" class="xref-target">ge-scyndan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="geāra" d:title="geāra">
		<body>
			<h1>geāra<span class="pron"> | Gæ͜ɑː.rɑ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adverb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">YORE, formerly, of old, long since, once</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. ōlim, antīquitus, quondam)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">qui olim huc a beato Gregorio directus fuit</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Se geāra hider fram ðam eādigan Gregorie sended wæs</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 2, 3; S. 504, 44)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">I princely treasures gave of old</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic þeōdenmādmas geāra forgeāfe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. 22; Th. 26, 21; Gen. 410)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">thou in youthful life long since didst say</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðū on geōguþfeore geāra gecwǣde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Beo. Th. 5322; B. 2664 : Ps. Th. 73, 12 : 80, 10 : 104, 6 : 118, 152)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Geāra iū</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 76 b; Th. 287, 30; Wand. 22 : 84 a; Th. 316, 31; Mōd. 57 : Bt. Met. Fox 1, 1; Met. 1, 1)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ǣr-geāra" class="xref-target">ǣr-geāra</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:fyrn-" class="xref-target">fyrn-</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:geō-" class="xref-target">geō-</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:iū-" class="xref-target">iū-</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:un-" class="xref-target">un-</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="byrcþ" d:title="byrcþ">
		<body>
			<h1>byrcþ<span class="pron"> | byrkθ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">barks; pres. of beorcan</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:beorcan" class="xref-target">beorcan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="stēr" d:title="stēr">
		<body>
			<h1>stēr<span class="pron"> | steːr |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:stǣr" class="xref-target">stǣr</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="rifelung" d:title="rifelung">
		<body>
			<h1>rifelung<span class="pron"> | ri.fe.lung |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A wrinkle</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. ruga, contractio pellis)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Riuelung ruga, contractio pellis</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Angl. xxxii. 506, 12)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="streng-līc" d:title="streng-līc">
		<body>
			<h1>streng-līc<span class="pron"> | streng.liːtʃ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Strong, flrm</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hū hē him strenglīcran stōl geworhte, heāhran on heofonum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. Th. 18, 14; Gen. 273)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:strang-līc" class="xref-target">strang-līc</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ǣ-mynde" d:title="ǣ-mynde">
		<body>
			<h1>ǣ-mynde<span class="pron"> | æː.myn.de |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>neuter noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Want of care (?), neglect</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Funde ic hwæt eorðe mæg wið andan and wið ǣminde and wið ðā micelan mannes tungan . . . beō gē gemindige mīnes gōdes</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lch. i. 384, 22)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="un-sōþ" d:title="un-sōþ">
		<body>
			<h1>un-sōþ<span class="pron"> | un.soːθ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>neuter noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Untruth, falsehood</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Mid unsōðe sōð oferswīðan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wulfst. 55, 16)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Leāslīce hīwian unsōð tō sōðe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (128, 9)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic nelle secgan unsōð on me sylfe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Skt. i. 12, 195)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ǣ-swutol" d:title="ǣ-swutol">
		<body>
			<h1>ǣ-swutol<span class="pron"> | æː.swu.tol |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">One who makes the law clear, a lawyer</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. legisperitus)</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:sweotol" class="xref-target">sweotol</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ed-ric" d:title="ed-ric">
		<body>
			<h1>ed-ric<span class="pron"> | ed.riK |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ed-roc" class="xref-target">ed-roc</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-rignan" d:title="ge-rignan">
		
		<body>
			<h1>ge-rignan<span class="pron"> | je.ri.ɣnɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">to rain on, wet with rain</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Bið gerīned conpluitur</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 22, 30)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="wlite" d:title="wlite">
		<body>
			<h1>wlite<span class="pron"> | wli.te |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Nǣnig mæg wlite and wīsan wordum gecȳþan</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Nǣnig mæg wlite and wīsan wordum gecȳþan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (491, 30; Rä. 81, 7)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">good looks, beautiful appearance, beauly, glory, ornament</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">an gemmarum fulgor oculos trahit ? si quid est in hoc splendors praecipui, gemmarum est lux ilia, non hominum</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hwæþer nū gimma wlite eōwre eāgan tō him getiō, heora tō wundrianne? seō duguð ðæs wlites ðe on ðām gimmum bið, biþ heora, næs eōwre</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 13; Fox 40, I: Cd. Th. 239, I ; Dan. 364: Exon. Th. 82, 32; Cri. 1347)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Fealwe blōstman wudubeāma wlite</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (202, 25 ; Ph. 75)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">gloria tua</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðīnes wuldres wlite</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 56, 13)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">magnificentia</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Weorð. īc wlite wuldres ðīnes</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (95, 6)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">species decoris ejus</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Se wlite his andwlitan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (49, 2 : Cd. Th. 278, 18 ; Sae. 223)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ǣlc wlite and ǣlc fægernes ðisse weorlde līfes. . . . Se wlite and seō fægernes ðære sāule</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Blickl. Homl. 57, 28-31 : 59, 6)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Priscianus se ðe ys ealre Lēdensprǣce wlite gehāten</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ǣlfc. Gr. 15 ; Zup. 94, 3)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Wlites wealdend</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 67, 12)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Se fulla mōna wyrð wlites bereāfad</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Met. 28, 42)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">decoris</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Wlittes</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Rtl. 92, 10)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">decore</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Wlite</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (97, 16 : stemmaie, Wrt. Voc. ii. 88, 46)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðe læs ðe hē for hire (Sarah's, v. Gen. 12, 11) wlite wurde ofslagen</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Boutr. Scrd. 22, I)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Sunnan beorhtra, æþeltungla wlite</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. Th. 181, 4; Gū. 1288)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Him mid sīðedon twǣgen sūnende englas mid wundorlīcre wlite swā hē sylf wæs geglenged</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Skt. ii. 25, 775)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Heō nalles on goldes wlite and on seolfres ne scīneþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Blickl. Homl. 197, 9: Elen. Kmbl. 2636; El. 1319: Exon. Th. 238, 24; Ph. 609)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Of wlite wendaþ wæstma gecyndu</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (104, 29 ; Gū. 15)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">in gloria decoris mei</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Siō micle Babilon ðe ic self ātimbrede mē selfum tō whte and wuldre</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 4; Swt. 39, 18: Exon. Th. 70, 18; Cri. 1140)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Wlitan duore (see wlita)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hpt. Gl. 520, 22)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">Dominus decorem induit</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Drihten hine mid weorðlīce wlite gegyrede</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 92, I : Cd. Th. 3, 15; Gen. 36)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Myceine wlite (decorem), ðū āsetst ofer hine</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Spl. 20, 5)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">speciem tiiam et pulcritudinem tuam intende</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Geheald ōlnne wlite and ðīne fægernesse</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 44, 5 : Hpt. Gl. 523, 60)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðes middangeard wæs tō ðon fæger, ðæt hē teāh men tō him þurh his wlite and þurh his fægernesse</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Blickl. Homl. 115, II: Met. 7, 31: Exon. Th. 86, 10; Cri. 1406 : Cd. Th. 132, 10; Gen. 2191 : 13, 23 ; Gen. 207)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðære rosan wlite</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 9; Fox 26, 20: Met. 6, 13)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Sprǣcon ymb ðæs wīfes wlite monige</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. Th. 110, 34; Gen. 1848)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">to mar their beauty</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Heora wlite gewemtnan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (231, l ; Dan. 240)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gif hē hafaþ ofer ealle men wlite and wisdom</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. Th. 299, 16; Cra. 103)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gǣstes wlite</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (53, ll; Cri. 849: 96, 29; Cri. 1581)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">His weorces wlite</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (97, 9; Cri. 1588)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">ajferte Domino gloriam et honorem</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Bringaþ Drihtne wlite and āre, wuldor ðridde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 95, 7)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">circumcincta varietnte</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gegyrede mid eallum mistlīcum hrægla wlitum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (44, 15)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē hiē gegiereþ myd ðām winsumestan wlitum, and eft geungewlitegaþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Shrn. 195)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:and-wlite" class="xref-target">and-wlite</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:mæg-wlite" class="xref-target">mæg-wlite</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:on-wlite" class="xref-target">on-wlite</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:wamm-wlite" class="xref-target">wamm-wlite</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:neb-wlitu" class="xref-target">neb-wlitu</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="earg-scipe" d:title="earg-scipe">
		<body>
			<h1>earg-scipe<span class="pron"> | æ͜ɑrɣ.ʃi.pe |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">cowardice, pusillanimity</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ongeān mōdstaðolnysse and mōdes strencðe se mānfulla deōfol sendeð wācmōdnesse and lyðerne earhscype (base cowardice)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wlfst. 53, 12)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">profligacy</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">mulierem in adulterio reprehensam</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ꝥ wīf in argscipe begrippene</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Jn. p. 5, 8)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="hīpe" d:title="hīpe">
		
		<body>
			<h1>hīpe<span class="pron"> | xiː.pe |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">a heap</span>
					</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">congeries</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hype</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (An. Ox. 4780)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">cumulis</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hȳpum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Germ. 401, 22)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">in rubicundas congeries</span>
							<span class="q-oe">On reāde hȳpan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (An. Ox. 1822)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:stān-hīpe" class="xref-target">stān-hīpe</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="wiþer-mēde" d:title="wiþer-mēde">
		<body>
			<h1>wiþer-mēde<span class="pron"> | wi.θer.meː.de |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">contrary-minded, contrary, adverse, hostile, opposed</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Se wiðermēda (the devil)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Andr. Kmbl. 2391; An. 1197)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">contraria</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gif huoelc uiðirmoedo (contraria) sindon in hūse esnes ðīnes</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Rtl. 123, 12)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">opposed to good, perverse, depraved</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic (Eve) wæs wiþermēde and unwīsum nētenum gelīc geworden</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Blickl. Homl. 89, 9)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:wiþer-mēdu" class="xref-target">wiþer-mēdu</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:wiþer-mōd" class="xref-target">wiþer-mōd</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="sige-hwīl" d:title="sige-hwīl">
		<body>
			<h1>sige-hwīl<span class="pron"> | si.Ge.xwiːl |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A time of victory, the hour of victory</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Wedra helm feōnd gefylde . . . Ðæt ðam þeōdne wæs sīðes sigehwīl</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Beo. Th. 5413 ; B. 2710)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="twi-lafte" d:title="twi-lafte">
		<body>
			<h1>twi-lafte<span class="pron"> | twi.lɑf.te |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Two-edged</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Twilafte æx bipennis securis</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 126, 27)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:læppa" class="xref-target">læppa</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:læfer" class="xref-target">læfer</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ful-wīte" d:title="ful-wīte">
		
		<body>
			<h1>ful-wīte<span class="pron"> | ful.wiː.te |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>neuter noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A full fine</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. plēna mulcta)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gielde he fulwīte [fullwīte MSS. B. H.] let him pay the full fine</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. In. 43; Th. i. 128, 18: 72; Th. 1. 148, 8: L. C. S. 49; Th. i. 404, 9, note 18, MS. G.)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-fylst" d:title="ge-fylst">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-fylst<span class="pron"> | je.fylst |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">help</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:fylst" class="xref-target">fylst</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="geond-brǣdan" d:title="geond-brǣdan">
		<body>
			<h1>geond-brǣdan<span class="pron"> | Ge͜ond.bræː.dɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -brǣdde</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -brǣded</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To overspread</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. supersternĕre)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">it was overspread with beds and bolsters</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hit geondbrǣded wearþ beddum and bolstrum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Beo. Th. 2483; B. 1239)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-genge" d:title="ge-genge">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-genge<span class="pron"> | je.Gen.Ge |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Convenient, suitable, agreeable</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Unc wearð God yrre for þon wit him noldon hnīgan mid heāfdum . . .: ac unc gegenge ne wæs þæt wit him on þegnscipe þeōwian wolden</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Gen. 743)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-ceōwan" d:title="ge-ceōwan">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-ceōwan<span class="pron"> | je.Ke͜oː.wɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -ceāw, pl: -cuwon</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -cowen</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To chew</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. rūmināre)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">some chew pennyroyal</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Sume dweorgedwostlan geceōwaþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. M. 2, 32; Lchdm. ii. 236, 11)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">lay chewed pennyroyal on the navel</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Lege dweorgedwostlan gecowene on ðone nafolan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (2, 30; Lchdm. ii. 228, 20)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="orc" d:title="orc">
		<body>
			<h1>orc<span class="pron"> | ork |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">The infernal regions (orcus)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Orc orcus</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ep. Gl. 16 f, 36: Wrt. Voc. ii. 115, 61)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Orcþyrs oððe heldeōfol Orcus (the god of the infernal regions)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (63, 49)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="-hwāra" d:title="-hwāra">
		<body>
			<h1>-hwāra<span class="pron"> | xwɑː.rɑ |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:æt-hwāra" class="xref-target">æt-hwāra</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:hwæt-hwāra" class="xref-target">hwæt-hwāra</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="and-wīsnes" d:title="and-wīsnes">
		<body>
			<h1>and-wīsnes<span class="pron"> | ɑnd.wiː.snes |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Experience, skilfulness</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. experientia)</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:wīs" class="xref-target">wīs</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="mete-gafol" d:title="mete-gafol">
		<body>
			<h1>mete-gafol<span class="pron"> | me.te.gɑ.fol |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>neuter noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Tax or rent paid in food</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">On sumen lande gebūr sceal syllan huniggafol, on suman metegafol, on suman ealugafol</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. R. S. 4; Th. i. 434, 32)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="good" d:title="good">
		<body>
			<h1>good<span class="pron"> | go.od |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:gōd" class="xref-target">gōd</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="seāw" d:title="seāw">
		<body>
			<h1>seāw<span class="pron"> | sæ͜ɑːw |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Genim þisse sylfan wyrte (foxglove) seāw mid rosan seāwe,</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Lch. i. 268, 5)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Þicgen þā mettas ðe gōd seāw wyrcen,</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (ii. 226, 12)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:sew" class="xref-target">sew</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-yrnan" d:title="ge-yrnan">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-yrnan<span class="pron"> | je.yr.nɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge-irnan" class="xref-target">ge-irnan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="bildu" d:title="bildu">
		
		
		
		
		
		<body>
			<h1>bildu<span class="pron"> | bil.du |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Boldness, confidence</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt ne weaxe tō ungemetlico beldo (praecipitatio), and swā ðrycce ðā belde ...</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 455, 21)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Bielde constantia</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 23, 58)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Bældo temeritate</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. p. 9, 4)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Mid hwylcre byldu mæg ic gān tō Godes temple?</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. A. 134, 617)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Mid bylde Godes gewinnes</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. Th. ii. 494, 31: Hml. S. 25, 319)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">auctoritatis fortitudine erecti</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt hiē habbað ðā arodnesse and ðā bieldo (bældo, v. l.) ðæt hiē magon anweald habban</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 41, 17)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē hæfde mid him myccle bælde (fiduciam) hīwcūþnesse</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Gr. D. 140, 7)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Baeldo</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Rtl. 89, 3)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Byldum fiducia, i. confidentia</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 148, 74)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:un-bildu" class="xref-target">un-bildu</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:byld" class="xref-target">byld</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-leoran" d:title="ge-leoran">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-leoran<span class="pron"> | je.le͜o.rɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -de</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -ed</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To go, depart, emigrate, die</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. īre, migrāre, emigrāre, deficere)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">let me depart</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Mec geleoran lǣt</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 118 b; Th. 455, 3; Hy. 4, 44 : Bd. 4, 23; S. 596, 11)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">non emigrābo</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic nā geleore</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Spl. C. 61, 6)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">inimīci defēcērunt frāmeæ in fīnem</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Seō rēdelse, and ðæt geþeaht ūrra feōnda geleorde [MS. geleorode], ðā hī hit endian sceoldon</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 9, 6)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">cum quis eōrum de sæcŭlo fuisset evŏcātus</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðonne heora hwylc of weorulde geleored wæs</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 4, 23; S. 595, 41, note)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">nunciavit Hild migrasse de sæculo</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Sægde Hilde of weorulde geleoran</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (596, 11)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">non præteribit</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ne gelioraþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. Kmbl. Lind. 24, 34)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">filia mea defuncta est</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Dōhter mīn geliored is</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (9, 18)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="īdel-georn" d:title="īdel-georn">
		<body>
			<h1>īdel-georn<span class="pron"> | iː.del.Ge͜orn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">frivolous, useless, unprofitable</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Sē ðe wǣre īdelgeorn, weorðe sē notgeorn</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wlfst. 72, 9)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">lazy</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:īdel" class="xref-target">īdel</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="weoloc-scill" d:title="weoloc-scill">
		<body>
			<h1>weoloc-scill<span class="pron"> | we͜o.lok.ʃill |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Weolcscille conquilio</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (An. Ox. 26, 65)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-healden" d:title="ge-healden">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-healden<span class="pron"> | je.xæ͜ɑl.den |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>participle</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Satisfied</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">be satisfied in thy kind, then hast thou enough</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Beō gehealden on ðīnum gecynde ðonne hæfst ðū genōh</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Kmbl. Sal. 264, 21)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:gehealdan" class="xref-target">gehealdan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-bēd-hūs" d:title="ge-bēd-hūs">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-bēd-hūs<span class="pron"> | je.beːd.xuːs |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>neuter noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A prayer-house, an oratory, house of prayer</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. orātorium, dĕmus orātiōnis)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the dwellings have a prayer-house</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Habbaþ ða wīc gebēd-hūs</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 5, 2; S. 614, 33)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">dŏmus mea dŏmus orātiōnis vocābitur</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Mīn hūs biþ genemned gebēd-hūs</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Mk. Bos. 11, 17)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">God's church is our prayer-house</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Godes cyrce is ūre gebēd-hūs</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. ii. 584, 3)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="āhlōwan" d:title="āhlōwan">
		<body>
			<h1>āhlōwan<span class="pron"> | ɑː.xloː.wɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To low or bellow again</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. reboare)</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:hlōwan" class="xref-target">hlōwan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-nyhtsum-līce" d:title="ge-nyhtsum-līce">
		
		<body>
			<h1>ge-nyhtsum-līce<span class="pron"> | je.nyxt.sum.liː.tʃe |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adverb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Abundantly, plentifully</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. abunde, abundanter)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">qui abundanter faciunt superbiam</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ða genyhtsumlīce dōeþ oferhygd</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Surt. 30, 24)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge-nihtsumlīce" class="xref-target">ge-nihtsumlīce</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="fyrdlīc" d:title="fyrdlīc">
		<body>
			<h1>fyrdlīc<span class="pron"> | fyrd.liːK |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Military, martial</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. mīlitāris)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">her course is compared to a martial band</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hire fær is wiðmeten fyrdlīcum truman</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. i. 444, 5: Jos. 11. 10)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="deōfulgyld-hūs" d:title="deōfulgyld-hūs">
		<body>
			<h1>deōfulgyld-hūs<span class="pron"> | de͜oː.ful.Gyld.xuːs |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>neuter noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A heathen temple</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. pagānōrum templum)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">Constantine ordered churches to be built, and every heathen temple to be closed</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Constantinus hēt ðæt man cyricean timbrede, and ðæt man belūce ǣlc deōfulgyldhūs</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 6, 30; Bos. 127, 36)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="feordian" d:title="feordian">
		<body>
			<h1>feordian<span class="pron"> | fe͜or.di.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -ode</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -od</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To be at war</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. bellum gěrěre)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">they were at war with Ætla king of the Huns</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hī feordodan wið Ætlan Hūna cininge</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 443: Erl. 11, 35)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:fyrdian" class="xref-target">fyrdian</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="mǣr-dic" d:title="mǣr-dic">
		<body>
			<h1>mǣr-dic<span class="pron"> | mæːr.diK |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A boundary dike</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">On ða mǣrdīc</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cod. Dip. Kmbl. iii. 378, 24)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">On ða ealdan mǣrdīc</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (449, 10)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="Engla feld" d:title="Engla feld">
		<body>
			<h1>Engla feld<span class="pron"> | en.glɑ, feld |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -feldes, dative sg: -felda, dative sg: -felde</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">ENGLEFIELD or INGLEFIELD, near Reading, Berkshire</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. loci nomen in agro Berkeriensi)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">in this year [A. D. 871] the army came to Reading in Wessex, and three nights after two earls rode up: then alderman Æthelwulf met them at Inglefield, and there fought against them, and gained the victory.</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Her cwom se here to Reādingum on West-Seaxe, and dæs ymb iii niht ridon ii eorlas up: ðā gemētte hie Æðelwulf aldorman on Engla felda, and him ðǣr wið gefeaht, and sige nam</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 871; Erl. 74, 5-8.)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="wīte-leās" d:title="wīte-leās">
		<body>
			<h1>wīte-leās<span class="pron"> | wiː.te.læ͜ɑːs |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Not having to pay a fine</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gelǣste ǣlc wuduwe ða heregeata binnan twelf mōnðum, būton hire ǣr tō onhagige, wīteleās</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. C. S. 74; Th. i. 416, 18)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="Finns buruh" d:title="Finns buruh">
		
		<body>
			<h1>Finns buruh<span class="pron"> | finns, bu.rux |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -burge</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Finnsburg</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">as if all Fin's castle were on fire</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Swylce eal Finnes buruh [MS. Finns] fȳrenu wǣre</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Fins. Th. 72; Fin. 36.)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">such as they might find at Finnesham</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Swylce hie æt Finnes hām findaa meahton</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Beo. Th. 2316; B. 1156.)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:Finn" class="xref-target">Finn</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="sige-beācen" d:title="sige-beācen">
		<body>
			<h1>sige-beācen<span class="pron"> | si.Ge.bæ͜ɑː.Ken |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">vox magna</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Cymeð sigebeācen</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Verc. Först. 122, 11)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="streōn" d:title="streōn">
		<body>
			<h1>streōn<span class="pron"> | stre͜oːn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>neuter noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">gain, acquisition, treasure</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. thesaurus)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">ubi est thesaurus tuus</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðēr is striōn ðīn</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. Kmbl. Lind. 6, 21: 12, 35 : Lk. Skt. Lind. 6, 45)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">thesauri</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Striōnes</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (p. 17, 5)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">quaestuum, lucrum</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Tilða ł stre (= streōna or streōn)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hpt. Gl. 452, 7)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">confidentes in pecuniis</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ða ðe gelēfeþ in striōnum (on gistriōn, Rush.)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Mk. Skt. Lind. 10, 24)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">de facultatibus suis</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Of striōnum hiora</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lk. Skt. Lind. 8, 3)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">thesauros</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Striōna</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. Kmbl. Lind. 6, 20)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">begetting(?), generating</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">si quis suam conjugem creandorum liberorum gratia utitur</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Swā hwylc monn swā his wīf for intingan ānum brūceþ tō streōnne (streōnenne ?; other text has bearna tō strȳnenne)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 1, 27 ; S. 495, 33 MS. T.)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">III.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">power (?)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">aestimate, quam vultis nimio corporis bona, dum sciatis hoc, quodcumque miramini, triduanae febris igniculo posse dissolvi</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Geþencaþ hwelc ðǣs flǣsclīcan gōd siēn and ða gesǣlþa ðe gēungemetlīce wilniaþ ðonne māgon gē ongeotan ðæt ð æs līchoman fæger and his streōn māgon (strengo mæg Cott. MS.) beōn āfeorred mid þreora daga fefre</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 32, 2; Fox 116, 31)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge-streōn" class="xref-target">ge-streōn</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:streōnan" class="xref-target">streōnan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-hwyrfednes" d:title="ge-hwyrfednes">
		
		<body>
			<h1>ge-hwyrfednes<span class="pron"> | je.xwyr.fed.nes |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A conversion, change</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. conversio)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">quōrum fīdei et conversiōni</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðara geleāfan and gehwyrfednesse</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 1, 26; S. 488, 13)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">tempore suæ conversionis</span>
							<span class="q-oe">In ða tīd heora gehwyrfenesse</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (4, 5; S. 572, 39)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="in-stæppan" d:title="in-stæppan">
		<body>
			<h1>in-stæppan<span class="pron"> | in.stæp.pɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -te</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To step, in, enter</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">non introibo</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic ne instæppe oððe ingā oððe ic ne fare</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Lamb. 25, 4)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">introite in conspectu ejus</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Insteppaþ oððe ingāþ on gesihþe his</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (99, 2)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">in innocentia mea ingressus sum</span>
							<span class="q-oe">On unscyldignysse mīnre instæppende ic eom</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (25, 11)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">some of them saw angels entering</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hī sume gesāwon englas instæppende</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. ii. 546, 23)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="āhycgan" d:title="āhycgan">
		
		<body>
			<h1>āhycgan<span class="pron"> | ɑː.xydʒ.dʒɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -hogde, sg: -hogode</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -[ge]-hugod</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To devise, search, invent</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. excogitare, perscrutari, invenire)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">more clearly than men may in mind devise it</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Leōhtor ðonne hit men mǣgen mōdum ahycgan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 21 a; Th. 56, 20; Cri. 903)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">besought them to devise counsel for this</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Bæd him ðæs rǣd ahicgan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. 94; Th. 122, 24; Gen. 2031: 178; Th. 224, 3; Dan. 130)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">they invented the sword</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hie ahogodan heoro</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 92 a; Th. 346, 9; Gn. Ex. 202)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:hycgan" class="xref-target">hycgan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="glydering" d:title="glydering">
		<body>
			<h1>glydering<span class="pron"> | gly.de.ring |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:glidering" class="xref-target">glidering</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="grunnung" d:title="grunnung">
		<body>
			<h1>grunnung<span class="pron"> | grun.nung |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:grunung" class="xref-target">grunung</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="in-feccan" d:title="in-feccan">
		<body>
			<h1>in-feccan<span class="pron"> | in.fek.kɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">to fetch in</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">he ordered the sorcerer to be fetched into his presence</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðā hēht hē ðone drȳ infeccan beforan hine</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Blickl. Homl. 175, 1)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="wrōht-spitol" d:title="wrōht-spitol">
		<body>
			<h1>wrōht-spitol<span class="pron"> | wroːxt.spi.tol |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Slanderous</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Wrōhtspitel stisurio</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Txts. 99, 1943)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="wealdian" d:title="wealdian">
		<body>
			<h1>wealdian<span class="pron"> | wæ͜ɑl.di.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -ode</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To rule, command</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. imperito)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">imperito</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic wealdige vel ofer bebeōde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. i. 54, 52)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:wealdan" class="xref-target">wealdan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ylp" d:title="ylp">
		
		<body>
			<h1>ylp<span class="pron"> | ylp |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">An elephant</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. elefans)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ylp elefans</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. i. 78, ll: 22, 41)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ylp is ormǣte nȳten, māre þonne sum hūs</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Skt. ii. 25, 566)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ylpes bile promuscida</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. i. 22, 42)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ylpes bān ebur</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Coll. Monast. Th. 27, 9: Lchdm. iii. 204, 2, 3)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē sende þrittig ylpas tō wīge gewenode . . . and on ǣlcum ylpe wæs ān wīghūs getimbrod</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Skt. ii. 25, 561)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē (the unicorn) fiht wið ðone myclan ylp, and hine oft gewundaþ on ðære wambe ōþ deāþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. i. 78, 1)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gif hē ylp gesihð lāðne oððe gramne, sume wrōhte hit getācnaþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lchdm. iii. 204, 1)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ða ylpas beōð swā mycele swylce ōðre muntas</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hexam. 9; Norm. 16, 9)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē geworhte ða ormǣtan ylpas</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Norm. 14, 34)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:elpend" class="xref-target">elpend</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="azīma" d:title="azīma">
		<body>
			<h1>azīma<span class="pron"> | ɑ.ziː.mɑ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>neuter noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive pl: -orum</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Unleavened</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. infermentata, azyma)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">dies festus azȳmorum, qui dicitur pascha; ἡ ἑορτὴ τῶν ἀζύμων ἡ λεγομένη πάσχα</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Freōlsdæg azīmorum, se is gecweden eāstre</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lk. Bos. 22, 1)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">dies azȳmorum; ἡ ἡμέρα τῶν ἀζύμων</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Se dæg azīmorum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lk. Bos. 22, 7)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="hlinaþ" d:title="hlinaþ">
		<body>
			<h1>hlinaþ<span class="pron"> | xli.nɑθ |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:hleōnaþ" class="xref-target">hleōnaþ</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="BRYCG" d:title="BRYCG">
		
		<body>
			<h1>BRYCG<span class="pron"> | brydʒː |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A BRIDGE</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. pons)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðeōs brycg hic pons</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. Gr. 9, 39; Som. 12, 59)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">that he could not come to the bridge</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt he ne myhte to ðære brycge cuman</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 2, 5; Bos. 48, 14)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">king Edward commanded the bridge over the Trent to be built</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Eādweard cyning hêt gewyrcan ða brycge ofer Treontan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 924; Erl. 110, 10: 887; Erl. 84, 30: 1071; Erl. 210, 17: Ors. 2, 5; Bos. 46, 7)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:stân-bricg" class="xref-target">stân-bricg</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ā-standendness" d:title="ā-standendness">
		<body>
			<h1>ā-standendness<span class="pron"> | ɑː.stɑn.dend.ness |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Continuance, persistence, perseverance</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">On þǣre gebedes āstandendnysse</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. S. 23 b, 272)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="six-hynde" d:title="six-hynde">
		
		
		<body>
			<h1>six-hynde<span class="pron"> | siks.xyn.de |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Of a class whose wergild is six hundred shillings</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gif wealh hafaþ fīf hȳda hē biþ sixhynde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. In. 24; Th. i. 118. 10)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Be syxhyndum men. Gif hit siē syxhynde mon, [gielde] ǣlc mon . lx. scil̄l̄. ,</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. Alf. pol. 30; Th. i. 80, 11)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gif hiō siē syxhyndu,</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (18; Th. i. 72, 14)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Syxhyndes monnes burhbryce . xv. scil̄l̄.,</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (40; Th. i. 88, 10)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gif syxhyndum ðissa hwæðer gelimpe, gebēte be ðæs syxhyndan bōte,</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (39; Th. I. 88, 2-5)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Syxhyndum men . c. scil̄l̄. gebēte,</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (10; Th. i. 68, 10)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
					<ol class="sub-senses">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sub-heading">applied to the wergild</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Æt twȳhyndum were mon sceal sellan tō monbōte .xxx. scil̄l̄. , æt syxhyndum . lxxx. scil̄l̄. ,</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (L. In. 70; Th. i. 146, 14)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:twelf-hynde" class="xref-target">twelf-hynde</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-dysigend" d:title="ge-dysigend">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-dysigend<span class="pron"> | je.dy.si.Gend |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">one acting foolishly</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">a praesumtoribus imperitis</span>
							<span class="q-oe">From dearflicum ł from gidyss-gindum unwīsum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. p. 2, l.)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="be-lǣfan" d:title="be-lǣfan">
		<body>
			<h1>be-lǣfan<span class="pron"> | be.læː.fɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">trans</span>
					</p>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(1)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">to leave, be survived by</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hē bearn ne belǣfð</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. Th. ii. 146, 20)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(2)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">to leave unconsumed, un-done, to spare</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">non dimiserunt ullas reliquias</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Hē ne belǣfde nāne lāte cuce</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Jos. 10, 28)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Nān hǣðengyld se hagol ne belǣfde</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. S. 4, 427: Hml. Th. ii. 194, 2)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Þone sǣdere hē belǣfde ūs tō sēcenne</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (90, 8)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Næs nān ele belǣfed tō his gebrōðra bricum</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (178, 20)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">intrans. To remain</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ān of him ne belāf (-lǣfde, MS. C)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Spl. 105, II)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē hēt ācwellan þā crīstenan, wolde ꝥ nān man ne belǣfde crīsten</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. S. 29, 202)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="eting" d:title="eting">
		<body>
			<h1>eting<span class="pron"> | e.ting |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Eating</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. in edendo)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">in edendo</span>
							<span class="q-oe">On etincge</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Scint. 170, 5)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="āweardian" d:title="āweardian">
		<body>
			<h1>āweardian<span class="pron"> | ɑː.wæ͜ɑr.di.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -ode, sg: -ede</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -od, past participle sg: -ed</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To ward off defend, protect</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. defendere, protegere)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">they defended themselves</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hī hī sylf aweardedon</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 5, 3; Bar. 182, 19)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:weardian" class="xref-target">weardian</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="folc-riht" d:title="folc-riht">
		
		<body>
			<h1>folc-riht<span class="pron"> | folk.rixt |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">According to folk-right, lawful</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. secundum publicum jus, legalis)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">let him be worthy of lawful compensation</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Sīe he wyrðe folcryhtre [-rihtre MS. G.] bōte</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. Alf. 13; Th. i. 46, 25)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
