<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="hlīt" d:title="hlīt">
		
		
		<body>
			<h1>hlīt<span class="pron"> | xliːt |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">a lot (the object which is used)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">cleros sors interpretatur</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Cleros an Crēcisc getācnaþ hlȳt an Englisc</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Chrd. 75, 28)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">super vestem meam miserunt sortem</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ofer hrægl mīn sendon hlēt (hlȳt, Ps. L.)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Vos. Srt. 21, 19)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hlētt</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Mk. R. 15, 24)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">I a.</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">the urn in which the lots were placed</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">urna (matronam, quam suprenia sors gernina mortis mulctaverat urna. Ald. 25, 9)</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Hlēte</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Hpt. Gl. 449, 58)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">the casting of lots</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">contradictiones comprimit sors, et (inter potentes) diiudicat</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Wiðercwidas ofþrect hlēt, and tō-scēd</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Kent. Gl. 655)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">sorte (territorii dirempta)</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Be hlēte</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hpt. Gl. 426, 42)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">sorte divisit eis terram</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hlēte tōdǣlde him eorþan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Vos. Srt. 77, 54)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">III.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">the share assigned to a person</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Seō sāwel þe bedǣled is þām gōdnyssum, heō gewilnige þæt se cystiga wealdend hī geþeōde þām hlȳte his gecorena</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. Th. i. 346, 29)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">sortem</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ne forlǣt Dryhten gird synfulra ofer hlēt (sortem) ryhtwīsra</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Vos. Srt. 134, 3)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">IV.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">lot, fate, fortune</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē Mercna rīce twā and twēntig wintra missenlice hlēte (hlȳte, v. l. varia sorte) fore wæs</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 2, 20; 184, l)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">simili sorte damnavit</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Þone hē gelīce hlēte (hlȳte, v. l.) geniðrade and ofslōh Eanfridum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (3, l; Sch. 192, 22)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">now are the apostles appointed to the task(?) of ever proclaiming her</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Nū syndon gesette þā apostolas in hlēt ǣ hiē bodian</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bl. H. 157, 35)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">in manibus tuis sortes meae</span>
							<span class="q-oe">On handum þīnum hlȳta mīne</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. L. 30, 16)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">IV a.</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">of death</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">sortis supremæ</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Þǣre ȳtemeste hlȳtes</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (An. Ox. 2294)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">suprema sorte</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Þæm ētemestan hlēte</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Hpt. GL, 453, 34)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:mid-hlīt" class="xref-target">mid-hlīt</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:hlyte" class="xref-target">hlyte</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ofer-hycgan" d:title="ofer-hycgan">
		<body>
			<h1>ofer-hycgan<span class="pron"> | o.fer.xydʒ.dʒɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">to despise, contemn, disdain, scorn</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gif hē ðis (lying at the feet of his superior) oferhigþ and hit dōn nelle</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (R. Ben. 131, 7)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">dum homo hominibus esse similis dedignatur</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðonne se mon oferhygþ (Hatt. MS. oferhȳþ) ðæt hē biō gelīc ōðrum monnum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 17, 4; Swt. 112, 3)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">tanto graviori improbitate contemnitur, quanto contemtus adhuc vocare non dedignatur</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Wē hine mid swā micle māran unryhte oferhycgeaþ swā hē læs forhogaþ ðæt hē ūs ðonne giet tō him spane, siððan wē hiene oferhycggeaþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (52, 4; Swt. 407, 17-19)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðeāh hī hine oferhogden, ne for-</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="an-gin" d:title="an-gin">
		<body>
			<h1>an-gin<span class="pron"> | ɑn.Gin |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">a beginning</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Angin origo.</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 128, 42)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Of anginne ex integra,</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (145, 4)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Tō anginne, tō edstaþelungum ad lumina vitae,</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (An. Ox. 2214)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Toanginnum ad lumina (v. Hpt. Gl. 507, 61, which has limina),</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (4342)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Seō wyrt gehnǣceþ ðā anginnu (the beginnings of the disease) þām wæterseōcum,</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lch. i. 272, 15)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">an enterprise, undertaking, attempt</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">ꝥ angin [building a fleet] wearð tīdlice þurhtogen,</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 4, 6; S. 172, 3)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">ꝥ ꝥ angin (a war) nǣre gestilled,</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (6, 4; S. 260, 5)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Romulus hiora anginn (founding Rome) geunclǣnsode mid his brōðor slege,</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (2, 2; S. 64, 23)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gif hwylc man ūre angin (writing Gulhlac's life) and weorc tǣle,</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Guth. 4, l.)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">III.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">persistent effort, enterprise, endeavour, pertinacity</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the pertinacity of the thanes in not desisting from breaking down the wall</span>
							<span class="q-oe">þāra þegna angin . . . ꝥ hiē noldon þæs weallgebreces geswīcan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 3, 9; S. 134, 27)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt hē ðā medwiisan tō māran angienne (ad majora) gespōne,</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 205, 17)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hū God þā mǣstan ofermētto and þæt mǣste angin on swā heānlice ofermētto ( the extreme perseverance in such contemptible pride ?) geniðerade,</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 2, 5; S. 84, 11)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Anginna pertinacia,</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Kent. Gl. 1170)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">IIIa.</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">practice of a rite, study</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Nǣfre nān man ne geþrīstlǣce ǣnigne deōfles bīgencg tō dōnne, ne on wiccedōme, ne on ǣnegum īdelum anginne,</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. A. 143, 123)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Forsægenum þām onginnum (studiis; v. l. bīgengum) þāra bðccræfta.</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Gr. D. 95, 26)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">ꝥ hē forlēte þā ongin þǣra bōccræfta relictis literarum studiis,</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (96, 19)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">IV.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">attempt on, attack</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ne becume mē fōt ł angin ofermōdignesse non veniat mihi pes superbiae,</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. L. 35, 12)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Onginnum inceptis (machinamentorum).</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (An. Ox. 4709)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">V.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">gesture, action</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Angin gesticulatio,</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (An. Ox. 2872)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē fǣringa feōll tō þǣre eorðan mid egeslicum anginne,</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 1042; P. 162, 14)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Anginnum gestibus,</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (An. Ox. 7, 241: 8, 180)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">VI.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">action, proceedings, behaviour, treatment</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Þā hē ðæs cāseres myclan hreōwsunga geseah, him ꝥ hreōw and his ꝥ sārlice anginn (his piteous proceedings).</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. S. 23, 402)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">he troubled the bishops by his audacious treatment of them</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē began tō dreccenne mid dyrstigum anginne þā bisceopas</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (37, 34)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">His cempan hine gelǣhton mid dyrstigum anginne (treated him with the utmost audacity),</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. Th. ii. 252, 24)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hī tīgdon þā fēt tōgædere mid gramlicum anginne,</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. S. 35, 166)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hī woldon Egeam ācwellan and ālǣdan ðone apostol of ðām cwearterne. Ðā cwæð Andreas: ' Ne āstyrige gē Drihten tō yrsunge mid eōwerum anginne,'</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. Th. i. 592, 4)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">while the citizens were engaged in such melancholy proceedings</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Mid þǣm þe þā burgware swā geōmorlic angin hæfdon</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 4, 5; S. 166, 15)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ongin" class="xref-target">ongin</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="EFENLĪCE" d:title="EFENLĪCE">
		<body>
			<h1>EFENLĪCE<span class="pron"> | e.fen.liː.Ke |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:EFEN-WEORÞ" class="xref-target">EFEN-WEORÞ</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ful-æðele" d:title="ful-æðele">
		<body>
			<h1>ful-æðele<span class="pron"> | ful.æ.θe.le |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">full noble, very noble</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:full-æðele" class="xref-target">full-æðele</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="Cent-rīce" d:title="Cent-rīce">
		<body>
			<h1>Cent-rīce<span class="pron"> | Kent.riː.Ke |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>neuter noun</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">in Cantia</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Æðelbyrht cyning on Centrīce</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. i. 25; Sch. 51, 15)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="simblunga" d:title="simblunga">
		
		<body>
			<h1>simblunga<span class="pron"> | sim.blun.gɑ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adverb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Always, continually</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. jugiter)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Symlinga jugiter</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Rtl. 33, 17)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Symlunge continuo</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (59, 33)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Symlinga continua (-o ?)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (17, 5)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="MIRRA" d:title="MIRRA">
		<body>
			<h1>MIRRA<span class="pron"> | mir.rɑ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Myrrh; myrrha</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. myrrha)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Mirra, wyrm-ellen, wermod</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. i. 67, 21)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Mirra vel myrra myrrha</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 125, 13)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="un-cyn[n]" d:title="un-cyn[n]">
		<body>
			<h1>un-cyn[n]<span class="pron"> | un.kynn, n |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Unsuitable, unfitting, improper</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">cui non inmerito potestas datur</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæm ne is uncynn mæht bið sald</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lk. Skt. p. 3, 3)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="mǣst-līce" d:title="mǣst-līce">
		
		<body>
			<h1>mǣst-līce<span class="pron"> | mæːst.liː.tʃe |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adverb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Very much</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. magnopere)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">magnopere</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Mǣstlīcust</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Angl. xiii. 447, 1169)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="hindan" d:title="hindan">
		<body>
			<h1>hindan<span class="pron"> | xin.dɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adverb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">where there is movement towards the back of an object</span>
					</p>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(1)</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">of the direction of an action</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hē hēt Mathēum hindan mid sweorde þurstingan</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Shrn. 131, 33)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">þ ā Engliscan hī hindan hetelīce slōgon</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 1066; P. 199, 15)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(2)</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">with verbs of pursuit</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-en">it comes up with the sun from behind and rises be ore the sun</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Hē ofi nþ þā sunnan hindan and cymþ wiþforan þā sunnan ūp</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 39, 13; F. 234, 2)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">marking position, at the back, behind</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:on-hindan" class="xref-target">on-hindan</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:wiþ-hindan" class="xref-target">wiþ-hindan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="rȳman" d:title="rȳman">
		<body>
			<h1>rȳman<span class="pron"> | ryː.mɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -de</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to make roomy, extend, spread, enlarge, amplify</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">dilatasti</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðū rȳmdest</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Lamb. 4, 2)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē ēðelþrym rȳmde and rǣrde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. Th. 98, 24; Gen. 1635)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">spread and drove the waters widely</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Sōð metod rȳmde, wīde wǣðde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (208, 7; Exod. 479)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt se gītsere his land mid unryhte rȳme</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 44, 8; Swt. 329, 21)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">quousque vos extenditis?</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hū feor wolde gē rȳman eōwer land</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Swt. 331, 1)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">I will multiply food again under heaven (after the deluge)</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic eft reorde under roderum rȳman wille</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. Th. 81, 13; Gen. 1344)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">ad dilatandum terminum suum</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hira mearce tō rȳmanne</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 48, 2; Swt. 367, 15)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Heora hūs tō rȳmende</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Chart. Th. 436, 18)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to make clear by removing obstructions, to clear a way (lit. and metaph.)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē sāwlum rȳmeþ līfwegas</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. Th. 148, 4; Gū. 739 : 436, 6; Rä. 54, 10)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">by such conduct he clears the way for an oath on behalf of the dead man, so that his (the dead man's) kinsmen may exculpate him</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðonne rȳmeþ hē ðam deādan tō ðam āþe ðæt hine mōton his mǣgas unsyngian</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. In. 21; Th. i. 116, 7)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">make the way to possession clear for him</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gif getrȳwe gewitnes him tō āgenunge rȳmþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. Eth. ii. 9; Th. i. 290, 20)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt syndan Antecristes þrǣlas ðe his weg rȳmaþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wulfst. 55, 9)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ða ðe ingang rȳmaþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Salm. Kmbl. 442; Sal. 221)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Se engel āwylte ðæt hlid; nā ðæt hē Criste ūtganges rȳmde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. i. 222, 9)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Se engel rȳmde him weg þurh ðæt fȳr</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (ii. 344, 13)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">(I will pull down my barns and build greater, Lk. 12, 18)</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic wille rȳman mīnne bertūn and mīne beornu geeācnian</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (104, 1 : Wulfst. 286, 19)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Seō sealf wile ǣrest ða dolh rȳman, and ðæt deāde flǣsc of etan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lchdm. ii. 332, 24)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">III.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to make room by removing one's self, yield, give place</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">caedo</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic fare āweg oððe ic rȳme (rume, MS. W.: hryme, hnime, other MSS.)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. Gr. 28, 4; Zup. 171, 9)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Se ōðer rȳmþ him setl</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. i. 248, 17)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">cedunt</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Rūmaþ, steppaþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 19, 19 : 87, 64)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">cessit</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Rȳmde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (81, 75)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ā man rȳmde (retreated) fram ðære sǣ, and hī fērdon ǣfre forþ æfter</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 999; Erl. 135, 35)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">they left the field clear for their foes</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hi rīmdon heora feōndum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (1015; Erl. 152, 16)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">da huic locum</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Rȳm ðysum men setl</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lk. Skt. 14, 9)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Rȳmaþ him (cease to oppose him) ðæt hē mē leng ne swence</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. i. 534, 17)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge-rȳman" class="xref-target">ge-rȳman</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ofer-hygdigian" d:title="ofer-hygdigian">
		<body>
			<h1>ofer-hygdigian<span class="pron"> | o.fer.xyɣ.di.Gi.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">to be proud</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">dum superbit impius</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðonne oferhygdgaþ se ārleāsa</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Surt. 9, 23)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="brogdettan" d:title="brogdettan">
		
		
		<body>
			<h1>brogdettan<span class="pron"> | broɣ.det.tɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -te</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to shake, quiver</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Brogdetteð vibrat</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Txts. 107, 2132)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">ut apparuerit cancussione mirifica tremendo palpitasse</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Swā ꝥ wæs æteōwed, ꝥ hē brōdette byfiende mid wundorlicre styrunge</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Gr. D. 166, 14)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">coepit ipse tremens et palpitans clamare . . . trementem et palpitantem monachum reduxerunt</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Þā ongan hē ofdrǣdd bifian and broddettan (forhtiende and brēdetende, v. l.) and clypian . . . Hī þone munuc cwakiendne and broddettendne (brōd-, v. l.) gelǣddon</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (156, 13-21)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Brogdetende vel cleppetende campus (can the English words be epithets applied to campus ( = aequor, cf. Corp. Gl. H. A. 314, aequor, pelagus vel campus) referring to the quivering of the surface of the water?)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Txts. 49, 411)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Brogdetende, brocdaettendi, brogdaethendi palpitans</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (83, 1472)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Brōdetende</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 67, 54)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to glitter, be splendid</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">stolidis pompis indruticans</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Mid dislicum glengcgum brottetende (v. brogdettung for form)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hpt. Gl. 435, 37)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="hirstan" d:title="hirstan">
		<body>
			<h1>hirstan<span class="pron"> | xir.stɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:hyrstan" class="xref-target">hyrstan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-hæplic" d:title="ge-hæplic">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-hæplic<span class="pron"> | je.xæ.pliK |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:un-ge-hæplic" class="xref-target">un-ge-hæplic</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="freōnd-heald" d:title="freōnd-heald">
		<body>
			<h1>freōnd-heald<span class="pron"> | fre͜oːnd.xæ͜ɑld |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Friend-inclined, friendly</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. amīcābĭlĭs)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">a child will be friendly</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Cild biþ freōndheald</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Obs. Lun. § 17; Lchdm. iii. 192, 15)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="GEŌ" d:title="GEŌ">
		
		<body>
			<h1>GEŌ<span class="pron"> | Ge͜oː |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adverb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Formerly, of old, before</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. quandam, olim, pridem)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the lays which I, an exile, formerly with delight sung, I shall now mourning sing</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ða liōþ ðe ic, wrecca, geō lustbǣrlīce song, ic sceal nu heōfiende singan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 2; Fox 4, 7: Bt. Met. Fox 10, 68; Met. 10, 34)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">thou of old didst strive against Christ</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðū wið Criste geō wunne</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 71 b; Th. 267, 25; Jul. 420: 19 b; Th. 51, 11; Cri. 814: Cd. 106; Th. 139, 12; Gen. 2308: Menol. Fox 34; Men. 17)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">this island was formerly adorned with the noblest cities</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Wæs ðis eālond geō gewurþad mid æðelestum ceastrum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 1, 1; S. 473, 25)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">do thou, sagacious prince, bear in mind what we have before spoken</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Geþenc se snottra fengel hwæt wit geō sprǣcon</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Beo. Th. 2957; B. 1476)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">long before</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Geō ǣr</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 4, 19; S. 589, 17)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">in days of old, formerly</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Geō dagum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (4, 27; S. 605, note 2)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">formerly</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Geō geāra</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 31, 1; Fox 112, 15)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">in times of old, formerly</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Geō hwīlum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (2; Fox 4, 9)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="word-beōt" d:title="word-beōt">
		<body>
			<h1>word-beōt<span class="pron"> | word.be͜oːt |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>neuter noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A promise</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ða com fēran Freā tō Sarran swā hē self gecwæð, hæfde wordbeōt leōfum gelǣsted</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. Th. 167, 6; Gen. 2761)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Wāciaþ wordbeōt</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. Th. 469, 22; Hy. II, 6)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:word-gebeōt" class="xref-target">word-gebeōt</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="of-fyllan" d:title="of-fyllan">
		<body>
			<h1>of-fyllan<span class="pron"> | of.fyl.lɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:of-fillan" class="xref-target">of-fillan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="eārðan" d:title="eārðan">
		<body>
			<h1>eārðan<span class="pron"> | æ͜ɑːr.θɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adverb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">before that</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. antequam)</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ǣr" class="xref-target">ǣr</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="georn-ness" d:title="georn-ness">
		<body>
			<h1>georn-ness<span class="pron"> | Ge͜orn.ness |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:wæfer-g" class="xref-target">wæfer-g</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ofer-līþan" d:title="ofer-līþan">
		<body>
			<h1>ofer-līþan<span class="pron"> | o.fer.liː.θɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">velut transvadato vasti gurgitis aequore</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Swā ic strange sǣ and mycele oferlīðe</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Guth. Gr. 102, 33)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="þwarm" d:title="þwarm">
		<body>
			<h1>þwarm<span class="pron"> | θwɑrm |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:þwearm" class="xref-target">þwearm</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ēsa" d:title="ēsa">
		<body>
			<h1>ēsa<span class="pron"> | eː.sɑ |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ōs" class="xref-target">ōs</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="Lindisfarnensisc" d:title="Lindisfarnensisc">
		<body>
			<h1>Lindisfarnensisc<span class="pron"> | lin.dis.fɑr.nen.siʃ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Of Lindisfarne</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Se hālga Cūþberhtus, Lindisfarnensiscere gelaþunge leōdbiscop</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. ii. 148, 22)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="tō-weard" d:title="tō-weard">
		<body>
			<h1>tō-weard<span class="pron"> | toː.wæ͜ɑrd |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>preposition (w. genitive)</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">Toward, in the direction of</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ða ðe gāþ on ryhtne weg tōweard ðæs hefonrīces</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 9; Swt. 59, 19)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē wæs hym syððan tōweard hys scypes farende</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Ass. 190, 258)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>preposition (w. dative)</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">Toward, in the direction of</span>
					</p>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(1)</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">preceding the governed word</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ðonne ærnaþ hȳ ealle tōweard ðæm feō</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 1, 1; Swt. 20, 36)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hī torfedon tōwærd ðam weofode . . . and scotedon tōweard ðam hālig-dōme</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 1083 ; Erl. 217, 17, 19)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Crist wæs tōweard ðære rōde gelǣd</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Btwk. 214, 27)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(2)</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">following the governed word</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">mors propinquat</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Hē eōw onet tōweard</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Met. 27, 8)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(3)</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">where tó precedes and weard follows (cf. to God ward, to us ward in A. V. )</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hē hine bær tō mynstre weard</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. i. 336, 12: Wulfst. 302, 26)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hē went ǣfre ðone hricg tō ðære sunnan weard</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Lchdm. iii. 266, 24)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Tō scipan weard</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 1009 ; Erl. 143, 11)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hī wendon him tō ðære burge weard</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (1048 ; Erl. 178, 1)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hī wǣron heom tō Lundene weard</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (1052; Erl. 185, 4)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hē hēt ðæt hē biheōlde tō his Drihtne werd</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Skt. ii. 31, 78)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="sealf" d:title="sealf">
		
		<body>
			<h1>sealf<span class="pron"> | sæ͜ɑlf |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Salve, ointment</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Salf, salb malagma</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Txts. 77, 127)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Sealf</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. i. 68, 6)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Smyrels vel sealf unguina vel unguenta</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (49, 29)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Fota, i. confortata vel sealf</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (ii. 149, 76)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Smyrels oððe sealfe unguentum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (i. 74, 8)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Sealfe nardi</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hpt. Gl. 517, 28)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">For hwī wæs ðisse sealfe forspillednes? Ðeōs sealf mihte beōn geseald</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Mk. Skt. 14, 4, 5: Jn. Skt. 12, 3, 5)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Wyrc tō salfe (sealfe, MSS. H. B.)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lchdm. i. 110, 18)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Sealfe fotu</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 90, 74)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Lǣcedōmnessa oððe sealfe cataplasma</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (18, 31)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:bæþ-sealf" class="xref-target">bæþ-sealf</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:bān-sealf" class="xref-target">bān-sealf</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:ciper-sealf" class="xref-target">ciper-sealf</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:cū-sealf" class="xref-target">cū-sealf</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:dolh-sealf" class="xref-target">dolh-sealf</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:eāg-sealf" class="xref-target">eāg-sealf</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:eār-sealf" class="xref-target">eār-sealf</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:ele-sealf" class="xref-target">ele-sealf</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:mūþ-sealf" class="xref-target">mūþ-sealf</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:sceāde-sealf" class="xref-target">sceāde-sealf</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:smeoru-sealf" class="xref-target">smeoru-sealf</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:tōþ-sealf" class="xref-target">tōþ-sealf</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:weax-sealf" class="xref-target">weax-sealf</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:weax—hlāf-sealf" class="xref-target">weax—hlāf-sealf</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:wen-sealf" class="xref-target">wen-sealf</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ācwelledness" d:title="ācwelledness">
		<body>
			<h1>ācwelledness<span class="pron"> | ɑː.kwel.led.ness |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A quelling, killing</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. occisio)</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:cwellan" class="xref-target">cwellan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="tīþe" d:title="tīþe">
		
		<body>
			<h1>tīþe<span class="pron"> | tiː.θe |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">in the phrases tīþe(-a) beōn, weorþan to obtain one's request, to have granted the request for something (gen.)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">statim edoctus impetrasse se quod petebat a Domino</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Sōna wæs gelǣred ðætte hē wæs from Drihtne tȳþe ðære bēne ðe hē bæd</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 4, 29; S. 607, 32)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Myceles ðū (masc.) bǣde, ac ðū bist tīða</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Skt. i. 18, 284)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Tȳða</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (3, 513)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðū (Abraham) ðæs tīða beō</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. Th. 142, 12; Gen. 2360)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē ongann tō Gode wīsdōmes wylnian, and hē eāc ðæs tīða wearð</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wulfst. 277, 19)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðū (Lot) scealt ðære bēne tīða weorðan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. Th. 152, 28; Gen. 2527)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Þeāh ðū (Esther) biddan wille healfne ðone anweald . . . ðū scealt beōn tīþu ðæs</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Anglia ix. 33, 185)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Heō ābæd æt Gode Godes willan tō ðām ðæt heō sunu hæfde, and heō sōna wæs tīðu (other MSS. tīða)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Ass. 38, 357)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">For swā hwæne swā heō bit, heō biþ tīða simle</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Skt. ii. 29, 274)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt ic (a widow) beō ðæs tīðe ðe ic bidde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. i. 566, 15)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">omnia quaecunque petieritis in oratione accipietis</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ealles ðæs ðe gē biddaþ gē beōþ tīða</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. Kmbl. 21, 22)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:bēn-tīðe" class="xref-target">bēn-tīðe</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:tīþ" class="xref-target">tīþ</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:tīþian" class="xref-target">tīþian</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="Denisc" d:title="Denisc">
		<body>
			<h1>Denisc<span class="pron"> | de.niʃ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">cum insurrexissent gentes innumerabiles, hoc est, Marcomanni atque omnis pene Germania</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Æfter þǣm him becōm on þæt Deniscæ gewinn mid eallum Germānium</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 6, 13; S. 268, 10)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-līman" d:title="ge-līman">
		
		<body>
			<h1>ge-līman<span class="pron"> | je.liː.mɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Hē (the conjunction) gelīmað þā word</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. Gr. Z. 258, 12)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">conglutinata</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Gelīmed</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 104, 69: 133, 36)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">glutinatum</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Tōsomne gelīmed</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (40, 26)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">visco glutinatam</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Fugellīme gelīmedne</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (81, 57: An. Ox. 3016)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">conglutinatae</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Gelīmedre</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (9, 6)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="candel-sticca" d:title="candel-sticca">
		<body>
			<h1>candel-sticca<span class="pron"> | kɑn.del.stik.kɑ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -an</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A CANDLESTICK</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. candelabrum)</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="nunn-fǣmne" d:title="nunn-fǣmne">
		<body>
			<h1>nunn-fǣmne<span class="pron"> | nunn.fæːm.ne |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">a nun</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. sanctimonialis femina)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">sanctimonialis femina</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Seō hālige nunfǣmne</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Gr. D. 223, 14)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē nȳde genam āne nunfǣmnan and tō him gegaderode mid unālȳfedum synscipe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (230, 13)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="andigende" d:title="andigende">
		<body>
			<h1>andigende<span class="pron"> | ɑn.di.Gen.de |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>participle</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">envying</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:andian" class="xref-target">andian</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="GREĀDA" d:title="GREĀDA">
		<body>
			<h1>GREĀDA<span class="pron"> | græ͜ɑː.dɑ |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ȲFER" class="xref-target">ȲFER</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="spircing" d:title="spircing">
		<body>
			<h1>spircing<span class="pron"> | spir.King |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A sprinkling, dropping</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. aspergine)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Spyrcinge aspergine</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Germ. 398, 225)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:previous word" class="xref-target">previous word</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="on-siēn" d:title="on-siēn">
		<body>
			<h1>on-siēn<span class="pron"> | on.si͜yːn |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:an-sȳn" class="xref-target">an-sȳn</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="wiþer-cwedung" d:title="wiþer-cwedung">
		<body>
			<h1>wiþer-cwedung<span class="pron"> | wi.θer.kwe.dung |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Gainsaying</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">verba praecipitationis</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Word wyþercwedunga</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Spl. 51, 4)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="Waller-wente" d:title="Waller-wente">
		<body>
			<h1>Waller-wente<span class="pron"> | wɑl.ler.wen.te |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">The Celtic inhabitants of Cumbria</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Nime hē his māga .xii. and .xii. Wallerwente</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. N. P. L. 51; Th. ii. 298, 8)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:Wente" class="xref-target">Wente</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="firgen-gāt" d:title="firgen-gāt">
		<body>
			<h1>firgen-gāt<span class="pron"> | fir.Gen.gɑːt |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Firgengaet, firgingaett ibices</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Txts. 69, 1037)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Firgengǣt</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 49, 3)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Firgiugāta hibicum</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Txts. 112, 49)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Firgengātum ibices</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 46, 7)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="fōre-sittan" d:title="fōre-sittan">
		<body>
			<h1>fōre-sittan<span class="pron"> | foː.re.sit.tɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -sæt, pl: -sǣton</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: present participle sg: -sittende, past participle sg: -seten</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To sit before or in front, to preside</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. præsidere)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the Archbishop Theodore was presiding</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Wæs fōresittende se Arcebiscop Þeodōrus</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 4, 5; S. 571, 25)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">præsidente Theodōro</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Fōresittendum Theodōre</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (4, 17; S. 585, 24)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="fǣhþ" d:title="fǣhþ">
		<body>
			<h1>fǣhþ<span class="pron"> | fæːxθ |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:mān-f" class="xref-target">mān-f</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="CĪÞ" d:title="CĪÞ">
		
		<body>
			<h1>CĪÞ<span class="pron"> | Kiːθ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">a young shoot of a herb or tree, a CHIT, sprout, germ, sprig, mote</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. germen, festuca)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">quasi stillæ super graminum germina</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Swā dropan ofer gærsa cīþas</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Deut. 32, 2)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">why should every seed turn to germs and roots?</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Forhwī ǣlc sǣd to cīþum and wyrtrumum weorþe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 34, 10; Fox 148, 32)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the germ formed on all cedar trees</span>
							<span class="q-oe">On eallum cedrum cīþ alǣded [MS. cuþ, ciiþ = cīþ alædeð]</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 148, 9)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">every shoot of the earth</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Eall eorþan cīþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (103, 12)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the snow covers the germ of herbs</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Se snāw bewrīhþ wyrta cīþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Salm. Kmbl. 605; Sal. 302)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the earth makes known by her plants, that the time is the beginning of the year</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Seō eorþe cȳþ mid hire cīþum, ðæt se tīma is geāres anginn</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. i. 100, 16)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">frost shall lock up the germs of the earth</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Forst sceal lūcan eorþan cīþas</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 90a; Th. 338, 7; Gn. Ex. 75)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">take three sprouts of plantain</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Genim wegbrǣdan þrȳ cȳþas</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Herb. 2, 14; Lchdm. i. 84, 14)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">thou canst see a little mote in thy brother's eye</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðū meaht gesiōn lytelne cīþ on ðīnes brōður eāgan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 33, 6; Cot. MS. 42b, 32)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the small mote</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Se smala cīþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (33, 6; Hat. MS. 43a, 2, 3)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">try if thou canst remove the mote from thy brother's eye</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Cunna hwæðer ðū mǣge adōn ðone cīþ of ðīnes brōður eāgan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (33, 6; Hat. MS. 43a, 6)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">seed</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. crementum)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Cȳþ crementum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Glos. Brux. Recd. 38, 7; Wrt. Voc. 64, 16)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Cīþ, vel weres sǣd crementum, vel hominis semen vel crementum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. Gl. 74; Som. 71, 73; Wrt. Voc. 44, 55)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:gærs-cīþ" class="xref-target">gærs-cīþ</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="eft-cerran" d:title="eft-cerran">
		<body>
			<h1>eft-cerran<span class="pron"> | eft.Ker.rɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To return</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. redīre)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">reversi sunt</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Eftcerdon</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lk. Skt. Lind. 10, 17)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="scrȳdan" d:title="scrȳdan">
		<body>
			<h1>scrȳdan<span class="pron"> | ʃryː.dɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -de</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to put clothes on a person, to clothe a person with (mid) a garment, to dress</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">induo</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic mē scrȳde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. Gr. 28, 2 ; Zup. 167, 2)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">induebar cilicio</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic [mē] scrȳdde mid hǣran</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Spl. 34, 15)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">vestibus valde bonis induit eum</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Heō scrȳdde Iacob mid ðam deōrwurðustan reāfe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Gen. 27, 15)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">Joseph totonderunt, ac veste mutata ob'ulerunt et</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hine man efosode and scrȳdde hine and brohte hine tō ðam cynge</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (41, 14)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē scrīdde (vestivit) ðone bisceop mid līnenum reāfe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lev. 8, 7)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic wæs nacud and gē mē scrȳddon (operuistis)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. Kmbl. 25, 36, 38)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Mōdor, scrȳd (vesti) ðīnne sunu</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Æltc. Gr. 18; Zup. 111, 3)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ne scrīde nān wīf hig mid wǣpmannes reāfe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Deut. 22, 5)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to clothe, to furnish with clothes, provide with clothes</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē scrȳt mē wel and fēlt</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Coll. Monast. Th. 22, 33)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gif æcyres weōd God scrȳt</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. Kmbl. 6, 30)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Scrȳtt</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lk. Skt. 12, 28)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē nī fēdan scolde and scrȳdan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 1012 ; Erl. 147, 11)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hingrigendumger. dum mele syllan and nacode scrȳdan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Blickl. Homl. 213, 18)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">III.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to put on a garment</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">decorem induisti</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Wlite ðū scrȳddest</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Spl. 103, 2)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">to put on a linen garment betokens some sickness</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Linen reāf scrēdan sume seōcnysse ge'ācnaþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lchdm. iii. 206. 30)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">IV.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to rig a ship</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Is ðeōs bāt fulscrīd</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ardr. Kmbl. 992 ; An. 496)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge-scrȳdan" class="xref-target">ge-scrȳdan</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:mis-scrȳdan" class="xref-target">mis-scrȳdan</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:un-scrȳdan" class="xref-target">un-scrȳdan</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:ymb-scrȳdan" class="xref-target">ymb-scrȳdan</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:wan-scrȳd" class="xref-target">wan-scrȳd</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ā-spyrian" d:title="ā-spyrian">
		<body>
			<h1>ā-spyrian<span class="pron"> | ɑː.spy.ri.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to track, reach by following the track</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hwā āspyreð ðæt deōfol of geofones holte and hine gebringeð on Crīstes cempena fæðmum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Sal. K. 146, 27)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to investigate, examine so as to get knowledge of a subject</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Se sceāwre þe þis gewrit āspyrað</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Angl. viii. 331)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Swȳðe nearwelīce hē hit lētt ūt āspyrian (of the compilation of Doomsday Book)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 1085; P. 216, 26)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ne magon ðǣre tungan mægnes swīðmōdnisse āspyrian</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Sal. K. 150, 4)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">that there was no man could settle by his investigations the doubt about the two (subst. this for trans, in Dict.)</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt nǣre nǣnig manna ðæt mihte ðǣra twēgra tweōn āspyrian</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Sal. 434)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">ob indaganda</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Tō āspyrienne</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 77, 64)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Fore tō āspyrianne</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (62, 55)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hyt ys tō āspyrianne hwæt hyt getācnað</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Angl. viii. 336, 46: 333, 8)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">indagantes</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Āspyrigende</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 44, 10)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">III.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to find out</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Iulius se cāsere þisne bissextum gemētte oððe āspirode</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Angl. viii. 306, 40)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="sceoldon" d:title="sceoldon">
		<body>
			<h1>sceoldon<span class="pron"> | ʃe͜ol.don |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">he bade throw, but he did not decide on which side they were to throw the net</span>
							<span class="q-oe">sceoldon he bade throw, but he did not decide on which side they were to throw the net</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. ii. 290, 9)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">III.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to bring a charge against a person</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Scīrde actionabatur</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 99, 11 : 3, 55)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">principes adversum me loquebantur</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ealdormenn swȳðe sprǣcon and wið me wrāðum wordum scīrdan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 118, 23)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Nes nan mon þat durste word sciren.</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Laym. 16822)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">IV.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to get clear of obligation, trouble, etc., get exemption</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">no man shall be exempt from the obligation</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gif hwylc man ðone āndagan forgēmeleāsige, æt forman cyrre . iii. messan, æt ōðerum cyrre. v. , æt þriddan cyrre ne scīre his nān man (no man shall be exempt from the obligation), būtun hit siē for mettrumnesse oððe for hlāfordes neōde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Chart. Th. 614, 18)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">there was trouble to the people on both accounts, that they had to bear a very great evil, and that they durst not get rid of it</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæm folce wæs ǣgðres waa ge ðæt hiē ðæt mǣste yfel forberan sceoldon ge eāc ðæt hiē his scīran ne dorstan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 3, 7 ; Swt. 114, 32)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="fōre-" d:title="fōre-">
		<body>
			<h1>fōre-<span class="pron"> | foː.re |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adverb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">before, used in composition as the English fore-</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="slege" d:title="slege">
		<body>
			<h1>slege<span class="pron"> | sle.Ge |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>neuter noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">the handle of an axe (?)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Heora ān his exe ūp ābrǣd, wolde hine sleān, ac him forwyrnde sum ōþer, swā ꝥ hē ꝥ hylfe gelǣhte and wiðhæfde ꝥ slege (held back the pole of the axe) þone slege the stroke, might have been expected)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. S. 31, 154)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="sār-bōt" d:title="sār-bōt">
		<body>
			<h1>sār-bōt<span class="pron"> | sɑːr.boːt |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Condensation paid for inflicting a wound</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ǣ" d:title="ǣ">
		<body>
			<h1>ǣ<span class="pron"> | æː |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">legis tuae</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Ǣs þīnre</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Rdr. 58, 12: 9, 21)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:heāfod-" class="xref-target">heāfod-</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:synder-ǣ" class="xref-target">synder-ǣ</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="hēdd-ern" d:title="hēdd-ern">
		
		<body>
			<h1>hēdd-ern<span class="pron"> | xeːdd.ern |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">a store-room</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Būton hit under þæs wīfes cǣglocan gebrōht wǣre . . . ac þǣra cǣgean heō sceal weardian ; þæt is hire hēddernes cǣge and hyre cyste cǣge and hire tǣgan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ll. Th. i. 418, 21 note)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">On kycenan oþþe on hēderne (cellario) oðþe on mynstres bæcerne</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (R. Ben. 71, 17 ; R. Ben. I. 82, 2)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hwā gefylþ cleafan</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="eahta-teōða" d:title="eahta-teōða">
		<body>
			<h1>eahta-teōða<span class="pron"> | æ͜ɑx.tɑ.te͜oː.θɑ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">octavus decimus</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Se eahtateōða</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. Gr. Z. 283, 5)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">On þone eahtategþan dæg</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Shrn. 71, 5: 92, 7)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Eahtateogðan</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (85, 23)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Eahtategeþan</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (105, 22)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="wæl-pīl" d:title="wæl-pīl">
		<body>
			<h1>wæl-pīl<span class="pron"> | wæl.piːl |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A deadly dart, death-pang</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Wæs his mondryhtne endedōgor, ... āwrecen wælpīlum wlō ne meahte oroð up geteōn</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. Th. 171, 15; Gū. 1127)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="þanne" d:title="þanne">
		<body>
			<h1>þanne<span class="pron"> | θɑn.ne |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:þonne" class="xref-target">þonne</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="forþ-hreōsan" d:title="forþ-hreōsan">
		<body>
			<h1>forþ-hreōsan<span class="pron"> | forθ.xre͜oː.sɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">present: 3sg: -he -hryst</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -hreas, pl: -hruron</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -hroren</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To rush forth</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. proruĕre)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Forþhrȳst proruit</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Scint. 26)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="æl-fæle" d:title="æl-fæle">
		<body>
			<h1>æl-fæle<span class="pron"> | æl.fæ.le |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">All-fell, very baleful</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. omnino perniciosus)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">very baleful poison</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Āttor ælfæle</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Andr. Kmbl. 1539; An. 771)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:eal-felo" class="xref-target">eal-felo</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="Creācisc" d:title="Creācisc">
		<body>
			<h1>Creācisc<span class="pron"> | kræ͜ɑː.Kiʃ |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:Crēcisc" class="xref-target">Crēcisc</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="heāh-sceāwere" d:title="heāh-sceāwere">
		<body>
			<h1>heāh-sceāwere<span class="pron"> | xæ͜ɑːx.ʃæ͜ɑː.we.re |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A chief overlooker, overseer</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. pontifex)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">pontifex</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hēhsceāware</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Rtl. 21, 1)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="mānful-ness" d:title="mānful-ness">
		<body>
			<h1>mānful-ness<span class="pron"> | mɑːn.ful.ness |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Wickedness</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Git Martianus for his mānfulnysse nolde on God gelȳfan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Skt. 4, 389)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē leornode ǣfre māran and māran on his mānfulnysse and ne lēt nānne his gelīcan on yfele</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. T. Grn. 17, 28)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="hīrsum-ness" d:title="hīrsum-ness">
		
		
		
		<body>
			<h1>hīrsum-ness<span class="pron"> | xiːr.sum.ness |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">obedience</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">he refused to allow Jesus to humble himself by the washing of feet, and yet in order that he might be obedient he consented</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē (Peter) eādmōdnysse wiðsōc, and hwæðere for hȳrsumnysse geðafode</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. A. 157, 135)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">I a.</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">obedience to one in authority</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Be hȳrsumnesse. Ðǣre forman eādmōdnesse stepe is hȳrsumnes būtan elcunge ... sōna swā heom ǣnig þing fram heora ealdre geboden bið, hī þæt būtan elcunge mid weorce gefremmað</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (R. Ben. 19, 14-19: 12, 12)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Se a&amp;r-tilde;ƀ āxode hȳrsumnesse mid āþswerunge at him, and hē hit forsōc</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 1070; P. 206, 21)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">I b.</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">subjection of one people to another</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hē hiē (the Welsh) tō eāþmōdre hērsumnesse gedyde</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 828; P. 62, 3)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Þā elreordegan kyningas ðe ic mid nēde tō hȳrsumnesse gedyde</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Nar. 32, 19)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">readiness to obey or serve, humility</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. humilitatis exemplo monstrato)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">humilitatis exemplo monstrato</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hērsumnisse mið bisene ædeāwed (cf. siē hē īwer hēra ł embehtmonna (minister), Mk. L. 10, 43)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Mk. p. 4, 15)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">III.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">service, appointed work</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Sȳ heom swylc hȳrsumnes betǣht swylc him sȳ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (R. Ben. 67, 6)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Þurh þā gemǣnan þēnunge þysse hȳrsumnesse (the work of the kitchen which all took in turn)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (58, 16)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">On þǣre hȳrsumnesse þe hē on hȳrsumode, āþer oðþe on kycenan, oþþe on hēderne, oðþe on mynstres bæcerne ... oðþe on ǣnigum ōðerum cræfte þe hē mid līchomlicum geswince on hȳrsumode</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (71, 16)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Faran tō swylcan weorce and hȳrsumnesse swylce him beboden sȳ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (85, 15)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">obsequiis</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē gefealh his þegnungum and hȳrsumnessum (obsequiis)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Gr. D. 299, 29)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:un-hȳrsumness" class="xref-target">un-hȳrsumness</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="hlyt" d:title="hlyt">
		<body>
			<h1>hlyt<span class="pron"> | xlyt |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:hlīt" class="xref-target">hlīt</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-endung" d:title="ge-endung">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-endung<span class="pron"> | je.en.dung |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">local</span>
					</p>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(1)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">an extreme part</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-en">the sun goes below the horizon</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Seō sunne undergǣd þǣre eorðan geendunge</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Lch. iii. 260, 7)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(2)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">a termination of a word</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Seō forme declinatio hæfð tres terminationes, þæt synd ðreō geendunga</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. Gr. Z. 24, 4: 26, 12)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(3)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">a concluding passage</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Seō geendung ūs sǣde ꝥ þā Iudēiscan þōhton ꝥ hī Crīst ofslōgon</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. A. 71, 161)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">temporal, a final period</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">in quos fines saeculorum devenerunt</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Wē sind ðā ðe worulda geendunga on becōmon</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. Th. ii. 372, 10)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">III.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">cessation, termination</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ꝥ æþele līf būton geendunge</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bl. H. 65, 18)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Geseah hē geneālǣcan his līfes geendunge</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. S. 26, 156)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">III a.</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">ending of life, death</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hē ābād þæs ōðres geendunge</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. Th. ii. 152, 18)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-en">in the eleventh year since his death</span>
									<span class="q-oe">On ðām endlyftan geāre his geendunge</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (31)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Se sunu sceolde fōn to þām hāde æfter his fæder geendunge</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. S. 10, 221: 18, 435)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Æfter ūre geendunge</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (28, 152: Shrn. 97, 30)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Þæt hī on eōwrum geendungum (cum defeceritis) onfōn eōw intō ēcum eardungstōwum</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. Th. i. 334, 28)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">III b.</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">ending of existence, end of the world</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Þās ðing sceolon ǣrest cuman, ac ne bið swā ðeāh þǣrrihte seō geendung (finis)</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. Th. ii. 538, 3)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">On ðissere worulde geendunge</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (300, 9: Hml. A. 165, 23: 23, 221)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ūres Drihtnes apostolas āhsadan hine sylfne ymbe þisre worulde geendunge</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Wlfst. 81, 2)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Oþ þā geendunga þisse worlde</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Bl. H. 157, 30)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="myrþ" d:title="myrþ">
		<body>
			<h1>myrþ<span class="pron"> | myrθ |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:mirigþ" class="xref-target">mirigþ</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="eāst-sūþ" d:title="eāst-sūþ">
		<body>
			<h1>eāst-sūþ<span class="pron"> | æ͜ɑːst.suːθ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adverb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">South-east</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. ad euronothum)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">ad euronothum</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Eāstsūth</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 98, 2l)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Eāstsūð</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (4, 19)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Be-eāstan him is Wineda lond . . . and eāst-sūþ Maroara</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 1, 1; S. 16, 10)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="samod-gesīþ" d:title="samod-gesīþ">
		<body>
			<h1>samod-gesīþ<span class="pron"> | sɑ.mod.Ge.siːθ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A companion, comrade</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. coheres)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Samodgesīþ coheres</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Germ. 400, 575)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="nīwe" d:title="nīwe">
		
		<body>
			<h1>nīwe<span class="pron"> | niː.we |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adverb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Newly, recently</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">we are newly turned to this faith</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Wē nīwe syndon tō ðissum geleāfan gedōn</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Blickl. Homl. 247, 34)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">after it (a cow) has recently calved</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Syððan heō nīge cealfod hæfþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. R. S. 13; Th. i. 438, 19)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">or let him drink goat's milk as newly milked as possible</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Sceal mon lācnian swilce ādle mid cū meolcum oððe gāte swā nīge molcene drince</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lchdm. ii. 218, 22 : 222, 13)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:nīwan" class="xref-target">nīwan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="gild" d:title="gild">
		<body>
			<h1>gild<span class="pron"> | Gild |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">payment</span>
					</p>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(1)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">of purchase or barter</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">quam dabit homo commutationem pro anima sua?</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Hwælc seleþ monn geld for ferh his</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. R. 16, 26)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(2)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">pay of troops</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Eādwerd cing scylode .ix. scypa of māle . . . and belifon .v. scypa bæftan; and se cing heom behēt .xii. mōnað gyld</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 1049; P. 171, 29)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(3)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">with idea of compulsion, payment exacted</span>
							</p>
							<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
								<li>
									<p>
										<span class="sense-label">(a)</span>
										<span class="meaning-en">by the State, a tax</span>
									</p>
									<ul class="quotes">
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Ālēde Eādweard cyng ꝥ heregyld . . . ꝥ gyld gedrehte ealle Engla þeōde . . . ꝥ wæs æfre ætforan ōðrum gyldum þe man geald</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 1052; P. 173, 18-22)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Þe cyng behēt heom þā betsta laga . . . and ælc unriht geold hē forbeād</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (1087; P. 223, 32)</span>
										</li>
									</ul>
								</li>
								<li>
									<p>
										<span class="sense-label">(b)</span>
										<span class="meaning-en">by the law as compensation or indemnity for loss</span>
									</p>
									<ul class="quotes">
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Norðleōda cynges gild is .xxx. þūsend þrymsa, fīftene þūsend þrymsa bið þæs wergildes, .xv. þūsend þæs cynedōmes</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Ll. Th. i. 186, 2)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Ðeāh æt stæltyhtlan lād teorie . . . gylde āngyldes ꝥ hē mid belēd wæs. Ðæs ōðres gyldes nān þing, ne þæs wītes þe mā</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (354, 16)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Gif mon wīf mid bearne ofsleā . . . forgielde þone wīfman fullan gielde, and ꝥ bearn healfan gelde</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (66, 24-68, 2)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Ne forlæte hē þā æscan . . . oþ þæt wē tō þām gilde cuman</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (234, 27)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Gylde hē ꝥ yrfe, oþþe . . . underwed lecge . . . and þæs on .ix. nihton ꝥ wed undō mid rihtan gylde</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (352, 10)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">ꝥ man gulde ꝥ ceāpgild, and swinge hine man þriwa, oþþe ꝥ ōðer gild (gylde, v. l.) sealde</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (208, 23)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Gif wē þonne gyld ārǣrdon</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (234, 5)</span>
										</li>
									</ul>
								</li>
								<li>
									<p>
										<span class="sense-label">(c)</span>
										<span class="meaning-en">by a superior foreign power, tribute</span>
									</p>
									<ul class="quotes">
										<li>
											<span class="q-la">temtantes de reddendo caesaris tribute</span>
											<span class="q-oe">Cunnende of gyld (cf. gild-selen) [ð]æs cæseres geselenne</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Mk. p. 4, 20)</span>
										</li>
									</ul>
								</li>
							</ol>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">that which takes the place of something lost</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Seth wæs Abeles gield on woruldrīce</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Gen. 1109)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">On wrāðra gield</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (101)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">III.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">in a religious sense</span>
					</p>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(1)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">what is offered</span>
							</p>
							<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
								<li>
									<p>
										<span class="sense-label">(1)(a)</span>
										<span class="meaning-en">concrete, an offering, a sacrifice</span>
									</p>
									<ul class="quotes">
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Hiē Drihtne lāc brōhton; brego engla beseah on Abeles gield eāgum sīnum</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Gen. 977)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Hē þæt gyld (cf. lāc, 1497) on þanc āgifen hæfde</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (1506)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-la">hostiae, sacrificia</span>
											<span class="q-oe">Geld</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Wülck. Gl. 202, 27)</span>
										</li>
									</ul>
								</li>
								<li>
									<p>
										<span class="sense-label">(1)(b)</span>
										<span class="meaning-en">abstract, worship, rite, service, sacrifice</span>
									</p>
									<ul class="quotes">
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Æt ðām gilde Luperc[a]lia</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 86, 27)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-la">cultum</span>
											<span class="q-oe">Gield</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (90, 27)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Gild</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (19, 24)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-la">ceremoniae</span>
											<span class="q-oe">Geld</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (UNCERTAIN. 28, 54)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-la">ceremonie, i. ritus sacrificandi, religiones, sacrificia</span>
											<span class="q-oe">Geld</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Wülck. Gl. 202, 27)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Þā þe æt þǣm geldum þǣr wæs swīn and sceāp and fear</span>
										</li>
									</ul>
								</li>
							</ol>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="weorold-gewritu" d:title="weorold-gewritu">
		
		<body>
			<h1>weorold-gewritu<span class="pron"> | we͜o.rold.Ge.wri.tu |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>neuter noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Profane literature</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. saeculari literatura instructus)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">saeculari literatura instructus</span>
							<span class="q-oe">On weoruldgewritum gelǣred</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 4, 1; S. 564, 11)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðā lǣrde se hyne godcunde gewritu ; ðā forlēt hē ða woruldgewrytu</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Shrn. 152, 20)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ǣr-nemned" d:title="ǣr-nemned">
		<body>
			<h1>ǣr-nemned<span class="pron"> | æːr.nem.ned |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Before-named</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Se ǣrnæmda cyning</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ll. Th. i. 36, 8)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="cilfer-lamb" d:title="cilfer-lamb">
		
		<body>
			<h1>cilfer-lamb<span class="pron"> | Kil.fer.lɑmb |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>neuter noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A female lamb</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. agna femina)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">offerat agnam</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Bringe ān cilforlamb</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lev. 5, 6)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="wed-bryce" d:title="wed-bryce">
		<body>
			<h1>wed-bryce<span class="pron"> | wed.bry.Ke |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Breach of a pledge or engagement</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gif hē ðæs weddie, ðe hym riht sȳ tō gelǣstanne, and ðæt āleōge . . . bēte ðone wedbryce swā him his scrift scrīfe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. Alf. pol. 1; Th. i. 60, 6-21)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Eāc syndan wide þurh āðbrycas and ðurh wedbrycas and ðurh mistlīce leāsunga forloren and forlogen mā ðonne scolde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wulfst. 164, 7)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Wed‒bricas</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (130, 6)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="-sprecan" d:title="-sprecan">
		
		<body>
			<h1>-sprecan<span class="pron"> | spre.kɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:sprecan" class="xref-target">sprecan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="gum-rinc" d:title="gum-rinc">
		<body>
			<h1>gum-rinc<span class="pron"> | gum.rink |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A man</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">a goodly man</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gōdlīc gumrinc a goodly man</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 129a; Th. 495, 7; Rä. 84, 4)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">a goddess of the foolish people, of men</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Dysiges folces gumrinca gyden a goddess of the foolish people, of men</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. Met. Fox 26, 105; Met. 26, 53: Cd. 75; Th. 93, 27; Gen. 1552)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="wreōn" d:title="wreōn">
		<body>
			<h1>wreōn<span class="pron"> | wre͜oːn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -wrāh, sg: -wreāh, pl: -wrigon, pl: -wrugon</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -wrigen, past participle sg: -wrogen</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To cover</span>
					</p>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">to put a covering on something</span>
							</p>
							<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
								<li>
									<p>
										<span class="sense-label">(1)</span>
										<span class="sub-heading">literal</span>
									</p>
									<ul class="quotes">
										<li>
											<span class="q-la">gut tegit aquis superiora ejus</span>
											<span class="q-oe">Se ðe wrīgð wæterum ða uferan his</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Spl. 103, 3)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Ōþer eāre hī him underbrēdaþ and mid ōðran hī wreōð (se cooperiunf)</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Nar. 37, 12)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Hē wreāh and þeahte mānfǣhðu bearn wonnan wǣge</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. Th. 83, 10; Gen. 1377)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Reste hē hiue sōfte, and wreō hine wearme: . . . lǣt drincan . . . , and wreōh hirie wearme</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Lchdm. ii. 292, 6-14)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-en">as you would cover the dead with earth</span>
											<span class="q-oe">Swā ðū worulddeāde wrige mid foldan</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 140, 4)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Ongunnun summe gehȳdæ ł wrīga (uelare) onsiōne his</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Mk. Skt. Lind. 14, 65)</span>
										</li>
									</ul>
									<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
										<li>
											<p>
												<span class="sense-label">(I a)</span>
												<span class="sub-heading">to cover with clothes, to clothe</span>
												<span class="meaning-en">to cover with clothes, to clothe</span>
											</p>
											<ul class="quotes">
												<li>
													<span class="q-oe">Ic wreō mē wǣda leāsne, leāfum þecce</span>
													<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. Th. 53, 26; Gen. 867)</span>
												</li>
												<li>
													<span class="q-la">eram nudus, et opertdstis me</span>
													<span class="q-oe">Ic wses nacod, and gē clǣððon ł wrigon (wriogan, Rush.) meh</span>
													<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. Kmbl. Lind. 25, 36)</span>
												</li>
												<li>
													<span class="q-oe">He ne nrihte hine handum self mid hrægle wryōn</span>
													<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. Th. 95, 2 ; Gen. 1572)</span>
												</li>
											</ul>
										</li>
										<li>
											<p>
												<span class="sense-label">(I b)</span>
												<span class="sub-heading">to cover a book, to bind a book</span>
												<span class="meaning-en">to cover a book, to bind a book</span>
											</p>
											<ul class="quotes">
												<li>
													<span class="q-oe">Mec (a book) wrāh hælet hleōbordum</span>
													<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. Th. 408, 13; Rä. 47, ll)</span>
												</li>
											</ul>
										</li>
									</ol>
								</li>
								<li>
									<p>
										<span class="sense-label">(2)</span>
										<span class="sub-heading">with the idea of concealment</span>
										<span class="meaning-en">to conceal, hide</span>
									</p>
									<ul class="quotes">
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">For hwon wāst ðū weān and wrīhst sceome</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. Th. 54, 13; Gen. 876)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Ða word ðe gē wrigon under womma scealum</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Elen. Kmbl. 1162 ; El. 582)</span>
										</li>
									</ul>
								</li>
								<li>
									<p>
										<span class="sense-label">(3)</span>
										<span class="sub-heading">with the idea of protection</span>
									</p>
									<ul class="quotes">
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Ic ðē wið weāna gehwam wreō and scylde folmum mīnum</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. Th. 131, 3; Gen. 2170)</span>
										</li>
									</ul>
								</li>
							</ol>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">to serve as a covering to something, be spread over</span>
							</p>
							<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
								<li>
									<p>
										<span class="sense-label">(1)</span>
										<span class="sub-heading">literal</span>
									</p>
									<ul class="quotes">
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Flōd ealle wreāh heā beorgas</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. Th. 83, 28; Gen. 1386)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Niht lagustreāmas wreāh</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (147, 34; Gen. 2449)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Mec (an oyster) ȳþa wrugon</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. Th. 488, 5 ; Rä, 76, 2)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Siō tilmen biþ þeccende and wreōnde ða wambe</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Lchdm. ii. 240, 17)</span>
										</li>
									</ul>
									<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
										<li>
											<p>
												<span class="sense-label">(l a)</span>
												<span class="sub-heading">of clothing</span>
											</p>
											<ul class="quotes">
												<li>
													<span class="q-la">vestem ad operiendam</span>
													<span class="q-oe">Woede tō wriānne</span>
													<span class="q-cite"> (Rtl. 103, 42)</span>
												</li>
												<li>
													<span class="q-la">quo operiemitr</span>
													<span class="q-oe">Of hwon wē bidon wrigen (gewrigene. Rush.)</span>
													<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. Kmbl. Lind. 6, 31)</span>
												</li>
											</ul>
										</li>
									</ol>
								</li>
								<li>
									<p>
										<span class="sense-label">(2)</span>
										<span class="sub-heading">with the idea of concealment</span>
									</p>
									<ul class="quotes">
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Ȳþa mec (a storm) wrugon</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. Th. 382, 23; Rä. 3, 15)</span>
										</li>
									</ul>
								</li>
								<li>
									<p>
										<span class="sense-label">(3)</span>
										<span class="sub-heading">with the idea of protection</span>
									</p>
									<ul class="quotes">
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Ic liæbbe mē on hrycge ðæt ǣr hādas wreāh foldbūendra</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. Th. 381, 17; Rä. 2, II)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Unc holt wrugon, wudubeāma helm, wonnum nihturn, scildon wið scūrurn</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (496, I; Rä. 85, 73)</span>
										</li>
									</ul>
								</li>
							</ol>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ā-wreōn" class="xref-target">ā-wreōn</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:be-wreōn" class="xref-target">be-wreōn</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge-wreōn" class="xref-target">ge-wreōn</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:in-wreōn" class="xref-target">in-wreōn</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:ofer-wreōn" class="xref-target">ofer-wreōn</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:on-wreōn" class="xref-target">on-wreōn</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:un-wreōn" class="xref-target">un-wreōn</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-þang" d:title="ge-þang">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-þang<span class="pron"> | je.θɑng |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">growth</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Fīfte wæs gyfe pund, þanon hym wæs geseald sefa and geðang (= geðanc thought)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (v. Mod. Lang. Rev. xi. 215)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="on-fundelness" d:title="on-fundelness">
		<body>
			<h1>on-fundelness<span class="pron"> | on.fun.del.ness |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Experience, proof</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">many authorities testify to the efficacy of this plant from experience</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðysse wyrte onfundelnysse manega ealdras gesēðaþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lchdm. i. 140, 9)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">it will give proof of the same thing, the second method will prove as efficacious as the first</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hyt dēþ onfundelnysse ðæs sylfan þinges</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (162, 1)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="-rǣpe" d:title="-rǣpe">
		<body>
			<h1>-rǣpe<span class="pron"> | ræː.pe |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:æfter-rǣpe" class="xref-target">æfter-rǣpe</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="freōlsian" d:title="freōlsian">
		<body>
			<h1>freōlsian<span class="pron"> | fre͜oːl.si.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -ode</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -od</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To keep holy day, to celebrate</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. celebrāre diem festum)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the witan have chosen, that St. Edward's mass-day should be celebrated over all England</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Sce. Eādweardes mæssedæg witan habbaþ gecoren, ðæt man freōlsian sceal ofer eal Engla land</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. Eth. v. 16; Th. i. 308, 21: L. C. E. 17; Th. i. 370, 7)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">sex diēbus oprāberis, die septimo cessābis</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Wirc six dagas and freōlsa ðone seofoðan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ex. 34. 21)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">sabbătīzes sabbătum Domino</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Freōlsiaþ Drihtnes restedæg</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lev. 25, 2)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">be thou mindful that thou keep holy the day of rest</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Beō ðū gemyndig ðæt ðū ðone restendæg freōlsige</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. ii. 198, 4: E. Eth. v. 14; Th. i. 308, 15)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge-freōlsian" class="xref-target">ge-freōlsian</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="GȲME" d:title="GȲME">
		<body>
			<h1>GȲME<span class="pron"> | Gyː.me |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Care, heed, attention</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="frig" d:title="frig">
		
		<body>
			<h1>frig<span class="pron"> | friG |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">l. frīg</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="BELG" d:title="BELG">
		
		
		
		<body>
			<h1>BELG<span class="pron"> | belɣ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A BULGE, budget, bag, purse, bellows, pod, husk, BELLY</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. bulga, follis, siliqua, uter)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Bylg bulga</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cot. 27)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Bylig follis</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. Gl. 27; Wrt. Voc. 86, 15)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Bilig uter</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Spl. M. 118, 83)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge-belg" class="xref-target">ge-belg</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="rǣran" d:title="rǣran">
		<body>
			<h1>rǣran<span class="pron"> | ræː.rɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -de</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To cause to rise, to rear, raise</span>
					</p>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">to lift up, move from a lower to a higher position</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hē ūs tō roderum up hlǣdre rǣrde</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. Th. 437, 11; Rä. 56, 6)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hī tō heofenum up hlǣdræ rǣrdon</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. Th. 101, 1; Gen. 1675)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hiē tō gūþe gārwudu rǣrdon</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (198, 20; Exod. 325)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Rǣre up ðīn heāfod and geseoh ðis ðæt Simon dēþ</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Blickl. Homl. 187, 35)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">to raise (a building)</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">domum aedifices</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Ðū rǣrst hūs</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Deut. 28, 30)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hī wībed setton neāh ðam ðe Abraham ǣror rǣrde</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. Th. 113, 7; Gen. 1883)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ðæt beācen (the tower of Babel) ðe rǣran ongunnon Adames eaforan</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (101, 13; Gen. 1681)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ongunnon him bytlian and heora burh rǣran</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (113, 1; Gen. 1880)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">III.</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">to set up, establish (a law, institution, etc.)</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">God sibbe rǣreþ ēce tō ealdre engla and monna</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. Th. 43, 16; Cri. 689)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">ecclesiam Christi in regno suo multum diligenter aedificare ac dilatare curavit</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Hē Cristes cyricean on his rīce geornlīce timbrede and rǣrde</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 3, 3; S. 525, 37)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Man unriht rǣrde and unlaga manege</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Wulfst. 156, 13)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ðonne rǣre man cyninges munde, ðæt is ðæt hȳ ealle ðam sēmende syllan ðæt cyninges mund stande</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (L. E. G. 13; Th. i. 174, 20)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Se ðe unlage rǣre oððe undōm gedēme</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (L. C. S. 15; Th. i. 384, 9)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">opera manuum ejus judicium</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Ys his handgeweorc ryhte dōmas ða hē rǣran wyle</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 110, 5)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">IV.</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">to raise, offer (a prayer)</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hyra þeōdnes dōm ðæt hiē to ðam beācne (the golden image) gebedu rǣrde</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. Th. 227, 24; Dan. 191)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">V.</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">to raise, begin, give rise to, excite (ill feeling)</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">exagitabat</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Rǣrde</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 30, 22)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-en">oft were their violence and enmity roused</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Oft hī þræce rǣrdon ... feōndscype rǣrdon</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. Th. 243, 18-22; Jul. 12-14)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hāteþ þræce rǣran ... ðæt hī ūsic binden and in bælwylme swingen</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (262, 16; Jul. 333)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Fǣhþe rǣran</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (113, 14; Gū. 157)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ne cūðon firena fremman ... elles ne ongunnon rǣran on roderum nymþe riht and sōð</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. Th. 2, 18; Gen. 21)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Geflitu rǣran</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Elen. Kmbl. 884; El. 443)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Sæce rǣran</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (1879; El. 941)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">VI.</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">to rouse, excite</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Saga hwā mec rǣre ðonne ic restan ne mōt, oððe hwā mec stæððe ðonne ic stille beom</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. Th. 387, 2; Rä. 4, 73)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">VII.</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">to raise, elevate, exalt, promote</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Gif ðū sōðne God lufast and his lof rǣrest</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. Th. 245, 22; Jul. 48 : 103, 17; Cri. 1681 : 111, 23; Gū. 131)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Se ǣrest æðelinga ēðelþrym rȳmde and rǣrde</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. Th. 98, 24; Gen. 1635)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Uton beōn ā ūrum hlāforde holde, and ǣfre eallum mihtum his wurðscipe rǣran</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (L. C. E. 20; Th. i. 372, 9 : Wulfst. 119, 14)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">quam prope esset hora qua fratres ad dicendas Domino laudes nocturnal excitari deberent</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Hū neāh ðære tīde wǣre ðætte ða brōðru ārīsan sceolden and Godes lof rǣran and heora ūhtsang singan</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 4. 24; S. 599, 4)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ā-rǣran" class="xref-target">ā-rǣran</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="lang-sceaft" d:title="lang-sceaft">
		<body>
			<h1>lang-sceaft<span class="pron"> | lɑng.ʃæ͜ɑft |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Having a long shaft</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">longas habebamus hastas</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Mid longsceaftum sperum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Nar. 13, 24)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">venabulis</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Mid longsceaftum sperum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (15, 28)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ēgor-streām" d:title="ēgor-streām">
		
		<body>
			<h1>ēgor-streām<span class="pron"> | eː.ɣor.stræ͜ɑːm |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A water-stream, water, the sea</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. unda, flŭvius, măre)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">this earth and sea can by no means extinguish that which in them remains</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðiōs eorþe mæg and ēgorstreām cræfta nāne adwæscan ðæt ðæt him on innan sticaþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. Met. Fox 20, 236; Met. 20, 118)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the water-streams sounded</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ēgorstreāmas swōgan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. 69 ; Th. 83, 4; Gen. 1374)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="firra" d:title="firra">
		<body>
			<h1>firra<span class="pron"> | fir.rɑ |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:feor" class="xref-target">feor</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="HEGE" d:title="HEGE">
		<body>
			<h1>HEGE<span class="pron"> | xe.Ge |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A HEDGE, fence</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. sepes)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hege sepes</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. 84, 56: Ælfc. Gr. 9, 27; Som. 11, 24)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">Bamborough was first enclosed with a hedge and afterwards with a wall</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Bebbanburh wæs ǣrost mid hegge betīned and ðǣræfter mid wealle</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 547; Erl. 17, 9)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">exi in vias et sepes</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gā geond ðās wegas and hegas</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lk. Skt. 14, 23)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">destruxisti omnes sepes ejus</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðū tōwurpe ealle hegas his</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Spl. 88, 39)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">if there be any beast that breaks hedges</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gif hryðera hwelc sīe ðe hegas brece</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. In. 42; Th. i. 128, 12)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">cum septis quibus erant circumdata</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Mid heora hegum ðe hī ymbsette wǣron</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 2, 13; S. 516, 39: Homl. Th. ii. 448, 22)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">a silvis</span>
							<span class="q-oe">From hegum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Rtl. 118, 35)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:hæg-" class="xref-target">hæg-</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:haga" class="xref-target">haga</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ymbren-fæsten" d:title="ymbren-fæsten">
		<body>
			<h1>ymbren-fæsten<span class="pron"> | ym.bren.fæ.sten |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>neuter noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">The fast of the Ember-days</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt man ǣlc beboden fæsten healde, sī hit ymbrenfæsten, sī hit lengctenfæsten</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. C. E. 16; Th. i. 368, 22)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt ymbrenfæsten byð on ðissum mōnþe (December)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Anglia viii. 311, 39)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">On ðam lenctenfæstene and on ǣlcum ymbrenfæstene</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. ii. 608, 17)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Feōwer ymbrenfæstenu beōð on twelf mōnðum, eallswā feōwer tīman beōð</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Anglia viii. 312, 14)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ymbrenfæstena healde man rihte, swā swā Scs. Gregorius Angelcynne sylf hit gedihte</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wulfst. 272, 16: L. Eth. vi. 23; Th. i. 320, 20)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="hālig-wæcca" d:title="hālig-wæcca">
		<body>
			<h1>hālig-wæcca<span class="pron"> | xɑː.liG.wæk.kɑ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -an</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">One who observes vigils</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">ut humiles simus et eleemosynis largi et sanctarum vigiliarum studiosi</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Beōn eāðmōde and ælmysfulle and hāligwæccan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. Ecg. P. 4, 64; Th. ii. 224, 27)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-hirdness" d:title="ge-hirdness">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-hirdness<span class="pron"> | je.xird.ness |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Keeping guard, watchful care</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge-heordnes" class="xref-target">ge-heordnes</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge-hyrdnes" class="xref-target">ge-hyrdnes</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="twidæg-līc" d:title="twidæg-līc">
		<body>
			<h1>twidæg-līc<span class="pron"> | twi.dæG.liːtʃ |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:twādæg-līc" class="xref-target">twādæg-līc</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="medu-wyrt" d:title="medu-wyrt">
		<body>
			<h1>medu-wyrt<span class="pron"> | me.du.wyrt |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Meadow-sweet, also mead-sweet</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Meodowyrt mel-leuna</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 59, 43: L. M. 1, 38; Lchdm. ii. 94, 14)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Medowyrt</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lchdm. ii. 96, 17: 1, 44; Lchdm. ii. 108, 11)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Medewyrt malletina(?)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. i. 31, 1: Lchdm. iii. 6, 12: 16, 9)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Meodeuyrt mellauna, papamo</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (304, 1, 35)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="hwioð" d:title="hwioð">
		<body>
			<h1>hwioð<span class="pron"> | xwi͜oθ |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:hwið" class="xref-target">hwið</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="tō-helpan" d:title="tō-helpan">
		<body>
			<h1>tō-helpan<span class="pron"> | toː.xel.pɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">glosses adjuvare</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. adjuvare)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic gilēfo, tōhelpe (adiuua) ungileōffulnisse mīne</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Mk. R. 9, 24)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ā-brǣdan" d:title="ā-brǣdan">
		<body>
			<h1>ā-brǣdan<span class="pron"> | ɑː.bræː.dɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -de</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To fry</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ābrǣd cicel</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lch. ii. 114, 25)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="tō-wyrd" d:title="tō-wyrd">
		<body>
			<h1>tō-wyrd<span class="pron"> | toː.wyrd |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Occasion</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">quaerentes occasionem divortii</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðā wǣron Seaxan sēcende intingan and tōwyrde heora gedāles wiþ Brittas</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 1, 15 ; S. 483, 37)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="þȳfel" d:title="þȳfel">
		<body>
			<h1>þȳfel<span class="pron"> | θyː.fel |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Hī eōdon þā sēcende tō þām wuda, sēcende gehwǣr geond þȳfelas and brēmelas</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. S. 32, 143)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="wundel" d:title="wundel">
		
		<body>
			<h1>wundel<span class="pron"> | wun.del |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e, genitive sg: -an</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A wound (lit. or fig.), sore</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gif hwylc lǣwede man ōðerne wundige, gebēte wið hine ða wunde (wundlan, wundlāc, v.ll.)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. Ecg. P. iv. 22; Th. ii. 210, 25)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Wið nīwe wundela (wunda, v.1.)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lchdrn. i. 8, 14: 10, 9: 92, 21: 100, 1: 108, 19: 296, 6, 17)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">vulnera</span>
							<span class="q-oe">His sāule wundela (vulnera) gehǣlan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (R. Ben. 72, 7)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:wyndle" class="xref-target">wyndle</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="fore-þanc" d:title="fore-þanc">
		<body>
			<h1>fore-þanc<span class="pron"> | fo.re.θɑnk |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(1)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">consideration of the future</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Forþances gleāw</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Hpt. 33, 71, 1)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">sollerti prescientia</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Of embehȳdigum foreþance</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (An. Ox. 7, 355: 8, 344)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">cum iracundi nulla consideratione se mitigant</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Ðonne ðā hātheortan hiē mid nāne foreðonce nyllað gestillan</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 297, 3)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">intentionem providam non tenere</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Ðone foreðonc his gesceādwīsnesse forlǣtan</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (431, 36)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hē ne meahte mōd oncyrran, fǣmnan foreþonc</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Jul. 227)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hē næfð nǣnne forðanc be his deāðe</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 48, 8)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(2)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">what is thought beforehand, a preconceived idea</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">On þone foreþonc . . . þȳ þe hȳ (the apostate angels) him sylfum sēllan þūhton þonne Crīst</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Hy. 4, 53)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="an-mitta" d:title="an-mitta">
		<body>
			<h1>an-mitta<span class="pron"> | ɑn.mit.tɑ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A measure, bushel</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. mensura, modius)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">habete justam mensuram</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Habbaþ rihtne anmittan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lev. 19, 35)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">pondus habebis justum et verum, et modius æqualis et verus erit tibi</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hæbbe ǣlc man rihtne anmittan, and rihte wǣgan, and rihte gemetu on ǣlcum þingum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Deut. 25, 15)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:mitta" class="xref-target">mitta</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="heortian" d:title="heortian">
		<body>
			<h1>heortian<span class="pron"> | xe͜or.ti.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">to encourage</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. cohortante)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">cohortante</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Heortendum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hpt. Gl. 425, 23)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:hirtan" class="xref-target">hirtan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-þyncþ(u)" d:title="ge-þyncþ(u)">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-þyncþ(u)<span class="pron"> | je.θynkθ, u |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">thriving, prosperous condition</span>
					</p>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(1)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">in temporal matters, dignity, honour</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ne maeg se mann mōdigan on geðincðum (-ðinðum, v. l.) for ðan þe fela synd geþungenran</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. S. 16, 372)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ān woruldcynincg ne mæg been wurðful cynincg būton hē hæbbe þā geþincðe þe him gebyriað</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (p. 6, 61)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hē swanc for heofonan rīce swīþor þonne hē hogode hū hē geheōlde on worulde þā hwīlwendlican geþincðu (-ðincða, v. l.), þe hē hwōnlīce lufode</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (26, 113)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(2)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">in spiritual matters, virtue, excellence</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Þā clǣnheortan þeōnde beōð on hālgum geþingðum</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. A. 23, 223)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">For hyre micclum geðingðum</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (25, 31)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ne derode Iōbe nāht þæs deōfles costnung, ac fremode, for ðan ðe hē wæs fulfremedre on geþincðum and Gode neār æfter ðæs sceoccan ēhtnysse</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. Th. ii. 450, 2)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Þām hālgum mannum þe þurh miccle geðincða Gode geþungon</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (i. 540, 16)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">advanced position</span>
					</p>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(1)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">of persons, rank, status, degree</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">catacuminorum gradu, i. ordine</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Leāfhlestendra geþincþe</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (An. Ox. 2191)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">in alto tribunalis culmine</span>
									<span class="q-oe">On heālicere dēmendre geþinhþe</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (3456)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">apice (Pontificatus praeditus)</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Geþinþe</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (5078)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Þā unrihtwīsan dēman behealdaþ þā geðincþo ðæs mannes</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Ll. Lbmn. 476, 26)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">sub cujus aestimatione populus grex vocatur</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Ðæt hē ongitē for hwæs geðyncðum ðæt folc siē genemned heord</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 75, 7)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">sicut honore ordinis superat</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Swǣ swǣ hē on geðyncðum bið furðor ðonne ōðre</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (80, 23)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hit waes hwīlum ꝥ leōd and lagu fōr be geþincðum</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Ll. Th. i. 190, 12)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Swā man bið mihtigra for worulde, oþþon þurh geþingða heārra on hāde</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (328, 14)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">in examine recti judicis muta merita ordinum qualitas actionum</span>
									<span class="q-oe">On ðæm dōme ðæs ryhtwīsan Dēman onwent siō geearnung ðone hād and ðā geðyncðo</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 411, 25)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
							<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
								<li>
									<p>
										<span class="sense-label">(1 a)</span>
										<span class="meaning-en">of a thing personified</span>
									</p>
									<ul class="quotes">
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Þes dǣl (the participle) næfð nǣnne stede of him selfum, ac byð of worde ācenned, and becymð syþþan tō his āgenre geþingðe (-þincþe, v. l.)</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. Gr. Z. 244, 18)</span>
										</li>
									</ul>
								</li>
							</ol>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(2)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">of things, degree, grade</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">graduum</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Geþincþa</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (An. Ox. 1404)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(3)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">high degree of moral excellence</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">fastigio (edito Virginitatis fastigio sublimati, Ald. 13, 36)</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Hēhnysse, geþinþe</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (An. Ox. 930)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">proposito, i. gradu (in summo Virginitatis proposito, Ald. 14, 23)</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Geþinþe</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (968)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">si summe humilitatis volumus culmen adtingere</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Gif heālicere eādmōdnesse wē wyllāð geþincðe hreppan</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (R. Ben. I. 27, 13)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:leōd-geþincþu" class="xref-target">leōd-geþincþu</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:weorold-geþincþu" class="xref-target">weorold-geþincþu</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="egenwirht" d:title="egenwirht">
		<body>
			<h1>egenwirht<span class="pron"> | e.Gen.wirxt |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Hire, wages, a gift</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. merces)</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="āweg" d:title="āweg">
		<body>
			<h1>āweg<span class="pron"> | ɑː.weG |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adverb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">AWAY, out; (this is its meaning both in and out of composition)</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. auferendi vim habet)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">autem abiit</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðā ēode he aweg</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. Bos. 19, 22)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">ye strain the gnat out</span>
							<span class="q-la">excolantes [ex out, colare to filter, strain] culicem</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ge drehnigeaþ ðone gnæt aweg</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. Bos. 23, 24)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">he quickly drove them away</span>
							<span class="q-oe">He hī raðe aweg aþȳwde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 6, 36; Bos. 131, 28 : Ps. Th. 77, 57)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:on-weg" class="xref-target">on-weg</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="in-geōtan" d:title="in-geōtan">
		<body>
			<h1>in-geōtan<span class="pron"> | in.Ge͜oː.tɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">jubar Sancti Spiritus infunde nostris sensibus</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Liōma hālges gǣstes ingeōt ūrum gehygdum</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Srt. ii. p. 201, 3)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-edstaðolian" d:title="ge-edstaðolian">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-edstaðolian<span class="pron"> | je.ed.stɑ.θo.li.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge-edstaðelian" class="xref-target">ge-edstaðelian</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="helm" d:title="helm">
		<body>
			<h1>helm<span class="pron"> | xelm |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">III.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">a covering [in this sense the word is preserved in some dialects. Thus in Yorkshire and Lincolnshire Glossaries, English Dial. Soc. vols. ii. v. vi, helm, a hovel, an open shed for cattle, a shed built on posts]</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the covering made by the wave, the sea</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Wǣges helm [holm?]</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Elen. Kmbl. 459; El. 230)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">under the air's covering</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Under lyfte helm</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 102 a; Th. 386, 19; Rä. 4, 64)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">concealed with a covering</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Helme gedȳgled</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (1226; Th. 470, 10; Hy. 11, 33)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">IV.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">in poetry the word is applied to persons, thus God and Christ are spoken of as æþelinga, hæleþa, hāligra, duguþa, dryhtfolca, engla, grāsta, heofona, heofonrīces, wuldres helm and helm wera, ælwihta. Similar phrases occur in speaking of earthly rulers, æþelinga, heriga, lidmanna, wedra, weoruda helm and helm Scyldinga, Scylfinga.</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:bān-helm" class="xref-target">bān-helm</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:grīm-helm" class="xref-target">grīm-helm</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:gūþ-helm" class="xref-target">gūþ-helm</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:hæleþ-helm" class="xref-target">hæleþ-helm</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:heaþu-helm" class="xref-target">heaþu-helm</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:heoloþ-helm" class="xref-target">heoloþ-helm</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:lyft-helm" class="xref-target">lyft-helm</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:mist-helm" class="xref-target">mist-helm</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:niht-helm" class="xref-target">niht-helm</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:sceadu-helm" class="xref-target">sceadu-helm</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:sund-helm" class="xref-target">sund-helm</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:wæter-helm" class="xref-target">wæter-helm</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="efenwyrþe" d:title="efenwyrþe">
		
		<body>
			<h1>efenwyrþe<span class="pron"> | e.fen.wyr.θe |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">very worthy</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. condignus)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">gradum condignis ornans actibus</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē þone hād mid efenwyrþum (-weorðum, v. l.) dǣdum frætwade</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 3, 27; Sch. 331, 23)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">episcopalem cathedram condignis gradu actibus seruat</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē ꝥ bysceopsetl efenwyrðum (efenwyrðe, v. l.) dǣdum his hādes heōld</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (5, 12; Sch. 632, 3)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="myndgian" d:title="myndgian">
		<body>
			<h1>myndgian<span class="pron"> | mynd.Gi.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
					</p>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(1)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">to bring to the notice of a person</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">ut agnoscas in his fortuitis rebus beatitudinem constare non posse, sic collige</span>
									<span class="q-oe">For ðām ic ðē mindgige, ꝥ þū ongite ðætte nān gesǣlþ nis on þisse andweardan līfe</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 11, 2 ; F. 34, 14)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(2)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">to remind a person of something (gen.)</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">utilius apud illos proficimus, si et eorum bene gesta memoramus</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Wē magon beōn suā nyttran æt him, gif wē hiē myndgiað hira gōdna weorca</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 211, 21)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hiē beōð tō myndgianne þǣra gōda ðe hiē ǣr dydon</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 303, 8)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:mynegian" class="xref-target">mynegian</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="here-beorg" d:title="here-beorg">
		<body>
			<h1>here-beorg<span class="pron"> | xe.re.be͜orɣ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Harbour, shelter, lodgings, quarters</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Þā genam hē þǣr herebeorge</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Nap. 82)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ofer-bebeōdan" d:title="ofer-bebeōdan">
		<body>
			<h1>ofer-bebeōdan<span class="pron"> | o.fer.be.be͜oː.dɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">to command, rule</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. imperito)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">imperito</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic wealdige vel oferbebeōde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt.Voc. i. 54, 52)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ǣ-reāfe" d:title="ǣ-reāfe">
