	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ā-wacan" d:title="ā-wacan">
		<body>
			<h1>ā-wacan<span class="pron"> | ɑː.wɑ.kɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">to spring, arise</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Fram þan Wōdne eall ūre cynecynn āwōc</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 449; P. 13, 25: 547; P. 17, 20)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Odo þe þās þyng of āwōcan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (1087; P. 223, 25)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hū fela þeōda āwōcon of his iii. bearnum?</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Sal. K. 182, 24, 26)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:on-wacan" class="xref-target">on-wacan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="weorold-sceamu" d:title="weorold-sceamu">
		<body>
			<h1>weorold-sceamu<span class="pron"> | we͜o.rold.ʃæ͜ɑ.mu |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Worldly shame, disgrace among men</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Wāla ðære woruldscame, ðe nū habbaþ Engle. . . . Oft twēgen sǣmen oððe þrȳ drīfaþ ða drāfe cristenra manna fram sǣ tō sǣ. . . ūs eallum tō woruldscame</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wulfst. 163, 3-7)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ða ðe for ege oððe lufe oððe ǣnigre worldscame eargiaþ and wandiaþ Godes riht tō sprecanne</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (191, 5)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">For woruldsceame</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. I. P. 12 ; Th. ii. 320, 22)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gif wīf be ōðrum were forlicge, and hit open weorðe, geweorðe heō tō woruldsceame hire sylfre</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. C. S. 54; Th. i. 406, 7)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Tō woroldscame</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wulfst. 168, 14)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="heoloþ-helm" d:title="heoloþ-helm">
		<body>
			<h1>heoloþ-helm<span class="pron"> | xe͜o.loθ.xelm |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A helm which conceals or makes invisible the wearer</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:hæleþ-helm" class="xref-target">hæleþ-helm</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="feōnd" d:title="feōnd">
		
		
		<body>
			<h1>feōnd<span class="pron"> | fe͜oːnd |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es, nominative pl: -feōndas, nominative pl: -fȳnd, nominative pl: -feōnd, accusative pl: -feōndas, accusative pl: -fȳnd, accusative pl: -feōnd, genitive pl: -feōnda, dative pl: -feōndum</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A FIEND, enemy, foe, the devil</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. ōsor, inimīcus, hostis, diabolus = διάβολος)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">idleness is the soul's enemy</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Seō ydelnes is ðære sāwle feōnd</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. E. I. 3; Th. ii 404, 9)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">persequātur inimīcus animam meam</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ēhteþ feōnd sāwle mīne</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Spl. 7, 5)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the fiend decked his favourites with honours</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Se feōnd his diōrlingas duguþum stēpte</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. Met. Fox 15, 14; Met. 15, 7; Beo. Th. 1455; B. 725: 1500; B. 748)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">hostis vel ōsor</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Feōnd</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. 86, 45)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the devil with all his company fell from heaven</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Se feōnd mid his gefērum eallum feōllon of heofnum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. 16; Th. 20, 10; Gen. 306: Salm. Kmbl. 140; Sal. 69: 995; Sal. 499)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">non gaudebit inimīcus meus super me</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Nā fægnian fȳnd mīn ofer me</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Spl. 40, 12)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the stout of heart found the foe's foot-trace</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Stearcheort onfand feōndes fōtlāst</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Beo. Th. 4567; B. 2289)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">si occurrēris bovi inimīci tui aut asino erranti, reduc ad eum</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gif ðū gemēte ðīnes feōndes oxan oððe assan, lǣd hine to him</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ex. 23, 4: Lk. Bos. l0, 19)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">he escaped from the fiend</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Se ðæm feōnde ætwand</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Beo. Th. 289; B. 143: Bt. Met. Fox 25, 31; Met. 25, 16)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">thou shalt overcome thy foe</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðū feōnd oferswiððest</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Elen. Kmbl. 186; El. 93: Cd. 144; Th. 179, 21; Exod. 32)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">thou didst put the enemy [the devil] to flight</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðū fiōnd geflǣmdest</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hy. 8, 25; Hy. Grn. ii. 290, 25)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">strong enemies took me there</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Genāmon me ðǣr strange feōndas</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Rood Kmbl. 60; Kr. 30: 65; Kr. 33)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">they are your enemies</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Fȳnd syndon eōwere</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Judth. 11; Thw. 24, 18; Jud. 195: 12; Thw. 26, 10; Jud. 320)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">cadent inimīci vestri in conspectu vestro</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Eōwre fȳnd feallaþ befōran eōw</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lev. 26, 8, 16: Deut. 32, 31)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">inimīci tui sonāvērunt</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðīne feōnd fǣcne forwurdan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 82, 2: 91, 8)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">her father delivered her up into her foes power</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hȳ fæder ageaf on feōnda geweald</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 68 a; Th. 252, 7; Jul. 159: Elen. Kmbl. 135; El. 68)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">reddam ultiōnem hostibus meis</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic agilde wrace mīnum feōndum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Deut, 32, 41, 43: Jos. 10, 25)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">I might have felled all his foes</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ealle ic mihie feōndas gefyllan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Rood Kmbl. 75; Kr. 38)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">thou mightest clearly distinguish thy friends and thy foes</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðū swutole mihtest tocnāwan ðīne frīnd and ðīne fȳnd [fiēnd Cot.]</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 20; Fox 72, 21)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">dilīgite inimīcos vestros</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Lufiaþ eōwre fȳgd</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. Bos. 5, 44, Lk. Bos. 6, 27, 35)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">confirmāvit eum super inimīcos ejus</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hiō ofer heora feōnd fæste getrymede</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 104, 20: 107 12)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">he regards neither friend nor foe</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ne murnþ nāuðer ne friēnd ne fiēnd</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 37, 1; Fox 186, 8)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the people's native land was overspread with enemies</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Wæs wera ēðelland geondsended feōndum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. 92; Th. 118, 22; Gen. 1969)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:eald-feōnd" class="xref-target">eald-feōnd</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:þeōð-" class="xref-target">þeōð-</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge-fȳnd" class="xref-target">ge-fȳnd</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ELN" d:title="ELN">
		<body>
			<h1>ELN<span class="pron"> | eln |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">an ELL, a measure of length, the space from the point of the elbow to the end of the middle finger, eighteen inches</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">quis autem vestrum cōgĭtans pŏtest adjĭcĕre ad stătūram suam cŭbĭtum ūnum?</span>
							<span class="q-oe">hwylc eōwer mæg sōþlīce geþencan ðæt he ge-eācnige āne elne to hys anlīcnesse?</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. Bos. 6, 27; Mt. Vulg. 6, 27)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">non longe ĕrant a terra, sed quăsi cŭbĭtis dŭcentis [18 in. × 200 ÷ 12 = 300 ft.]</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hī wǣron unfeor fram lande, swylce hit wǣre twā hund elna</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Jn. Bos. 21, 8)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the deluge stood deep over the downs, fifteen ells of man</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Fīftena stōd deōp ofer dūnum se drenceflōd monnes elna</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. 69; Th. 84, 17; Gen. 1399)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Eln ulna</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Glos. Brux. Recd. 38, 62; Wrt. Voc. 64, 71)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">the Royal</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="mid-weg" d:title="mid-weg">
		<body>
			<h1>mid-weg<span class="pron"> | mid.wej |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">cum in medium iter venisset</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Þā þā hē wæs on midwege</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Gr. D. 314, 11)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-en">before he had gone halfway</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Ǣr þām þe hē tō midwege cōme</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. S.31, 946)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="bryne-ness" d:title="bryne-ness">
		<body>
			<h1>bryne-ness<span class="pron"> | bry.ne.ness |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Fierce trial</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">torrido rigore (caenobialis vitae)</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hātum brynenesse</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hpt. Gl. 469, 64)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:next word" class="xref-target">next word</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="on-styrigendlic" d:title="on-styrigendlic">
		<body>
			<h1>on-styrigendlic<span class="pron"> | on.sty.ri.Gend.liK |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:un-onstyrigendlic" class="xref-target">un-onstyrigendlic</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="rēn-līc" d:title="rēn-līc">
		<body>
			<h1>rēn-līc<span class="pron"> | reːn.liːtʃ |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:regn-līc" class="xref-target">regn-līc</a>
			</p>
		</body>
