<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="efen-hāda-bisceop" d:title="efen-hāda-bisceop">
		<body>
			<h1>efen-hāda-bisceop<span class="pron"> | e.fen.xɑː.dɑ.bi.ʃe͜op |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A co-bishop</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. co-episcopus)</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="stær-blind" d:title="stær-blind">
		<body>
			<h1>stær-blind<span class="pron"> | stær.blind |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Blind from giddiness, purblind, quite blind</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">scotomaticus (cf. scotomaticorum, cecorum, 78, 20)</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Stæ[r]-blind scotomaticus</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 119, 81)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Næfþ nān man tō ðæs unhāle æāgan, ðæt hē ne māge lybban be ðare sunnan and hire nyttian, gyf hē ēnyg wiht geseōn mæg, būton hē stareblind sī</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Shrn. 187, 5)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Sume unæāðe āwiht geseōþ; sume beōþ stæreblinde and nyttiaþ þeāh ðare sunnan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (27)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">scotomaticos</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Stærbli[nde] scotomaticos</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hpt. Gl. 478, 20)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="swǣslǣcan" d:title="swǣslǣcan">
		<body>
			<h1>swǣslǣcan<span class="pron"> | swæː.slæː.kɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -lǣhte</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To flatter, cajole, speak fair</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">blanditur</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hiō swēslēcþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Kent. Gl. 194)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge-swǣslǣcan" class="xref-target">ge-swǣslǣcan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="þurh-wunian" d:title="þurh-wunian">
		<body>
			<h1>þurh-wunian<span class="pron"> | θurx.wu.ni.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to continue, last, not to come to an end, not to pass away</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">timor Domini permanens in seculum seculi</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Godes ege þurhwunaþ ā worlda world</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 58, 8)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">His rīce þurhwunaþ on ēcnesse</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Blickl. Homl. 65, 16)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hūs rihtwīsra þurhwunaþ (permanebit)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Scint. 73, 2, 16)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Heora gemyud þurhwunaþ ā tō worulde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. T. Grn. 1, 11)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">God, se ðe ǣfre þurhwunode būton ǣlcum anginne</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (2, 3)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">duraverunt</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Þurhwunedan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 28, 58: Wülck. Gl. 256, 2)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">nostri non mansere parentes</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ūre nā þurh-wunedun fæderas</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (6)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">illa discere in terris quorum nobis notitia perseueret in coelis</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Þa leornian on eorþan ðæra ūs cȳþ þurhwunige on heofenum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Scint. 218, 13)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Lang mid þingum ūrum þurhwunian (durare) wē nā magan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (183, 4)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">languor perseuerans</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ādl þurhwunigende</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (153, 17)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to continue in a place, with a person, to remain, not to leave</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic þurhwunode (perseveravi) on ðam munte feōwertig daga and feōwertig nihta</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Deut. 9, 9)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gē synt ðe mid mē þurhwunedon (ðerhwunadon(-un) permansistis, Lind., Rush.) on mīnum geswincum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lk. Skt. 22, 28)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">monks have continued to live in Christchurch</span>
							<span class="q-la">permanserunt</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Þurhwunedan munecas on Xpes cyrican</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 995; Th. 1. 244, 29)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt hē symle on ūs eardige, and wē on him þurhwunian (permaneamus)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Scint. 16, 11)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt gē þuthwunion lange on ðam lande</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Deut. 4, 40)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">haereant ancorae, precor; illis namque manentibus, utcumque se res habeant, enatabimus</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Eālā wǣran ða ancras swā trume and swā þurhwuniende, ðonne mihte wē ðȳ ēþ geþolian swā hwæt earfoþnessa swā ūs on becōme</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 10; Fox 30, 10)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">III.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to continue in a condition, not to change; where purpose or effort is implied, to persevere, persist, hold out</span>
					</p>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(1)</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">absolute</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">qui perseveraverit usque in finem, hic salvus erit</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Se þurhwunaþ (ðerhwunes ł ðerhwunia wælla, Lind.) ōð ende, se byþ hāl</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. Knbl. 10, 22: Scint. 90, 2: Blickl. Homl. 21, 36)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Se ðe ōð ende þurhwunaþ (sustenuerit)</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Mk. Skt. 13, 13)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Nā ongynnendum mēd ys behāten ac þurhwunigendum (perseverantibus) ys geseald</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Scint. 91, 3, 1)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(2)</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">where the condition is given by a complementary noun or adjective</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ǣfre hē biþ ānes mōdes, and glæd þurhwunaþ</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. i. 456, 25)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Heō þurhwunode mǣden</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (24, 27)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">manet adhuc et regnat incolumis</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Heō onwealg on hiere onwalde æfter þurhwunade</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 2, 1; Swt. 62, 24)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Heō ā clǣne þurhwunode</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Blickl. Homl. 3, 18)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hē þurhwunode unspecende and mihteleās forð ōð ðone Ðunresdæg</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 1053; Erl. 186, 23)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Is rihtost ðæt hē ðananforð wydewa þurhwunige</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (L. I. P. 22; Th. ii. 332, 32)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(3)</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">where the condition is given in a phrase</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">in bono quo coepit usque in finem perdurat</span>
									<span class="q-oe">On gōde on ðam hē ongan ōþ ende hē þurhwunaþ</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Scint. 227, 55)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-en">ye still persist in your obstinacy</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Gyt git þurhwuniaþ on incre ānwilnesse</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Blickl. Homl. 187, 33)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">His (Adam's) bendas wǣron onlȳsde ... Eua ðāgyt on bendum þurhwunode</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (89, 6)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hiē þurhwunian on rihtum geleāfan</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (77, 19)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hē nolde þurhwunian on ðære sōðfæstnisse ðæs sōðfæstan Godes sunu</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. T. Grn. 2, 41)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Se ðe on ðām gesǣlþum ðurhwunian ne mōt</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 2; Fox 4, 15)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">IV.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to continue an action, persevere with or in, not to desist from, not to leave off</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Eua ðāgyt on wōpe þurhwunode</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Blickl. Homl. 89, 6)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hiē forþ on heora yfelum þurhwunedon</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (79, 8)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðā hig þurhwunedon (perseuerarent) hine āxsiende</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Jn. Skt. 8, 7)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">On ðam gewinne þurhwunian</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 37, 1; Fox 186, 31: Met. 25, 70)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Þurhwunian on fulfremedlīcum weorcum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Blickl. Homl. 77, 19)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">persistere petitioni sue</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Þurhwunian his bēne</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (R. Ben. Interl. 95, 16)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē þurhwunigende mid gebedum wæs Drihtnes lōf singende</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Blickl. Homl. 231, 9)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Drihten eallum mannum þurhwuniggendum on sōþre andetnesse cwæþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (171, 15)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="willīce" d:title="willīce">
		<body>
			<h1>willīce<span class="pron"> | wil.liː.Ke |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adverb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Willingly, voluntarily</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. voluntarie)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">cetera queque quao uoluntarie suscepimus</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ōþre gehwylce ða wyllīce wē onfēngon</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Anglia xiii. 375, 138)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ellen-lǣca" d:title="ellen-lǣca">
		<body>
			<h1>ellen-lǣca<span class="pron"> | el.len.læː.kɑ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -an</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A champion</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. pugil, agonista)</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="geōmrian" d:title="geōmrian">
		
		<body>
			<h1>geōmrian<span class="pron"> | Ge͜oːm.ri.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -ode</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: present participle sg: -geōmrigende, present participle sg: -geōmriende, present participle sg: -geōmerigende, present participle sg: -geōmrende, past participle sg: -od</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To be sad, to sigh, groan, murmur, mourn, sorrow, lament, bewail</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. gēmere, murmurāre, ingemere, ingemiscere, lūgēre, queri)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">who for ever will mourn in spirit</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Se ðe ā wile geōmrian on gihða</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Salm. Kmbl. 701; Sal. 350)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">preces gementes fundimus</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Bēna geōmrigende we asendaþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hymn. Surt. 21, 13)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">men and women together go sorrowing</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gāþ geōmriende weras wīf samod</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Andr. Kmbl. 3328; An. 1667: Bd. 1, 27; S. 497, 35: Gen. 42, 38: Mk. Bos. 5, 38: 8, 12)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">mourning</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Geōmerigende</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Boutr. Scrd. 20, 42)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">ye, murmuring, grieve in spirit</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gē, geōmrende, gehðum mǣnaþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 9 a: Th. 6, 26; Cri. 90: 48 a; Th. 164, 34; Gū. 1021)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">gemo</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic geōmrige</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. Gr. 28, 3; Som. 30, 58)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">murmurabunt</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hī murcniaþ oððe geōmriaþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Spl. 58, 17)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">they murmur</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hī geōmeriaþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. i. 142, 17)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the lady bewailed in songs</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ides geōmrode giddum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Beo. Th. 2240; B. 1118)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">suspiciens in cœlum, ingemuit</span>
							<span class="q-oe">On ðone heofon behealdende, geōmrode</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Mk. Bos. 7, 34: Jn. Bos. 11, 33, 38)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">be not thou sad</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ne geōmra ðū</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. l00; Th. 132, 25; Gen. 2198)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="swer" d:title="swer">
		<body>
			<h1>swer<span class="pron"> | swer |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:sweor" class="xref-target">sweor</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="geong-lǣcan" d:title="geong-lǣcan">
		<body>
			<h1>geong-lǣcan<span class="pron"> | Ge͜ong.læː.kɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">to grow up, become adult</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">adholesceret</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Iunglǣhte</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (An. Ox. 4361)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="cyrf" d:title="cyrf">
		<body>
			<h1>cyrf<span class="pron"> | Kyrf |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A cutting off, an instrument to cut with</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. abscissio, ferrum abscissionis)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">abscissio</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Cyrf abscissio</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (R. Ben. 28)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">of this cutting</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Be ðisum cyrfe of this cutting</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. ii. 406. 33)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">ferrum abscissionis</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Cyrf ferrum abscissionis</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (C. R. Ben. 40)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:æ-cyrf" class="xref-target">æ-cyrf</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:of-cyrf" class="xref-target">of-cyrf</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="wer-þeōd" d:title="wer-þeōd">
		<body>
			<h1>wer-þeōd<span class="pron"> | wer.θe͜oːd |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">a people, nation; pl. nations, men</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Wē ðē freōndlīce on ðisse werþeōde wīc getǣhton</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. Th. 162, 26; Gen. 2687: Elen. Kmbl. 1283; El. 643)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">On ðære werþeōde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Andr. Kmbl. 273; An. 137)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðū ðās werðeōde gesōhtest</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. Th. 149, 21; Gen. 2478: 171, 2; Gen. 2822)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">In ðære folcsceare geond ða werþeōde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Elen. Kmbl. 1934; El. 969)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ongunnon wercan werþeōda (cf. leāse men, Bt. 38, 1; Fox 194, 30) spell</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Met. 26, 73)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Werþiōda</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (29, 28)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Werðeōde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. Th. 211, 1; Exod. 519)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt is ðæs wyrðe, ðætte werþeōde secgen Dryhtne þonc</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. Th. 38, 2; Cri. 600: 281, 9; Jul. 643)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Waldend werþeōda</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (45, 4; Cri. 714: Cd. Th. 202, 4; Exod. 383)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē manegum wearð geond middangeard mannum tō hrōðre, werþeōdum tō wræce</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Elen. Kmbl. 33; El. 17)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Werþeōdum Filistina</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Salm. Kmbl. 424; Sal. 212)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Se ðe waldeþ giond werþiōda ealra ōþra eorþan cyninga</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Met. 24, 35)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">disperdamus eos ex gente</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Wutun hī tōwyrpan geond werþeōda</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 82, 4: 105, 19: 59, 1: Cd. Th. 61, 2; Gen. 991)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Geond wærðeōda</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Menol. Fox 252; Men. 127)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Geond ealle werðeōda</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 90, 16)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">in omnibus gentibus</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Geond ðās werþeōde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (66, 2)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ofer werþeōda</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (104, 6)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ge nēh ge feor is ðīn nama hālig ofer werþeōda</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Andr. Kmbl. 1086; An. 543)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Wīde geweorðod ofer werþeōda</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Apstls. Kmbl. 30; Ap. 15: Beo. Th. 1802; B. 899: Exon. Th. 243, 12; Jul. 9: Lchdm. iii. 36, 24)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Werþiōde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Met. 9, 21)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">inter gentes</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ofer ealle werþeōde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 104, 1)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">men, the world, cf. weorold, VI a</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hū mihte ðæt gewyrðan in werþeōde (how in the world did it happen?), ðæt ðū ne gehȳrde Hǣlendes miht?</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Andr. Kmbl. 1146; An. 573)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Werðeōde glosses nixu</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 114, 73)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-fadung" d:title="ge-fadung">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-fadung<span class="pron"> | je.fɑ.dung |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Se hlāford sceal beōn līðe þām goodum and egefull þām dysegum ... elles ne bið his gefadung ne fæst ne langsum</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (O. E. Hml. i. 301, 15)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">hac dispositione credimus utraque tempora ordinari</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Wē gelȳfaþ þæt mid þisse gefaduncge ǣgðres weorces tīma mæge beōn geendebyrd</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (R. Ben. 73, 7)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-en">according to the Septuagint</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Æfter þǣra hundseofontigra gefadunge</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Angl. viii. 336, 10)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">in uerbi dispensatione</span>
						<span class="q-oe">On Godes wordes gefadunge</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (vii. 10, 93)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Ne dō hē nān þing ongeān þæs abbodes willan and gefadunge (ordinationem)</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (R. Ben. 125, 19)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Þā wīslican gefadunge þe geset is be incūþra ðinga endebyrdnesse</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Lch, iii. 440, 25)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-wēnan" d:title="ge-wēnan">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-wēnan<span class="pron"> | je.weː.nɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">estimata uespertina hora</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gewēnedre ǣfentȳde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Chrd. 114, 20)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="and-weard-līce" d:title="and-weard-līce">
		<body>
			<h1>and-weard-līce<span class="pron"> | ɑnd.wæ͜ɑrd.liː.tʃe |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adverb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Presentially, in the presence of, present</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. præsentialiter)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">who saw him present</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðe hine andweardlīce gesāwon</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 4, 17; S. 585, 30: Elen. Grm. 1141)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="and-wlītan" d:title="and-wlītan">
		<body>
			<h1>and-wlītan<span class="pron"> | ɑnd.wliː.tɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -wlāt, pl: -wliton</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -wliten</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To look upon</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. intueri)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">that they might not look on the Eternal</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Nō ðæt hī mōsten in ðone Ēcan andwlītan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. 221; Th. 288, 10; Sat. 378)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:wlītan" class="xref-target">wlītan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="mær-weorc" d:title="mær-weorc">
		<body>
			<h1>mær-weorc<span class="pron"> | mær.we͜ork |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>neuter noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A great, splendid work</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="fȳst-gebeāt" d:title="fȳst-gebeāt">
		<body>
			<h1>fȳst-gebeāt<span class="pron"> | fyːst.Ge.bæ͜ɑːt |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>neuter noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A blow with the fist</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. pugni ictus)</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="Scrobbes-burh" d:title="Scrobbes-burh">
		<body>
			<h1>Scrobbes-burh<span class="pron"> | ʃrob.bes.burx |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Shrewsbury</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðā fērdon hī intō Stæffordscīre and intō Scrobbesbyrig</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 1016; Erl. 154, 4)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="frōf(e)rian" d:title="frōf(e)rian">
		<body>
			<h1>frōf(e)rian<span class="pron"> | froːf, e, ri.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:frēfran" class="xref-target">frēfran</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ofer-rano" d:title="ofer-rano">
		<body>
			<h1>ofer-rano<span class="pron"> | o.fer.rɑ.no |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Over-luxuriant, extravagant, sumptuous</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">God lǣteþ reāfian eōwere dohtra heora gyrla and tō oferrancra heāfodge—wǣda.</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wulfst. 46, 1)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="heāh-hweōlad" d:title="heāh-hweōlad">
		<body>
			<h1>heāh-hweōlad<span class="pron"> | xæ͜ɑːx.xwe͜oː.lɑd |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">High-wheeled</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hēhhwiōlad wǣn carracu—tium</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. i. 34, 26)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="hleahtrian" d:title="hleahtrian">
		<body>
			<h1>hleahtrian<span class="pron"> | xlæ͜ɑx.tri.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -ode</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To laugh to scorn, deride</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">omnes uidentes me deriserunt me</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ealle geseōnde mē hlehtredon l̄ tǣldun [mē]</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. L. 21, 8)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gif þū mid þan þeāwe tǣlendra mē hleahtrige</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Guth. Gr. 101, 23)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:hleahtor" class="xref-target">hleahtor</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="betost" d:title="betost">
		<body>
			<h1>betost<span class="pron"> | be.tost |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Best</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. optimus)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">now is speed best, that we may see there the great king</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Nū is ōfost betost, ðæt we þeōdcyning ðǣr sceāwian</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Beo. Th. 6007; B. 3007)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:betst" class="xref-target">betst</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="milts" d:title="milts">
		
		<body>
			<h1>milts<span class="pron"> | milts |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">mildness, kindness, favour, mercy (most commonly with reference to the Deity)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">apud te propitiatio est</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Mid ðec milds is</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Surt. 129, 4)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðonne wurþe ūs eallum Godes milts ðē gearuwre</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. C. E. 19; Th. i. 372, 5: L. C. S. 85; Th. i. 424, 23: Past. 44; Swt. 325, 13)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Biþ ðǣr seō miccle milts āfyrred ... ðæs Ælmihtigan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 28 a; Th. 84, 10; Cri. 1371)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ūs wæs ā syððan Merewioingas milts ungyfeþe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Beo. Th. 5835; B. 2919)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Þolige hē clǣnes legeres and Godes mildse</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. N. P. L. 62; Th. ii. 300, 19)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">thou shalt depart with my favour</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðū mid mildse mīnre fērest</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Andr. Kmbl. 3344; An. 1676)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">misericordiam Domini invocaret, et eam generi humano propitiari rogaret</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē Drihtnes mildheortnesse gecȳgde and ða mildse bæd monna cynne</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 4, 3; S. 569, 9)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Miltse gecȳðan, onwreōn</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Blickl. Homl. 39, 23: 107, 2)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hæbbe hē Godes miltse (mildse)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. Eth. v. 9; Th. i. 306, 20: L. N. P. L. 64; Th. ii. 300, 24)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">reminiscere miserationum tuarum</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gemyne mildsa ðīnra</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Surt. 24, 6: 68, 17)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Secggan wē him þanc ealra his miltsa</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Blickl. Homl. 103, 26: 109, 10)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Āsecggan ða miltsa ðe hē wið ðis mennisce cynn gecȳðde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (103, 19)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">by his mercies</span>
							<span class="q-oe">For his miltsum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 88 b; Th. 333, 6; Vy. 98: 42 a; Th.)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="līdeþ" d:title="līdeþ">
		<body>
			<h1>līdeþ<span class="pron"> | liː.deθ |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:leōdan" class="xref-target">leōdan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="morþ-weorc" d:title="morþ-weorc">
		<body>
			<h1>morþ-weorc<span class="pron"> | morθ.we͜ork |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>neuter noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">An act which causes death (by witchcraft or poison)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hǣðenscipe biþ ðæt man ... wiccecræft lufige oððe morþweorc gefremme (causes death by witchcraft or poison, v. morþ. III)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L.C.S. 5; Th. i. 378, 21)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Deōflīce dǣda on morþweorcum and on manslihtan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. Eth. v. 25; Th. i. 310, 15: vi. 28; Th. i. 322, 16)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:morþ-dǣd" class="xref-target">morþ-dǣd</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-hīwian" d:title="ge-hīwian">
		
		<body>
			<h1>ge-hīwian<span class="pron"> | je.xiː.wi.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -ode</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -od</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To marry</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">for it is written that it is better to marry than to burn, because a man may marry without sin</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Forðæm hit is awriten ðæt hit sīe betere ðæt mon gehiewige ðonne he birne, forðæm būtan synne he mæg gehīwian</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 51, 9; Swt. 401, 33; Hat. MS.)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="WEOROLD" d:title="WEOROLD">
