			<h1>Tiig<span class="pron"> | ti.iG |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:Tiw" class="xref-target">Tiw</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="up-cund" d:title="up-cund">
		<body>
			<h1>up-cund<span class="pron"> | up.kund |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Supernal, celestial</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">illustrates superno lumine</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Onǣled mid ðȳ upcundan leōhte</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 49; Swt. 379, 24)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Cuman tō ðam upcundan æþelan rīce</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. Th. 17, 10; Cri. 268)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt wē magon upcund rīce gestīgan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (348, 27; Sch. 34)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">supernorum civium</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Upcundra ceastergewarena</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hpt. Gl. 423, 5)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">sedibus superum beatis</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Upcundra eādegum setlum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Dōm. L. 303)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="æt-is" d:title="æt-is">
		<body>
			<h1>æt-is<span class="pron"> | æt.is |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">present: 3sg: -æt-is</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">is present</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. adest)</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:æt-eom" class="xref-target">æt-eom</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="wyndrian" d:title="wyndrian">
		<body>
			<h1>wyndrian<span class="pron"> | wyn.dri.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:wundrian" class="xref-target">wundrian</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="hlosnian" d:title="hlosnian">
		<body>
			<h1>hlosnian<span class="pron"> | xlo.sni.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -ode</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To listen, be silent in expectation of hearing, listen for the coming of a person, watch, await, be on the look out</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">then one night another monk was on the watch for his going, and with stealthy tread followed his footsteps</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ða on sumere nihte hlosnode sum ōðer munuc his færeldes and mid sleaccre stalcunge his fōtswaðum filigde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. ii. 138, 5)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">he went then to mass and waited eagerly for the living sacrifice</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Eoda ðā tō mæssan and hlosnode georne be ðære līflīcan onsægednesse</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Swt. 3, 157)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">after these words the multitude listened [astonished or expectant], all were silent</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Æfter ðissum wordum weorud hlosnode swīgodon ealle</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Andr. Kmbl. 1522; An. 762)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">populus suspensus erat audiens ilium</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt folc hlosnende wæs gehērde hine</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lk. Skt. Lind. 19, 48)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">attonitus</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hlosniend</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cot. 3, Lye)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="āstīgan" d:title="āstīgan">
		<body>
			<h1>āstīgan<span class="pron"> | ɑː.stiː.ɣɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">present: 1sg: -stīge, 2sg: -stīgest, 2sg: -stīhst, 3sg: -stīgeþ, 3sg: -stīhþ, pl: -stīgaþ</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -stāg, sg: -stāh, pl: -stigon</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -stigen</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">imperative: sg: -stīh</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to go, come, step, proceed, climb</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. ire, venire, gradi, procedere, scandere)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">thither shall the mind of man go</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hwider sceal ðæs monnes mōd astīgan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 32 b; Th. 103, 21; Cri. 1691)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">dread shall come</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Egsa astigeþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (102 a; Th. 385, 24; Rä. 4, 49)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the sound of words came</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Word-hleōðor astāg</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Andr. Kmbl. 1416; An. 708: Bd. 4, 3; S. 568, 2)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the Holy Spirit came in bodily form</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Se Hālega Gāst astāh lichamlīcre ansȳne</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lk. Bos. 3, 22)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">he may climb the delight of glory</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Se mōt wuldres dreām astīgan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 84 b; Th. 317, 30; Mōd. 73: Ps. Th. 79, 10)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">scando</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic astīge</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. Gr. 28, 6; Som. 32, 30)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to go in any direction</span>
					</p>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">1.</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">generally indicated by a preposition or adverb, hence to rise, ascend, descend, etc</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">generally indicated by a preposition or adverb, hence to rise, ascend, descend, etc</span>
								<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. surgere, ascendere, descendere)</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-en">who comes up through pride</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Ðe þurh oferhyd up astīgeþ</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. 198; Th. 247, 11; Dan. 495)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-en">he came from hell</span>
									<span class="q-oe">He from helle astāg</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 48 b; Th. 168, 14; Gū. 1077)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-en">that he came down with the blow</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Ðæt he mid ðam dynte nyðær astāh</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 1012; Th. 268, 29, col. 2)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-en">the mountains ascend, and the fields go down into their place</span>
									<span class="q-la">ascendunt montes et descendunt campi in locum</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Astīgaþ [Spl. C. upastīgaþ] mūntas, and niðer astīgeþ feldas on stōwe</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Lamb. 103; 8)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-en">Moses alone goes to the Lord</span>
									<span class="q-la">solus Moyses ascendit ad Dominum</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Moises āna astīhþ to Drihtne</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Ex. 24, 2)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-en">go to the top of mount Pisgah</span>
									<span class="q-la">ascende cacumen Phasgæ montis</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Astīh on Fasgan mūntes cnæpp</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Deut. 3, 27)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-en">he went into a ship</span>
									<span class="q-la">ascendit in naviculam</span>
									<span class="q-oe">He astāh on scyp</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. Bos. 8, 23 : 9, 1)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-en">he shall come down as rain on a fleece, and as falling [rain] comes down, dropping over the earth</span>
									<span class="q-la">descendet sicut pluvia in vellus, et sicut stillicidium stillantium [MS. stillicidia stillantia] super terram</span>
									<span class="q-oe">He nyðer astīhþ swā swā rēn on flȳs, and swā swā niðer astīhþ droppetung, droppende ofer eorþan</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Lamb. 71, 6)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">2.</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">but sometimes the direction is indicated in the sentence without a preposition</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">but sometimes the direction is indicated in the sentence without a preposition</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-en">her mind rose</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Hire mōd astāh</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. 101; Th. 134, 35; Gen. 2235: 205; Th. 253, 18; Dan. 597)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-en">he shall come as the rain falleth on a fleece</span>
									<span class="q-la">descendet sicut pluvia in vellus</span>
									<span class="q-oe">He astīgeþ swā se rēn fealleþ on flȳs</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 71, 6)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="hīrsum-līce" d:title="hīrsum-līce">
		
