<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="bearhtm" d:title="bearhtm">
		<body>
			<h1>bearhtm<span class="pron"> | bæ͜ɑrxtm |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A twinkling of an eye, an instant</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">in atomo</span>
							<span class="q-oe">On breahtme</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 79, 27: 46, 60)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Þonne (at the last day) englas blāwað bȳman on brehtme (cf. 1 Cor. xv. 52)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cri. 882)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-fæd" d:title="ge-fæd">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-fæd<span class="pron"> | je.fæd |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Orderly</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. dispositus)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">that every priest at the synod have an orderly man for servant</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt preōsta gehwilc to sinoþe hæbbe gefædne man to cnihte</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. Edg. C. 4; Th. ii. 244, 14)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-cunnian" d:title="ge-cunnian">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-cunnian<span class="pron"> | je.kun.ni.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -ode, sg: -ade</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -od, past participle sg: -ad</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To try, enquire, experience</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. probare, explorare, experiri)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">that they should try which of them had the swiftest horse</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt hi mōstan gecunnian hwylc heora swiftost hors hæfde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 5, 6; S. 618, 42 : Nar. 25, 29)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðe ðone wīgend aweccan dorste oððe gecunnian, hū who dared to awake the warrior or to enquire how . . .</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Judth. 12; Thw. 25, 14; Jud. 259)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">I have experienced many places of sorrow</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic hæbbe gecuunad cearselda fela</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 81 b; Th. 306, 9 ; Seef. 5)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:cunnian" class="xref-target">cunnian</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="fille-seōcness" d:title="fille-seōcness">
		<body>
			<h1>fille-seōcness<span class="pron"> | fil.le.se͜oː.kness |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:fylle-seōcness" class="xref-target">fylle-seōcness</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="lǣfan" d:title="lǣfan">
		<body>
			<h1>lǣfan<span class="pron"> | læː.fɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -de</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to leave</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. relinquere)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">relinquo vobis</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic lǣfe eōw sibbe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Jn. Skt. 14, 27)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic lēfe lego</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 49, 66)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">si cujus frater mortuus fuerit et dimiserit uxorem</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gif hwæs brōðor deād biþ and lǣfþ his wīf</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Mk. Skt. 12, 19)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">non relinquent in te lapidem super lapidem</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hig ne lǣfaþ on ðē stān ofer stāne</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lk. Skt. 19, 44)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">primus reliquit uxorem suam fratri suo</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Se forma lǣfde his brōðer his wīf</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Mt Kmbl. 22, 25)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">those men that before he had left behind him</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ða men ðe hē beæftan him lǣfde ǣr</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 755; Erl. 50, 13)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">they got wealth and left it us</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hiē hegeāton welan and ūs lǣfdon</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Past. pref; Swt. 5, 15)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Swā hit his yldran begeāton and lētan and lǣfdon ðam tō gewealde ðe hȳ wel ūðan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. O. 14; Th. i. 184, 3)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">leave to thy kinsmen people and power</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðīnum māgum lǣf folc and rīce</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Beo. Th. 2361; B. 1178)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">when his death happens, let his lord take charge of what he leaves</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðonne him forþsīð gebyrige gȳme his hlāford ðæs hē lǣfe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. R. S. 4; Th. i. 434, 28: 5; Th. i. 436, 9)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ne biþ lǣfed stān uppan stāne</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. Kmbl. 24, 2)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ān byþ genumen and ōðer byþ lǣfed</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (24, 41)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">their landed property that was left them</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Heora landāre ðe him lǣfed wæs</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Skt. 4, 82)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">non relicto semine</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Nā lǣfedum sǣde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Mk. Skt. 12, 20)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">so that the bones only are left</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt ða bān āne beōn lǣfed</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. Med. ex Quad. 3, 11; Lchdm. i. 340, 26)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to remain, be left remaining</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">if anything remained</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gif hwæt lǣfde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. ii. 40, 14)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">superaverunt</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hia lǣfdun</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Jn. Skt. Rush. 6, 12)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:be-lǣfan" class="xref-target">be-lǣfan</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge-lǣfan" class="xref-target">ge-lǣfan</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:ofer-lǣfan" class="xref-target">ofer-lǣfan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-cȳþedness" d:title="ge-cȳþedness">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-cȳþedness<span class="pron"> | je.Kyː.θed.ness |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Testimony</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. testimonium)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">testimonium</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gecȳþednesse</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. L. 121, 4)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="un-ceāp" d:title="un-ceāp">
		<body>
			<h1>un-ceāp<span class="pron"> | un.Kæ͜ɑːp |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">without price, gratis</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">gratis date</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Unboht ł unceāp, būta ēghuelcum worðe seallas</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. L. 10, 8 margin)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="fōstor-leān" d:title="fōstor-leān">
		<body>
			<h1>fōstor-leān<span class="pron"> | foː.stor.læ͜ɑːn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>neuter noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Remuneration for fostering</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. nutrīcii merces)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the Saviour had repaid the virgin the reward for fostering, in eternal life</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hæfde Nergend fōstorleān fǣmnan forgolden, ēce to ealdre</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Menol. Fox 301; Men. 152)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:fōster-leān" class="xref-target">fōster-leān</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-dīfan" d:title="ge-dīfan">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-dīfan<span class="pron"> | je.diː.fɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -ed</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To plunge, immerse</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Rammes wul on wætere gedȳfed and æfter þām on ele</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lch. i. 356, 12)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:dīfan" class="xref-target">dīfan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="þwang" d:title="þwang">
		<body>
			<h1>þwang<span class="pron"> | θwɑng |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">a strip of skin</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. corrigiam)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Befleh ǣnne þwang (corrigiam) þām biscope fram þām hneccan oþ þone hōh</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Gr. D. 198, 4)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">a shoelace</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">'Cum and unscō mē' , . . Þā þwangas þāra scōna ongunnon heom sylfe tōslūpan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Gr. D. 221, 22)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="gemynd-blīþe" d:title="gemynd-blīþe">
		<body>
			<h1>gemynd-blīþe<span class="pron"> | Ge.mynd.bliː.θe |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Happy from what one recollects (?), having happy memories (?). The word, however, glosses memoriale</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. memoriale)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gemynd-blīþe memoriale</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Spl. T. 101, 13)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-yrsian" d:title="ge-yrsian">
