			<h1>tō-dǣlness<span class="pron"> | toː.dæːl.ness |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">fecerunt omnes</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Tōdǣlnisse dydon alle discumbere</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Lk. L. 9, 15)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="āfæstan" d:title="āfæstan">
		<body>
			<h1>āfæstan<span class="pron"> | ɑː.fæ.stɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -fæste</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -fested</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To fast</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. jejunare)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">he fasted till evening</span>
							<span class="q-oe">He afæste to ǣfenes</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 3, 23; S. 554, 32 : 3, 27; S. 559, 13)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="þorn-stybb" d:title="þorn-stybb">
		
		<body>
			<h1>þorn-stybb<span class="pron"> | θorn.stybb |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">The stump of a thorn-tree</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Tō ðæm þornstybbe; of ðam þornstybbe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cod. Dip. Kmbl. v. 252, 28)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Tō ðan þornstybbe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (vi. 8, 33, 37)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">On ðonæ þornstub</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (v. 291, 11)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">On ðone þornstyb; of ðam stybbe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cod. Dip. B. iii. 169, 33)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-yrfian" d:title="ge-yrfian">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-yrfian<span class="pron"> | je.yr.fi.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge-irfian" class="xref-target">ge-irfian</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="helfling" d:title="helfling">
		<body>
			<h1>helfling<span class="pron"> | xel.fling |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A halfpenny</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">are not five sparrows sold for two farthings</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ne becȳpaþ hig fīf spearwan tō helflinge</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lk. Skt. 12, 6)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="grīming" d:title="grīming">
		<body>
			<h1>grīming<span class="pron"> | griː.ming |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A spectre</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Grīming mascam</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 57, 25)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:grīma" class="xref-target">grīma</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="-ness" d:title="-ness">
		<body>
			<h1>-ness<span class="pron"> | ness |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">The suffix is attached to nouns, v. hæftnīd-, mægenþrym-, wyndreām-ness; to adjectives, e. g. gōd-, swīt-, gīfer-, nearu-ness; to numerals or pronouns, v. ān-, hwilc-ness; to past participles, v. ālīfed-, gedrēfed-ness; for-sewen-, āgoten-, gecoren-ness; to verbal roots, (l) weak : v. īc-, līf-, nere-, styre-ness. (2) strong: v. foreseō-, grōw-, weax-ness. (3) pret. pres. wit-ness.</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:hæftnīd-ness" class="xref-target">hæftnīd-ness</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:mægenþrym-ness" class="xref-target">mægenþrym-ness</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:wyndreām-ness" class="xref-target">wyndreām-ness</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:gōd-ness" class="xref-target">gōd-ness</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:swīt-ness" class="xref-target">swīt-ness</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:gīfer-ness" class="xref-target">gīfer-ness</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:nearu-ness" class="xref-target">nearu-ness</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:ān-ness" class="xref-target">ān-ness</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:hwilc-ness" class="xref-target">hwilc-ness</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:ālīfed-ness" class="xref-target">ālīfed-ness</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:gedrēfed-ness" class="xref-target">gedrēfed-ness</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:for-sewen-ness" class="xref-target">for-sewen-ness</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:āgoten-ness" class="xref-target">āgoten-ness</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:gecoren-ness" class="xref-target">gecoren-ness</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:īc-ness" class="xref-target">īc-ness</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:līf-ness" class="xref-target">līf-ness</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:nere-ness" class="xref-target">nere-ness</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:styre-ness" class="xref-target">styre-ness</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:foreseō-ness" class="xref-target">foreseō-ness</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:grōw-ness" class="xref-target">grōw-ness</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:weax-ness" class="xref-target">weax-ness</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:wit-ness" class="xref-target">wit-ness</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="bearn-le(ā)st" d:title="bearn-le(ā)st">
		<body>
			<h1>bearn-le(ā)st<span class="pron"> | bæ͜ɑrn.le, ɑː, st |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">orbitatis</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Bearnleās(t)e</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (An. Ox. 4873)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="for-bor" d:title="for-bor">
		<body>
			<h1>for-bor<span class="pron"> | for.bor |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:wyrt-forbor" class="xref-target">wyrt-forbor</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ful-" d:title="ful-">
		<body>
			<h1>ful-<span class="pron"> | ful |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:full-" class="xref-target">full-</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="hræd-līce" d:title="hræd-līce">
		<body>
			<h1>hræd-līce<span class="pron"> | xræd.liː.tʃe |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adverb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Quickly, hastily, speedily, immediately, at once, forthwith</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hrædlīce actutum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. Gr. 38; Som. 41, 64)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">confestim ascendit de aqua</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hrædlīce hē āstāh of ðam wætere</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. Kmbl. 3, 16: continuo, 13, 5, 20)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">if thou wilt do us kindness, tell us so at once</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gif ðū wille mildheortnesse ūs dōn sæge ūs ðæt hrædlīce</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Blickl. Homl. 233, 19)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">they swore oaths to him that they would speedily march out of his kingdom</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Him ðā āþas swōron ðæt hie hrædlīce of his rīce fōren</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 876; Erl. 78, 11)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">very soon after that he was consecrated king</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē wæs æfter ðam swīðe hrædlīce gehālgod tō cyninge</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (979; Erl. 129, 30)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hrædlīcor ocius; hrædlīcost ocissime</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. Gr. 38; Som. 42, 9)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">he can perform the journey more quickly</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Se hit mæg hrædlīcor gefēran</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Blickl. Homl. 231, 24: Bd. 3, 14; S. 540, 19)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="oþ-hrīnan" d:title="oþ-hrīnan">
		<body>
			<h1>oþ-hrīnan<span class="pron"> | oθ.xriː.nɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">of physical contact, to touch</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Se rodor þǣre eorþan ǣfre ne oðrīneð</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Met. 20, 138)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic hys hrægles fnædes oðhrān</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. A. 189, 228)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē hire fēt mid teārum oþrān . . . heō mid ðǣre hālgan rōde gedryncnesse Iordanem oþhrīnan (ongan)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. S. 23 b, 719-723)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">se quis immundis manibus cibum aliquem tetigerit, vel canis, vel felis, vel mus tetigerit</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gif man mid unclǣnum handum hwylces metes onhrīne, oððe him hund oððe catt oððe mūs oðhrīne</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ll. Th. ii. 164, 9)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē hire fēt mid his teārum þwōh, ne geþrȳstlǣhte hē nān ōþer þæs līchaman oðhrīnan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. S. 23 b, 745)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to touch the heart, mind, &amp;c.</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic wearð gelǣd mid þǣre hǣtu þæs geleāfan, and mid þām trūwan oþhrinon (æthrinen, v. l.)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. S. 23 b, 456)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="seō" d:title="seō">
		<body>
			<h1>seō<span class="pron"> | se͜oː |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:sī" class="xref-target">sī</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="weōce" d:title="weōce">
		<body>
			<h1>weōce<span class="pron"> | we͜oː.Ke |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Þā gefyllde hē mid wætere ealle þǣre cyrcean ciellan and sette weōcon (tapor, v.l.) onmiddan (in media papyrum posuit), and þā mid fȳre ontennde</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Gr. D. 44, 15)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="fealo tubulo" d:title="fealo tubulo">
		<body>
			<h1>fealo tubulo<span class="pron"> | fæ͜ɑ.lo, tu.bu.lo |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:fala" class="xref-target">fala</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="eft-cyme" d:title="eft-cyme">
		<body>
			<h1>eft-cyme<span class="pron"> | eft.Ky.me |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A coming again, return</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. rēditus, reversio)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the warrior band sat in expectation of the return of the dear man</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt eorlwerod sæt on wēnum eftcymes leōfes monnes</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Beo. Th. 5785; B. 2896: Exon. 121 b; Th. 466, 33; Hö. 130)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the tree-fowls' offspring by signs made known the blessed man's return</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Treōfugla tuddor tācnum cȳðdon cādges eftcyme</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 43 a; Th. 146, 11; Gū. 708)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-wlō" d:title="ge-wlō">
		
		<body>
			<h1>ge-wlō<span class="pron"> | je.wloː |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:an-wlōh" class="xref-target">an-wlōh</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:wlōh" class="xref-target">wlōh</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="lustlīce" d:title="lustlīce">
		<body>
			<h1>lustlīce<span class="pron"> | lust.liː.Ke |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adverb</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">beata sors omnis est aequinamitate tolerantis</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Yfel biþ gesǣlþ gif hit mon lustlīce dēð and geðyldi līce āræfnþ</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 11. l ; F. 32, 31 : 38, 7; F. 210, 14)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Ic liōða fela lustlīce (v. lustbǣrlīce) sanc</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Met. 2, l)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Sē ðe Godes beboda lustlīce gehȳrð, and lustlīcor mid weorcuni gefylð</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. Th. i. 552, 2)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Hē sylþ mē hors oþþe beāh þæt þe lustlīcor cræft mīnne ic (the hunter) begancge</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Coll. M. 22, 38)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:lustbǣrlīce" class="xref-target">lustbǣrlīce</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="scilfe" d:title="scilfe">
		<body>
			<h1>scilfe<span class="pron"> | ʃil.fe |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -an</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A shelf, ledge, floor</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">With lower, second, and third stories shalt thou make the ark, Gen. 6, 16</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gescype scylfan on scipes bōsme</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. Th. 79, 4; Gen. 1306)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="cnafa" d:title="cnafa">
		<body>
			<h1>cnafa<span class="pron"> | knɑ.fɑ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -an</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A boy, lad, young man</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">jocari cum parvulo</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gamenian mid cnafan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Scint. 172, 19)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">puero tuo</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Cnafan þīnum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Spl. C. 85, 15)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Sȳn twēgen tō þām sylfan gescyfte cnafan (pueri)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Angl. xiii. 410, 640)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:mǣg-cnafa" class="xref-target">mǣg-cnafa</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="cyrr" d:title="cyrr">
		
		
		<body>
			<h1>cyrr<span class="pron"> | Kyrr |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A turn, space of time, an occasion, affair</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. versio, vices, temporis spatium, negotium)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">at the fourth turn or time</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Æt ðam feōrþan cyrre [sǣle, q. v.]</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Herb. 100, 3; Lchdm. i. 214, 5, 6, 7, 8: Gen. 38, 18)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">at some turn or time, when; aliquando</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Æt sumum cyrre</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lk. Bos. 22, 32)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">who is busied, in a journey with other affairs</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Se biþ abīsgod, on færelde mid ōðrum cierrum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 4, 1; Hat. 9b, 7)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ed-cyrr" class="xref-target">ed-cyrr</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:frum-cyrr" class="xref-target">frum-cyrr</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:ofer-cyrr" class="xref-target">ofer-cyrr</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:on-cyrr" class="xref-target">on-cyrr</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:sǣ-cyrr" class="xref-target">sǣ-cyrr</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="sciphere-līc" d:title="sciphere-līc">
		<body>
			<h1>sciphere-līc<span class="pron"> | ʃip.xe.re.liːtʃ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Relating to a fleet, naval</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">classicis</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Scipherelīcum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hpt. Gl. 406, 40)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-edðrawen" d:title="ge-edðrawen">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-edðrawen<span class="pron"> | je.ed.θrɑ.wen |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>participle</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Twisted again or back</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. retortus)</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="gāst-gemynd" d:title="gāst-gemynd">
		<body>
			<h1>gāst-gemynd<span class="pron"> | gɑːst.Ge.mynd |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">thought of mind or spirit</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:gǣst-gemynd" class="xref-target">gǣst-gemynd</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="blysige" d:title="blysige">
		<body>
			<h1>blysige<span class="pron"> | bly.si.Ge |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -an</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A torch</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. fax)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">þæcile, blysige fax</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. 284, 20)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:þæcele" class="xref-target">þæcele</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="hǣmdere" d:title="hǣmdere">
		<body>
			<h1>hǣmdere<span class="pron"> | xæːm.de.re |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:unriht-hǣmdere" class="xref-target">unriht-hǣmdere</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="flǣsc-tawere" d:title="flǣsc-tawere">
		<body>
			<h1>flǣsc-tawere<span class="pron"> | flæːʃ.tɑ.we.re |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A flesh-tawer or tormentor, an executioner</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. lānio, carnifex)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">lānio, vel lānista, vel carnifex, vel macellārius</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hyldere, oððe cwellere, oððe flǣsctawere [MS. flæctawere]</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. Gl. 113; Som. 79, 120; Wrt. Voc. 60, 27)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="spranca" d:title="spranca">
		<body>
			<h1>spranca<span class="pron"> | sprɑn.kɑ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Sprancena sarmentorum, i, uiminum</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (An. Ox. 2640)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:æcern-spranca" class="xref-target">æcern-spranca</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="syfer-līce" d:title="syfer-līce">
		
		<body>
			<h1>syfer-līce<span class="pron"> | sy.fer.liː.tʃe |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adverb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">with cleanliness, without impurity</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt gē witen ðæt hit (the preparation of the wafers for the mass) clǣnlīce and sȳferlīce gedōn sȳ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. E. I. 5; Th. ii. 404, 36)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">soberly, purely, without excess or grossness</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Sidefulle on ðeāwum and sȳferlīce lybbende</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Ass. 37, 327)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">III.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">soberly, prudently, circumspectly</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ða cild ðe beōþ sȳferlīce āfēdde (cf. the contrast in l. 9, cild rēceleāslīce āfēdd), and wið unðeāwum gestȳrede</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. ii. 326, 17)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">precantes sobrie</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Biddende sēferlīce</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hymn. Surt. 19, 11)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="æt-sæcst" d:title="æt-sæcst">
		<body>
			<h1>æt-sæcst<span class="pron"> | æt.sækst |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:æt-sacan" class="xref-target">æt-sacan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="WĒSAN" d:title="WĒSAN">
		<body>
			<h1>WĒSAN<span class="pron"> | weː.sɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:WESTAN" class="xref-target">WESTAN</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="lacu" d:title="lacu">
		<body>
			<h1>lacu<span class="pron"> | lɑ.ku |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A stream, water-course</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">On scegbrōc oð seō lacu scȳt west þanon ūt on hǣðfeld</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (C.D.B. iii. 624, 19)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Oþ woggawilllacu ūt scȳt; on þā lace oð wocggawilles heāfod</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cht. E. 266, 24)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Be healfan strēme intō Sandfordes læce; swā andlang ðǣre lace intō Sandforda; of Sandforda eāst andlang ðǣre lace</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (C.D. iv. 134, 21-24)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Oð ðā lace; andlang lace ūt on Temese</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (v. 302, 34: 330, 28: vi. 2, 12: vi. 8, 26)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">On þā fūlan lace</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (v. 13, 22)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">On streām oþ þā laca tōlicgaþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cht. Crw. 3, 12)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
					<ol class="sub-senses">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sub-heading">as second part of a compound</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ūt on æsclace ðǣr æsclace fylð ūt on Wuorf ... of ðǣre ealdan dīc on Grindewylles lace ... on Ættanpennes lace</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (C.D. vi. 48, 8-14)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">On brōmlace; ðonne andlang streāmes</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (iii. 452, 13)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">On ðā gemǣrlace; andlang lace</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (vi. 8, 26)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">On þā mǣrlace</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (9, 2)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">On sandlace; andlang sandlice tō ceōles īge</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (v. 303, 3)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:fisc-lacu" class="xref-target">fisc-lacu</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:mǣd-lacu" class="xref-target">mǣd-lacu</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ālǣtnes" d:title="ālǣtnes">
		
		<body>
			<h1>ālǣtnes<span class="pron"> | ɑː.læːt.nes |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A loss, losing</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. amissio)</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="in-gelǣdan" d:title="in-gelǣdan">
		<body>
			<h1>in-gelǣdan<span class="pron"> | in.Ge.læː.dɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -de</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To lead or bring in, introduce</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the Lord brought upon them the water of the sea</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ingelēdde ofer hie Drihten weter sēwe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cantic. Moys. 23; Thw. notæ, p. 30)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">until I bring thee into my father's house</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ōþ ðæt ic ðē ingelǣde on mīnes Fæder hūs</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Blickl. Homl. 191, 19)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">introducta</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ingelǣded</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 4, 9; S. 576, 37)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="pægel" d:title="pægel">
		<body>
			<h1>pægel<span class="pron"> | pæ.Gel |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">a wine-vessel, a pail</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Pægel (Wright gives wægel, but see Anglia viii. 450) gillo</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. i. 25, 26)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="be-lādiendlic" d:title="be-lādiendlic">
		<body>
			<h1>be-lādiendlic<span class="pron"> | be.lɑː.di͜ynd.liK |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Apologetic</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. apologeticus, excusabilis)</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="-lēsan" d:title="-lēsan">
		<body>
			<h1>-lēsan<span class="pron"> | leː.sɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:-līsan" class="xref-target">-līsan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="cwide" d:title="cwide">
		<body>
			<h1>cwide<span class="pron"> | kwi.de |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">IV.</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Þā geceās hē Laurentium ... and hē þurhwunode in his cwide (sententia)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Gr. D. 329, 18)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">VIII.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">an agreement</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē nā tō him hwearf æfter heora cwyde (gecwide, v.l. condictum) ... wæs hē gemyndig heora cwydes</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 4, 25; Sch. 329, 18)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:folc-c" class="xref-target">folc-c</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:heāfod-c" class="xref-target">heāfod-c</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="-swind" d:title="-swind">
		<body>
			<h1>-swind<span class="pron"> | swind |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ǣ-swind" class="xref-target">ǣ-swind</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="cōlode" d:title="cōlode">
		<body>
			<h1>cōlode<span class="pron"> | koː.lo.de |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -cōlode</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">cooled</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">cōlode</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 51b; Th. 180, 18; Gū. 1281)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:cōlian" class="xref-target">cōlian</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="wāc-scipe" d:title="wāc-scipe">
		<body>
			<h1>wāc-scipe<span class="pron"> | wɑːk.ʃi.pe |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Remissness</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt hī stȳran ǣlcum ðara ðe ðis ne gelǣste and mīnra witena wed ābrecan mid ǣnigum wācscipe wille</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. Edg. S. 1; Th. i. 272, 7)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:wāce" class="xref-target">wāce</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="fore-witol" d:title="fore-witol">
		<body>
			<h1>fore-witol<span class="pron"> | fo.re.wi.tol |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Se forewitola Scyppend wiste on ǣr hwæt hē of hyre gedōn habban wolde</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 1067; P. 201, 26)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="wundor-clam[m]" d:title="wundor-clam[m]">
		<body>
			<h1>wundor-clam[m]<span class="pron"> | wun.dor.klɑm, m |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A wondrous clasp</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Wæs gebunden deōran since duru ormǣte, wundurclommum bewriþen</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. Th. 19, 33; Cri. 310)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="cīte" d:title="cīte">
		<body>
			<h1>cīte<span class="pron"> | Kiː.te |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -an</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">a hut, cabin, cottage</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Cētan gurgustione</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. i. 110, 17)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gecōm hē tō hyre cȳtan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. Th. ii. 182, 26: 184, 7)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">posuerunt Hierusalem velut pomorum custodiam</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Settan Hierusalem samod anlīcast swā hī æppelbearu āne cȳtan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 78, 2)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē lēt ārǣran ealle ābūtan ðā dūne his hyrdecnapan cȳtan, ꝥ hī ðǣr gehende mid heora hlāfordes yrfe lāgon, and wið cyle and wið hǣton hī sylfe geburgon</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. S. 23, 418)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">a cell of a monk, hermit, &amp;c.</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Cȳte, hulce (hulce ł cēte, Hpt. Gl. 465, 45) tugurio .i. cella (the cell of John the hermit)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (An. Ox. 2515)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">fratribus infirmis sit cella super se deputata</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Sȳ þām untrumum gebrōðrum synderlīce cȳte (hūs, cȳte, R. Ben. I. 67, 17) geset and tō þām ānum betǣht</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (R. Ben. 60, 20)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Þæs muneces cȳte mid leōhte wearð āfylled</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. S. 31, 811)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Heō began faran tō ðæs foresǣdan wēstensetlan cȳtan, and on þǣre cȳtan duru cnocode</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. A. 196, 25)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē eōde on þā cētan þǣr se līchoma wæs</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bl. H. 217, 25: 219, 14)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Se geatweard sceal cȳtan (hūs cellam, R. Ben. I. 112, 7) habban wið þæt geat</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (R. Ben. 126, 18)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gangende in þā cȳtan (cellam) Benedictes</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Gr. D. 140, 10)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">¶ in a local name, Cētwudu Chetwood</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (C. D. i. 292, 20)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:cete" class="xref-target">cete</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:cyte" class="xref-target">cyte</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-tydd" d:title="ge-tydd">
