			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ār-gesweorf" d:title="ār-gesweorf">
		<body>
			<h1>ār-gesweorf<span class="pron"> | ɑːr.Ge.swe͜orf |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Brass filings</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. limatura æris)</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:gesweorf" class="xref-target">gesweorf</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:sweorfan" class="xref-target">sweorfan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="gylden" d:title="gylden">
		
		<body>
			<h1>gylden<span class="pron"> | Gyl.den |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Golden</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. aureus)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gylden wed vel feoh arra</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. Gl. 14; Som. 58, 11; Wrt. Voc. 21, 6)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gylden læfr bractea</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (58; Som. 67, 111; Wrt. Voc. 38, 34)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gylden fel bractea</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cot. 27, Lye)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gyldena vel gegylde fatu crisendeta</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. Gl. 67; Som. 69, 97; Wrt. Voc. 41, 48)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">then stood there a golden image</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðā stōd ðǣr gyldenu onlīcnes</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Shrn. 88, 22)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">there is a golden gate</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðǣr is geat gylden</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. 227; Th. 305; 19; Sat. 649)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">to a golden wedge</span>
							<span class="q-oe">On sumum gyldenum wecge</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. i. 60, 29)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">under a golden crown</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Under gyldenum beāge</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Beo. Th. 2330; B. 1163)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">to the idol of gold</span>
							<span class="q-oe">To ðam gyldnan gylde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. 182; Th. 228, 18; Dan. 204)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">a golden ring</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hring gyldenne</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Beo. Th. 5611; B. 2809)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:eal-gylden" class="xref-target">eal-gylden</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="CAPŪN" d:title="CAPŪN">
		<body>
			<h1>CAPŪN<span class="pron"> | kɑ.puːn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A CAPON</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. gallinaceus, capo)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Capūn gallinaceus</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. 63, 9: Ælfc. Gl. 39; Som. 63, 48: Wrt. Voc. 30, 3)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Capūn capo</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (39; Som. 63, 46; Wrt. Voc. 30, 1)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-fylstan" d:title="ge-fylstan">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-fylstan<span class="pron"> | je.fyl.stɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">present: 1sg: -fylste, sg: -fylste</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -fylstede, sg: -fylste, pl: -fylston</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -fylsted</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To help, give help</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. adjuvare)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">that she might assist them</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt heō him gefylste</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 3, 11; Bos. 73, 45)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">Deus adjuvat me</span>
							<span class="q-oe">God gefylsteþ me</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Spl. 53, 4)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">Domine, ad adjuvandum me festina</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Driht, to gefylstan me efste</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (69, 1)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:fylstan" class="xref-target">fylstan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="rīce" d:title="rīce">
		<body>
			<h1>rīce<span class="pron"> | riː.Ke |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>neuter noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I a.</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">medio imperii sui Babylonem condidit</span>
							<span class="q-oe">On middeweardum hire rīce hiō getimbrede Babylonia þā burg</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 2, 1; 8. 62, 14)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">God forgifð rīce ðām ðe hē wile</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. Th. ii. 434, 4)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I b.</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">summus locus bene regitur, cum is, qui praeest, vitiis potius quam fratribus dominatur</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðonne bið ðæt rīce wel gereht, ðonne sē ðe ðǣr fore bið suīðor wilnað ðæt hē rīcsige ofer monna unðeāwas ðonne ofer ōðre gōde menn</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 117, 9)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ærce-rīce" class="xref-target">ærce-rīce</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:ærcebisceop-rīce" class="xref-target">ærcebisceop-rīce</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:Breoten-rīce" class="xref-target">Breoten-rīce</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:feōwer-rīce" class="xref-target">feōwer-rīce</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:fiþer-rīce" class="xref-target">fiþer-rīce</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:Franc-rīce" class="xref-target">Franc-rīce</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:heāfod-rīce" class="xref-target">heāfod-rīce</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:land-rīce" class="xref-target">land-rīce</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:middel-rīce" class="xref-target">middel-rīce</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="hungrian" d:title="hungrian">
		<body>
			<h1>hungrian<span class="pron"> | xun.gri.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:hyngrian" class="xref-target">hyngrian</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="efen-lāste" d:title="efen-lāste">
		<body>
			<h1>efen-lāste<span class="pron"> | e.fen.lɑː.ste |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -an</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">The everlasting</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. gnaphălium)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">take the netherward [part] of everlasting</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Genim efenlāstan nyðowearde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lchdm. iii. 2, 2)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:efe-lāste" class="xref-target">efe-lāste</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-rǣdend" d:title="ge-rǣdend">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-rǣdend<span class="pron"> | je.ræː.dend |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A disposer</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. dispositor)</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="eft" d:title="eft">
		<body>
			<h1>eft<span class="pron"> | eft |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adverb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">of repetition, again</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">identidem</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Eft gelīce identidem</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 47, 50)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">lectitando</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Eft rǣdende lectitando</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (50, 23)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Wē nū gehȳrdon þis godspel rǣdan, and þēh wē hit sceolan eft ofercweþan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bl. H. 15, 31)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Wæs culufre eft (a second time) of cofan sended</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Gen. 1464: B. 1377)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Eft . . . nīwan stefne</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Gen. 1885: An. 1304)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Eft . . . ōðre sīðe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (706: 1677: Sat. 75)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Eft swā ǣr</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (An. 1276: 1343)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Eft swā ǣr . . . niōwan stefne</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (B. 1787)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">I a.</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">of replacement, restoration, renewal</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">lotis pedibus recalcient se</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Geðwegenum fōtum eft sceōgian hī</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Angl. xiii. 413, 687)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Sceal beōn se ingang eft geopenod</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Bl. H. 9, 8)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hū hē eft gesette seld sēlran werode</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Gen. 94: Dan. 641)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Þā wæs eft swā ǣr þeōd on sǣlum</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (B. 642: An. 1478)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">of return, reversal, back, again</span>
					</p>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(a)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">to a place</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hī eōden and eft cōmon</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. Th. i. 64, 7: Gen. 1478)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hām eft becuman</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (El. 143)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Se heofonlica ǣrendwreca eft hām cerde</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Bl. H. 9, 24)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Wǣron Egypte eft oncyrde</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Exod. 451)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Nū wille ic eft þām līge neār</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Gen. 760)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-en">they did not expect the prince back</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Hig æðelinges eft ne wēndon</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (B. 1596)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(b)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">to a condition</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Þū tō eorþan scealt eft geweorþan</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Cri. 624)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Willflōd ongan lytligan eft</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Gen. 1413)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(c)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">of giving</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hē hāteþ þā eorþan eft āgifan ꝥ heō ǣr onfēng</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Bl. H. 21, 30)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(d)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">reversal of order</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Agof is mīn noma eft onhwyrfed</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Rä. 24, 1)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">III.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">afterwards</span>
					</p>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(a)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">in reference to the past</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Siō ǣ wæs ǣrest on Ebrisc geðiōde funden, and eft Creācas wendon hiē on hiora āgen geðiōde, and eft Lædenware swǣ same</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 7, 1-3)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Swā hiē eft dydon</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Cri. 455: Exod. 389: Sat. 374)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ic sōna eft mē sylfum andwyrde</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 5, 21)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Gesceōp God Adam and Evah eft siððan . . . Beswāc se ðeōfol siððan eft ðā men</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. T. Grn. 3, 4-8)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hē spræc tō Abrahame . . . Cwæð þā eft raðe tō Sarran</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Gen. 2726: Sat. 229)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hē eft æfter fæce geþrowade</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Bl. H. 23, 30)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Eft ufaran dōgrum</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (B. 2200)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(b)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">in reference to the future, hereafter</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Þæt þū ne secge eft, 'Ic gewelegode Abram,'</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Gen. 14, 23: Gen. 2145)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ǣr seō mengeo eft tōfaran sceolde</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (1663: 2702)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Wā eōw þe nū hlihaþ, for þon gē eft wēpað on ēcnesse</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Bl. H. 25, 23, 20: 55, 24: B. 1753)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Wē wǣron on wræcsīþ sende, and nū eft sceolon ōþerne ēþel sēcan</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Bl. H. 23, 6: Sat. 212: Gū. 1159)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">III a.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">afterwards, in a later part of a book</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">infra subdit</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Eft rehþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (An. Ox. 5167)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">IV.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">where there is a sequence of propositions, statements, again</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Wæs gecueden ðætte ðā sācerdas ne scoldon nō hiera heāfdu scieran . . ., ne eft hī ne scoldon hira loccas lǣtan weaxan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 139, 13)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Sē ðe āgiēmeleāsað ðā giēmene . . ., oððe eft folgað ðǣre giēmenne</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (87, 11: 321, 16)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gehiēren hwæt āwriten is . . . and eft gehiērað ðone cwide</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (323, 10: Met. 7, 27: 11, 26)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hwīlum . . . hwīlum eft</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (20, 215: Cri. 648: B. 2111)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">again no one . . .</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Nǣnig eft . . .</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Crä. 18)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">so, again, Isaiah said it of you</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Swā hit eft be eōw Esaias mǣlde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (El. 350)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="of-sceōtan" d:title="of-sceōtan">
		<body>
			<h1>of-sceōtan<span class="pron"> | of.ʃe͜oː.tɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To shoot off, shoot down</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="āttor-drinca" d:title="āttor-drinca">
		<body>
			<h1>āttor-drinca<span class="pron"> | ɑːt.tor.drin.kɑ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -an</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A poisonous drink, poison</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. potio venenata, venenum)</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="be-weddendlic" d:title="be-weddendlic">
		<body>
			<h1>be-weddendlic<span class="pron"> | be.wed.dend.liK |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Relating to espousals</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. sponsalia)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">sponsalia</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Beweddendlice</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (An. Ox. 1122)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="missenlic-ness" d:title="missenlic-ness">
		<body>
			<h1>missenlic-ness<span class="pron"> | mis.sen.liK.ness |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">dispar retributionis qualitas</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Þ UNCERTAIN is ān eādignes þe hī þǣr onfōþ, and ungelīc missenlicnes þæs edleānes</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Gr. D. 315, 24)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Seō missenlicnes (diversitas) manna līchamena . . . seō missenlicnes manna synna</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (333, 23)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="līf" d:title="līf">
		<body>
			<h1>līf<span class="pron"> | liːf |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:leāf" class="xref-target">leāf</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="wagung" d:title="wagung">
		<body>
			<h1>wagung<span class="pron"> | wɑ.ɣung |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Shaking, looseness</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Wið tōþa sāre and wagunge, genim ðās ylcan wyrte, syle etan fæstendum, heō ða tēþ getrymeþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lchdm. i. 210, 11: 334, 6)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:wagian" class="xref-target">wagian</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="salowig" d:title="salowig">
		<body>
			<h1>salowig<span class="pron"> | sɑ.lo.wiG |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:saluwig" class="xref-target">saluwig</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="hweowol" d:title="hweowol">
		
		
		<body>
			<h1>hweowol<span class="pron"> | xwe͜o.wol |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>neuter noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A wheel</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. rota)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the firmament turns on those two stars just as a wheel turns on an axle</span>
							<span class="q-oe">tyrnþ on eaxe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lchdm. iii. 270, 22)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">ut rotam</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Swā swā hweowol</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Spl. 82, 12)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">a waggon-wheel</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Wǣnes hweowol</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Shrn. 32, 12)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Swā swā yrnende hweowol</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hexam. 5; Norm. 8, 29)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">solis rota</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðære sunnan hweogul</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hymn. Surt. 22, 25)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">rota</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hweōl</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. Gl. 2; Som. 55, 48; Wrt. Voc. 16, 20)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt hweōl hwerfþ ymbūtan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 39, 7; Fox 220, 29)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt unstille hweōl ðe Ixion wæs tō gebunden ðæt ōþstōd</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (35, 6; Fox 168, 31)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæs hweohles [hweoles, MS. Cott.] felga</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (39, 7; Fox 222, 19)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">in rota</span>
							<span class="q-oe">On hweōhle</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Spl. 76, 17)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">rota in rota</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hwēl in hwēlum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. Kmbl. p. 9, 20)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="heg-hūs" d:title="heg-hūs">
		
		<body>
			<h1>heg-hūs<span class="pron"> | xeG.xuːs |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>neuter noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A hay-house</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. fœnile)</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="Æl-mehtig" d:title="Æl-mehtig">
		<body>
			<h1>Æl-mehtig<span class="pron"> | æl.mex.tiG |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Almighty</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:eall-mihtig" class="xref-target">eall-mihtig</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="scendness" d:title="scendness">
		<body>
			<h1>scendness<span class="pron"> | ʃend.ness |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge-scendness" class="xref-target">ge-scendness</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="hell-rȳnigu" d:title="hell-rȳnigu">
		<body>
			<h1>hell-rȳnigu<span class="pron"> | xell.ryː.ni.ɣu |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">a sorceress</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Helrȳnegu pithonissa</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 69, 21)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="belene" d:title="belene">
		
		<body>
			<h1>belene<span class="pron"> | be.le.ne |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -an</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Henbane</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. hyoscyamus niger)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">mix henbane with lard</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Belenan meng wið rysele</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. M. 1, 31; Lchdm. ii. 72, 1)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">apply the juice of henbane</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Dō belenan seāw</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (3, 3; Lchdm. ii. 310, 7)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">take the seed of henbane</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Genim beolonan sǣd</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (1, 2; Lchdm. ii. 38, 1)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:beolone" class="xref-target">beolone</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:henne-belle" class="xref-target">henne-belle</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="fyrd" d:title="fyrd">
		
		<body>
			<h1>fyrd<span class="pron"> | fyrd |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">a ford, found in the compound Twȳ-fyrd Twyford</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ford" class="xref-target">ford</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="þeōf" d:title="þeōf">
		<body>
			<h1>þeōf<span class="pron"> | θe͜oːf |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A thief</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Þeōf fur, scaþa latro</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. i. 74, 23)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gyf se hīrēdes ealdor wiste on hwylcere tīde se þeōf (ðeāf, Lind. fur) tōwerd wǣre</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. Kmbl. 24, 43)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ealle ða ðe cōmun wǣron þeōfas (ðeāfas, Lind.) and sceaþan (fures et latrones) ... Þeōf (ðeāf, Lind. fur) ne cymþ būton ðæt hē stele and sleā</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Jn. Skt. 10, 8-10)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Þeōf ðe on þȳstre færeþ, on sweartre niht</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. Th. 54, 21; Cri. 872: 432, 10; Rä. 48, 4)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðeōf sceal gangan in ðȳstrum wederum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Menol. Fox 543; Gn. C. 42)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðǣr þeōfas (ðeāfas, Lind. fures) hit delfaþ and forstelaþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. Kmbl. 6, 19)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">On helle beōþ þeōfas and gītseras ðe on mannum heora ǣhta on wōh nimaþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Blickl. Homl. 61, 21)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hēr syndan rȳperas and reāferas and woruldstrūderas and ðeōfas and þeōdscaðan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wulfst. 165, 36)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Þeōfum grassatoribus</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 40, 35)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ealle niht ic (the ox-herd) stande ofer ða oxan waciende for þeōfan (propter fures)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Coll. Monast. Th. 20, 29)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gif feorrancumen man oþþe fræmde būton wege gange, and hē ðonne nāwðer ne hrȳme, ne hē horn ne blāwe, for þeōf hē biþ tō prōfianne</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. Wih. 28; Th. i. 42, 23: L. In. 20; Th. i. 114, 15)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðeōfas wē hātaþ ōð .vii. men; from .vii. hlōð ōð .xxxv.; siþþan biþ here</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. In. 13; Th. i. 110, 13)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Wē wyllaþ ðæt ǣlc man ofer twelfwintre sylle ðone āð, ðæt hē nelle þeōf beōn ne þeōfes gewita</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. C. S. 21; Th. i. 388, 6)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Se ðe þeōf gefēhþ, hē āh .x. scill.</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. In. 28; Th. i. 120, 5)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gesēce ǣbera þeōf ðæt ðæt hē gesēce, oððe se ðe on hlāfordsearwe gemēt sȳ, ðæt hī nǣfre feorh ne gesēcen, būton se cyningc him feorhgeneres unne</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. Edg. ii. 7; Th. i. 268, 22: L. C. S. 26; Th. i. 390, 27)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Sȳ hē þeōf, and þolige heāfdes and ealles ðæs ðe hē āge</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. Edg. S. 11; Th. i. 276, 13)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Se ðe þeōf fylle beforan ōðrum mannum, ðæt hē wǣre of ūre ealra feō .xii. pæng ðe betera for ðære dǣda and ðon anginne</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. Ath. v. 7; Th. i. 234, 22)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gif man frigne man æt hæbbendre handa gefō, ðanne wealde se cyning þreora ānes: oþþe hine man cwelle, oþþe ofer sǣ selle, oþþe hine his wergelde ālēse</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. Wih. 26; Th. i. 42, 15)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gif þeōf siē gefongen, swelte hē deāðe oþþe his līf be his were man āliēse</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. In. 12; Th. i. 110, 8)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gif man þeōf on carcerne gebringe, ðæt hē beō .xl. nihta on carcerne, and hine mon ðonne ālȳse ūt mid .cxx. scill.</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. Ath. i. 1; Th. i. 198, 21)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Beō se þeōf ūtlah wið eall folc</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. C. S. 30; Th. i. 394, 24)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:beō-þeōf" class="xref-target">beō-þeōf</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:gold-þeōf" class="xref-target">gold-þeōf</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:mann-þeōf" class="xref-target">mann-þeōf</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:mūs-þeōf" class="xref-target">mūs-þeōf</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:regn-þeōf" class="xref-target">regn-þeōf</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:sǣ-þeōf" class="xref-target">sǣ-þeōf</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:stōd-þeōf" class="xref-target">stōd-þeōf</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:wergild-þeōf" class="xref-target">wergild-þeōf</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:infangene-þeōf" class="xref-target">infangene-þeōf</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:þīfþ" class="xref-target">þīfþ</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="sǣtere" d:title="sǣtere">
		<body>
			<h1>sǣtere<span class="pron"> | sæː.te.re |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">a robber</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. latro)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">fur et latro</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Þeāf and sēttere</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Jn. Skt. Lind. 10, 1)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">fures et latrones</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Þeāfas and sētteras</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (10, 8)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">fig. one who acts insidiously</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. insidiator, seductor)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Se sǣtere (insidiator), ðæt is se diōful, hē hine spænþ on wōh</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 53, 7; Swt. 417, 23)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðonne cymþ se lytega sǣtere (seductor) tō ðæm slāwan mōde, and āteleþ him eall ðæt hē ǣr tō gōde gedyde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (65, 2; Swt. 463, 12)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hī sendon sēteras (insidiatores) ðætte genōmo hine on word</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lk. Skt. Lind. 20, 20)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:sǣt" class="xref-target">sǣt</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:sǣtian" class="xref-target">sǣtian</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-mēting" d:title="ge-mēting">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-mēting<span class="pron"> | je.meː.ting |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A meeting, an assembly, association, a society</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. conventus, conventio, conventiculum, congregatio)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">our meeting is not secret</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Is undyrne uncer gemēting</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Beo. Th. 4006; B. 2001)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gemētingc conventus vel conventio</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. 72, 75)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">protexisti mea conventum malignantium</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðū bewruge me fram gemētinge awyrgedra</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Spl. 63, 2: Ps. Th. 105, 16)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">in congregatione</span>
							<span class="q-oe">On gemētingum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (110, 1)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">non congregabo conventicula eorum</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ne ic ne gederige gemētinga heora</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Spl. 15, 4)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">conciliis</span>
							<span class="q-oe">To gemoetingum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Mk. Skt. Lind. 13, 9)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="heolor-bledu" d:title="heolor-bledu">
		<body>
			<h1>heolor-bledu<span class="pron"> | xe͜o.lor.ble.du |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">The scale of a balance</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">justa lance</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Mid þā efnan helurblede</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 48, 40)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="swēgend-līc" d:title="swēgend-līc">
		<body>
			<h1>swēgend-līc<span class="pron"> | sweː.Gend.liːtʃ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Vocal, vowel</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">I and u beōþ āwende tō consonantes, gif hī beōþ tōgædere gesette oððe mid ōðrum swēgendlīcum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. Gr. 2; Zup. 6, 15)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="fryþ" d:title="fryþ">
		<body>
			<h1>fryþ<span class="pron"> | fryθ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>neuter noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Peace</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. pax)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the remainder made peace with the army</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Seō lāf [MS. lafe] wið ðone here fryþ nam</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 867; Erl. 73, 16: 1036; Th. 294, 9, col. 2)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">that he be not worthy of any peace</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt he ne beō nānes fryþes weorðe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. Eth. iii. 15; Th. i. 298, 12)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:friþ" class="xref-target">friþ</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="pīle" d:title="pīle">
		<body>
