<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="lyre-wrenc" d:title="lyre-wrenc">
		<body>
			<h1>lyre-wrenc<span class="pron"> | ly.re.wrenk |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A trick that causes damage or loss</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Lā, hwī ne mōt ic habban þæt ic mē sylf beget mid mīnum lyrewrencum ?</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Verc. Först. 168)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ĀTE" d:title="ĀTE">
		
		<body>
			<h1>ĀTE<span class="pron"> | ɑː.te |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -ātan, nominative pl: -ātan, genitive pl: -ātena</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">OATS, tares, darnel, cockle</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. avena fatua, Lin. lolium)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">take groats of oats</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Nim ātena grātan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lchdm. iii. 292, 24)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">take meal of oats</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Genim mela ǣtena</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. M. 1, 35 ; Lchdm.ii. 84, 5 : Chr. 1124; Th. 376, 6)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Āte lolium</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cot. 126)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ātan or lasor tares; zizania</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cot. 204)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ferian" d:title="ferian">
		
		
		<body>
			<h1>ferian<span class="pron"> | fe.ri.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -ode, sg: -ede</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -od, past participle sg: -ed</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">infinitive: sg: -to ferianne</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to carry, convey, bear, lead, conduct</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. ferre, portāre, vehĕre, dedūcĕre, afferre)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">he commanded the warriors to carry the holy tree before him</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hēht wīgend ðæt hālige treō him befōran ferian</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Elen. Kmbl. 215; El. 108: Cd. 67; Th. 80, 18; Gen. 1330)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">we will gladly convey thee over the fish's bath [the sea]</span>
							<span class="q-oe">We ðē willaþ ferigan freōlīce ofer fisces bæþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Andr. Kmbl. 585; An. 293)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the giver of life commanded his angels to bear the dear one over the stronghold of the waves</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hēt līfes brytta englas sīne ferigean leōfne ofer lagufæsten</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (1647; An. 825)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">ad portandum</span>
							<span class="q-oe">To ferianne</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Gen. 46, 5)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">circumfĕro</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic ferige onbūtan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. Gr. 47; Som. 48, 33)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the vessel conveys me over the floods</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Mec merehengest fereþ ofer flōdas</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 104 a; Th. 395, 13; Rä. 15, 7: 114 b; Th. 439, 16; Rä. 59, 4)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">they bear it over the fish's bath [the sea]</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hī hine feriaþ ofer fisces bæþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Runic pm. 16; Kmbl. 342, 17; Hick. Thes. i. 135, 31)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">whence bear ye your stout shields?</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hwanon ferigeaþ gē fætte scyldas</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Beo. Th. 671; B. 333)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">deduxisti sīcut ŏves pŏpŭlum tuum</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Folc ðīn ðū feredest swā sceāp</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 76, 17)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">he bare it to his minster with honour</span>
							<span class="q-oe">He ferode ðone to his mynstre mid ārwurþnysse</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. ii. 358, 7: Chr. 1009; Erl. 141, 23)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">a noble one conducted us over the realm of oars [the sea]</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Us ofer ārwēlan æðeling ferede</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Andr. Kmbl. 1706; An. 855)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">they conveyed the saint to the city</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hī ðone sanct ferodon to ðære byrig</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. ii. 518, 29)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">in mănĭbus portābunt te</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðē on folmum feredan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 90, 12: 82, 3)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">afferte nōbis de fructĭbus terræ</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Feriaþ mid ēow of ðære eorþan wæstmum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Num. 13, 21)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">ferēbātur in cælum</span>
							<span class="q-oe">He wæs fered on heofen</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lk. Bos. 24, 51)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to betake oneself to</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. se gerĕre, versēri)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">thou hast long betaken thyself to evil arts</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðū aclǣccræftum lange feredes</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Andr. Kmbl. 2725; An. 1365)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">they betook themselves to lying</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hī on līge feredon</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 58, 12)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">III.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to go, depart</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. vehi, īre)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">to depart in peace</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Mid friþe ferian</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Byrht. Th. 136, 68; By. 179)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">Deus, dum transgrediēris per desertum</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðonne God geond wēstena wīde feraþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 67, 8)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:āferian" class="xref-target">āferian</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:æt-ferian" class="xref-target">æt-ferian</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge-ferian" class="xref-target">ge-ferian</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:of-ferian" class="xref-target">of-ferian</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:-ōþ-ferian" class="xref-target">-ōþ-ferian</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:to-ferian" class="xref-target">to-ferian</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:wið-ferian" class="xref-target">wið-ferian</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="mis-tūcian" d:title="mis-tūcian">
		<body>
			<h1>mis-tūcian<span class="pron"> | mis.tuː.Ki.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">vehementer caesus</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Hē beōt Liberlinum on ꝥ heāfod and on þā ansȳne, oð ꝥ eall his andwlita wearð tōswollen and āwannod. Ðā þā hē swā swīðe mid geþersce mistūcod wæs (vehementer caesus)</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Gr. D. 20, 33)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">equi calcaribus cruentati</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Þā hors mid þām spurum mistūcode (geblōdgode, v.l.) equi calcaribus cruentati</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (15, 5)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="be-lādian" d:title="be-lādian">
		<body>
			<h1>be-lādian<span class="pron"> | be.lɑː.di.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">present: 1sg: -lādige</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -ode</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -od</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To clear, excuse</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. excusare)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">that he might clear his mother</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt he wolde belādian his mōdor</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 3, 9; Bos. 65, 24 : Ælfc. Gr. 28, 6; Som. 32, 35)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:lādian" class="xref-target">lādian</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="þurh-wæccendlīc" d:title="þurh-wæccendlīc">
