			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A publican</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="neāh-west" d:title="neāh-west">
		
		<body>
			<h1>neāh-west<span class="pron"> | næ͜ɑːx.west |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">nearness, neighbourhood</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">he dare not come into his neighbourhood</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē ne dorste his neāwiste geneālǣcan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. i. 88, 21)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">uninhabitable on account of the nearness of the sun</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ungewuniendlīc for ðære sunnan neāweste</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lchdm. iii. 260, 21)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">On ðære neāwiste næs nān wæterscipe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Jud. 15, 18)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">in quorum vicinia</span>
							<span class="q-oe">In ðara neāwiste</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 5, 14; S. 634, 28)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hig on neāwiste (in vicino) eardodon</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Jos. 9, 16: Elen. Kmbl. 133; El. 67)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Wæs ðǣr on neāweste (in proximo) hūs</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 4, 24; S. 598, 27 : Blickl. Homl. 197, 20: Chr. 924; Erl. 110, 13)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðā wīcode se cyng on neāweste ðare byrig</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (896; Erl. 94, 5)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Swā feala earmra manna swā on ðæs rīcan neāweste sweltaþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Blickl. Homl. 53, 5)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ða ðe on hire neāwiste lifgeaþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (43, 2)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">flagella non appropiabunt tabernaculo tuo</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ne [māgon] hūse ðīnum on neāweste nāhwǣr sceþþan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 90, 10)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ealle ða wǣpnedmen ðe him on neāweste wǣron</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 1, 10; Swt. 46, 2)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ealle ða rīcu ðe him under beōþ oððe on neāweste</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 16, 1 ; Fox 50, 3)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">ad cujus vicina pertinet locus ille</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Tō ðæs rīces neāwiste belimpeþ seō stōw</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 5, 12 ; S. 630, 22)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">the being with another, presence, society, fellowship</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">what is better than to serve and be with the king ?</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hwæt is betere ðonne ðæs cyninges folgaþ and his neāwest (cf. ðæs cyninges gefērrǣden, l. 2)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 29, 1 ; Fox 102, 7)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hwelc is ǣngum men māre daru ðonne hē hæbbe on his gefērrǣdenne and on his nēweste feōnd on freōndes anlīcnesse</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (29, 2 ; Fox 106, 14)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Þincþ his neāwist (the presence of the dead body) lāþlīco and unfæger</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Blickl. Homl. 111, 30)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ne cume he nā on ðæs cyninges neāwiste (ansȳne, MS. H.)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. Edm. E. 3 ; Th. i. 246, 3)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the priest judged that he (the leper) should be separated from the society of men</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Se sacerd dēmde ðæt hē sceolde beōn āscyred fram manna neāwiste</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. i. 124, 25)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē fērde tō folces neāwiste and bodade</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (352, 11)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">From alre nēweste geleāfulra sȳn heō āsceādene</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Chart. Th. 29, 19)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Mid ðȳ ic wæs him on neāwiste, hē ðus wæs sprecende</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 3, 13 ; S. 538, 23)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Forlǣt mec englas geniman on ðīnne neāwest (into thy presence)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. Th. 455, 13 ; Hy. 4, 49)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">ne mulieris alicujus societatem secum habeant</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic forboden ǣlcon bisceope and mæssepreōste ðæt hig nānes wīfmannes neāweste mid him næbbon</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. Ecg. P. ii. 6; Th. ii. 198, 8)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Wē lǣraþ ðæt ǣnig preōst ne lufige wīfmanna neāwiste</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. Edg. c. 60; Th. ii. 256, 21)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hī wīfes neāwiste forlēton</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. Ælfc. C. 1 ; Th. ii. 342, 14 : Homl. Skt. 10, 204)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Libia and Agrippina wurdon swā gelȳfede ðæt hī forbugon heora wera neāwiste</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. i. 374, 33)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ne can ðara idesa ōwðer þurh gebedscipe beorna neāwist</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. Th. 148, 36; Gen. 2467)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="dwolma" d:title="dwolma">
		<body>
			<h1>dwolma<span class="pron"> | dwol.mɑ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -n</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">a state or place of confusion</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Duolma, dualma chaus, chaos, prima confusio omnium rerum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Txts. 49, 457)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Dwolma chaos (abstrusum, et torpens confusio rerum, Ald. 150, 10), i. tenebre</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (An. Ox. 17, 9)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">tristius coelum tenebris obducitur atris</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Eal bið ūpheofon sweart and gesworcen, deorc and dimhīw and dwolma sweart</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Dōm. L. 106: Wlfst 137, 10)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Dwolma cahus ( = chaos, Lk. 16, 26)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 73, 65: 17, 56)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Dwolman (in antiquum) chaos</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (An. Ox. 2483)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge-dwolma" class="xref-target">ge-dwolma</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="uferor" d:title="uferor">
		<body>
			<h1>uferor<span class="pron"> | u.fe.ror |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adverb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Higher</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. ut altius)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">ut altius</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Swā swā heālīcor, þæs uferur</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (An. Ox. 5058)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ufor" class="xref-target">ufor</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-twisa" d:title="ge-twisa">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-twisa<span class="pron"> | je.twi.sɑ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -an</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A twin</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">two twins</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Twegen getwisan two twins</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Gen. 38, 27: Swt. A. S. Rdr. 62, 197)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">gemini</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Getwisan gemini</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. Gr. 13; Som. 16, 13: Bd. de nat. rerum; Wrt. popl. science 7, 5; Lchdm. iii. 244, 24)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="stician" d:title="stician">
		<body>
			<h1>stician<span class="pron"> | sti.Ki.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -ode</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">trans. To stick, stab, pierce, prick</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Oxa spæc and cwæð: 'Tō hwon sticast ðū mē,'</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Shrn. 30, 12)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Mē on fæðme sticaþ hygegālan hond,</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. Th. 394, 1; Rä. 13, 11)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē(the wounded elephant) ða ōþre elpendas sticade,</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 4, 1; Swt. 156, 13)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gē hyne (Christ) myd spere sticodon,</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Nicod. 13; Thw. 6, 35)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Sticedon,</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. Th. 297, 1; Sat. 510)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Stycodon,</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Shrn. 147, 36)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hī ne mihte þorn stician,</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (66, 17)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">stimulosa,</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Stycigende</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Scint. 104, 6)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">I a.</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">to kill (to stick is still used of killing pigs. Cf. sticung, II)</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">aut jugulamur aut mergimur,</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Wē oþþe sticode beōþ oþþe on sǣ ādruncene</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 1, 13; S. 482, 1)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">nonnulli comprehensi acervatim jugulabantur,</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Monige fanggene wǣron and heāpmǣlum sticode</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (1, 15; S. 484, 5)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">I b.</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">to thrust out (cf. stingan)</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">efossis oculis,</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Sticode him mon ða eāgan ūt</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 4, 5; Swt. 168, 4)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">I c.</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">intrans.</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ðæt mē ongeān sticaþ,</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. Th. 497, 20; Rä. 87, 3)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">intrans.</span>
					</p>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(1)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">To stick, remain fixed</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ðæs spācan sticaþ ōþer ende on ðære felge, ōþer on ðære nafe,</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 39, 7; Fox 222, 7)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Lǣt ða sāglas stician ðǣron . . . Ða sāglas sticiaþ eallne weg inn on ðām hringum . . . Simle ða ofergyldan sāglas sceolden stician on ðǣm gyldnum hringum,</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 22; Swt. 171, 1-22)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Mē on hreðre heāfod sticade,</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. Th. 479, 10; Rä. 62, 5)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">On ðære rōde sticodon mænige arewan,</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 1083; Erl. 217, 21)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Sting ðīn seax on ða wyrte, lǣt stician ðǣron,</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Lchdm. ii. 346, 12, 20: Jud. 3, 22)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(2)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">fig. to be involved, be prevented from free action, lie encumbered</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">quanto in coeno probra volvantur,</span>
									<span class="q-oe">On hū ðiōstrum hora seāþe þara unþeāwa ða yfelwillendan sticiaþ</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (37, 2; Fox 188, 2)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">latet obscuris condita virtus clara tenebris,</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Sticiaþ gehȳdde beorhte cræftas</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (4; Fox 8, 15)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ðæt ða synfullan sāwla sticien helle tōmiddes,</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Salm. Kmbl. 344; Sal. 171)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(3)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">to be inherent</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Seō godcundnys ðe on ðam men sticode,</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. ii. 386, 19)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(4)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">to be in possession of (of demoniacal possession), to lurk</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">daemonium habes,</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Deōfol ðē sticaþ on</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Jn. Skt. 7, 20)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">'Ðonne gesihst ðū hwæt ðǣron sticaþ' . . . Ðǣr gewende ūt of ðam fæte ān næddre,</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. ii. 170, 19)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Wē bebeōdaþ ðām deōflum ðe on ðisum anlīcnyssum sticiaþ, ðæt hī ūt faron,</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (496, 8)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Se apostol cwæð tō ðam āwyrgedan gāste ðe hire on sticode,</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (i. 464, 22)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ða deōflu ðe on ðām anlīcnyssum sticodon,</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (ii. 482, 8)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">III.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">of direction, to run, lie (cf. sceōtan)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ūt æt ðæs croftes heāfod ðæt sticaþ on ðære lace,</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cod. Dip. Kmbl. iii. 37, 24)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Andlang weges ðæt hit sticaþ on norðeweardum cynges steorte. . . andlang weges ðæt hit sticaþ æt wīchām,</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (48, 8-11)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðonne swā forð ðæt hit sticaþ on miclancumb; and of miclancumbe ðæt hit sticaþ on litlancumb,</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (405, 30)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðonne tō ðam wuduwege ðæt hit sticaþ innan Nodre; ðonne andlang Noddre ðæt hit sticaþ on Eatstānes landscare; ðæt hit sticaþ up tō herpoðe,</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (446, 8-11)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Wið sūðan ða mēde ðæt it sticaþ tōemnes ðam wiðigðyfelum,</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (v. 194, 32)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:of-stician" class="xref-target">of-stician</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:tō-stician" class="xref-target">tō-stician</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:þurh-stician" class="xref-target">þurh-stician</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="for-tȳnan" d:title="for-tȳnan">
		<body>
			<h1>for-tȳnan<span class="pron"> | for.tyː.nɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -de</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -ed</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To shut in, stop, hinder</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. interclūdere)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">qui crebris accūsātiōnibus iter illi cœleste interclūdere contendēbant</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hī mid gelomlīcum oncunningum tiledon ðæt hī him ðone heofonlīcan weg fōrsetton and fortȳndon</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 3, 19; S. 548, 4)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="āloccian" d:title="āloccian">
		<body>
			<h1>āloccian<span class="pron"> | ɑː.lok.Ki.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -ode</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -od</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To entice</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. allicere)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">that they might entice those out, who were there within</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt hī aloccodan ūt ða, ðe ðǣr binnan wǣran</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 4, 11; Bos. 97, 39)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="blāc-hleōr" d:title="blāc-hleōr">
		<body>
			<h1>blāc-hleōr<span class="pron"> | blɑːk.xle͜oːr |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Having a pale face, pale-faced, fair</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. pallidus vel candidus genis)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">many a pale-faced damsel must trembling go</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Sceolde monig blāchleōr ides bifiende gān</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. 92; Th. 118, 23-25; Gen. 1969, 1970)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="helle-mere" d:title="helle-mere">
		<body>
			<h1>helle-mere<span class="pron"> | xel.le.me.re |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">The lake of hell, Styx</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. styx)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hellemere hæc styx</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. Gr. 9; Som. 14, 13)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Helemere Styx</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. Gl. 54; Som. 66, 99; Wrt. Voc. 36, 22)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="hundteōntigfealde" d:title="hundteōntigfealde">
		<body>
			<h1>hundteōntigfealde<span class="pron"> | xund.te͜oːn.tiɣ.fæ͜ɑl.de |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adverb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A hundredfold</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">centuplum accipiet.</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hundteantigfalde (hund—rað sīða monigfallīce, L. ) onfooð centuplum accipiet.</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. R. 19, 29.)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="lefel" d:title="lefel">
		<body>
			<h1>lefel<span class="pron"> | le.fel |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:læfel" class="xref-target">læfel</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="þurh-lǣred" d:title="þurh-lǣred">
		<body>
			<h1>þurh-lǣred<span class="pron"> | θurx.læː.red |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Very learned</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">expertus, i. multum peritus</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Þurhlǣred vel gleāw</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. i. 22, 35)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="of-spring" d:title="of-spring">
		<body>
			<h1>of-spring<span class="pron"> | of.spring |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Offspring, progeny, posterity, descendants</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Of-spring styrps</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. Gr. 9, 58 ; Som. 13, 36)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ofsprincg progenies</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (12 ; Som. 15, 53)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Eall heora ofspring ðe him of com</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. T. Grn. 3, II)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Eall heora ofsprinc boren and unboren</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cod. Dip. Kmbl. iv. 263, 29)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gif his sunu and sunu-sunu swā micel landes habban, siððan biþ se ofsprinc (cf. hiora æftergengas, 24) gesīðcundes cynnes</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. Wg. II ; Th. i. 188, II)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic sette feōndrǣdene betweox ðīnum ofspringe and hire ofspringe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Gen. 3, 15)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðīnum ofspringe (semini tuo) ic forgife ðis land</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (12, 7 : 13, 15)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic dō ðīnne ofspring swā menigfealdne swā ðære eorþan dust</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (13, 16)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hī gesworen habbaþ ge for hȳ sylfe ge for heora ofspryng (gingran, MS. B. )</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. A. G. tit. ; Th. i. 152, 17)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðis sȳ gedōn for Sīferþ and for his ofsprincg tō hyra sāwle þearfe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cod. Dip. Kmbl. ii. 300, 15)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="feōnd-rǣs" d:title="feōnd-rǣs">
		<body>
			<h1>feōnd-rǣs<span class="pron"> | fe͜oːnd.ræːs |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A hostile attack, an onslaught, assault</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">I (Eve) wickedly made onslaught and despoiled the tree in the garden</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic fracoðlīce feōndrǣs gefremede . . . and reāfode beām on bearwe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Gen. 900)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="flōd-wudu" d:title="flōd-wudu">
		<body>
			<h1>flōd-wudu<span class="pron"> | floːd.wu.du |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Flood-wood, a ship</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. mǎrīnum lignum, nāvis)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">as if we journey in vessels over the cold water, convey our ships through the wide sea</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Swā we ofer cald wæter ceōlum līðan, geond sīdne sǣ flōdwudu fergen</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 20a; Th. 53, 21; Cri. 854)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ātor-coppe" d:title="ātor-coppe">
		<body>
			<h1>ātor-coppe<span class="pron"> | ɑː.tor.kop.pe |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Þā weōfodu beōð tō þan swīðe forlǣtene ꝥ ðā āttor-coppan (araneae) habbaðinnan āwefene</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Verc. Först. 102, 6)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="gyrnan" d:title="gyrnan">
		
		<body>
			<h1>gyrnan<span class="pron"> | Gyr.nɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -de</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To desire, beg, yearn</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">I do not desire much for myself</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic ne me micles gyrne</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 37 a; Th. 121, 20; Gū. 291)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">joyous is eager to perform very many good deeds</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Glædmōd gyrneþ ðæt he gōdra mǣst dǣda gefremme</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (62 b; Th. 229, 28; Ph. 492)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the maiden desired to die</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt mǣden hire deāþes girnde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Apol. Th. 2, 24: 3, 8)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">vos nolite vocari Rabbi</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ne gyrne gē ðæt eōw man Lāreōwas nemne</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. Kmbl. 23, 8)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">orontes</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gyrnende</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Mk. Skt. 11, 24)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:geornan" class="xref-target">geornan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="-hering" d:title="-hering">
