					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Attack, assault</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðǣra wyrma ongrype and ðæra sorhwīta mǣst</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wulfst. 187, 2)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-cweccan" d:title="ge-cweccan">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-cweccan<span class="pron"> | je.kwek.kɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">vellebant discipuli ejus spicas</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Gecwecton ðegnas his ða croppas</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Lk. Skt. Lind. 7, 1)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="for-pǣran" d:title="for-pǣran">
		<body>
			<h1>for-pǣran<span class="pron"> | for.pæː.rɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -de</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -ed</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To turn away, pervert, ruin, destroy</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. pervertěre, perděre)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">he perverts the other's soul by his evil instigations</span>
							<span class="q-oe">He ðæs ōðres sāwle forpǣrþ þurh his yfelum tihtingum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. ii. 226, 31: 208, 20)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">měritis pervertunt</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hie forpǣraþ ðæm edleāne</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 39, 3; Hat. MS. 53 b, 8)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">if we do not destroy ourselves</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gif we us sylfe ne forpǣraþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. i. 216, 9: ii. 50, 5)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">Adam ruined us by the eating of an apple</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Adam us forpǣrde þurh ānes æpples þigene</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. ii. 330, 32)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">that he may destroy the man</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt he ðone man forpǣre</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Boutr. Scrd. 20, 20)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="strica" d:title="strica">
		<body>
			<h1>strica<span class="pron"> | stri.kɑ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
