			<h1>hed-clāþ<span class="pron"> | xed.klɑːθ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A thick upper garment of coarse material, like a chasuble</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:heden" class="xref-target">heden</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="forþ-geleōredness" d:title="forþ-geleōredness">
		<body>
			<h1>forþ-geleōredness<span class="pron"> | forθ.Ge.le͜oː.red.ness |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Departure, decease, death</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">pro expectatione sui exitus</span>
							<span class="q-oe">For þǣre bāde his ændes and forþgeleōrodnesse</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Gr. D. 282, 11)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="and-wlita" d:title="and-wlita">
		
		<body>
			<h1>and-wlita<span class="pron"> | ɑnd.wli.tɑ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -an</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">The face, countenance, personal appearance, forehead, form, surface</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. facies, vultus, aspectus, frons, forma, superficies)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the bolster received his cheek, the hero's face</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hleōr bolster onfēng, eorles andwlitan the bolster received his cheek, the hero's face</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Beo. Th. 1382; B. 689: Exon. 24 a; Th. 69, 20; Cri. 1123: Bt. Met. Fox 31, 33; Met. 31, 17)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">lamen vultas tui</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Leōht andwlitan ðīnes</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Spl. 4, 7: Ps. Th. 89, 8)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">all creatures receive form from God</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ealle gesceafta onfōþ æt Gode andwlitan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 39, 5; Fox 218, 15)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">on the face of the wide earth</span>
							<span class="q-oe">On andwlitan wīdre eorþan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. 67; Th. 81, 21; Gen. 1348)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">he had a pale countenance</span>
							<span class="q-oe">He hæfde blācne andwlitan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 2, 16; S. 519, 34)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="rynelīce(?)" d:title="rynelīce(?)">
		<body>
			<h1>rynelīce(?)<span class="pron"> | ry.ne.liː.Ke |</span>
