						<span class="meaning-en">sight</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge-sihþ" class="xref-target">ge-sihþ</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="molde" d:title="molde">
		<body>
			<h1>molde<span class="pron"> | mol.de |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">dust, earth</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">pulveris</span>
							<span class="q-oe">bæd ðæt hyre man sumne dǣl ðære hālwendan moldan (pulveris) sealde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 3, 11; S. 536, 5-8: 3, 10; S. 534, 23, 29)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">pulvere terras</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ða ðe for hund wintrum mid eorþan moldan (pulvere terras) bewrogene wǣron</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. Ecg. P. iv. 66; Th. ii. 226, 23)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðonne hit (cadaver) biþ on ða byrgenne set, ðonne wyrpeþ man moldan ofer hit</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. Ecg. C. 36; Th. ii. 162, 3)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">adgesto a militibus pulvere, terrae figeretur</span>
							<span class="q-oe">His þegnas mid moldan hit (a cross) gefæstnedon</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 3, 2; S. 524, 19)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Be moldan ða ðe on ðære stōwe genumene wǣron</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (3, 9; S. 533, 27)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">ground, earth, land</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. humus, rus, arvum)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">humus, rus, arvum</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Molde vel land humus, rus, arvum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. i. 41, 61: humus, 70, 12: Ælfc. Gr. 8; Som. 7, 53)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">from the grass of the ground</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Of ðære moldan tyrf</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 56 b; Th. 202, 8; Ph. 66)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">de humo</span>
							<span class="q-oe">God forþ āteāh of ðære moldan (de humo) ǣlces cynnes treōw</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Gen. 2, 9)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">rose from the grave</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Þeōda wealdend ārās of moldan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hy. 10, 34; Hy. Grn. ii. 293, 34: Exon. 120 a; Th. 460, 24; Hö. 22)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðonne of ðisse moldan men onwecniaþ, deāde of duste ārīsaþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. 227; Th. 302, 22; Sat. 604)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">humum lacte et melle fluentem</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ða moldan ðe meolce and hunige flēwþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Num. 14, 8)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the steed trod the ground</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Mearh moldan træd</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Elen. Kmbl. 109; El. 55)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">III.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">earth (the dwelling place of men)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">no man on earth might number them</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ne mihte ða on moldan man gerīman</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 104, 30: 127, 5: Cd. 202; Th. 251, 21; Dan. 567: Exon. 99 a; Th. 371, 13; Seel. 75)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">from earth to heaven</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Of moldan on ða mǣran gesceaft</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. Met. Fox 20, 561; Met. 20, 281)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">men upon earth</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Men ofer moldan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Rood Kmbl. 23; Kr. 12: Hy. 3, 12; Hy. Grn. ii. 281, 12: Exon. 50 b; Th. 176, 2; Gū. 1203)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Meotud ða moldan gesette</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (56a; Th. 198, 15; Ph. 10)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:græs-molde" class="xref-target">græs-molde</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="wāg-hrægel" d:title="wāg-hrægel">
		<body>
			<h1>wāg-hrægel<span class="pron"> | wɑːɣ.xræ.Gel |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>neuter noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A wall-covering, a curtain, veil (of the temple)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">velum templi</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Wāghrægl (-hrǣl, Rush.) temples velum templi</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Mk. Skt. Lind. 15, 38)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Wāghrǣl (-hrægl, Rush.)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lk. Skt. Lind. 23, 45)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Wāghruhel</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. Kmbl. Lind. 27, 51)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Bitwih wāghrǣle (wǣghrægle, Rush.)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lk. Skt. Lind. 11, 51)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:wāg-rift" class="xref-target">wāg-rift</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="efn" d:title="efn">
		<body>
			<h1>efn<span class="pron"> | efn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Even, equal</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. æquus, plānus, æquālis)</span>
					</p>
					<ol class="sub-senses">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sub-heading">On efn, adv.</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">Together</span>
								<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. simul, ūna)</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-en">Together</span>
									<span class="q-la">simul, ūna</span>
									<span class="q-oe">On efn</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 116, 1)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sub-heading">On efn, prep.</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">On even ground, by, near, aside with</span>
								<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. in æquāli, juxta)</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">On efn</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Beo. Th. 5798; B. 2903)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:efen" class="xref-target">efen</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="līn-wyrt" d:title="līn-wyrt">
