<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="eaxl-gestealla" d:title="eaxl-gestealla">
		<body>
			<h1>eaxl-gestealla<span class="pron"> | æ͜ɑksl.Ge.stæ͜ɑl.lɑ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">a competitor(?)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">cum aemulo</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Mid exlistealle</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hpt. Gl. 405, 33)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="mearc-hlinc" d:title="mearc-hlinc">
		<body>
			<h1>mearc-hlinc<span class="pron"> | mæ͜ɑrk.xlink |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A boundary hlinc (q. v.)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Eāst tō mearchlince; and swā eāst be ðæs bisceopes mearce, . . . be Byrhtswȳðe mearce</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (C. D. vi. 33, 32)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:hlinc" class="xref-target">hlinc</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="gōd" d:title="gōd">
		<body>
			<h1>gōd<span class="pron"> | goːd |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">GOOD</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. bonus)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the goodness of the good is his own good</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Þæs gōdan gōdnes biþ his āgen gōd</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 37, 3; Fox 190, 14)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">bonus homo de bono thesauro profert bona</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gōd mann sōþlīce of gōdum goldhorde bringþ gōd forþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. Bos. 12, 35)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">a Nazareth potest aliquid boni esse?</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Mæg ǣnig þing gōdes beōn of Nazareth</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Jn. Bos. 1, 46)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">Christ who is ever good, though we are weak</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Crist, seðe ǣfre is gōd ðeāh ðe we wāce sindon</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. ii. 48, 20)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">there was bishop Heahmund slain and many good men</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðǣr wearþ Heāhmund bisceop ofslægen and fela gōdra monna</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 871; Erl. 74, 34)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the men put them to flight and slew a good part of them</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Þa men hie gefliēmdon and hira gōdne dǣl ofslōgon</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (921; Erl. 106, 24: 913; Erl. 102, 7)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">take good handfuls of leaves of githcorn</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Genim giþcornes leāfa gode handfulle</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. M. ii. 65, 1; Lchdm. ii. 292, 10)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">quam dulcia faucibus meis eloquia tua</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Me is on gōmum gōd and swēte ðīn āgen word</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 118, 103)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">bonum est confiteri domino</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gōd is ðæt man Drihtne andette</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (91, 1: 134, 1)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">a king and queen shall be liberal</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Cyning and cwēn sceolon geofum gōd wesan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 90 a; Th. 338, 35; Gn. Ex. 84)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">there is no man so good in his qualities</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Nis mon his gifena ðæs gōd</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (82 a; Th. 308, 15; Seef. 40)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">he is good as a friend</span>
							<span class="q-oe">He is to freōnde gōd</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (67 a; Th. 248, 28; Jul. 102)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">we stood there a good while</span>
							<span class="q-oe">We ðǣr gōde hwīle stōdon</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Rood Kmbl. 140; Kr. 70)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the ruler of life will repay them that with benefits</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Him ðæt geleānaþ līfes waldend gōdum dǣdum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 117 a; Th. 450, 13; Dōm. 87)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">to please God by good deeds</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Þurh gōde dǣda Gode līcian</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Blickl. Homl. 129, 34)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">to those who are of goodwill</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðām ðe gōdes willan sȳn</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (93, 10: 37, 27)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">to set an example of good life</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gōdes līfes bysene onstellan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (81, 6)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">he was of very noble and good birth</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Wæs he swīðe æþelra gebyrda and gōdra</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (211, 19)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">good singers</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gōde sangeras</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (207, 31)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="on-slûpan" d:title="on-slûpan">
		<body>
			<h1>on-slûpan<span class="pron"> | on.sl, pɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">to unloose, untie</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">dissolvere</span>
							<span class="q-oe">þâ þwangas þâra scôna ongunnon heom sylfe onslûpan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Gr. D. 221, 23)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="āwegan" d:title="āwegan">
		<body>
			<h1>āwegan<span class="pron"> | ɑː.we.ɣɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -wæg, sg: -wæh, pl: -wǣgon</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -wegen</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to lift up, take or carry away</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. levare, auferre)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">they shall ever advise peace, which the unblest have before taken away</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hī ā sibbe gelǣraþ, ða ǣr wonsǣlge awegen habbaþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 89 a ; Th. 334, 25; Gn. Ex. 21: Homl. Th. i. 308, 17)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to weigh out, weigh to any one</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. appendere)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">Abraham appendit quadringentos siclos argenti</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Abraham ðā awæh feōwer hund scillinga seolfres</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Gen. 23, 16)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">utinam appenderentur peccata mea et calamitas in statera</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Eālā gif mīne synna and mīn yrmþ wǣron awegene on ānre wǣgan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Job 6, 2 ; Thw. 167, 18)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To move, shake</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Aweged</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 12; Fox 36, 18)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:āwecgan" class="xref-target">āwecgan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ā-hiltan" d:title="ā-hiltan">
		<body>
			<h1>ā-hiltan<span class="pron"> | ɑː.xil.tɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -te</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To make to halt, to cripple a person's movement</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">qui cogitaverunt supplantare gressus meos</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Þā on hyge þōhtan þæt hī āhyltan mē and mīnne gang</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 139, 5)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="cniht-gebeorþor" d:title="cniht-gebeorþor">
		<body>
			<h1>cniht-gebeorþor<span class="pron"> | knixt.Ge.be͜or.θor |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>neuter noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -gebeorþres</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A boy-bearing, child-bearing</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. pueri partus)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">in child-bearing she continued ever immaculate</span>
							<span class="q-oe">On ðæm cnihtgebeorþre heō ā clǣne þurhwunode</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Blick. 3, 12)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ā-hildendlic" d:title="ā-hildendlic">
		<body>
			<h1>ā-hildendlic<span class="pron"> | ɑː.xil.dend.liK |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Ready to incline</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Sume (conjunctions) synd gehātene inclinativae, þæt is on Englisc āhyldendlice</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. Gr. Z. 265, 1)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="hord-ern" d:title="hord-ern">
		<body>
			<h1>hord-ern<span class="pron"> | xord.ern |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">proma cella prumptuaria</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Hordren proma cella prumptuaria.</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Hpt. 33, 245, 41)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">monachus qui cellarium tenebat</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Se munuc þe ꝥ hordern heōld monachus qui cellarium tenebat (cf. Hml. Th. ii. 178, 22 under hordere)</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Gr. D. 159, 15)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-cirran" d:title="ge-cirran">
