	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="-estre" d:title="-estre">
		
		<body>
			<h1>-estre<span class="pron"> | e.stre |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -an</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">are the feminine terminations of nouns of action, same as the Latin -ix and English -ess</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Fiðelestre a female fiddler</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. 73, 62)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">hleāpestre a female dancer</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (73, 71)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">lǣrestre an instructress</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">meretrix vel scortum</span>
							<span class="q-oe">myltestre</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. 86, 72)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">rǣdistre a female reader</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. 72, 7)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">sangestre [MS. sangystre] a songstress</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. 72, 5)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">seāmestre a seamstress</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (74, 13)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-mǣre" d:title="ge-mǣre">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-mǣre<span class="pron"> | je.mæː.re |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>neuter noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es, nominative pl: -a, nominative pl: -o, nominative pl: -u</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">An end, boundary, termination, limit</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. finis)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gemǣro limes</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. Gr. 9; Som. 11, 16)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">terminum posuisti</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gemǣre ðū settest</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Spl. 103, 10)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">terminum non transgredientur</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ne māgon hī ofer gemǣre gegangan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 103, 10)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">in confinio Huicciorum et occidentalium Saxonum</span>
							<span class="q-oe">On Hwicna gemǣre and West-Sexna</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 2, 2; S. 502, 7 : 5, 23; S. 646, 25 : Exon. 93 a; Th. 349, 28; Sch. 53)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">terminos terræ</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gemǣro eorðan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Spl. 2, 8)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">usque ad terminos</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ōþ gemǣru</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (71, 8)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">these are the land's boundaries</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðis sind ðæs londes gemǣra</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Kmbl. Cod. Dipl. iii. 78, 20)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">metas sui cursus implevit</span>
							<span class="q-oe">He ða gemǣro his rynes gefylde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 3, 20; S. 550, 25)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">omnes fines terræ</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Eall eorðan gemǣru</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 66, 6 : 73, 16)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">mare magnum et spatiosum</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Mycel sǣ and on gemǣrum wīd</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (103, 24)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">in finibus eorum</span>
							<span class="q-oe">On gemǣru</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (104, 27 : Bt. Met. Fox 29, 17; Met. 29, 9 : Th. Apol. 9, 14)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">tell this people not to cross the bounds</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Cȳð ðis folc ðæt hīg ne gān ofer ða gemǣro</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exod. 19, 21, 12)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="hand-wyrst" d:title="hand-wyrst">
		
		<body>
			<h1>hand-wyrst<span class="pron"> | xɑnd.wyrst |</span>
			</h1>
