	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="gaful-rǣden" d:title="gaful-rǣden">
		
		<body>
			<h1>gaful-rǣden<span class="pron"> | gɑ.ful.ræː.den |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A tax, tribute</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. census, tribūtum)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the children paid the tax</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ða byre onguldon gafulrǣdenne the children paid the tax</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon, 47 a; Th. 161, 16; Gū. 959 : 73 b; Th. 274, 7; Jul. 529 : Andr. Kmbl. 591; An. 296)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:gafol-rǣden" class="xref-target">gafol-rǣden</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="lād-leās" d:title="lād-leās">
		<body>
			<h1>lād-leās<span class="pron"> | lɑːd.læ͜ɑːs |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Innocent, harmless, free from harm or annoyance</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gif hē lāðleās [MS. H. ladleas] beō sēce swylcne hlāford swylcne hē wille forðȳ ðe ic an ðæt ǣlc ðara ðe lāðleās [MS. H. ladleas] beō folgie swylcum hlāforde swylcum hē wille</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. Ath. iv. 1; Th. 1, 220, 24-222, 1)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Lāðleāse immunes</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 43, 68)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="tylung" d:title="tylung">
		<body>
			<h1>tylung<span class="pron"> | ty.lung |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:tilung" class="xref-target">tilung</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="gearwian" d:title="gearwian">
		
		
		
		
		<body>
			<h1>gearwian<span class="pron"> | Gæ͜ɑr.wi.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -ode, sg: -ade, sg: -ede</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -od, past participle sg: -ad, past participle sg: -ed</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To make ready, prepare, procure, supply, put on, clothe</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. pārāre, præpārāre, præstāre, induere, vestīre)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">præibis ante faciem Domini, pārāre vias ejus</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðū gǣst befōran Drihtnes ansȳne, his wegas gearwian</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lk. Bos. 1, 76 : Exon. 58 b; Th. 210, 21; Ph. 189 : 119 a : Th. 456, 27; Hy. 4, 73 : Elen. Kmbl. 1997; El. 1000)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">sapientiam præstans parvulis</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Wīsdōm oððe snytro gearwiende lytlingum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Spl. 18, 8)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">usque in æternum præpārābo sēmen tuum</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ōþ on ēcnysse ic gearwie sǣd ðīn</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (88, 4)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">he prepares life's way for souls</span>
							<span class="q-oe">He līfes weg gǣstum gearwaþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 34 a; Th. 108. 11; Gū. 71 : 117 a; Th. 450, 21; Dōm. 91)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">pārāvi lucernam Christo meo</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic gearwode leōhtfæt cyninge mīnum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Spl. 131, 18)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">præstitisti decori meo virtūtem</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðū gearwodest wlite mīnum mægn</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (29, 8)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">laqueum pārāvērunt pedibus meis</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Grinu hī gearwodon fōtum mīnum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Spl. 56, 8)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">to one a wondrous skill in goldsmith's art is provided</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Sumum wundorgiefe þurh goldsmiþe gearwad weorþeþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 88 a; Th. 331, 25; Vy. 73)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">let us prepare before ourselves a green path to the angels above</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gearwian us togēnes grēne strǣte up to englum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. 219; Th. 282, 15; Sat. 287)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">quid induamini</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hū gē eōwic gearwige</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. Kmbl. Rush. 6, 25 : 27, 29)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the very water did reverence before his feet</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt selfe wæter ðegnunge gearwode beforan his fōtum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (St. And. 22, 19)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:āgearwian" class="xref-target">āgearwian</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge-gearwian" class="xref-target">ge-gearwian</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="tȳma" d:title="tȳma">
		<body>
			<h1>tȳma<span class="pron"> | tyː.mɑ |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:tīma" class="xref-target">tīma</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="æcer-weg" d:title="æcer-weg">
		<body>
			<h1>æcer-weg<span class="pron"> | æ.Ker.wej |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A field-road</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Andlang æcerweges . . . eft on ðone æcerweg</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (C. D. vi. 137, 17, 22)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ā-syndran" d:title="ā-syndran">
		<body>
			<h1>ā-syndran<span class="pron"> | ɑː.syn.drɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge-ā" class="xref-target">ge-ā</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-glengan" d:title="ge-glengan">
		
		
		<body>
			<h1>ge-glengan<span class="pron"> | je.glen.gɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -glengde, sg: -glencde</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -glenged, past participle sg: -glencged, past participle sg: -glengd, past participle sg: -glend</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To adorn, embellish, set in order, compose</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. ornāre, cōmere, compōnere)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">ye priests should religiously observe your order, and always adorn it with good habits</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gē preōstas sculon eōwerne hād healdan ārwurþlīce, and mid gōdum þeāwum symle geglæncan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. Ælf. P. 5; Th. ii. 366, 2)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic geglenge cōmo</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. Gr. 28, 4; Som. 31, 13)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic smicere geglengce orno</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. Gl. 99; Som. 76, 116; Wrt. Voc. 54, 58)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">Nero adorned himself with gems of every kind</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Nerōn hine mid ǣlces cynnes gimmum geglengde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 28; Fox 100, 27 : Bt. Met. Fox 15, 7; Met. 15, 4)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">hoc ipse post pusillum verbis poeticis maxima suavitate et compunctione compositis, in sua, id est, Anglorum lingua proferret</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt he æfter medmiclum fæce in sceōpgereorde mid ða mǣstan swētnesse and inbrydnesse geglencde, and in Englisc gereorde wel gehwǣr forþbrohte</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 4, 24; S. 596, 35)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">quod bonis lapidibus et donis ornatum esset</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt hit wǣre geglenged mid gōdum stānum and gōdum gifum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lk. Bos. 21, 5 : Elen. Kmbl. 179; El. 90)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Geglenged discriminātus</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. Gl. 61; Som. 68, 48; Wrt. Voc. 39, 32)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">God's church is adorned with precious ornament</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Godes gelaðung is geglencged mid deōrwurþre frætewunge</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. ii. 586, 17)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">it was embellished by the miracles of God</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Heō wæs geglengd þurh Godes wundra</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Th. Diplm. A. D. 970; 241, 6)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">who are greatly adorned with swords and belts</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ða biōþ sweordum and fetelum swīðe geglende</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. Met. Fox 25, 20; Met. 25, 10)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="-flōwedlicness" d:title="-flōwedlicness">
		<body>
			<h1>-flōwedlicness<span class="pron"> | floː.wed.li.kness |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ofer-f" class="xref-target">ofer-f</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="bæceþ" d:title="bæceþ">
		<body>
			<h1>bæceþ<span class="pron"> | bæ.Keθ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">baketh, = baceþ, 3rd sing. pres. of bacan</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:bacan" class="xref-target">bacan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="āhērian" d:title="āhērian">
		<body>
			<h1>āhērian<span class="pron"> | ɑː.xeː.ri.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -ede</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -ed</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To praise fully, celebrate enough</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. plene laudare, satis celebrare)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">not any men can fully praise thee</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ne mæg ðē ahērian hæleða ǣnig</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hy. 3, 10; Hy. Grn. ii. 281, 10; prec. 3 ad calcem Cœdm. l. 5)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="hwāstrung" d:title="hwāstrung">
		
		<body>
			<h1>hwāstrung<span class="pron"> | xwɑː.strung |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A whispering, murmuring, muttering</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">per susurrationem</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Þurh hwāstrunge</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Confess. Peccat.)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">murmur multus</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Huǣstrung micel</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Jn. Skt. Lind. 7, 12)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="dolh-bōt" d:title="dolh-bōt">
		
		<body>
			<h1>dolh-bōt<span class="pron"> | dolx.boːt |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A wound-fine or compensation for a wound</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. vulneris compensatio)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Bēte dolgbōte [dolhbōte MS. H.] let him make compensation for the wound</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. Alf. pol. 23; Th. i. 78, 7)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="mōd-sefa" d:title="mōd-sefa">
		<body>
			<h1>mōd-sefa<span class="pron"> | moːd.se.fɑ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -an</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">The inner man, mind, spirit, soul, heart</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">that thy mind would be mightier and far fairer thy body</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt ðīn mōdsefa māra wurde and ðīn līchoma leōhtra micle</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. 25; Th. 32, 10; Gen. 501)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">greatly then was his heart gladdened</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðā wæs mōdsefa miclum geblissod</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Andr. Kmbl. 1783; An. 894: Elen. Kmbl. 1748; El. 876)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">my soul longed to be gone</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Wæs mōdsefa āfȳsed on forþwege</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Rood Kmbl. 246; Kr. 124)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">you please me</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Mē ðīn mōdsefa līcaþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Beo. Th. 3711; B. 1853)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">his heart did not fail</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ne gemealt him se mōdsefa</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (5249; B. 2628)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">hell had they in mind</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Helle gemundon in mōdsefan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (362; B. 182)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic ne mētte on mōdsefan māran snyttro</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Andr. Kmbl. 1107; An. 554)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ne sceal se Dryhtnes þeōw in his mōdsefan (in his heart) māre gelufian eorþan ǣhtwelan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 38a; Th. 125, 22; Gū. 358: 66b; Th. 247, 1; Jul. 72)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">dicet homo</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Man cweþeþ on his mōdsefan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 57, 10)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">On mōdseofan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (115, 2)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">to open one's heart to another</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Mōdsefan āsecgan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 76b; Th. 287, 6; Wand. 10)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">he his soul surely stablished</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē his mōdsefan fæste trymede</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (46b; Th. 159, 26; Gū. 933: Andr. Kmbl. 2420; An. 1211)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">after he knew my heart</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Syððan hē mōdsefan mīnne cūðe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Beo. Th. 4028; B. 2012: Exon. 54a; Th. 188, 24; Az. 50)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Beōþ mōdsefan dālum gedǣled, sindon dryhtguman ungelīce</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (83b; Th. 314, 29; Mōd. 21)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="un-druncen" d:title="un-druncen">
		<body>
			<h1>un-druncen<span class="pron"> | un.drun.Ken |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Not drunk, sober</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">he recognized his own folly so much better as he was more sober</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē suā micle bet his āgen dysig oncnēw suā hē undruncenra wæs</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 40; Swt. 295, 8)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="berþ" d:title="berþ">
		<body>
			<h1>berþ<span class="pron"> | berθ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">a birth</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:berþ-estre" class="xref-target">berþ-estre</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:berþ-ling" class="xref-target">berþ-ling</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:beorþ" class="xref-target">beorþ</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="hand-seax" d:title="hand-seax">
		<body>
			<h1>hand-seax<span class="pron"> | xɑnd.sæ͜ɑks |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>neuter noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A short sword, dagger</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. sicam bicipitem)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">habebat sicam bicipitem</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hæfde hē twigecgede handseax</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 2, 9; S. 511, 15)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">habentes in manibus vomeres</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hæfdon handseax on heora handa</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (5, 13; S. 633, 16)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">God's angel stood with a dagger</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Godes engel stōd mid handsexe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. ii. 272, 17)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">a dagger worth eighty mancuses of gold</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ān handsecs on hundeahtotigan mancysan goldes</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Th. Chart. 501, 3: 502, 16)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Handsex</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (527, 8)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="grōwnes" d:title="grōwnes">
		<body>
			<h1>grōwnes<span class="pron"> | groːw.nes |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">flourishing condition, prosperity</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">vobis deus talem dabit fructum qualem nunquam habuerunt prophetae</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Drihten ingc syleð swā myccle grōwnysse on ingcran beorðre swā hē nǣfre nǣnigan hālgan ǣr ne sealde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. A. 124, 257)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">offspring (?)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">genitrix, gentis, germine</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Flind genitrix, mīnes cynnes gentis, mid mīnre grōwnesse germine</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 41, 71-73)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="scearn-wifel" d:title="scearn-wifel">
		<body>
			<h1>scearn-wifel<span class="pron"> | ʃæ͜ɑrn.wi.fel |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A dung-beetle</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. scarabeus)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Scearnwifel (-fifel, MS.) scarabeus</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. i. 23, 69)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="heoru-grim" d:title="heoru-grim">
		<body>
			<h1>heoru-grim<span class="pron"> | xe͜o.ru.grim |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Very fierce or cruel, savage</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="DǢD" d:title="DǢD">
		<body>
			<h1>DǢD<span class="pron"> | dæːd |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -dǣde, dative sg: -dǣde, accusative sg: -dǣde, accusative sg: -dǣd, nominative pl: -dǣda, nominative pl: -dǣde, accusative pl: -dǣda, accusative pl: -dǣde</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A DEED, action</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. actio, actus, factum)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">actio</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Dǣd actio</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. Gr. 9, 3; Som. 8, 38: actus, 11; Som. 15, 12)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">according as the deed may be</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Be ðam ðe seō dǣd sȳ according as the deed may be</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. Eth. v. 31; Th. i. 312, 10: vi. 38; Th. i. 324, 23: L. C. E. 3; Th. i. 360, 13)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the goodly deed</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Seō ārfæste dǣd</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 3, 6; S. 528, 22: Cd. 28; Th. 37, 24; Gen. 594: 226; Th. 301, 4; Sat. 576: Bt. Met. Fox 9, 36; Met. 9, 18: Chr. 1036; Erl. 165, 11; Ælf. Tod. 6)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">they inhabited a land more barren than the first settlement was, which they, after their deed, were driven from</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gesǣton land unspēdigran ðonne se frumstōl wæs, ðe hie, æfter dǣde, ofadrifen wurdon</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. 46; Th. 59, 15; Gen. 964)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">for that deed</span>
							<span class="q-oe">For ðære dǣde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (125; Th. 159, 23; Gen. 2639: 126; Th. 161, 24; Gen. 2670)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">she urged him to that dark deed</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hiō speōn hine on ða dimman dǣd</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (32; Th. 43, 3; Gen. 685)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">he must expiate the deed</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Sceolde he dǣd ongyldan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (15; Th. 19, 23; Gen. 295: 17; Th. 20, 15; Gen. 309: 25; Th. 32, 23; Gen. 507: Beo. Th. 5772; B. 2890: Elen. Kmbl. 772; El. 386)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the deponent verbs signify action</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ða alecgendlīcan word getācniaþ dǣde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. Gr. 19; Som. 22, 56)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">I wrestle; here is action</span>
							<span class="q-la">luctor</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic wraxlige I wrestle; luctor, hēr is dǣd here is action</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (19; Som. 22, 57)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">with this deed</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Mid ðisre dǣde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. i. 218, 7: Exon. 103 b; Th. 393, 8; Rä. 12, 7)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">deeds are not dark to him</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ne sindon him dǣda dyrne</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (23 a; Th. 65, 5; Cri. 1050: 39 b; Th. 130, 12; Gū. 437)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">that his good deeds be more prevailing than his misdeeds</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt his gōde dǣda swȳðran wearþan ðonne misdǣda</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 959; Erl. 121, 5)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">men's deeds shall be open</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Opene weorþaþ monna dǣde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 23 a; Th. 64, 34; Cri. 1047)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">thou shalt expiate the error of thy deeds</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðū scealt þrōwian ðīnra dǣda gedwild</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. 43; Th. 57, 2; Gen. 922: 188; Th. 233, 27; Dan. 282: Bd. pref; S. 471, 13: Exon. 53 a; Th. 185, 16; Az. 8)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">although he were daring in every deed</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðeāh ðe he dǣda gehwæs dyrstig wǣre</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Beo. Th. 5668; B. 2838: Elen. Kmbl. 2563; El. 1283)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">in his deeds</span>
							<span class="q-oe">In his dǣdum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 82 a; Th. 308, 17; Seef. 41: 76 a; Th. 284, 34; Jul. 707: Cd. 29; Th. 38, 6; Gen. 602: Chr. 755; Erl. 49, 21)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the Lord himself will hear of the deeds</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Wile Dryhten sylf dǣda gehȳran</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 99 b; Th. 372, 14; Seel. 91: Beo. Th. 393; B. 195)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">facta ejus intellexerunt</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Dǣda his hī ongeāton</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Spl. 63, 10)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">that we consider the deeds of the pious</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt we ǣfæstra dǣde dēmen</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 40 a; Th. 133, 31; Gū. 498: 44 a; Th. 148, 13; Gū. 744: Ps. Th. 118, 17, 43)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">by good deeds</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gōdum dǣdum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. 74; Th. 91, 5; Gen. 1507: 91; Th. 116, 14; Gen. 1936: Exon. 53 a; Tb. 185, 5; Az. 3: Ps. Th. 104, 7: 124, 1: 135, 3)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ǣr-dǣd" class="xref-target">ǣr-dǣd</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:bealu-" class="xref-target">bealu-</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:deōfol-" class="xref-target">deōfol-</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:ellen-" class="xref-target">ellen-</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:fācen-" class="xref-target">fācen-</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:firen-" class="xref-target">firen-</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:gleō-" class="xref-target">gleō-</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:gōd-" class="xref-target">gōd-</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:gu-" class="xref-target">gu-</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:iu-" class="xref-target">iu-</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:lof-" class="xref-target">lof-</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:mægen-" class="xref-target">mægen-</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:mis-" class="xref-target">mis-</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:oncȳþ-" class="xref-target">oncȳþ-</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:syn-" class="xref-target">syn-</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:weā-" class="xref-target">weā-</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:wel-" class="xref-target">wel-</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:wom-" class="xref-target">wom-</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:won-" class="xref-target">won-</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:yfel-" class="xref-target">yfel-</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-stīran" d:title="ge-stīran">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-stīran<span class="pron"> | je.stiː.rɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -de</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -ed</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To correct, restrain</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. corrigere, cohibere)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">in order that the punishments might restrain others from daring to do so</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Forðæm ðæt ða wītu gestīrdon [gestīrden, MS. Cot.] ōðrum ðæt hī swā dōn ne dorsten</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 39, 11; Fox 230, 7)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge-stȳran" class="xref-target">ge-stȳran</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="biter-līce" d:title="biter-līce">
		<body>
			<h1>biter-līce<span class="pron"> | bi.ter.liː.tʃe |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adverb</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Swīþe bitterlīce (biter- v. l.) weōpende</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Gr. D. 140, 12)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Ðæt rēðe flōd biterlīce (amare) bærnð ðā earman sāula</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Dōm. L. 166)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Wearð seō mōder biterlīce gegremod</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. Th. ii. 30, 3)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-wemmendlic" d:title="ge-wemmendlic">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-wemmendlic<span class="pron"> | je.wem.mend.liK |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Corrupting, polluting</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">commentis lenocinnantibus, i. maculantibus (illectus)</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Mid gewemmendlicum hīwungum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (An. Ox. 2912)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="twī" d:title="twī">
