<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ā-wreōn" d:title="ā-wreōn">
		<body>
			<h1>ā-wreōn<span class="pron"> | ɑː.wre͜oːn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -wrāh, pl: -wrigon</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -wrigen</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Be þǣre deōpnysse þe him Drihten āwreāh</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. T. Grn. 13, 1)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Swefne sint gewisse, nelle þū āwreōn</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lch. iii. 186, 19)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">in apocalypsi</span>
							<span class="q-oe">On āwrigenre bēc</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (An. Ox. 5178)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
					<ol class="sub-senses">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sub-heading">in the Lindisfarne Gospels the verb means to cover</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">to cover</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">cooperuimus</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Wē āwrigon</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. 25, 38)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">operuistis</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Āwrigon giē</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (43)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">uelauerunt</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Āwrigon</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Lk. 22, 64)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">operite</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Āwuriāð</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (23, 30)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">operit</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Āwriā</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (8, 16)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">uelatum</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Āwrigen</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (9, 45)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">opertum</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Āwrigen</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (12, 2)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">obscuratum</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Fore āwrigen</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (23, 45)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ā-wrīhan" class="xref-target">ā-wrīhan</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:ā-wriōhan" class="xref-target">ā-wriōhan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-smyltan" d:title="ge-smyltan">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-smyltan<span class="pron"> | je.smyl.tɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -te</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -ed</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To appease, quiet</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. plācāre)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">tumida æquora plācāvit</span>
							<span class="q-oe">He ðone aþundenan sǣ gesmylte</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 5, 1; S. 614, 8)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-wildan" d:title="ge-wildan">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-wildan<span class="pron"> | je.wil.dɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">to exercise power over, rule over</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge-wyldan" class="xref-target">ge-wyldan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="berige" d:title="berige">
		<body>
			<h1>berige<span class="pron"> | be.ri.Ge |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -an</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A berry, grape</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:berie II" class="xref-target">berie II</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="þeōf-feng" d:title="þeōf-feng">
		<body>
			<h1>þeōf-feng<span class="pron"> | θe͜oːf.feng |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Seizing of thieves</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. comprehensio (or captio) furis (-um))</span>
					</p>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">The word seems to denote the obligation of one who holds land to arrest and bring to justice those who committed theft on that land, and occurs generally in connection with the burdens from which land, when granted, was relieved</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ic forgyfe ðisne freōls tō ðære hālgan stōwe æt Scīreburnan, ðæt hit sȳ gefreōd alra cynelīcra and alra dōmlīcra þeōwdōma, ge þeōffenges ge ǣghwelcre [un]iēðnesse ealles worldlīces broces, nymðe fyrde and bryceweorces</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Chart. Th. 125, 11)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ðæt hit (the monastery at Horton) sȳ gefreōd ealra cynelīcra and ealdordōmlīcra þeōwdōma, ge þeōffengces ge ǣghwylcere uneāðnesse ealles woroldlīces broces būton fyrdsōcne and burhgcweorce and bryggeweorce</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (389, 28)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">In other passages, however, the word implies advantage, and seems to refer to the right to receive the fines which might be exacted in case of conviction for theft</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Gif frigman stelþ ... cyning āge ðæt wīte and ealle ða ǣhtan</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (L. Ethb. 9; Th. i. 6, 2)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ealle wītu (in cases of theft) sint gelīce, .cxx. scillingas.</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (L. Alf. pol. 9; Th. i. 68, 7: L. Ath. i. 1; Th. i. 198, 23)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Gif þeuw stele ... hine man ālēse .lxx. scillingum.</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (L. Wih. 27; Th. i. 42, 20)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hine man his wergelde ālēse</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (26; Th. i. 42, 17: L. In. 12; Th. i. 110, 8)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Concedo consuetudines, ut ab omnibus apertius et plenius intelligantur Anglice scriptas, scilicet, mundbryce, feardwītæ, fihtwīte ... þiēfphang, hangwīte, gryðbryce ... toll et teām, aliasque omnes consuetudines quae ad me pertinent</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Chart. Th. 384, 24)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="hwanan" d:title="hwanan">
		
		
		<body>
			<h1>hwanan<span class="pron"> | xwɑ.nɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adverb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">Whence</span>
					</p>
					<ol class="sub-senses">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sub-heading">in direct questions</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Interrogativa synd āxigendlīce, unde hwanan</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. Gr. 38; Som. 41, 58)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">unde habet zizania?</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Hwanon hæfde hē coccel</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. Kmbl. 13, 27)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">unde hoc sciam?</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Hwanun wāt ic þis</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Lk. Skt. 1, 18)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-en">how should you speak in Hebrew?</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Hwanone sceoldest ðū specan on Hebrēisc</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Nicod. 4; Thw. 2. 27)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">Whence</span>
					</p>
					<ol class="sub-senses">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sub-heading">in dependent clauses</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">investigantes unde vel quis esset</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Hī spyredan hwæt and hwonan hē wæs</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 1, 33; S. 499, 12)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-en">I know not whence is his coming</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Ic ne wāt hwonon his cyme sindon</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 50 b; Th. 175, 18; Gū. 1196)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hwanan</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Beo. Th. 4798; B. 2403)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-en">he had not means to pay his 'wer,'</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Ðā næfde hē hwanon hē his wer āgulde</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Chart. Th. 207, 36)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ǣg-hwanon" class="xref-target">ǣg-hwanon</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge-hwanon" class="xref-target">ge-hwanon</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:nā-hwanon" class="xref-target">nā-hwanon</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:ō-hwanon" class="xref-target">ō-hwanon</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="wæscestre" d:title="wæscestre">
		<body>
			<h1>wæscestre<span class="pron"> | wæ.ʃe.stre |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -an</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">One who washes</span>
					</p>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(l)</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">used of a man</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Iobinus wæs mīn wæscestre (fullo)</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Gr. D. 191, 23 : 192)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(2)</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">of a woman</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hē wæs lufigende his wæscestran (presbyteram) swā swā his āgne swuster . . . þā þā hine geseah seō his wæscestre</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Gr. D. 276, 1-14)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="stærling" d:title="stærling">
		<body>
			<h1>stærling<span class="pron"> | stær.ling |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A starling</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. sturnus)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Stærlinc sturnus</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hpt. 33, 241, 54)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="be-gēton" d:title="be-gēton">
		<body>
			<h1>be-gēton<span class="pron"> | be.Geː.ton |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">begot; p. of be-gitan</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">be-gēton</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. 223; Th. 294, 20; Sat. 474)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:be-gitan" class="xref-target">be-gitan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="læs" d:title="læs">
		
		<body>
			<h1>læs<span class="pron"> | læs |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adverb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">adv. or conj.</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Næfð nān man tō þæs hāl eāgan þæt hē ǣni hwīle mage lōcigan ongeān þas sunnan þe wē hǣr geseōð, and hūru þæs þe lǣs (all the less) gyf heō hefð unhāle</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Solil. H. 35, 1)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hys mē lyst swā læng swā lǣs</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (36, 17)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðū hǣtst mē forlǣtan þā unrōtnesse, ðȳ lǣst ic . . . þȳ mettrumra sī</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (49, 1)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">ne offenderet</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Þe lǣste ( = lǣs þe) gehremde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (An. Ox. 3675)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Þe lǣste (ne forte) beō gemētt brōþor āsolcen</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Angl. xiii. 434, 982)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">as subst.</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic oft wīscte ꝥ hyra lǣs wǣre swā gewinfulra</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Nar. 2, 29)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="lund-laga" d:title="lund-laga">
		<body>
			<h1>lund-laga<span class="pron"> | lund.lɑ.ɣɑ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -an</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Rein, kidney</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðes lundlaga hic rigen oððe ren</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. Gr. 9, 13; Som. 9, 34)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Lundlaga lien</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. 45, 14: renunculus, ii, 118, 72)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Lundlagan renunculi</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc, 44, 67: renunculæ, 65, 58)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðū nymst twegen lundlagan sumes duos renes</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ex. 29, 13: Lev. 8, 25)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:gelynd" class="xref-target">gelynd</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:gelyndu" class="xref-target">gelyndu</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="cūðest" d:title="cūðest">
		<body>
			<h1>cūðest<span class="pron"> | kuː.θest |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">knewest, couldst; 2nd pers. p. of cunnan</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:cunnan" class="xref-target">cunnan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="full-cāflīce" d:title="full-cāflīce">
		<body>
			<h1>full-cāflīce<span class="pron"> | full.kɑː.fliː.Ke |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adverb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Full quickly, very eagerly</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. velocissime)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">he very eagerly plucked the bloody dart from the chief</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Se fullcāflīce bræd of ðæm beorne blōdigne gār</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Byrht. Th. 136, 19; By. 153)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="burh-riht" d:title="burh-riht">
