			<h1>long<span class="pron"> | long |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:lang" class="xref-target">lang</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="on-rād" d:title="on-rād">
		<body>
			<h1>on-rād<span class="pron"> | on.rɑːd |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Riding on horseback</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">let them seek for themselves fatigue in riding on horseback and in a carriage</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Sēcen hiē him broc on onrāde and on wǣne</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lchdm. ii. 184, 13)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-teldung" d:title="ge-teldung">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-teldung<span class="pron"> | je.tel.dung |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A tent, tabernacle</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. tabernāculum)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">in sōle pŏsuit tabernācŭlum suum</span>
							<span class="q-oe">On sunnan gesette geteldunge his</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Spl. T. 18, 5: 26, 9)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="smeoru-þearm" d:title="smeoru-þearm">
		<body>
			<h1>smeoru-þearm<span class="pron"> | sme͜o.ru.θæ͜ɑrm |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">An entrail</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Smeruþearm extale</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 145, 29)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Smæreþerm julium (in a list 'de stiibus')</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (i. 286, 61)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="dūru" d:title="dūru">
		
		<body>
			<h1>dūru<span class="pron"> | duː.ru |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e, dative sg: -e, dative sg: -a, accusative sg: -e, accusative sg: -a, accusative sg: -u, nominative pl: -a, genitive pl: -ena, dative pl: -um, accusative pl: -a, accusative pl: -u</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">An opening, a door, the door of a house</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. ostium, jānua, fŏris)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">keep the door [opening ostium] of my lips</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Dūru ymbstandennesse welerum mīnum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Eng. versn. Ps. Lamb. 140, 3)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">clausa erat jānua</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Seō dūru wæs belocen</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. Bos. 25, l0)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">soon he rushed on the door</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Dūru sōna on arn</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Beo. Th. 1447; B. 721)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Dūra</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Andr. Kmbl. 1998; An. l001)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">cum fores essent clausæ</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðā ða dūra wǣron belocene</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Jn. Bos. 20, 19)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">from the door</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Of ðære dūra</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. Bos. 26, 71)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">januis clausis</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Belocenum dūrum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Jn. Bos. 20, 26)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:dōr" class="xref-target">dōr</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ābutan" d:title="ābutan">
		
		<body>
			<h1>ābutan<span class="pron"> | ɑː.bu.tɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adverb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">ABOUT</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. circa)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">beset the castle about</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Besæt ðone castel abūtan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 1088; Th. i. 357, 29)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">they beset the castle about</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Besǣton īone castel abūton</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 1090; Th. i. 358, 25)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="sealm-wyrhta" d:title="sealm-wyrhta">
		<body>
			<h1>sealm-wyrhta<span class="pron"> | sæ͜ɑlm.wyrx.tɑ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -an</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A psalmist</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Se psalmwyrhta (David)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. ii. 82, 32)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Sealmwyrhta</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. T. Grn. 1, 24)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ǣn-līce" d:title="ǣn-līce">
		<body>
			<h1>ǣn-līce<span class="pron"> | æːn.liː.tʃe |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adverb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">ONLY, singularly, elegantly</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. eleganter)</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="sǣdere" d:title="sǣdere">
		<body>
			<h1>sǣdere<span class="pron"> | sæː.de.re |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A sower</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. sator, seminator)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Sǣdere sator, seminator</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hpt. Gl. 461, 73)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Sum sǣdere fērde tō sāwenne his sǣd</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. ii. 88, 12: Mk. Skt. 4, 3)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Be sǣdere</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. R. S. 11; Th. i. 438, 8)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:next word" class="xref-target">next word</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-fremðian" d:title="ge-fremðian">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-fremðian<span class="pron"> | je.frem.θi.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">to curse</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. anathematizare)</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="oþþe" d:title="oþþe">
		<body>
			<h1>oþþe<span class="pron"> | oθ.θe |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>conjunction</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
					</p>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(1)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">a particle co-ordinating words, phrases, or clauses, between which there is an alternative</span>
							</p>
							<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
								<li>
									<p>
										<span class="sense-label">(a)</span>
										<span class="meaning-en">words</span>
									</p>
									<ul class="quotes">
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Feorran oððe neān</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Gen. 1047)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Ǣr oððe sīþ</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Cri. 1053)</span>
										</li>
									</ul>
								</li>
								<li>
									<p>
										<span class="sense-label">(b)</span>
										<span class="meaning-en">phrases</span>
									</p>
									<ul class="quotes">
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Wīs on gewitte oððe on wordcwidum</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Crä. 13)</span>
										</li>
									</ul>
								</li>
								<li>
									<p>
										<span class="sense-label">(c)</span>
										<span class="meaning-en">clauses</span>
									</p>
									<ul class="quotes">
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Þonne þæt mōd ymbe hwæt tweōnode, oðþe hit hwæs wilnode tō witanne</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Solil. H. 2, 22)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Hū mæg ic lādigan lāðan sprǣce oððe andsware ǣnige findan ?</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Cri. 184)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Oðþo</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 1, 27; Sch. 74, 14)</span>
										</li>
									</ul>
								</li>
							</ol>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(2)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">where an alternative is not expressed</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hē wolde fandian hū longe þæt land norþryhte lǣge, oþþe hwæðer ǣnig mon benorðan þǣm wēstenne būde</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 1, 1; S. 17, 8)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I b.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">used after hwæþer</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hwæþer sceal geeācnad wīf fulwad beōn, oððe æfter þon þe heō bearn cenneð?</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 1, 27; Sch. 75, 20)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Beseah Drihten . . . hwæðer his mihta andgyt ǣnig hæfde, oððe God wolde sēcan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 52, 3)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II b.</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Eālā, wǣre hē āuðer oððe hāt, oððe ceald</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 445, 36)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">III.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">after a primary statement, appending a secondary alternative or consequence of setting aside the primary statement</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">interrogavit eos dicens, 'Salvusne est pater vester. . . ? adhuc vivit ?</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē āxode hig hwæðer hire fæder wǣre hāl . . . oððe hwæðer hē lifode</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Gen. 43, 27)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ūt-irnende" d:title="ūt-irnende">
		<body>
			<h1>ūt-irnende<span class="pron"> | uːt.ir.nen.de |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Running out of the body</span>
					</p>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(1)</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">of medicine, purging, purgative</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Wyrtdrenc ðe ne bið ūtyrnende</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Lchdm. ii. 282, 9: 170, 25)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Sele him wyrtdrenc ūtyrnende</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (280, 17)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ūtyrnendne</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (336, 1)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Mid swelcum ūtyrnendum drencum</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (222, 25: 82, 17)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(2)</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">of a disease, diarrhoeic</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ðisse ādle fruman mon mæg gelācnian on ða ilcan wīsan ðe ða ūtyrnendan</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Lchdm. ii. 232, 17)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(3)</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">of persons, suffering from diarrhoea or dysentery</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hū mon ða ūtyrnendan men scyle lācnian</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Lchdm. ii. 278, 16)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ūt-ryne" class="xref-target">ūt-ryne</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="tȳdred" d:title="tȳdred">
		<body>
			<h1>tȳdred<span class="pron"> | tyː.dred |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Provided with offspring</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">oves eorum foetosae</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Heora sceāp wǣron swylce tydred</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 143, 17)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:tȳdran" class="xref-target">tȳdran</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="hnāh" d:title="hnāh">
		<body>
			<h1>hnāh<span class="pron"> | xnɑːx |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Bent down, low, lowly, humble, abject, mean, poor</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">adoravitque eum pronus in terram</span>
							<span class="q-oe">And hē hnāh tō eorþan āleāt wið ðæs engles</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Num. 22, 31)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">she was not mean nor too sparing of gifts</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Næs hiō hnāh ne tō gnēþ gifa</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Beo. Th. 3863; B. 1929)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">Judas said that he expected for himself humiliating pain</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Iudas cwæþ ðæt hē wēnde him trage [Kmbl. þrage] hnāgre</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Elen. Kmbl. 1333; El. 668)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">they expected the death of men, a still worse time</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Wēndon hie wera cwealmes þræge hnāgran</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Andr. Kmbl. 3195; An. 1600)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">I think myself no worse man than does Grendel himself</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Nō ic me hnāgran talige ðonne Grendel hine</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Beo. Th. 1359; B. 677)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">full oft have I appointed reward to a warrior inferior and of less worth in battle</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ful oft ic leān teohhode hnāhran rince sǣmran æt sæcce</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (1909; B. 952)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="un-līfedlic" d:title="un-līfedlic">
		
		<body>
			<h1>un-līfedlic<span class="pron"> | un.liː.fed.liK |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Unallowed, unallowable, illicit</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">ab inlicitis</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Fram unlȳuendlicum (-lēfedlicum, v.l.)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hpt. 31, 8, 131)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-wrixl" d:title="ge-wrixl">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-wrixl<span class="pron"> | je.wriksl |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Changing, vicarious</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. vicarius; alternans, aptus)</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ece" d:title="ece">
		
		<body>
			<h1>ece<span class="pron"> | e.Ke |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">An AKE, pain</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. dōlor)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">as if the bishop had borne the ake and the sore out with him</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Efne swā se bisceop ðone ece and ðæt sār mid him ut bǣre</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 5, 3; S. 616, 37: 5, 4; S. 617, 22)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:acan" class="xref-target">acan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="hēr" d:title="hēr">
		<body>
			<h1>hēr<span class="pron"> | xeːr |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adverb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Sume (adverbs) synd localia, þæt synd stōwlice, for ðan ðe hī getācniað stōwa . . . hic hēr</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. Gr. Z. 224, 15)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Sume cumað of naman speliendan, hic hēr</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (233, 9)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">in this place</span>
								<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. hic)</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Wē nabbað hēr (hic) būtun fīf hlā as</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. 14, 17)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Gōd ys ūs hēr tō beōnne</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (17, 4)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ic hēr on sōðre gewitnesse stande</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Ll. Th. i. 180, 27)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hē ārās, nis hē hēr (hīr, L.)</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Mli. 16, 6)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
							<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
								<li>
									<p>
										<span class="sub-heading">marking place to which a person has come to get something</span>
									</p>
									<ul class="quotes">
										<li>
											<span class="q-la">ut non ueniam huc haurire</span>
											<span class="q-oe">Þ UNCERTAIN ic ne durfe hēr feccan</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Jn. 4, 15)</span>
										</li>
									</ul>
								</li>
								<li>
									<p>
										<span class="sense-label">I a.</span>
										<span class="meaning-en">in this country, region, place of residence</span>
									</p>
									<ul class="quotes">
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Ūre ieldran, ðā ðe ðās stōwa ǣr hiōldon, hiē lufodon wīsdōra . . . Hēr mon mæg giēt gesiōn hiora swæð, . . . Hiē woldon ðæt hēr ðȳ māra wīsdōm on londe wǣre</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 5, 13-25)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Hē onfēhð friccan scīre and foreryneles ðā hēr iernað beforan kyningum</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (91, 21)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Hēr mid ūs</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Ph. 23 : 31)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Hēr is ǣghwylc eorl ōðrum getrȳwe</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (B. 1228)</span>
										</li>
									</ul>
								</li>
								<li>
									<p>
										<span class="sense-label">I b.</span>
										<span class="meaning-en">used with a noun qualified by this</span>
									</p>
									<ul class="quotes">
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Rufinus wolde habban him self þon anwold þǣr east, and Stileca wolde sellan his suna þisne hēr west</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 6, 37; S. 296, 7)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Hēr sægeð on þissum bōcum</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Bl. H. 45, 3)</span>
										</li>
									</ul>
								</li>
								<li>
									<p>
										<span class="sense-label">I c.</span>
										<span class="meaning-en">in answer to a call</span>
									</p>
									<ul class="quotes">
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">'Hwǣr eart þū ?' Him andwyrde ꝥ heāfod, 'Hēr, hēr, hēr, '</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. S. 32, 151)</span>
										</li>
									</ul>
								</li>
							</ol>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">in a weakened sense, more or less</span>
							</p>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="-flōwend-līce" d:title="-flōwend-līce">
		
		<body>
			<h1>-flōwend-līce<span class="pron"> | floː.wend.liː.tʃe |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ofer-f" class="xref-target">ofer-f</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="reccend" d:title="reccend">
		<body>
			<h1>reccend<span class="pron"> | rek.Kend |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">(2)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Eādgār Angla reccent (engla cyning, v. l.)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 975; P. 119, 14)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">de rectoribus</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Be reccendrum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Scint. 116, 2)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">substitutis praepositis</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē gesette gewisse prāfostas and reccendas</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Gr. D. 119, 21)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-liger" d:title="ge-liger">
		
		<body>
			<h1>ge-liger<span class="pron"> | je.li.Ger |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">adulterium</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Geligere adulterium</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 7, 76)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Ic eom ondetta sodomiscre synne þe hiē on gegyltan, þæt is geligre</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Angl. xi. 98, 21)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">prostibuli</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Geligeres prostibuli</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 65, 77)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Þurh ꝥ grimme bismergleōw þæs mānfullan geligeres</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. S. 23 b, 451)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">adulterinae cogitationis reus</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Diernes gelīres scyldig</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 143, 2)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Ealra þāra Rōmāna wīf þe hē mehte, hē tō geligre geniēdde</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 2, 2; S. 66, 29)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">haec, libidine ardens, . . . inter incessabilia stupra . . . tandem filio inceste cognito . . . praecepit ut inter parentes et filios . . . de conjugiis adpetendis . . . liberum fieret</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Sameramis . . . mid ungemetlicre wrǣnnesse manigfeald geligre fremmende wæs. . . æt nēhstan hyre āgene sunu hiō genam hyre tō geligere . . . hiō gesette . . . þæt nān forbyrd nǣre æt geligere betwuh nānre sibbe</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (l, 2; S. 30, 26-35)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">incerta (incesti ?) judicium</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Geligra wītnung</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 49, . . 9)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">ut abstineatis vos ab . . . fornicatione, Acts 15, 29</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Þ UNCERTAIN gē forberen . . . from dernum geligerum</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Ll. Th. i. 56, 26)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:dirne-geligere" class="xref-target">dirne-geligere</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="gemynd-beniming" d:title="gemynd-beniming">
		<body>
			<h1>gemynd-beniming<span class="pron"> | Ge.mynd.be.ni.ming |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge-mynd" class="xref-target">ge-mynd</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="boda" d:title="boda">
		<body>
			<h1>boda<span class="pron"> | bo.dɑ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -an</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">a messenger, ambassador, herald, apostle, angel</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. nuntius, legatus, præco, apostolus, angelus)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">O Wisdom, thou art the messenger and forerunner of true light</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Eālā Wīsdōm, ðū eart boda and fōrrynel ðæs sōðan leōhtes</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 36, 1; Fox 170, 28)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">this messenger told me in cautious words</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Me ðes boda sægde wǣrum wordum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. 32; Th. 42, 30; Gen. 680: 32; Th. 43, 6; Gen. 686: 33; Th, 45, 11; Gen. 725)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">she obeyed the advice of the loathsome messenger</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Heō ðæs lādan bodan lārum hȳrde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (33; Th. 44, 18; Gen. 711)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">nuntii nos terruerunt</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ða bodan us fǣrdon</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Deut. 1, 28: Exon. 27 a; Th. 80, 9; Cri. 1305)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">misit nuntios ante conspectum suum</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Sende he bodan befōran his ansȳne</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lk. Bos. 9, 52: Gen. 32, 3: Exon. 24 b; Th. 71, 7; Cri. 1152)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">to receive a king's ambassador</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Cyninges bodan underfōn</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lchdm. iii. 210, 15)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">verus summæ lucis præco ab omnibus prædicatur Augustinus</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Se sōda boda ðæs hean leōhtes Agustinus wæs fram him eallum bodad</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 2, 2; S. 502, 32)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">præco nautarum</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Brimmanna boda</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Byrht. Th. 133, 12; By. 49)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">heralds of war</span>
							<span class="q-la">præfeciales</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gefeohtes bodan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. Gl. 53; Som. 66, 81; Wrt, Voc. 36, 7)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">thou art the Lord's angel from heaven</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðū Drihtnes eart boda of heofnum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. 26; Th. 34, 5; Gen. 533: Elen. Kmbl. 153; El. 77)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">angels announced to the shepherds true joy</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Bodan hyrdum cȳðdon sōþne gefeān</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 14 a; Th. 28, 20; Cri. 449)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">a foreboder, prophet</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. propheta, vates)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">skilled in a prophet's prediction</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gleāw bodan ǣrcwide</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 83 a; Th. 313, 23; Mōd. 4)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ǣ-boda" class="xref-target">ǣ-boda</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:ēðel-boda" class="xref-target">ēðel-boda</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:fōr-boda" class="xref-target">fōr-boda</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:heāh-boda" class="xref-target">heāh-boda</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:nȳd-boda" class="xref-target">nȳd-boda</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:sīþ-boda" class="xref-target">sīþ-boda</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:spel-boda" class="xref-target">spel-boda</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:wil-boda" class="xref-target">wil-boda</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-teāma" d:title="ge-teāma">
		
		<body>
			<h1>ge-teāma<span class="pron"> | je.tæ͜ɑː.mɑ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -an</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">An advocate, avoucher, a warranter</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. advŏcātus, qui rei emptæ fĭdem præstat)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">I will that every man have his warranter</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic wille ðæt gehwilc man hæbbe his geteāman</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. Ed. 1; Th. i. 158, 9: L. Eth. ii. 8; Th. i. 288, 16)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:teām" class="xref-target">teām</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge-tēman" class="xref-target">ge-tēman</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="scealc" d:title="scealc">
		<body>
			<h1>scealc<span class="pron"> | ʃæ͜ɑlk |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">a servant</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">O Domine, quia ego servus tuus, ego servus tuus, et filius ancillae tuae</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Eālā ic eom ðīn āgen esne Dryhten and ðīn swylce eom scealc ombehte (cf. ambeht-scealc) and ðīure þeōwan suna</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 115, 6)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">tuus sum ego</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic eom ðīn hold scealc</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (118, 94)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Dō ðīnes scealces (servi) sāwle blīðe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (85, 3)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">in servum</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Tō scealce</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (104, 15)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">salvum fac servum tuum</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hǣl ðīnne scealc</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (85, 2: 88, 17)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">misit Moysen servum suum</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē Moyses sende his sylfes scealc</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (104, 22)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">respice in servos tuos</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Beseoh on ðīne scealcas</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (89, 18)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Babilone weard hēt his scealcas scūfan ða hyssas in bǣlblyse</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. Th. 230, 10; Dan. 231)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">as a term of reproach</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðā hine heōwon hǣðene scealcas</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Byrht. Th. 137, 5; By. 181)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hwīlum ic gehēre helle scealcas, gnorniende cynn</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. Th. 273, 8; Sat. 133)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">III.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">a man, soldier, sailor</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Scealc (Beowulf) hafaþ dǣde gefremede, ðe wē ealle ǣr ne meahton</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Beo. Th. 1883; B. 939)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Eode scealc monig swīð—nicgende tō sele searowundor seōn</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (1841; B. 918)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hū mæg ðæt gesceādwīs scealc (cf. gesceādwīs mon, Bt. 28; Fox 100, 30) gereccan, ðæt hē him ðȳ sēlra þince</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Met. 15, 14)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Brugdon scealcas (the Jews who defeated the Assyrians) of sceāðum scīrmǣled swyrd</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Judth. Thw. 24, 38; Jud. 230)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">there was no one</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Næs scealca nān</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Met. 8, 21)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">ships with their crews</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Scipu mid scealcum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. Th. 362, 3; Wal. 31)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ambeht-scealc" class="xref-target">ambeht-scealc</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:beōr-scealc" class="xref-target">beōr-scealc</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:freoðo-scealc" class="xref-target">freoðo-scealc</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="mǣg-gemōt" d:title="mǣg-gemōt">
		<body>
			<h1>mǣg-gemōt<span class="pron"> | mæːG.Ge.moːt |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>neuter noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A meeting of kinsmen</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē bebeād ofer ealne middangeard ðæt ǣlc mǣgþ tōgædere cōme, ðæt ǣlc man ðȳ gearor wiste hwǣr hē gesibbe hæfde. Ðæt tācnode ðæt on his dagum sceolde beōn geboren se se ðe ūs ealle tō ānum mǣggemōte gelaþaþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 5, 14; Swt. 248, 18)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="þeād" d:title="þeād">
		<body>
			<h1>þeād<span class="pron"> | θæ͜ɑːd |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:þeōd" class="xref-target">þeōd</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="eal-mihtig" d:title="eal-mihtig">
		<body>
			<h1>eal-mihtig<span class="pron"> | æ͜ɑl.mix.tiG |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">All-mighty</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. omnĭpŏtens)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">in the name of almighty God</span>
							<span class="q-oe">On Godes ealmihtiges naman</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Th. Diplm. A.D. 886-899; 138, 34)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:eall-mihtig" class="xref-target">eall-mihtig</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="CAMP" d:title="CAMP">
		
		<body>
			<h1>CAMP<span class="pron"> | kɑmp |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A contest, war, battle</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. certamen, pugna, bellum)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">I care not for the contest</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic ne gȳme ðæs compes</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 105b; Th. 402, 26; Rä. 21, 35)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">Dominus docet manus meas ad prælium, et digitos meos ad bellum</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Drihten tǣcþ handa mīne to gefeohte, and fingras mīne to slehte oððe to campe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Lamb. 143, 1: Bd. 3, 24; S. 556, 21: Judth. 11; Thw. 14, 21; Jud. 200: Beo. Th. 5003; B. 2505: Chr. 937; Th. 202, 2, col. 1, 2; Æðelst. 8: Andr. Kmbl. 2651; An. 1327)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">Christ has placed me in battle</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Mec gesette Crist to compe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 102b; Th. 389, 3; Rä. 7, 2: Andr. Kmbl. 468; An. 234)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">he overcame the liberty of enemies in battle</span>
							<span class="q-oe">He ofercom campe feōnda folcriht</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. 143; Th. 178, 33; Exod. 21)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:camp-dōm" class="xref-target">camp-dōm</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:camp-hād" class="xref-target">camp-hād</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:camp-rǣden" class="xref-target">camp-rǣden</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:camp-stede" class="xref-target">camp-stede</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:camp-wǣpen" class="xref-target">camp-wǣpen</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:camp-wered" class="xref-target">camp-wered</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:camp-weorud" class="xref-target">camp-weorud</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:camp-wīg" class="xref-target">camp-wīg</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:camp-wudu" class="xref-target">camp-wudu</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:comp-wǣpen" class="xref-target">comp-wǣpen</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:comp-weorod" class="xref-target">comp-weorod</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:comp-wīg" class="xref-target">comp-wīg</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="eāst-ende" d:title="eāst-ende">
		<body>
			<h1>eāst-ende<span class="pron"> | æ͜ɑːst.en.de |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">The east-end</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. pars orientālis)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">at the east-end of the wood</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Æt ðæs wuda eāst-ende</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 893; Th. 162, 28)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ān-būende" d:title="ān-būende">
		<body>
			<h1>ān-būende<span class="pron"> | ɑːn.buː.en.de |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>participle</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Dwelling alone</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. anachoreticam vitam agens)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">persecutes those dwelling alone</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Eāhteþ ānbūendra</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 33b; Th. 107, 15; Gū. 59)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="æt-standend" d:title="æt-standend">
		<body>
			<h1>æt-standend<span class="pron"> | æt.stɑn.dend |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A bystander, an attendant</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Seō heofenlice cwēn cwæð tō hire ætstandendum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. Th. i. 450, 31)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē þone Hǣlend bodode eallum ætstandendum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. S. 29, 255)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-þȳan" d:title="ge-þȳan">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-þȳan<span class="pron"> | je.θyː.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge-þeōwan" class="xref-target">ge-þeōwan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="sceard" d:title="sceard">
		<body>
			<h1>sceard<span class="pron"> | ʃæ͜ɑrd |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>neuter noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A gap, notch</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">subtract from this fourth part (of the earth) all of it that the sea has covered, and all the gaps (bays and creeks) it has taken</span>
							<span class="q-la">huic quartae, si quantum maria premunt subtraxeris</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Dō of ðam feōrþan deāle eall ðæt seō sǣ his ofseten hæfþ and eall ða sceard ðe heō him on genumen hæfþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 18, 1 ; Fox 62, 13)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:dīc-sceard" class="xref-target">dīc-sceard</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:hær-sceard" class="xref-target">hær-sceard</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="heort-hama" d:title="heort-hama">
		<body>
			<h1>heort-hama<span class="pron"> | xe͜ort.xɑ.mɑ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -an</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A covering of the heart</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Heorthama bucleamen</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. Gl. 75; Som. 71, 102; Wrt. Voc. 45, 9)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">thou shalt take the fat that covers the inwards</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðū nymst ðone hearthaman</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ex. 29, 22)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="dol-sceaða" d:title="dol-sceaða">
		<body>
			<h1>dol-sceaða<span class="pron"> | dol.ʃæ͜ɑ.θɑ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -an</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A foolish or rash robber</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. temerārius spoliātor)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">God may easily sever the doltish robber from his deeds</span>
							<span class="q-oe">God eāðe mæg ðone dolsceaðan dǣda getwǣfan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Beo. Th. 962; B. 479)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="æfter-spræc" d:title="æfter-spræc">
		
		<body>
			<h1>æfter-spræc<span class="pron"> | æf.ter.spræK |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:sprecan" class="xref-target">sprecan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="FELG" d:title="FELG">
		
		<body>
			<h1>FELG<span class="pron"> | felɣ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A FELLY, part of the circumference of a wheel</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. canthus, absis rotæ)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">one end of every spoke is fixed in the nave, the other in the felly</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ǣlces spācan biþ ōðer ende fæst on ðare nafe, ōðer on ðære felge</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 39, 7; Fox 222, 3, 7, 10)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the fellies depend on the spokes</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ða felga hangiaþ on ðām spācan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (222, 13, 19, 21, 27)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">nearer to the fellies</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Neār ðām felgum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (222, 11)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Felge [MS. felga] canthus</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. Gl. 2; Som. 55, 48; Wrt. Voc. 16, 21)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the wheel turns round, and the nave, being nearest to the axle-tree, goes much more firmly and more securely than the fellies do</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt hweōl hwerfþ ymbūton, and siō nafa, nēhst ðære eaxe, siō færþ micle fæstlīcor and orsorglīcor ðonne ða felgan dōn</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 39, 7; Fox 220, 30)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="HEBBAN" d:title="HEBBAN">
		
		<body>
			<h1>HEBBAN<span class="pron"> | xeb.bɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -hōf, pl: -hōfon</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -hafen, past participle sg: -hæfen</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To HEAVE, lift up, raise</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">expandi manus meas ad te</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic mīne handa tō ðē hebbe and þenige</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 87, 9)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">ad te levavi animam meam</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Tō ðē ic hæbbe mīn mōd</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (24, 1)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">raises itself into a lofty tree</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hine sylfne hefeþ on heāhne beām</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 57 b; Th. 205, 13; Ph.112: Ps. Th. 148, 14)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">propterea exaltabit caput</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Forðon hiora heāfod hebbaþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (l09, 8)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">ad te levavi oculos meos</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Tō ðē ic mīne eāgan hōf</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (122, 1)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">raised a loud voice</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hōfon hlūde stefne</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. 170; Th. 214, 24; Exod. 574: Exon. 45 b; Th. 156, 8; Gū. 871)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">leva manum tuam</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hefe ðū dīne handa</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 73, 4)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">levate oculos vestros</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hebbaþ upp eōwre eāgan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Jn. Skt. 4, 35)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">God has given his angels charge concerning thee, that they may preserve thee and lift thee up in their hands</span>
							<span class="q-oe">God bebeād his englum be ðē ðæt hī ðē healdon and on heora handum hebban</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. i. 516, 30)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">since I could lift hand and shield</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Siððan ic hond and rond hebban mihte</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Beo. Th. 1317; B. 656)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">he was lifted up in angels' bosoms</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē wæs upp hafen engla fæðmum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 17 a; Th. 41, 5; Cri. 651: 756; Th. 284, 7; Jul. 693)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">then was a cry raised</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Wæs wōp hæfen</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Andr. Kmbl. 2311; An. 1157: Beo. Th. 6038; B. 3023)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="hālig-dæg" d:title="hālig-dæg">
		<body>
			<h1>hālig-dæg<span class="pron"> | xɑː.liG.dæj |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A holy day, Sunday</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">of the festival of Sunday</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Be hālidæiges freōlse</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. C. S. 45; Th. i. 402, 8)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">sabbatis</span>
							<span class="q-oe">On hāligdagum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Mk. Skt. Lind. 3, 2)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="blōd-hrǣce" d:title="blōd-hrǣce">
		<body>
			<h1>blōd-hrǣce<span class="pron"> | bloːd.xræː.Ke |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A spitting of blood</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. sanguinis excreatio)</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:blōd" class="xref-target">blōd</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:hrǣce" class="xref-target">hrǣce</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="hlētan" d:title="hlētan">
		<body>
			<h1>hlētan<span class="pron"> | xleː.tɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:hlēcan" class="xref-target">hlēcan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="lencten-bere" d:title="lencten-bere">
		<body>
			<h1>lencten-bere<span class="pron"> | lenk.ten.be.re |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">spring-sown barley (?cf. lenten corne as . . . otys, pecys, barley. v. N. E. D. lenten-corn)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Nime þonne clǣnne lengten‒bere and grinde on handcwyrna</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Nap 42)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:lencten-eorþe" class="xref-target">lencten-eorþe</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="mortere" d:title="mortere">
		<body>
			<h1>mortere<span class="pron"> | mor.te.re |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A mortar</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. mortariola)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Mortere mortariola</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 58, 28)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Se ealra mǣsta mortere girba</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (42, 22: i. 20, 25)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gepuna eall tōsomne on ānum mortere</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lchdm. i. 216, 13: 142, 18)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="seuoþ" d:title="seuoþ">
		<body>
			<h1>seuoþ<span class="pron"> | se.u.oθ |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:seonoþ" class="xref-target">seonoþ</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="hræd-sprǣce" d:title="hræd-sprǣce">
		<body>
			<h1>hræd-sprǣce<span class="pron"> | xræd.spræː.Ke |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:un-hrædsprǣce" class="xref-target">un-hrædsprǣce</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="fore-teōn" d:title="fore-teōn">
		<body>
			<h1>fore-teōn<span class="pron"> | fo.re.te͜oːn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -teōde</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -teōd</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To pre-dispose, pre-ordain</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. prædispōnĕre, præordĭnāre)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">ecce nātio filiōrum tuōrum quibus dispŏsui</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Swā ðē bearn weorþaþ geboren syððan, ða ylcan ic ǣr fōreteōde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 72, 12)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">quotquot ĕrant præordĭnāti ad vītam æternam</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Swā monige swā fōreteōde wǣron to ēcum life</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 2, 14; S. 517, 36)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="dop-fugel" d:title="dop-fugel">
		<body>
			<h1>dop-fugel<span class="pron"> | dop.fu.Gel |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A dipping-fowl, a water-fowl, a moorhen</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. mergus, mergŭlus)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Dop-fugel mergus</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. 280, 12)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Dop-fugel mergŭlus</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Glos. Brux. Recd. 36, 6; Wrt. Voc. 62, 6)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="læs-boren" d:title="læs-boren">
		<body>
			<h1>læs-boren<span class="pron"> | læs.bo.ren |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Of inferior birth</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">we enjoin that any highborn priest do not despise the one of inferior birth</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Wē lǣraþ ðæt ǣnig forþboren preōst ne forseō ðone læsborenan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. Edg. C. 13; Th. ii. 246, 21)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="-lǣcness" d:title="-lǣcness">
		<body>
			<h1>-lǣcness<span class="pron"> | læː.kness |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:gelōm-lǣcness" class="xref-target">gelōm-lǣcness</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:þrīst-lǣcness" class="xref-target">þrīst-lǣcness</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="Īra-land" d:title="Īra-land">
		<body>
			<h1>Īra-land<span class="pron"> | iː.rɑ.lɑnd |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">For argument in favour of taking Iceland to be the country intended where this word is used in Ohthere's narrative see Dr. Craigie's note in Mod. Lang. Rev. vol. xii, p. 200.</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="unriht-cyst" d:title="unriht-cyst">
		<body>
			<h1>unriht-cyst<span class="pron"> | un.rixt.Kyst |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Vice, excess</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic andette ... unrihtgilp and īdel word and unrihtcysta and ǣlcne glængc (cf. ic ondette ... unnyttes gilpes bigong and īdle glengas, uncyste..., Anglia xi. 98, 27) ðe tō mīnes līchaman unrǣde ǣfre belimpe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. de Cf. 7; Th. ii. 262, 28)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="wæl-dreōr" d:title="wæl-dreōr">
		<body>
			<h1>wæl-dreōr<span class="pron"> | wæl.dre͜oːr |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">The blood of the slain</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Wæter wældreōre fāg</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Beo. Th. 3267; B. 1631)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Eorðe wældreōre (the blood of Abel) swealh of handum ðīnum (Cain's)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. Th. 62, 19; Gen. 1016)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic fylde mid folmum ordbanan Abeles, eordan sealde wældreōr weres</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (67, 9; Gen. 1098)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="giþ-corn" d:title="giþ-corn">
		<body>
			<h1>giþ-corn<span class="pron"> | Giθ.korn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">herba munda</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Giðcorn herba munda</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. i. 30, 60)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">citocacia</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Giþcorn citocacia</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (31, 45)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="fæste" d:title="fæste">
		<body>
			<h1>fæste<span class="pron"> | fæ.ste |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adverb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">so as not to be moved or shaken, firmly, fast (in to stand fast) (lit. and fig.)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Þæt treōw fæste stōd</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Dan. 557)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Nānwuht nis fæste stondendes weorces on worulde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 9; F. 26, 21)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic fæste stande for þīnre campunga</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bl. H. 225, 34)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the travellers fix their abode on him</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Him þā fērend on fæste wuniað</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wal. 25 : 36)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Oþ þæt þīn fōt weorðe fæste on blōde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 67, 22)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ꝥ man Godes cyricean fæste tremede</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bl. H. 43, 6 : 111, 4: An. 1673)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ꝥ se stemn mōte þȳ fæstor standon</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 34, 10; F. 148, 34)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">I a.</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">of sleeping</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">On middre nihte þā men fæstost slēpon</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. S. 31, 857)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">I b.</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">expressing fixity of intention, attention or purpose</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-en">my steward quite means his children to be heirs after me</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Gerēfa mīn fæste mynteð þæt mē æfter siē eaforan sīne yrfeweardas</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Gen. 2182)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hwæþer þū ǣnig þing swā fæste getiohhod hæbbe ꝥ hit nǣfre þīnum willum onwended weorþe</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 41, 3 ; F. 250, 6)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-en">the matters that we handled and with which we were diligently engaged</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Þā þing þe wē handledon UNCERTAIN and fæste ymbe wǣron</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Angl. viii. 304, 24)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">I c.</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">expressing vigorous action or thoroughness of condition</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-en">they attacked each other vigorously</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Hī fæste tōgedere fēngon</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 999; P. 131, 21: Cri. 980: Ps. Th. 70, 6, 4)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-en">they hated me fiercely and violently</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Hī mē georne ǣr fæste feōdan</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (85, 16)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Fæste wiðhycgan</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Jul. 42)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Fæste wiðsacan</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (El. 933)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-en">very hard-boiled eggs</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Swīðe fæste gesoden ǣgra</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Lch. ii. 194, 5)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Fæste geþūf luxoriante (prosperitate)</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 77, 76: 52, 28)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">flumen Dei repletum est aqua</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Beōð Godes streāmas gōde wætere fæste gefylde</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 64, 10)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-en">if he were quite dead</span>
									<span class="q-la">si jam obisset</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Gif geliōrade fæst</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Mk. L. 15, 44)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">with firm grasp or attachment, fast (in to bind, hold fast) (lit. and fig.)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Dō on ꝥ dolg and bind fæste</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lch. ii. 132, 18 : Sat. 324)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Oft þrǣl þegen cnyt swȳðe fæste</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wlfst. 163, 2 : Gen. 374)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē þone cniht genam fæste mid folmum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exod. 407: B. 554)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">crucifigatur</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Siē fæste genæglad on rōde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. L. 27, 22)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gefēg fæste</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Gen. 1310 : Crä. 66)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">fixum tene quod loquor</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Nim þē fæste ꝥ ic sprece</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Gr. D. 172, 33)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē nam of hire eall ꝥ āhte, for ðām heō hit heōld ǣr tō fæste wið hine</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 1043; P. 162, 26)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Fæste bewunden</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (An. 58 : El. 937)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Fæste genearwod</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Gen. 2603)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">II a.</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">of command, promise, urgently, strictly, solemnly</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">eandem dilectionem instantius commendans</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Ðā ilca lufu suīðe fæst bebeād</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Jn. p. 7, 11)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Þā senatus him hæfden þā dǣd fæste forboden</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 4, 10; S. 196, 8: Gen. 895)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hē him fæste gehēt ꝥ . . .</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Met. 1, 35)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">II b.</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">of concealment, securely</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-en">though he succeeded in keeping it secret from the senate</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Þēh þe hē hit fæste wið þā senatus hǣle</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 4, 10; S. 196, 16)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-en">be sure to keep the truth from them</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Þū him fæste hel sōðan sprǣce</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Gen. 1836)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Þū heora fyrene fæste hǣle</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 84, 2)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">tanto magis cunctis propter timorem abditis, diu apparente nemine</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Wǣron hiē þȳ swȳðor āfyrhte and hiē fæstor hȳddan</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Nar. 10, 26)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">II c.</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">fast (as in to stick fast), so as to be unable to move</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">pedem furis a sepe in qua inhaererat solvit</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Hē þæs þeōfes fōt onlȳsde of þām gærde þe hē ǣr fæste on clyfode</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Gr. D. 25, 11)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">III.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">fast (as in to shut fast)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Stōd on merigen þæt cweartern fæste belocen</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. Th. i. 230, 22)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē þā grimman gōman bihlemmeð fæste tōgædre</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wal. 77)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Wearð sē hālga wong þurh feōndes searo fæste bitȳned</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ph. 419)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">IV.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">so as to make secure</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the town was so surrounded by rocks that it was exceedingly strong</span>
							<span class="q-la">saxum mirae asperitatis et altitudinis</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Seō burg wæs ungemettan fæste mid clūdum ymbweaxen</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 3, 9; S. 132, 10)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">V.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">speedily, at once</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ricene weorðe his feōnda gehwylc, fæste tōworpen</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 67, 1)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">that I did not straightway fall</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic mē helpe fand þæt ic fæste ne feōll</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (117, 13)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Þæt þone māndrinc geceāpað wer fæste feōre sīne</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Rä. 24, 14)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:fæstlīce" class="xref-target">fæstlīce</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="wiþ-ferian" d:title="wiþ-ferian">
		<body>
			<h1>wiþ-ferian<span class="pron"> | wiθ.fe.ri.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -ede</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To carry off; to rescue</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">redemisti filios Israel et Joseph</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðū wiðferedes (fæderas, MS.) Israhēla bearn of Ægyptum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 76, 12)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē of heofenum hider onsende, ðe mē</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:wiþ" class="xref-target">wiþ</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="slidor" d:title="slidor">
		<body>
			<h1>slidor<span class="pron"> | sli.dor |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Slippery</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ȳs byþ ungemetum slidor</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Runic pm. Kmbl. 341, 15; Rūn. 11)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">lubrici</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Slideres</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hpt. Gl. 405, 46)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">fiant viae eorum tenebrae et lubricum</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Sȳn heora wegas þȳstre and slidore</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 34, 7)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="fȳsian" d:title="fȳsian">
		
		<body>
			<h1>fȳsian<span class="pron"> | fyː.si.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">to send forth, to drive away</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. relēgāre)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">let them then be driven from the country</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðonne fȳsie hī man of earde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. E. G. 11; Th. i. 174, 1)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:fȳsan" class="xref-target">fȳsan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="gældan" d:title="gældan">
		<body>
			<h1>gældan<span class="pron"> | Gæl.dɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">to pay, depend, suspend</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. pendēre, dependēre, suspendĕre)</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:geldan" class="xref-target">geldan</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:gildan" class="xref-target">gildan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="brūcan" d:title="brūcan">
		<body>
			<h1>brūcan<span class="pron"> | bruː.kɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to use</span>
					</p>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(1)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">with concrete object</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">indigne acta felicitas</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Hī welan habbaþ . . . and his ungemetlīce brūcað</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 39, 11; F. 230, 23)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Þū heora bruce</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (7, 1; F. 16, 21)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hē his āgenes ungemetlīce breāc</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 339, 2)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Brūc ðīnra ǣhta, ðā hwīle ðe ðū hāl sȳ</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Prov. K. 52)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Swā hwæt swā ūs God sylle māre þonne wē nēde brūcan sceolan</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Bl. H. 53, 15)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ne mihte nānwuht libbendes ðǣre eorþan brūcan, ne þæs wæteres</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 33, 4; F. 130, 9)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ūre æfter his bebodum tō brūcanne</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (7, 5 ; F. 24, 9)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">bonis male utens</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Wæs þæt folc þæs micclan welan ungemetlīce brūcende</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 1, 3; S. 32, 8)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">utentibus</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Brūccendurn</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Rtl. 98, 12)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
							<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
								<li>
									<p>
										<span class="sense-label">(1 a)</span>
										<span class="meaning-en">to use clothes, wear</span>
									</p>
									<ul class="quotes">
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Hē wyllenia hrægla breāc</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Shrn. 93, 7: 94, 28)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Gesāwon wē men deōra hȳdum gegyrede, and nānes ōðres brucon</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Nar. 26, 15)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-la">uti</span>
											<span class="q-oe">Heō nǣfre līnenum hræglum brūcan wolde</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 4, 19; Sch. 443, 3)</span>
										</li>
									</ul>
								</li>
								<li>
									<p>
										<span class="sense-label">(1 b)</span>
										<span class="meaning-en">to use food, eat or drink</span>
									</p>
									<ul class="quotes">
										<li>
											<span class="q-la">carnibus vescor</span>
											<span class="q-oe">Flǣscmettum ic brūce</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Coll. M. 34, 21: 35, 3)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-la">non manducabo</span>
											<span class="q-oe">Ne brūco (brūcco, L.) ic</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Lk. R. 22, 16)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-la">qui manducavit</span>
											<span class="q-oe">Sē ðe ettað ł būcað</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (L. 14, 15)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-la">qui manducat</span>
											<span class="q-oe">Sē ðe brūceð</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Jn. L. 6, 57)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Brūccað</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (56)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-la">utimini</span>
											<span class="q-oe">Eōw þe ne wyrtum eōwrum būtan mē brūcaþ</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Coll. M. 28, 23)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Gē eōwerne beōrscipe brūcaþ on unriht</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Wlfst. 297, 30)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-la">ab hostibus devorabitur</span>
											<span class="q-oe">Eōwre fȳnd his brūcað</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Lev. 26, 16)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-la">edunt</span>
											<span class="q-oe">Huoelpas brūcas</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. L. 15, 27)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Þǣ;ra (hlāfa) ic breāc</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. S. 23 b, 521)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-la">manducavimus</span>
											<span class="q-oe">Wē brēcon ł ēton</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Lk. L. 13, 26: Mk. L. 6, 44)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-la">ovium lacte fructi estis</span>
											<span class="q-oe">Þǣ;ra ēwena meolc gē brucon</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Ll. Th. ii. 202, 23)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-la">manduca</span>
											<span class="q-oe">Ett ł brūc</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Jn. L. R. 4, 31)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-la">comede</span>
											<span class="q-oe">Brūce (brȳce, R.)</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Lk. L. 12, 19)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Him weaxað untrumnyssa, þæt hē ne mæg ǣtes oððe wǣtes brūcan</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. Th. i. 66, 9)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Brūcan his estmettas</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (330, 15)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-la">manducare</span>
											<span class="q-oe">Brūca (brūcca, R.)</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Mk. 3, 20)</span>
										</li>
									</ul>
								</li>
								<li>
									<p>
										<span class="sense-label">(1 c)</span>
										<span class="meaning-en">to use a person (of cohabitation)</span>
									</p>
									<ul class="quotes">
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Þonne mǣden weres brīcð, þonne bið hire mægðhād ādȳlegod . . . Maria weres ne breāc</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. Th. ii. 10, 6, 11)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">His mōdor is mǣden, and his fæder wīfes ne breāc</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. S. 7, 50)</span>
										</li>
									</ul>
								</li>
							</ol>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(2)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">with abstract object</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">uetere usus augurio</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Breāc hē ealdre hǣ;lsunge</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 1. 25 ; Sch. 53, 25)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Þæs gemānan heō was twelf winter brūcende (brȳcende, v. l.)</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (4, 19; Sch. 440, 10)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to possess what may cause pleasure, profit, &amp;c., to enjoy</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">nemo vestrum gaudio fruitur</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Nān eōwer blisse brȳcþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Coll. M. 28, 9)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Þæt ꝥ hē gesǣ;llīce brȳcþ, hē ondrǣ;t ꝥ hē scyle forlǣ;tan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 11, 1; F. 32, 15)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">perfruetur (abundantia)</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē brēcð</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Kent. Gl. 16)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ne breāc hē his cynerīces mid gesundfulnysse</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. Th. i. 84, 33)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">may the horse be of service to you</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Farað gē teala and his (the horse) wel brūcað</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Gr. D. 15, 22)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ealra manna brūce gē betst ǣ;gþres ge penega ge hlāfa</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. S. 23, 583)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Þeāh þū wīfes brūce and blysse on līfe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (2, 161)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Brūce hē his gōdes dǣl</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ll. Th. ii. 176, 23)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">potiretur</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Bruce</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (An. Ox. 3757)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">coelo fruens</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Seō sāwl mōt brūcan þæs heofenlican</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 18, 4; F. 68, 17 : 24, 2 ; F. 82, 16 : Bl. H. 39, 24)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Seō sǣ mōt brūcan smyltra ȳþa</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 7, 3; F. 20, 23)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">III.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to perform the duties of an office, execute an office</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">he executed the priest's office</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Zacharias his sācerdes hādes breāc</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lk. 1, 8)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">functi sunt sacerdotio</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hī brucon sācerdhādes</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Num. 3, 4)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">honore pastorali uti</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Brūcan ðǣre hirdelican āre</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 133, 3)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">cum episcopatus officio fungeretur</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Þā hē bisceopðegnunge brūcende wæs</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 3, 23; Sch. 299, 1)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">fungentes, i. utentes (monachica professione)</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Þā brūcende</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (An. Ox. 3766)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ā-brūcan" class="xref-target">ā-brūcan</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:be-brūcan" class="xref-target">be-brūcan</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:gāst-brūcende" class="xref-target">gāst-brūcende</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="for-weorþan" d:title="for-weorþan">
		
		<body>
			<h1>for-weorþan<span class="pron"> | for.we͜or.θɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">present: 1sg: -weorþe, 2sg: -weorþest, 2sg: -wyrst, 3sg: -weorþeþ, 3sg: -wyrþ, pl: -weorþaþ, pl: -wyrþaþ</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: 1sg: -wearþ, 3sg: -wearþ, 2sg: -wurde, pl: -wurdon</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -worden</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To become nothing, to be undone, to perish, die</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. ad nihilum devēnīre, pērīre, interīre, deficēre)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">so shall every soul perish after unlawful lust, unless the man turn to good</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Swā sceal ǣlce sāwl forweorþan æfter ðam unrihthǣmede, būton se mon hweorfe to gōde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 31, 2; Fox 112, 27: 34, 9; Fox 148, 12)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">pērībunt simul?</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Sceolon hig ealle samod forweorþan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Gen. 18, 24: Ps. Th. 118, 176)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">pērībis,</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðū forwyrst</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ex. 9, 15)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">until this earth shall all perish</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ōþ-ðæt ðiōs eorþe eall forweorþeþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. Met. Fox 11, 170; Met. 11, 85)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">iter impiōrum pērībit.</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Sīþfæt ārleāsra forwyrþ oððe losaþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Lamb. 1, 6)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">pērībunt,</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hi forweorþaþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Spl. 79, 17: Ps. Th. 63, 5: 67, 2: 72, 22)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">ipsi pērībunt,</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hig forwyrþab oððe losiaþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Lamb. 101, 27)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the multitude perished</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Seō mænegeo forwearþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. 121; Th. 156, 14; Gen. 2588: 213)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ān-stonde" d:title="ān-stonde">
		<body>
			<h1>ān-stonde<span class="pron"> | ɑːn.ston.de |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">one standing alone, a monk</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ān-standende" class="xref-target">ān-standende</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="cealdian" d:title="cealdian">
		<body>
			<h1>cealdian<span class="pron"> | Kæ͜ɑl.di.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -ode</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -od</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To become cold</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. frigescere)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">earthly power grows old,</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Eorþmægen ealdaþ, ellen cealdaþ [MS. cōlaþ]</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ǣn-īge" d:title="ǣn-īge">
		
		<body>
			<h1>ǣn-īge<span class="pron"> | æːn.iː.Ge |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">one-eyed</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">if he make them one-eyed</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gif he hī gedō ǣnīgge</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. Alf. 20; Wilk. 30, ll: Cot. 179)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ān-eāge" class="xref-target">ān-eāge</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="deāþ-scyld" d:title="deāþ-scyld">
		<body>
			<h1>deāþ-scyld<span class="pron"> | dæ͜ɑːθ.ʃyld |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A death-fault, capital crime</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. capitāle crīmen)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">if a man in orders ruin himself with capital crime</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gif gehādod man hine forwyrce mid deāþscylde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. E. G. 4; Th. i. 168, 22; L. C. S. 43; Th. i. 400, 27)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="drepan" d:title="drepan">
		<body>
			<h1>drepan<span class="pron"> | dre.pɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">Dominus corporali hunc molestia percussit</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Drihten hine drep mid līchamlicere untrumnesse</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Gr. D. 325, 26)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">cancri ulcere in mamilla percussa est</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Heō wearð drepen and gestonden on þā breōst mid cancre þǣre wunde</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (279, 26)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">mortalitate percussus</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Mid cwylde drepen and slægen</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (289, 11)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Drepen and gestelled</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (298, 27)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">percussus in inguine</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Hē wearð drepen in þā sceare</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (324, 14)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Hē wæs in feorh dropen</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (B. 2981)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-en">stupefied</span>
						<span class="q-oe">On gemynd drepen</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Gen. 1571)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="be-hlæstan" d:title="be-hlæstan">
		<body>
			<h1>be-hlæstan<span class="pron"> | be.xlæ.stɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">to load a ship</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. navem onerare)</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:be" class="xref-target">be</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:hlæstan" class="xref-target">hlæstan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="norþan-eāstan-wind" d:title="norþan-eāstan-wind">
		<body>
			<h1>norþan-eāstan-wind<span class="pron"> | nor.θɑn.æ͜ɑː.stɑn.wind |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">a north-east wind</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. eurus, euroauster, circius)</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="dwyld" d:title="dwyld">
		<body>
			<h1>dwyld<span class="pron"> | dwyld |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">error, heresy</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:dwild" class="xref-target">dwild</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="wǣdl" d:title="wǣdl">
		
		<body>
			<h1>wǣdl<span class="pron"> | wæːdl |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Poverty, want</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Wēðl penuria</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 117, 2)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">poverty, indigence, want, penury</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. egestas)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Þār þār word synd fela gelōme ys wǣdl (egestas)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Scint. 78, 9: Dōm. L. 265: Wulfst. 139, 31)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Seō mennisce wǣdl, ðe nǣfre gefylled ne biþ wilnaþ ǣlce dæg hwæthweg ðises woruldwelan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 26, 2; Fox 94, 2)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Wēðel</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. Th. 238, 30; Ph. 212)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">de inopia</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Of wǣdle weān de inopia</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 106, 40: Exon. Th. 201, 12; Ph. 55)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Þearfan ic lǣrde ðæt hiē heora wǣdle gefeān hæfdon</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Blickl. Homl. 185, 18)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hī wilniaþ ða heafene ðysse gestreōnfullan wǣdle</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (R. Ben. 136, 1)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">ad murmurationem proruunt, sed cogente se inopia usque ad avaritiam devolvuntur</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hiē for wǣdle weorðen on murcunga, ðæt hiē eft ongiennen giētsian for hiera wǣdle</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 45; Swt. 341, 2-4: Ps. Th. 87, 9)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Wǣre ðū on wǣdle, sealdest mē wilna geniht</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Soul Kmbl. 284; Seel. 146)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">angustia rei familiaris inclusi</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Mid wǣdle and mid hēnþe ofþrycte</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 11, 1; Fox 30, 33)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">choose want as his portion and refuse the food</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt hē hlāfes ne gȳme, gewende tō wǣdle and ða wiste wiðsæce</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Elen. Kmbl. 1230; El. 617)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">dum subjectorum inopiam satiant</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðonne hiē gefylden and gebēten ða wǣdle hiera hiēremonna</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 18; Swt. 137, 22: 44; Swt. 325, 11: Bt. 13; Fox 38, 32)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðū tilast wǣdle (indigentiam) tō fliōnne</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 14, 2; Fox 44, 7)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ða hreōsendan welan ne magon eōwre wǣdle (indigentiam) eōw fram ādōn, ac gē ēcaþ eōwre ermðe (wǣdle, Cott. MS.) mid ðam ðe hī eōw tō cumaþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (26, 2; Fox 94, 8-10)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē wilnaþ welan and flīhð ða wǣdle (penuriam)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (33, 2; Fox 122, 33)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðe læs ðe þurh wǣdle and hæfenleāste ðære ǣfestnesse welm āwlacige</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lchdm. iii. 442, 19)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Wēdle egestatem</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Kent. Gl. 316)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðǣr is wyrma slite and ealra wǣdla gripe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wulfst. 114, 24)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sub-heading">weak forms</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">servies inimico tuo, quem immittet tibi Dominus, in fame et siti et nuditate et omni penuria</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Gē þeōwiaþ eōwrum feōndum and Drihten āsent hungor on eōw and þurst and næcede and ǣlce wǣdlan</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Deut. 28, 48)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Man sceal gesceādlīce tōsceādon ylde and geōguðe, welan and wǣdlan</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (L. Edg. C. 4; Th. ii. 262, 5)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">I a.</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">with gen. of that which is wanting</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Wǣdl hlāfes</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Greg. Dial. 2, 21)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hit tācnaþ nȳtena wǣdla</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Lchdm. iii. 180, 21)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">unproductiveness, barrenness</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. sterilitas)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Cumaþ seofen swīðe wæstmbǣre geār and swīðe welige ... and ðǣræfter cumaþ ōðre seofene mid swā micelre wǣdle (tantae sterililatis) and hungre, ðæt man forgitt ða ǣrran geār</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Gen. 41, 30)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē ðæs landes wæstmbǣrnesse ðara syfan geāra sǣde, and ðara ōþera syfan geāra wǣdle (agrorum sterilitatem)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 1, 5; Swt. 34, 10)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-hȳt" d:title="ge-hȳt">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-hȳt<span class="pron"> | je.xyːt |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">hides; 3rd sing. pres. of ge-hȳdan</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge-hȳdan" class="xref-target">ge-hȳdan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="margen" d:title="margen">
		<body>
			<h1>margen<span class="pron"> | mɑr.Gen |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:morgen" class="xref-target">morgen</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="giongor-scipe" d:title="giongor-scipe">
		<body>
			<h1>giongor-scipe<span class="pron"> | Gi͜on.gor.ʃi.pe |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Youngership, service</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. juvenilis status, ministerium)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">that they would follow his service</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt hie his giongorscipe fyligan woldan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. 14; Th. 16, 26; Gen. 249)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="DARU" d:title="DARU">
		
		<body>
			<h1>DARU<span class="pron"> | dɑ.ru |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Hurt, harm, damage</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. damnum, noxa)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">what is a greater hurt?</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hwelc is māre daru</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 29, 2; Fox 106, 14)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">he found his arm and his hand so hale and so sound, as if breach or hurt had never been done to them</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gemētte he his earm and his hand swā hāle and swā gesūnde swā him nǣfre bryce ne daro gedōn wǣre</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 3, 2; S. 525, 17)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">to his harm</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Him to dare</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 42 b; Th. 144, 2; Gū. 672)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">stretch thou not thine hand over thy son, nor do him any harm</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ne astrece ðū ðīne hand būfon ðam cilde, ne him nāne ðare ne gedō</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. ii. 60, 35)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">without any hurt</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Būton ǣlcere dare</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (i. 102, 8)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the mind will meditate harm to others with perverse thoughts</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt mōd mid þwyrlīcum geþohtum hogaþ ōðrum dara</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (i. 412, 28)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="micgern" d:title="micgern">
		
		<body>
			<h1>micgern<span class="pron"> | midʒ.dʒern |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Of micgerne aruina . i. adeps ł pinguedo</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (An. Ox. 2, 105)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Mycgernne seuo</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (2763)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Micgernu exugiam</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Lch. i. lxxiv. 3)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Midirnan</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (lxx. 2)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="blǣst" d:title="blǣst">
		<body>
			<h1>blǣst<span class="pron"> | blæːst |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A blowing, BLAST or gust of wind, a breeze</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. flatus)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the south wind, the sea breeze, dried up the depths of the sea</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Sǣgrundas sūþwind fornam, bæþweges blǣst</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. 158; Th. 196, 11; Exod. 290)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="GE-WIS" d:title="GE-WIS">
		<body>
			<h1>GE-WIS<span class="pron"> | je.wis |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:GE-WIT" class="xref-target">GE-WIT</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="hǣs" d:title="hǣs">
		<body>
			<h1>hǣs<span class="pron"> | xæːs |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">a bidding, an order</span>
					</p>
					<ol class="sub-senses">
						<li>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Streclicere hǣse (quod) violenti pręcepti (imperio complendum jubelur)</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (An. Ox. 1294)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Petrus and Andreas be Crīstes hǣse forlēton heora nett . . . hī æfter stemne ānre hǣse þæt þæt hī hæfilon forgeāton</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. Th. i. 578, 24)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Deōflu be eōwere hǣse þā deōfolseōcan forlēton</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (64, 26)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Seō menigo hāligra sāula mid Drilitnes hǣse wǣron of þǣm cwicsūslum āhafena</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Bl. H. 87, 18)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Be hyre āgenum cyre, nā geneādod mid nānre hǣse</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. A. 32, 204)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Þurh his hālige hǣs</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (An. 1522: 1588: El. 86: Wlfst. 255)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Fēran sceal þurh freān hǣse sundor ānra gehwæs sāwl of līce</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Az. 92)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hē hēt him tō clypian ealne þone here ꝥ hī his hǣse gefyldon</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. S. 28, 27: Angl vii. 52, 406)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">audivit jubentis verba, sed implere distulit</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Hē gehȳrde þā word þæs hātendan, ac hē yldode ꝥ hē þā hǣsa gefyllan nolde</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Gr. D. 159, 16)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hē bead þæs apostoles hǣsa (-e, v. l.) Dyonisie</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. S. 29, 63)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">an invitation from a superior</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">innitatione Honorii amistitis et Eadbaldi regis</span>
							<span class="q-oe">S&amp;c-tilde;s Paulinus þǣre cyricean scīre onfēng mid þæs arcebisceopes hǣse and Eādboldes þæs cyninges</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 2, 20 ; Sch. 188, 12)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">III.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">an office, service one is bidden to perform (?)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Þēnunge. hǣse munia</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 57, 8)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:nīd-hǣs" class="xref-target">nīd-hǣs</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:hātan" class="xref-target">hātan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="-wǣre" d:title="-wǣre">
		<body>
			<h1>-wǣre<span class="pron"> | wæː.re |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:on-wǣre" class="xref-target">on-wǣre</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="lǣce-cræftig" d:title="lǣce-cræftig">
		<body>
			<h1>lǣce-cræftig<span class="pron"> | læː.Ke.kræf.tiG |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Skilled in medicine</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">there was a king named Arestolobius, he was wise and skilled in medicine, for which reason he composed a good-morning drink for all infirmities that stir throughout man's body</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Arestolobius wæs hāten ān cing hē wæs wīs and lǣcecræftig hē ðā gesette forðon gōdne morgendrænc wið eallum untrymnessum ðe mannes līchoman iond styriaþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lchdm. iii. 70, 16)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="scrid" d:title="scrid">
		<body>
			<h1>scrid<span class="pron"> | ʃrid |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">currus</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Cræt ł sc[r]id</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Cam. 67, 18)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">igneos currus</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Fȳrene scridu</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Chrd. 99, 9)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">bigarum</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Cræta, scriþena</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (An. Ox. 2185)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">bigis</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Scriddum</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (18, 22)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">carpentum</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Scridū</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Germ. 393, 154)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="under-þeōdan" d:title="under-þeōdan">
		<body>
			<h1>under-þeōdan<span class="pron"> | un.der.θe͜oː.dɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To subject, subordinate</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="dēgle" d:title="dēgle">
		<body>
			<h1>dēgle<span class="pron"> | deː.ɣle |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">secret, hidden</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:dīgol" class="xref-target">dīgol</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="frum-tīd" d:title="frum-tīd">
		<body>
			<h1>frum-tīd<span class="pron"> | frum.tiːd |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">The first part of a period</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">inclusionis suae tempore primo</span>
							<span class="q-oe">On þǣre frumtīde his inbetȳnednesse</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Gr. D. 212, 5)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="DATIA" d:title="DATIA">
		<body>
			<h1>DATIA<span class="pron"> | dɑ.ti.ɑ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Dative case</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="-hǣme" d:title="-hǣme">
		<body>
			<h1>-hǣme<span class="pron"> | xæː.me |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge-hǣme" class="xref-target">ge-hǣme</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="un-īþian" d:title="un-īþian">
		<body>
			<h1>un-īþian<span class="pron"> | un.iː.θi.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -ode</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To disquiet, molest</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">cum me molesti essent</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðonne mē unȳþgiende wǣron</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Spl. T. 34, 15)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ōþ-standan" d:title="ōþ-standan">
		<body>
			<h1>ōþ-standan<span class="pron"> | oːθ.stɑn.dɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to stop in one's course, to come to a standstill</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðonne ōþstandeþ se blōdgyte sōna</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lchdm. i. 88, 10)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Sōna ðæt blōd ōþstænt</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (180, 3)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt unstille hweōl ōþstōd</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 35, 6; Fox 168, 32)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">Ia.</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">metaphorically</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">to cease to act</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Gif se hlyst ōþstande, ðæt hē ne mǣge gehiēran</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (L. Alf. pol. 46; Th. i. 92, 23)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to remain standing, remain</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Uneāþe ǣnig grot staþoles ōþstōd</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 6, 1; Swt. 252, 23)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt is lang tō sæcganne, hū ða wurdon generede in ðære Noes earce, ða ðe ðǣr tō lāfe ōfstōdon</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wulfst. 206, 30)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">III.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to remain standing and so prove an obstacle</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt swefn swīðe ōþstōd manegum mīnra leōda (the dream interpreted by Daniel)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. Th. 246, 23; Dan. 483)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:æt-standan" class="xref-target">æt-standan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="eornigende" d:title="eornigende">
		<body>
			<h1>eornigende<span class="pron"> | e͜or.ni.Gen.de |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>participle</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">murmuring</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. murmurans)</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="yfel" d:title="yfel">
		<body>
			<h1>yfel<span class="pron"> | y.fel |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Evil, ill, bad</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. malus)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">malus</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Yfel malus</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. i. 74, 47)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">in a moral sense</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Yfel mann of yfelum goldborde bringð yfel forð</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. Kmbl. 12, 35)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hiē nǣnigo firen ne gewundode, ne yfel gewitnes (witness of wrong-doing) ne wrēgde</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Blickl. Homl. 161, 33)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ðæt ðǣr mæge yfelu uncyst on eardian</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (37, 10)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Se yfela dēma onfēhþ medmycclum feō, and onwendeþ ðone rihtan dōm</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (61, 30)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Se yfela þeōw</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. Kmbl. 24, 48)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Se yfela willa</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 36, 7; Fox 184, 31)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Se yfela unrihtwīsa cynincg</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Met. 15, 1)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">ab homine malo</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Fram yfelum menn ab homine malo</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 139, 1)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Yflum</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. Th. 96, 20; Cri. 1577)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">a lingua dolosa</span>
									<span class="q-oe">From ðære inwitfullan yflan tungan a lingua dolosa</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 119, 3)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">rem malam</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Ne sette ic mē fore eāgum yfele wīsan (rem malam)</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (100, 3)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Synnigra cirm, yfele sprǣce</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. Th. 145, 20; Gen. 2408)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Āfyr fram ðē ða yfelan sǣlþa and ða unnettan, and ðone yflan ege ðisse worulde</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 6; Fox 14, 33)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Yfele men magon yfel dōn</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (36, 7; Fox 184, 4: Blickl. Homl. 45, 23)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Yfele geþancas</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Mk. Skt. 7, 21)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hyra weorc wǣron yfele</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Jn. Skt. 3, 19)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Se anweald ðara yflena cymþ of unþeāwum</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 36, 7; Fox 182, 26)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">dixi iniquis</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Ic tō yflum cwæð dixi iniquis</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 74, 4: Exon. Th. 57, 15; Cri. 919)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Yfflum</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Blickl. Homl. 33, 22)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Yfelum wordum</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (39, 3)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">He wile gesceāwian wlitige and unclǣne, tile and yfle</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. Th. 303, 10; Sat. 610)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hē āraþ ða gōdan, and hē wītnaþ ða yfelan</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 41, 2; Fox 246, 20)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">of things, bad, not good of its kind</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Siō yfele gillestre and ðæt yfele blōd</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Lchdm. ii. 148, 6)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Gif eāran willen ādeāfian, oþþe yfel hlyst siē . . . Gif mon yfelne hlyst hæbbe (cf. wiþ yfelre hlyste, 2, 13)</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (40, 22-26)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Nys gōd treōw ðe yfelne wæstm dēð, ne nis yfel treōw gōdne wæstm dōnde</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Lk. Skt. 6, 43)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Heō is on onsȳne ūtan yfeles heōwes</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Blickl. Homl. 197, 11)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ðā gecuron hig ða gōdan (fiscas) on hyra fatu, ða yflan hig āwurpon ūt</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. Kmbl. 13, 48)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">III.</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">of what is grievous, hurtful, etc.</span>
							</p>
							<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
								<li>
									<p>
										<span class="sense-label">(1)</span>
										<span class="sub-heading">of animate objects</span>
									</p>
									<ul class="quotes">
										<li>
											<span class="q-la">phantasma</span>
											<span class="q-oe">Yfel wiht phantasma</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Mk. Skt. Lind. 6, 49)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Hē sealde yfelan wyrme hiora wyrta</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 77, 46)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Hī ǣtan yfle tostan</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (77, 45)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Hē gehǣlde manega of yfelum (yflum, Lind.) gāstum</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Lk. Skt. 7, 21)</span>
										</li>
									</ul>
								</li>
								<li>
									<p>
										<span class="sense-label">(2)</span>
										<span class="sub-heading">of things</span>
									</p>
									<ul class="quotes">
										<li>
											<span class="q-la">malus oculus</span>
											<span class="q-oe">Yfel gesihð malus oculus</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Mk. Skt. 7, 22)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-en">bad fortune</span>
											<span class="q-oe">Yfel wyrd bad fortune</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 40, 2; Fox 236, 22)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Him ðæs æfter becwom yfel endeleān</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. Th. 227, 15; Dan. 187)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-en">bad to take hold of</span>
											<span class="q-oe">Ðorn byð þearle scearp, anfengys yfel (bad to take hold of)</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Runic pm. Kmbl. 340, 1; Rūn. 3)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Ic hit mid yfelre bysene inc forgylde</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Blickl. Homl. 189, 25)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Yfele habban sorge</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. Th. 376, 32; Seel. 163)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Earmne gehȳnan yflum yrmþum</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (280, 24; Jul. 634)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Ic wīte þolade, yfel earfeþu</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (89, 6; Cri. 1453)</span>
										</li>
									</ul>
								</li>
							</ol>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:wirsa" class="xref-target">wirsa</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="un-āberiende" d:title="un-āberiende">
