			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:hyge-fæst" class="xref-target">hyge-fæst</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="reām-wīn" d:title="reām-wīn">
		<body>
			<h1>reām-wīn<span class="pron"> | ræ͜ɑːm.wiːn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>neuter noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Thick wine, wine with a froth on it (?)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">quantum distal dulcisapa a merulento temeto, Ald. 81, 1</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Reāmwīn dulcisapa</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (An. Ox. 8, 417: 8 b, 12)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Merum hlūttor wīn, dulcisapa āwilled wīn</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. i. 290, 55-56)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="dæg-sang" d:title="dæg-sang">
		<body>
			<h1>dæg-sang<span class="pron"> | dæj.sɑng |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Daily service</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Þē ðe his dægsang cunne, singe þone swā hē oftest mage</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wlfst. 290, 22)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hiss Drihhtin to cwemenn wiþþ daggsang</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Orm. 6360)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="dohter doctor" d:title="dohter doctor">
		<body>
			<h1>dohter doctor<span class="pron"> | dox.ter, dok.tor |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">bonus doctor</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Dohter gōd (bonus doctor, L.) rabboni</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Jn. R. 20, 16)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="stān-gefeall" d:title="stān-gefeall">
		<body>
			<h1>stān-gefeall<span class="pron"> | stɑːn.Ge.fæ͜ɑll |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>neuter noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A mass of fallen stones</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Twā wīf āhȳddon ðone lȳchaman under myclum stāngefealle</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Shrn. 152, 4)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ā-cennan" d:title="ā-cennan">
		<body>
			<h1>ā-cennan<span class="pron"> | ɑː.Ken.nɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:hīwan-ācenned" class="xref-target">hīwan-ācenned</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="grafu" d:title="grafu">
		<body>
			<h1>grafu<span class="pron"> | grɑ.fu |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -græfe</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A cave, den</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. speluncam latronum)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">speluncam latronum</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Grǣfe (the MS. has the accent) ðeāfana (cf. illvirkja gröf in the Icelandic version of Mt. 21, 13)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. L. 21, 13)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:græf" class="xref-target">græf</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="wyn-beām" d:title="wyn-beām">
		<body>
			<h1>wyn-beām<span class="pron"> | wyn.bæ͜ɑːm |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A tree that causes delight, an epithet of the cross</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Wuldres wynbeām</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Elen. Kmbl. 1684; El. 844)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="byriga" d:title="byriga">
		<body>
			<h1>byriga<span class="pron"> | by.ri.ɣɑ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -an</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A surety</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. fidejussor)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">he has given him surety</span>
							<span class="q-oe">He him byrigan gesealdne hæbbe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. H. E. 10; Th. i. 30, 17)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:byrgea" class="xref-target">byrgea</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="gǣstlīc" d:title="gǣstlīc">
		<body>
			<h1>gǣstlīc<span class="pron"> | Gæːst.liːK |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Ghostly, spiritual</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. spīrĭtālis)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">spiritual grace</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Giofu gǣstlīc</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon, 8 b; Th. 3, 26; Cri. 42 : 18 a; Th. 44, 7; Cri. 699 : 71 a; Th. 265, 26; Jul. 387)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">through spiritual miracles</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Þurh gǣstlīcu wundor</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 34 b; Th. 111, 14; Gū. 126)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">with spiritual weapons</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Mid gǣstlīcum wǣpnum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (35 a; Th. 114, 24; Gū. 148)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:gāstlīc" class="xref-target">gāstlīc</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="un-gerīm" d:title="un-gerīm">
		<body>
			<h1>un-gerīm<span class="pron"> | un.Ge.riːm |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>neuter noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A countless number, an immense number or quantity</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Feala ōðra gōdra þegna and folces ungerīm</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. l010; Erl. 143, 23)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðara wæs ungerīm</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Shrn. 48, 31)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðara ys forneān ungerīm</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. Gr. 5; Zup. 18, 3)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt hē gegaderige ungerīm ðissa welena</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 26, 3; Fox 94, 13)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hire olfendas bǣron ungerīm goldes</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. ii. 584, 11)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ungerīm feōs syllan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Skt. i. 12, 101)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Countless, numberless, innumerable, incalculable, immense</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðǣr is ungerīm fæc betweox hyre and ðære eorðon</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lchdm. iii. 254, 12)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt wæs ungerīm (uugerīmlīc, MS. E.), ðæt intō helle behreās</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wulfst. 8, 15)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Cōmon ða hǣðengildan mid ungerīmum folce</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. ii. 494, 16)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">S. Anastasius, scs Basilius and ungerīme ōðre</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. Ælfc. C. 6; Th. ii. 344, 30: Ælfc. Gr. 9, 21; Zup. 46, 14)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ōðre ungerīme</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (9, 37; Zup. 62, 5: 9, 38; Zup. 63, 8)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Tō gefremminge ungerīmra tācna</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. i. 310, 17)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">innumeris</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ungerīmum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wülck. Gl. 255, 14)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Se deōfol ... wyrcð uugerīma wundra</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. i. 4, 16)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">numerosas praedas</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ungerīme hūðe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hpt. Gl. 522, 20)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Mikell follc and unngerim iss onn erþe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Orm. 18993)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:un-rīm" class="xref-target">un-rīm</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:un-getel" class="xref-target">un-getel</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-frēdnes" d:title="ge-frēdnes">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-frēdnes<span class="pron"> | je.freːd.nes |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A feeling, sense, perception</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. sensus)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">sight, and hearing, and feeling perceive the body of the man</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gesiht, and gehērnes, and gefrēdnes ongitaþ ðone līchoman dæs monnes</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 41, 4; Fox 252, 7, 10)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ā-seōþan" d:title="ā-seōþan">
		<body>
			<h1>ā-seōþan<span class="pron"> | ɑː.se͜oː.θɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. decoqui)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">decoqui</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Āseōþan decoqui</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Germ. 396, 196)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">to clear from impurity</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">obrisum metallum</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Āsoden weax obrisum metallum</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 65, 14)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">carenum</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Āsoden wīn carenum</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (An. Ox. 4, 5)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">to clear impurity from something</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">uitia exquoquit languor</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Leahtras āsēð ādl uitia exquoquit languor</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Scint. 165, 6)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">excogueret</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Þæt eall ꝥ se ofen þǣre costunge of āsude (excogueret)</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 4, 9; Sch. 393, 16)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">III.</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">to try, examine</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">examinasti, probasti</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Āsude examinasti, probasti</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 144, 57)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">expendere</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Tō āseōdenne expendere (see ā-seōdan above, d sometimes-= ð in this glossary)</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 108, 2)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="hofer" d:title="hofer">
		<body>
			<h1>hofer<span class="pron"> | xo.fer |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A hump, swelling</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. gibbus vel struma)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hofer gibbus vel struma</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. 86, 71)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="an-medla" d:title="an-medla">
		
		<body>
			<h1>an-medla<span class="pron"> | ɑn.med.lɑ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Pride, pomp, arrogance, presumption</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. superbia, fastidium, arrogantia, præsumptio)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">for the arrogance which they before had practised</span>
							<span class="q-oe">For ðam anmedlan ðe hie ǣr drugon</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. 214; Th. 269, 16; Sat. 74)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">thou, in thy presumption, barest for a possession the holy sacrificial vessels into the hands of men</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðū for anmedlan in ǣht bǣre [MS. bēre] hūsl-fatu hālegu on hand werum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. 212; Th. 262, 22; Dan. 748)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="nædder-" d:title="nædder-">
		<body>
			<h1>nædder-<span class="pron"> | næd.der |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:næder-" class="xref-target">næder-</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="crundel" d:title="crundel">
		
		<body>
			<h1>crundel<span class="pron"> | krun.del |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -crundeles, genitive sg: -crundles, dative sg: -crundle, dative sg: -crundelle</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">a barrow, mound raised over graves to protect them</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. tumulus)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">to the retired barrow; from the retired barrow to the thorn</span>
							<span class="q-oe">On ðone durnan [MS. durnen] crundel; of ðam durnan crundelle on ðone þorn</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cod. Dipl. 1053; A. D. 854; Kmbl. v. 105, 26)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">thence to the death-barrow [to the tumulus of the dead]; from the tumulus of the dead to the broad military road</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðonan on morþcrundle; of morþcrundle on ðone brādan herpæþ [MS. herpaþ]</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cod. Dipl. 543; A. D. 968; Kmbl. iii. 23, 34, 35)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">there across over three barrows</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðēr þwyres ofer þrȳ crundelas</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cod. Dipl. 985; Kmbl. v. 13, 32)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>neuter noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">in later times crundel is n</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">to the barrow</span>
							<span class="q-oe">On dæt crundel</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cod. Dipl. 1283; Kmbl. vi. 120, 8)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:morþ-crundel" class="xref-target">morþ-crundel</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:stān-" class="xref-target">stān-</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="hrāca" d:title="hrāca">
		<body>
			<h1>hrāca<span class="pron"> | xrɑː.kɑ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">flegma ex pectore</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Hrāca of breōste</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Chrd. 23, 7)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Flegmata, ꝥ byð hrāca oððe geposu, deriað þām ealdan</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Angl. viii 299, 36)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">flegmata</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Hrāca ł snofol</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (An. Ox. 31, 3)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:hrǣcan" class="xref-target">hrǣcan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="mann-þrymm" d:title="mann-þrymm">
		<body>
			<h1>mann-þrymm<span class="pron"> | mɑnn.θrymm |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Array of men, retinue, troop</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Se cāsere fērde mid ealle his manþrymme (cf. mid ealle his werede, 15)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Verc. Först. 97, 11)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:here-þrymm" class="xref-target">here-þrymm</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="-sittende" d:title="-sittende">
		<body>
			<h1>-sittende<span class="pron"> | sit.ten.de |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:slæc" class="xref-target">slæc</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="eormen-cyn" d:title="eormen-cyn">
		<body>
			<h1>eormen-cyn<span class="pron"> | e͜or.men.kynn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>neuter noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">The human race</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. hūmānum genus)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">God has borne his decrees to every one of the human race on earth</span>
							<span class="q-oe">God gesceapo ferede ǣghwylcum on eorþan eormencynnes</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 88 b; Th. 333, 3; Vy. 96)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="glencg" d:title="glencg">
		<body>
			<h1>glencg<span class="pron"> | glendʒː |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:glenge" class="xref-target">glenge</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="niþer-stige" d:title="niþer-stige">
		<body>
			<h1>niþer-stige<span class="pron"> | ni.θer.sti.Ge |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A descent</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the ascent and descent (of the angels seen by Jacob in his dream)</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Se upstige and se niþerstige</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (R. Ben. 23, 7)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">ad descensum montis Oliveti</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Tō Olivetes muntes nyþerstige</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lk. Skt. 19, 37)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="hleōwþ" d:title="hleōwþ">
		<body>
			<h1>hleōwþ<span class="pron"> | xle͜oːwθ |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:hlīwþ" class="xref-target">hlīwþ</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ābrocen" d:title="ābrocen">
		<body>
			<h1>ābrocen<span class="pron"> | ɑː.bro.Ken |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>participle</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">broken</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ābrecan" class="xref-target">ābrecan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="un-wil[l]" d:title="un-wil[l]">
		<body>
			<h1>un-wil[l]<span class="pron"> | un.wil, l |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>neuter noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Absence of good will, dislike, despite, repugnance, reluctance; the genitive, with adverbial force, against one's will, not willingly, without one's consent, without intention, involuntarily, is (almost) the only case used.</span>
					</p>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(1)</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">alone</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">si praeter voluntatem id fecerit</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Gif hē hit dide unwilles</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (L. Ecg. P. ii. 1; Th. ii. 182, 13)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Unwilles wē magon forleōsan ða hwīlwendlīcan gōd, ac wē ne forleōsaþ nǣfre unwilles ða ēcan gōd</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. i. 576, 7-9: Hexam. 17; Norm. 26, 3)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Gif ðū mē unwilles gewemman dēst</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Skt. i. 9, 90)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hē ðǣr wunode ða niht unwilles, se ðe sylfwilles nolde</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. ii. 184, 13: L. Eth. vi. 52; Th. i. 328, 21)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(2)</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">with pronouns</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Þeāh ðū mē geoffrige mīnes unwilles, ic beō þeāh unscyldig</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Skt. i. 9, 87)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">invita ipsa</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Hire unwilles</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (L. Ecg. P. ii. 15, tit.; Th. ii, 180, 27)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">ab eo invita aberat</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Heō wæs hire unwilles fram him</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (15; Th. ii. 186, 29)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Heora unwilles</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (L. Edg. S. 2; Th, i. 274, 5)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:un-willes" class="xref-target">un-willes</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="mynster-lic" d:title="mynster-lic">
		<body>
			<h1>mynster-lic<span class="pron"> | myn.ster.liːtʃ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Mynsterlicere monasticae (conuersaiionis)</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (An. Ox. 9, 3)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Ðā Godes þeōwas, þonne heō intō cyrican cuman, habban gāstlice þeāwas. . . and mynsterlice wīsan</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Wlfst. 234, 10)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ofer-mēttu" d:title="ofer-mēttu">
		<body>
			<h1>ofer-mēttu<span class="pron"> | o.fer.meːt.tu |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Pride, arrogance, haughtiness</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hine his hyge gespeōn and his ofermētto ealra swīðost</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. Th. 22, 35; Gen. 351)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">þurh heora miclan mōd, and þurh ofermētto</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (22, 7 ; Gen. 337 : 21, 30; Gen. 332)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">in elationem permutatur. . . intumuit</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē biþ on ofermēttu (-mētto, Cott. MSS.) āwended . . . hē āstāg on ofermētto</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 3, 2 ; Swt. 35, 13-16)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">in superbiam</span>
							<span class="q-oe">On ofermētto</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (19, 3 ; Swt. 147, 3: Bt. 6; Fox 14, 34)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">God hyra ofermǣtan ofermētto genyðerode</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. l, 7; Swt. 38, 28)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">God ða mǣstan ofermētto gewræc on ðam folce</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (6, 2; Swt. 256, 5)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">qui faciunt superbiam</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðe ofermētto dōþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 30, 27)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">fastu</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ofermētto</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 33, 62)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðis synt ða īdelnyssa ðisse worulde: ǣrest is ofermētta (arrogantia)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. Ecg. P. i. 8 ; Th. ii. 174, 32)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ne gerīsaþ heom prīta, ne micele ofermētta</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. I. P. 10; Th. ii. 318, 32)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Heora eāþmētto ne mihton nāuht forstandan, ne hūru heora ofermētta</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 29, 2 ; Fox 106, 1)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðonne weaxaþ ða ofermētta (cf. ðonan mǣst cymeþ yfla ofermēta, Met. 25, 44)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (37, 1; Fox 186, 19)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">suo judicio superbiae cervicem calcat</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Mid his āgnum wordum ðone swiran gebiēge his āgenra ofermētta</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 26, 3; Swt. 185, 15)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">in superbia</span>
							<span class="q-oe">On heora ofermēttum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 30, 20)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">On ofermēttum āþunden</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Past. proem.; Swt. 25, 6)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Biscopum gebiraþ ealdlīce wīsan būton ofermēttum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. I. P. 10 ; Th. ii. 318, 31)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Lēt befeallan on ðæt ēce fȳr ðe him gegearcod wæs for heora ofermēttum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. i. 12, 4: Met. 5, 32 : Bt. 16, 1; Fox 50, 9-11)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">superbia</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Mid ofermētum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 42, 2; Swt. 307, 7)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ne mæg hē wið ofermētta</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 12; Fox 36, 10)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Mūþ heora spræc ofermētta (superbiam)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Lamb. 16, 10 : Met. 7, 8)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="irfe-lāf" d:title="irfe-lāf">
		<body>
			<h1>irfe-lāf<span class="pron"> | ir.fe.lɑːf |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">An hereditary relic, heirloom, what is left of an inheritance, inheritance, heir</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">pascere Jacob servum suum, et Israel hæreditatem suam</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē fēdeþ folc Iacobes and Israhēla yrfelāfe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 77, 70)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">to each he gave a gift, an heirloom</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ǣghwylcum māððum gesealde yrfelāfe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Beo.Th. 2110; B. 1053)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē bātwearde swurd gesealde, ðæt hē syððan wæs mādme ðȳ weorðra, yrfelāfe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (3810; B. 1903)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">he [Abraham] was ready to give to the flame, his dear son, the only heir that was left him on earth</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Wolde līge gesyllan his swǣsne sunu āngan ofer eorþan yrfelāfe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. 162; Th. 203, 14 ; Exod. 403)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-þeōdendlīc" d:title="ge-þeōdendlīc">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-þeōdendlīc<span class="pron"> | je.θe͜oː.dend.liːK |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Conjunctive, joining</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. copulativus)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">that is, joining together</span>
							<span class="q-la">Copulativæ</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Copulativæ ðæt synd geþeōdendlīce</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. Gr. 44; Som. 45, 36)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="bǣdde" d:title="bǣdde">
		<body>
			<h1>bǣdde<span class="pron"> | bæːd.de |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>participle</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">solicited; p. of bǣdan</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">bǣdde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Beo. Th. 4040; B. 2018)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:bǣdan" class="xref-target">bǣdan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="hōlinga" d:title="hōlinga">
		<body>
			<h1>hōlinga<span class="pron"> | xoː.lin.gɑ |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:hōlunga" class="xref-target">hōlunga</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="woede" d:title="woede">
		<body>
			<h1>woede<span class="pron"> | wo.e.de |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:wēde" class="xref-target">wēde</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="cneātung" d:title="cneātung">
		<body>
			<h1>cneātung<span class="pron"> | knæ͜ɑː.tung |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A debate, an inquiry, a search</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. disputatio, scrutinium)</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="hrǣw" d:title="hrǣw">
		<body>
			<h1>hrǣw<span class="pron"> | xræːw |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">A living body</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Sceal þīn hrā dǣlan . . . Hiē þīn feorh ne magon deāðe gedǣlan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (An. 954: 1033)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">a dead body, corpse</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Eālā þū earma līchama, nū þū scealt gewurðan tō fūlan hrǣwe and wyrmum tō mete</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wlfst. 141, 1)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">cadaueri</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Rǣwe (reāwe, Hpt. Gl. 441, 14)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (An. Ox. 1480)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">[Geed]cuced rǣw (reāw, Hpt. Gl. 458, 45)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="FLEŌGE" d:title="FLEŌGE">
		<body>
			<h1>FLEŌGE<span class="pron"> | fle͜oː.Ge |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:FLET" class="xref-target">FLET</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="matt" d:title="matt">
		<body>
			<h1>matt<span class="pron"> | mɑtt |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">stramenta lectorum sufficiant matta et sagum, lena et capitula</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Tō bedreāfe genihtsumige tō haebbenne meatte and hwītel and bedfelt and heāfodbolster</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (R. Ben. 90, 15)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">praecepit eum in psiathio, quo vulgo matta vocatur, in quo orare consueverat, projici</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Ꝥ hine man ālegde on þā meattan þe hē him on gebæd</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Gr. D. 125, 26)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="on-sægness" d:title="on-sægness">
		<body>
			<h1>on-sægness<span class="pron"> | on.sæ.ɣness |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A sacrifice</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. holocausta)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Onsægnessa holocausta</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Blickl. Gl.)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="hrace" d:title="hrace">
		<body>
			<h1>hrace<span class="pron"> | xrɑ.Ke |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">of living creatures</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hrace gula</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 40, 46)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hrace ł þrotu guttur</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. L. Spl. Rdr. Vos. 5, 11: Ps. Rdr. Vos. 13, 3)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hraece</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Srt. 5, 11)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hraecae</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (13, 3)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hraca</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Cam. 5, 11: 13, 3)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Raca ł þrotu</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. L. 13, 3)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Mīn hraca guttur meum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Kent. Gl. 234)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðīnre hraca gutturi tuo</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (29: 157)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">In hreacan his</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Srt. 113, 7)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hracan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (134, 17)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hracan (hræcean, lxx, 8) guttori</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lch. i. lxxiv, 9)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">ab omnibus quae ventris et gutturis provocant appetitum</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Fram eallum þām þigenum þe hracan oþþ innoþ tō miclum luste getȳhþ ab omnibus quae ventris et gutturis provocant appetitum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (R. Ben. 138, 14)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hracan fauces</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 39, 56)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">of places, a gorge, narrow outlet at the upper end of a valley(?)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Anlang cumbes hracan (cf. andlang cumbes tō ðæs cumbes heāfde, 434, 35)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (C. D. iii. 440, 22)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="feolu-ferþ" d:title="feolu-ferþ">
