			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="firen-full" d:title="firen-full">
		
		<body>
			<h1>firen-full<span class="pron"> | fi.ren.full |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">ab originali, i. principali piaculo, i. peccalo</span>
							<span class="q-oe">On þǣre fernlican, [fern]fullum māndǣde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (An. Ox. 2005)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">flagitiasum, i. maculosum</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Fyrenfulle</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (875)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">fagitiosis facinoribus</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Fyrenfullum māndǣdum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (2922; 917)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Fyrnfullum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (4, 49)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
					<ol class="sub-senses">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sub-heading">used substantively, a sinner</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">custodi me de manu peccatoris</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Geheald mē wið firenfulles folmum</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 139, 4)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ne forhtige gē for ðæs fyrnfullan þreātum</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. S. 25, 260)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">preces pro peccatore</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Gebeda for þone fyrenfullan</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Ll. Th. ii. 136, 27)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="æt-ferian" d:title="æt-ferian">
