						<span class="q-oe">berigeblæ farcille</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 40. 1)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="mǣr-þyrne" d:title="mǣr-þyrne">
		<body>
			<h1>mǣr-þyrne<span class="pron"> | mæːr.θyr.ne |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">a boundary thornbush</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">On ðā blacan þyrnan . . . of ðǣre þyrnan. . . andlang fūrena on mǣrðyrnan; ðanan on mǣrdīc</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (C. D. vi. 220, 22)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="un-wærscipe" d:title="un-wærscipe">
		<body>
			<h1>un-wærscipe<span class="pron"> | un.wær.ʃi.pe |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Heedlessness, inconsiderateness, imprudence</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ða gē forluron þurh unwærscipe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. i. 68, 4)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="fīftigoða" d:title="fīftigoða">
		
		<body>
			<h1>fīftigoða<span class="pron"> | fiːf.ti.ɣo.θɑ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">The fiftieth</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. quinquāgēsimus)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Fīftigoða quinquāgēsimus</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Gr. Dial. 2, 2)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Fīftigeða</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (C. R. Ben. 25)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the fiftieth year shall be holy</span>
							<span class="q-la">sanctificābis annum quinquāgēsimum</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt fīftigoðe [MS. fīfteōðe] gēr biþ hālig</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lev. 25, 10)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="fixas" d:title="fixas">
		<body>
			<h1>fixas<span class="pron"> | fik.sɑs |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">fishes</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:fisc" class="xref-target">fisc</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="rihtlǣcan" d:title="rihtlǣcan">
		<body>
			<h1>rihtlǣcan<span class="pron"> | rixt.læː.kɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -lǣhte</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To make right, rectify, correct, amend</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gif hē ðonne (after punishment) swā ne bēte and rihtlǣce, hē sȳ of ðam ealdorscype āworpen</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (R. Ben. 46, 19)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Se ðe ǣr ðysum misdyde, ðæt hē hit georne gebēte and rihtlǣce hine sylfne</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wulfst. 277, 2)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ūton wē nū ǣlces yfeles geswīcan and rihtlǣcan ūs sylfe on eallan þingan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (174, 30)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">after his own life was ordered aright, he began to set the monasteries in order</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Æfter ðam ðe hē sylf geriht wearþ hē began georne mynstera wīde geond his cynerīce tō rihtlǣcynne</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lchdm. iii. 440, 2)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge-rihtlǣcan" class="xref-target">ge-rihtlǣcan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="un-gewune-līce" d:title="un-gewune-līce">
		
		<body>
			<h1>un-gewune-līce<span class="pron"> | un.Ge.wu.ne.liː.tʃe |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adverb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Unusually, in an unwonted manner</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Cometae synd gehātene ða steorran ðe fǣrlīce and ungewunelīce æteōwiaþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lchdm. iii. 272, 4)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">it has not been unusual for them to occur already</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðære sǣ gemengednyssa and ðæra ȳða swēg ungewunelīce gyt ne āsprungon</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. i. 610, 12)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="regn-heard" d:title="regn-heard">
		<body>
			<h1>regn-heard<span class="pron"> | reɣn.xæ͜ɑrd |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Exceedingly hard, wondrous hard</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Rondas regn-hearde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Beo. Th. 657; B. 326)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:regn-" class="xref-target">regn-</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-fleōgan" d:title="ge-fleōgan">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-fleōgan<span class="pron"> | je.fle͜oː.ɣɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">His gāst sceolde gefleōgan tō heofena heāhnysse</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Shrn. 112, ii)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Se earn on ðām ōfre gesæt, mid fisce geflogen, þone hē ðǣrrihte gefēng</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. Th. ii. 140, 3)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="treaf-līce" d:title="treaf-līce">
		
		<body>
			<h1>treaf-līce<span class="pron"> | træ͜ɑf.liː.tʃe |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adverb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Grievously, painfully</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">omnibus injuriam patientibus</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Eallum ðe deōpe and ful treaflīce teōnan þolian</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 102, 6)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="oþ-windan" d:title="oþ-windan">
		<body>
			<h1>oþ-windan<span class="pron"> | oθ.win.dɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Būtan hē oðwinde (æt-, v. l.)</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Ll. Th. i. 210, 9: 12)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="of-teōn" d:title="of-teōn">
		<body>
			<h1>of-teōn<span class="pron"> | of.te͜oːn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To draw off, withdraw, withhold</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="un-gerēde-līce" d:title="un-gerēde-līce">
		
		<body>
			<h1>un-gerēde-līce<span class="pron"> | un.Ge.reː.de.liː.tʃe |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:un-gerȳdelīce" class="xref-target">un-gerȳdelīce</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="wyrd" d:title="wyrd">
		<body>
			<h1>wyrd<span class="pron"> | wyrd |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">IV 2.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">what is done, a deed, an action</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">in virtute facti (a miracle just performed) favore humano pulsatus</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gif hē ō wǣre gecnysseð mid mænniscre herenesse fram þām mægne þyssere wyrde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Gr. D. 59, 31)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē gefealh his gebede for þone seōcan man, and þā sōna eft hine gelǣdde tō his āgenre ræste hālne . . . Of þǣre wyrde (ex quo ejus uno facto) þæs weres wē geleornodon ꝥ wē gelȳfdon eallra ōþra weorca</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (248, 4)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">quoniam ipsa signa quae fiunt, bonae vitae testimonium ferunt, quaeso te, si qua sunt, referas</span>
							<span class="q-oe">For þon þā wundru þe þonne geweorðað bringað þā gewitnysse þæs gōdan līfes, þȳ ic bidde, gif hwylce sȳn þē cūþe þāra hāligra wyrda, ꝥ þū secge</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (91, 20)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">dum facta fortium virorum narro</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Þā þā ic sǣde þā wyrda hāligra wera</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (188, 5)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">V.</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">ferre talenti pondus non valet</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hit ne mæg āberan þā byrðene swā mycelre wyrde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Gr. D. 228, l)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">V a.</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">eripuit eos de interitu eorum</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē nerede hȳ of wyrde heora</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Rdr. 106, 20)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="sella" d:title="sella">
		<body>
			<h1>sella<span class="pron"> | sel.lɑ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -an</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A giver</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. hilarem datorem)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">hilarem datorem</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðone glædan syllan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (R. Ben. Interl. 25, 6)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="helle-hinca" d:title="helle-hinca">
		<body>
			<h1>helle-hinca<span class="pron"> | xel.le.xin.kɑ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -an</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">The hell-limper, -hobbler, the devil lamed by his fall from heaven</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="feormend" d:title="feormend">
		<body>
			<h1>feormend<span class="pron"> | fe͜or.mend |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">An entertainer</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Sum sceal on fēðe on feorwegas nȳde gongan and his nest beran . . . āh hē feormendra lyt lifgendra</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Vy. 30)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:feormian" class="xref-target">feormian</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="cyric-hālgung" d:title="cyric-hālgung">
		
		<body>
			<h1>cyric-hālgung<span class="pron"> | Ky.riK.xɑːl.ɣung |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Church-hallowing, consecration of a church</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. encænia = GREEK , ecclesiæ consecratio)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">this shall be for the consecration of a church</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðys sceal to cyric-hālgungum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Rubc. Jn. Bos. 10, 22; Notes, p. 580)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">at the old church-hallowing</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Æt ðære ealdan cyrchālgunge</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. ii. 582, 27)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="Mōr-hop" d:title="Mōr-hop">
		<body>
			<h1>Mōr-hop<span class="pron"> | moːr.xop |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>neuter noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A pool in a marsh</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">he (Grendel) will bear the bloody corse . . . will mark the marshy pools (with the blood)</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē byreþ blōdig wæl . . . mearcaþ mōrhopu</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Beo. Th. 904; B. 450)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:fen-hop" class="xref-target">fen-hop</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="þeōfian" d:title="þeōfian">
		
		<body>
			<h1>þeōfian<span class="pron"> | θe͜oː.fi.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">to thieve, steal</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">qui quid illinc abstulerit</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Se ðe ða āre þænce tō þeōfigenne</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Chart. Th. 177, 13)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">stolen waters</span>
							<span class="q-la">aque furtive</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðiōfende weteru stolen waters</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Kent. Gl. 309)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge-þeōfian" class="xref-target">ge-þeōfian</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="cnōdan" d:title="cnōdan">
		
		<body>
			<h1>cnōdan<span class="pron"> | knoː.dɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -[ge-]cnōden</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to impute, attribute</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">omnes subditi, si qua bene gesta sunt, laudibus efferunt</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gif hwæt welgedōnes bið, ðonne cnōdað him ðæt ealle ðā ðe him underðiēdde biōð mid herenesse</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 111, 3)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to attribute, call by a person's name, name after a person</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">cujus nomine vicus cognominatur</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Þone tūn mon his naman cneōdeð (cweðeþ, v. l.)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 2, 20; Sch. 189, 8)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the leader bore the Christian name</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Wæs se heretēma (Theodoric) Crīste gecnōden (cf. hē wæs Crīsten, Bt. 1; F. 2, 6)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Met. 1, 32)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="fisc-deāg" d:title="fisc-deāg">
		
		<body>
			<h1>fisc-deāg<span class="pron"> | fiʃ.dæ͜ɑːG |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Purple dye obtained from a shell-fish</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Fiscdeāh, weolces conquilii</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (An. Ox. 5193)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="sworettend-līc" d:title="sworettend-līc">
		<body>
			<h1>sworettend-līc<span class="pron"> | swo.ret.tend.liːtʃ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Panting</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. anhela)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Sworetendleca anhela</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 9. 47)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="sǣ-naca" d:title="sǣ-naca">
		<body>
			<h1>sǣ-naca<span class="pron"> | sæː.nɑ.kɑ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -an</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A sea-going vessel</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="lot-wrenc" d:title="lot-wrenc">
		<body>
			<h1>lot-wrenc<span class="pron"> | lot.wrenk |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Deceit, deception, cunning, fraud, device, wile, craft</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">deceptio, fraus</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Lotwrænc deceptio, fraus</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 138, 13)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">with what deception devils did it</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Mid hwelcum lotwrence hit deōfla dȳdon</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 3, 3; Swt. 102, 18)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">Philip, with his craftiness, allowed their powers to stand as they did before</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Philippus mid his lotwrence āliēfde ðæt heora anwaldas mōston standan swā hiē ǣr dydon</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (3, 7; Swt. 118, 9)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">si quis versutiis suis alius hominis pedisequam ab eo allexerit</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gif hwā mid his lotwrencum ōðres mannes folgere fram him āpǣce</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. Ecg. P. ii. 14; Th. ii. 186, 22)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðā wearþ se mann mid deōfles lotwrencum bepǣht</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. i. 192, 11: 376, 9: Wulfst. 84, 19)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">For his lotwrencium</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 30, 1; Swt. 203, 19)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">daemonum varia solertia</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Þurh ðara scuccena mislīce lotwrencas</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 36, 6; Fox 220, 14)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">sciens versutiam eorum</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē heora lotwrencas [-wrencceas, MS. B.] wiste</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Mk. Skt. 12, 15)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">sapientes hujus seculi</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ða ðe ðisse worulde lotwrenceas cunnon</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 30, 1; Swt. 203, 5: Swt. 205, 17)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="for-feran" d:title="for-feran">
		<body>
			<h1>for-feran<span class="pron"> | for.fe.rɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -de</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -ed</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To go or pass away, perish</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. pērīre)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">very nearly all the tilth in the marsh-land perished</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Fōrneāh ǣlc tilþ on mersclande forferde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 1098; Erl. 235, 13)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-hammen" d:title="ge-hammen">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-hammen<span class="pron"> | je.xɑm.men |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Clouted, patched</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. clavatis calceatus caligis)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">clavatis calceatus caligis</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gescōd mid gehammenum scōn</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Gr. D. 37, 13)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="hwearf" d:title="hwearf">
