			<h1>-lǣce<span class="pron"> | læː.Ke |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:eāþ-lǣce" class="xref-target">eāþ-lǣce</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:efen-lǣce" class="xref-target">efen-lǣce</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="cystig" d:title="cystig">
		<body>
			<h1>cystig<span class="pron"> | Ky.stiG |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Bountiful, generous, liberal</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Devotus, i. largus, honorabilis cystig voluntarius</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 139, 48)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Cystig devota</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (106, 33)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">cf. Osuald pauperibus et peregrinis semper humilis, benignus et largus fuit, Bd. 3, 6</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ōswold wearð swīðe ælmesgeorn and eādmōd on þeāwum and on eallum þingum cȳstig</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. S. 26, 84)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">non prodigus</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Nā cystig</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (R. Ben. I. 61, 6)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">prodiga liberalitate</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Cystigre sylene</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hpt. Gl. 517, 35)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">munifica</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Cystigan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 114, 29)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">effusis largitatibus nutriunt histriones</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hī fēdað yfle gliigmenn and beōð tō ungemetlīce kystige</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 327, 7)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">ut prodigis effusionis frena minime laxentur</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Swā hē ðā cystgan on merringe ne gebringe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (453, 27)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="lata" d:title="lata">
		<body>
			<h1>lata<span class="pron"> | lɑ.tɑ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">erat tarda soboli, sed non tarda Deo</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Þeāh þe heō þæs bearnes lata wǣre, heō þonne Gode (þæs bearnes MS., but see Latin) nōht lata ne wæs</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Archiv cxxii. 248, 20-22; Bl. H. 163, 8)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:dǣd-lata" class="xref-target">dǣd-lata</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="þearlwīsness" d:title="þearlwīsness">
		<body>
			<h1>þearlwīsness<span class="pron"> | θæ͜ɑrl.wiː.sness |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Severity, strictness</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">districtio vitae arctioris</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Seō ðearlwīsnes ðæs heardan līfes</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 4, 25; S. 599, 31)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">sciscitabatur apostolica districtione</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē hine wæs frignende mid ða apostolīcam ðearlwīsnesse</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (2, 6; S. 508, 14)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="twi-" d:title="twi-">
		<body>
			<h1>twi-<span class="pron"> | twi |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adverb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">in composition with force of two</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="cniht-þeāw" d:title="cniht-þeāw">
		<body>
			<h1>cniht-þeāw<span class="pron"> | knixt.θæ͜ɑːw |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Boyish habit</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Placidus þāgyt heōld his cniht-</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="hālsigend" d:title="hālsigend">
		<body>
			<h1>hālsigend<span class="pron"> | xɑːl.si.Gend |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Hē beād him ꝥ hē wǣre gehādod tō exorcista, ꝥ wē hātað hālsigend þe ðe bebȳt deōflum ꝥ hī of gedrehtum mannum faran</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. S. 31, 141)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-ǣfenian" d:title="ge-ǣfenian">
		
		<body>
			<h1>ge-ǣfenian<span class="pron"> | je.æː.fe.ni.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -ode, sg: -ede</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -od, past participle sg: -ed</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To draw towards evening, become evening</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. vesperascěre, advesperascěre)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">veperasco</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Geǣfnaþ me</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. Gr. 35; Som. 38, 10)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">advesperascente die</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Geǣfenedan dæge</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Prov. 7)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="crāw-leāc" d:title="crāw-leāc">
		<body>
			<h1>crāw-leāc<span class="pron"> | krɑːw.læ͜ɑːK |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Crāwanleāc poloten</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. i. 69, 11)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">hermodoctula vel tidolora</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (79, 57)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="stefn" d:title="stefn">
		
		<body>
			<h1>stefn<span class="pron"> | stefn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">a voice, sound uttered by the mouth (lit. or fig.)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Stemn is geslagen lyft gefrēdendlīc on hlyste ... Ǣlc stemn byþ geworden of ðæs mūðes clypunge and of ðære lyfte cnyssunge; se mūð drīfþ ūt ða clypungee, and seō lyft byþ geslagen mid ðære clypunge and gewyrð tō stemne. Ǣlc stemn is oððe andgytfullīc oððe gemenged; andgytfullīc stemn is, ðe mid andgyte biþ geclypod...; gemenged stemn is, ðe biþ būtan andgyte, swylc swā is hrȳðera gehlōw and horsa hnǣgung, hunda gebeorc, treōwa brastlung et cetera</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. Gr. 1; Zup. 4, 5-16)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Stebn vox</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 124, 18)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Stefn of heofenum ðus cwæð</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. Kmbl. 3, 17: Mk. Skt. 1, 11)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Seō ārleāse helwarena stefn wæs gehȳred and heora gnornung</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Blickl. Homl. 87, 3)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Seō stemn ðære heortan biþ gedrēfed</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (19, 9)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Seō stemn ys Iacobes stefn</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Gen. 27, 22)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Seō stefen heom andswarode</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Nicod. 24; Thw. 13, 5)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Swā him seō stefen beād</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Gl. Prud. 1 a)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Siō bȳman stefen</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. Th. 65, 29; Cri. 1062)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Heō clypode micelre stefne</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lk. Skt. 1, 42)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē cūþre stæfne wæs tō mē sprecende</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 4, 25; S. 600, 43)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gif ðū sanges stæfne gehȳrdest</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (4, 3; S. 568, 30)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hig gecnāwaþ his stefne</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Jn. Skt. 10, 4)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hig mycelre stefne bǣdon ðæt hē wǣre āhangen; and hyra stefna swīðredon</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lk. Skt. 23, 23)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Stæfna</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Spl. 18, 3)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Lāðe cyrmdon fǣgum stæfnum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. Th. 207, 5; Exod. 462)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">as a grammatical term, form to mark relation</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Se forma hād and se ōðer hād habbaþ ǣnlīpige stemna, forðan ðe hī beōþ ǣfre ætgædere and him betwȳnan sprecaþ. Ðonne ic cweþe ego ic, and ðū cwest tō mē tu ðū, ðonne beō wyt ætgædere and for ðī ne behōfaþ nāðor ðissera pronomina nā mā stemna būton twegra. Se ðridda hād hæfþ syx clypunga, forðan ðe hē ys hwīlon mid, hwīlon on ōðre stōwe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. Gr. 15; Zup. 93, 2-8)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:þunorrād-stefn" class="xref-target">þunorrād-stefn</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:wæter-stefn" class="xref-target">wæter-stefn</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="byrgere" d:title="byrgere">
		<body>
			<h1>byrgere<span class="pron"> | byr.Ge.re |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A burier, corpse-bearer</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. vespillo)</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="swīgen[n]" d:title="swīgen[n]">
		<body>
			<h1>swīgen[n]<span class="pron"> | swiː.Gen, n |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Silence, refraining from speech</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðam lāreōwe sylfum deraþ hwīlon his swīgen, ac heō deraþ symle his underðeōddum, gif him biþ seō heofenlīce lār oftogen</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. ii. 532, 4)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="un-wittol" d:title="un-wittol">
		<body>
			<h1>un-wittol<span class="pron"> | un.wit.tol |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Ignorant</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">in multis esto quasi inscius</span>
							<span class="q-oe">On manegum beō ðū swylce unwittol</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Scint. 80, 12)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="gilpan" d:title="gilpan">
		<body>
			<h1>gilpan<span class="pron"> | Gil.pɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to boast</span>
					</p>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(1)</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">absolute</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">jactat</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Gelpð jactat</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Kent. Gl. 1051)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">gloriati sunt qui oderunt te</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Gylpaþ gramhȳdige, þā þīn ēhtan</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 73, 4)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ne mōt nān preōst beōn tō mōdig ne tō gilpende</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Ll. Th. ii. 386, 10)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(2)</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">to boast of (gen)</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Gif þū þæs gilpst, hū ne gilpst þū heora gōdes, næs þīnes?</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 14, l; F. 42, 26)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Geþenc be ðæm ge-byrdum, gif hwā þæs gilpþ (gelpð, v. l.)</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (30, l ; F. 108, 19)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hē morðres gylpeð</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (B. 2055)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Þā gealp hē and fægnode Godes fultumes</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 4, arg.)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">dum de abstinentiae virtute gloriantium praecepta perstringeret</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Ða hē ongeat þæt hiē gulpun hiera fæstenes</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 313, l)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(3)</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">to glory in (inst.)</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Līfe ne gielpeð, hlāfordes gifum</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Rä. 59, 12)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Þā hine wīg begeat, nealles folccyning fyrdgesteallum gylpan þorfte</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (B. 2874)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hē cwæð ꝥ hȳ gielpan ne þorftan dǣdum wið Dryhtnes meahtum</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Gū. 210)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(4)</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">with prep.</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">cum animus de virtutum meritis laeta apud se securitate gloriatur</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Ðonne ðæt mōd for his cræfta geearnunga gilpð and orsorglīce fægnað on him selfum</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 463, 27)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Tō þǣm tīdun þe ūs Rōmāne oþwītaðand tō ðǣre genihtsumnisse þe hiē ūs ealneg fore giel-paþ, ꝥ ūre ne siēn ðæm gelīcan</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 4, 7 ; S. 182, 16)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Þæt sindon þā gōdan tīda þe hiē ealneg fore gielpaþ</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (5, I; S. 214, 4)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Tō ðæm gōdan tīdan þe Rōmāne fore gulpon</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (S. 4, 18)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">glorietur</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Oððe hē for his gōda mierringe gielpe</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 149, 20)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(5)</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">with clause giving the boast</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Þā wēnde hē þæt hit Godes āgen wǣre; and se deōfles man gealp þæt hē eāc swā wǣre</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Wlfst. 99, 18)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">num audes alicujus talium splendore gloriari?</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Hwæþer þū durre gilpan ꝥ heora fægernes þīn siē?</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 14, I ; F. 40, 22)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Gylpan ꝥ þū mæge Crīstes þegnas ofersw īþan</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Bl. H. 175, 32)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(6)</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">uncertain construction</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">ne innitaris (v. ? Prov. 3, 5)</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Ne gilp þū</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 62, 2)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(7)</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">with acc.?</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Swā [ne] gylpan þearf Grendles māga [ænig] ūhthlem þone [the MS. is defective, but as Thorkelin's transcript gives b after swā perhaps begylpan may have been the original form : it is not found elsewhere however]</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (B. 2006)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to speak highly of (gen.), praise, applaud</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">subplaudo</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic gilpe subplaudo</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. i. 22, 29)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">applaudunt</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Þā gylpaþ applaudunt</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (An. Ox. 4196)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gulpan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 85, 5 : 3, 38 : 5, 33)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">sic proximorum facta diligendo laudent</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ða welwillend-an sint tō manianne þæt hiē suā gielpan (gilpan, v. l.) hiera niēhstena dǣda</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 229, 14)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">subplaudans</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gelpende subplaudans</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 121, 46)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:for-gilpan" class="xref-target">for-gilpan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="hlūtor-līce" d:title="hlūtor-līce">
		<body>
			<h1>hlūtor-līce<span class="pron"> | xluː.tor.liː.tʃe |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adverb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">clearly, plainly, simply</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">hanc historiam simpliciter ob salutem legentium siue audientium narrandam esse putaui</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðis spell ic for þǣra hǣlo þe hit leornade oððe gehȳrde hlūttorlīce āwrāt and sǣde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 5, 13 ; Sch. 643, 5)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">cunctis perspicue oslenditur</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Allum lūtorlīce æteāwas</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. p. 10, 8)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">with sincerity</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Þǣr man cyrcean rǣre, Þǣr mon Gode ārwurðlīce hlūttorlice (with reverence and sincerity) offrigean mæge</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ll. Th. ii. 408, 17)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:hlūtor" class="xref-target">hlūtor</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="cynn" d:title="cynn">
		<body>
			<h1>cynn<span class="pron"> | kynn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">suitable, fit</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:cyn" class="xref-target">cyn</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="helle-duru" d:title="helle-duru">
		<body>
			<h1>helle-duru<span class="pron"> | xel.le.du.ru |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">ad nefandas tartari fauces perducunt</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Tō þām sweartum tintrehstōwum helleduru (tintreges gōmum helledures (= -dores?), v.l.) hī hine gebrōhton</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Guth. Gr. 131, 185)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Þonne wendeð Scs. Petrus fram þǣre helleduru, and hē belūceð þā helleduru</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Verc. Forst. 128, 12)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">On helleduru gelǣded.</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 5, 14; Sch. 644, 21)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-mang" d:title="ge-mang">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-mang<span class="pron"> | je.mɑng |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:mang" class="xref-target">mang</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="wræccan" d:title="wræccan">
		<body>
			<h1>wræccan<span class="pron"> | wræk.kɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:wreccan" class="xref-target">wreccan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="hran" d:title="hran">
		
		<body>
			<h1>hran<span class="pron"> | xrɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A whale, a mussel [?]</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">ballena</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hran ballena</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. 65, 62)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">ballena vel pilina</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hron ballena vel pilina</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (281, 55)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">musculus</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hran musculus</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. Gl. 102; Som. 77, 78; Wrt. Voc. 56, 1)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">in venationem balenæ</span>
							<span class="q-oe">On huntunge hranes</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Coll. Monast. Th. 24, 25)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">capiuntur sæpissime et vituli marini, et delphines necnon et ballenæ</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hēr beōþ oft fangene seolas and hronas and mereswȳn</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 1, 1; L. 473, 16)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hronesnæs</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Beo. Th. 5603, 6264; B. 2805, 3136)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="on-hyrian" d:title="on-hyrian">
		<body>
			<h1>on-hyrian<span class="pron"> | on.xy.ri.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -ede</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To imitate, emulate (with dat. acc.)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hwīlum ic onhyrge gūþfugles hleōþor</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. Th. 406, 20; Rä. 25, 4: 391, 2; Rä. 9, 10)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">homo comparatus est jumentis insipientibus</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Mon onhyreþ dysegum neātum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 48, 11)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">ad imitandum bonum auditor sollicitus instigatur</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Se ðe hit gehȳreþ hē onhyreþ ðam</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. pref.; S. 471, 15: Bt. 41, 5; Fox 254, 5)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ða cild onhyriaþ ealdum monnum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (36, 5; Fox 180, 10)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðonne wē onhyrigaþ Criste</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 51; Swt. 397, 1)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt hȳ ne onhyredon ðǣm yfelwillendum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 36, arg.)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ne onhyre (emulatus fueris) ðam ðe byþ orsorh</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (36, 7)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Onhyriaþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (36, 1)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">ne emuleris</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ne ðū ne onhere</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Kent. Gl. 58)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">ne emuletur</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ne onherie</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (885)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt wē onhyrigen ðǣm þeāwum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 34; Swt. 231, 3: Swt. 229, 15)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Onhyrgean wē ðone blindan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Blickl. Homl. 21, 9)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Wē sceolan onherian Marian ðære ðe smerede Hǣlendes fēt</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (75, 11)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Onhyrian (-hirian, Cott. MS.)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 40, 4; Fox 240, 4: Bd. 1, 7; S. 477, 2)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt onhyrian woldan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (4, 3; S. 569, 43)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Heora līf onhyrian wolde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (4, 13; S. 582, 24: 5, 9; S. 622, 12)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Onhyrigean</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (1, 26; S. 487, 32)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Onhyrgan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (3, 18; S. 545, 43)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē ðære frymþelīcan cyrican līf wæs onhyrigende</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (1, 26; S. 487, 28: 4, 23; S. 593, 15)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Onhyrgende</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. Ecg. P. iv. 68, 8; Th. ii. 228, 29)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="gærs-bed" d:title="gærs-bed">
		
		<body>
			<h1>gærs-bed<span class="pron"> | Gærs.bed |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>neuter noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A grass-bed, grave</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. sub cæspite lectus, sepulcrum)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">when he gives up his spirit, then must he inhabit a grave</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðonne he gāst ofgifeþ, syððan hine (?) gærsbedd sceal wunian</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 102, 15)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="flān-hred" d:title="flān-hred">
		<body>
			<h1>flān-hred<span class="pron"> | flɑːn.xred |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">arrow-swift</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. sāgittārius expedītus)</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="-tog" d:title="-tog">
		<body>
			<h1>-tog<span class="pron"> | toɣ |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:lang-tog" class="xref-target">lang-tog</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:sceaft-tog" class="xref-target">sceaft-tog</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="treōwness" d:title="treōwness">
		<body>
			<h1>treōwness<span class="pron"> | tre͜oːw.ness |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:un-treōwness" class="xref-target">un-treōwness</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:unge-treōwness" class="xref-target">unge-treōwness</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:treōwþ" class="xref-target">treōwþ</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-ȳwan" d:title="ge-ȳwan">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-ȳwan<span class="pron"> | je.yː.wɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge-īwan" class="xref-target">ge-īwan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="of-slītan" d:title="of-slītan">
		<body>
			<h1>of-slītan<span class="pron"> | of.sliː.tɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">to wound by the bite (of a snake, dog, etc. )</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the Israelites who were bitten by the serpents</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ða ðe ofslitene wǣron</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Num. 21, 9)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="gleōmung" d:title="gleōmung">
		<body>
			<h1>gleōmung<span class="pron"> | gle͜oː.mung |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:glōmung" class="xref-target">glōmung</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="spere" d:title="spere">
		<body>
			<h1>spere<span class="pron"> | spe.re |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>neuter noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A spear, lance, pike, javelin</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Spere lancea, falarica</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. i. 35, 11: 84, 17: falarica, ii. 86, 82: hasta, i. 287, 4: ii. 43, 19)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Getridwet spere hasta</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (i. 35, 40)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">His sceaft ætstōd ætforan him, swā ðæt ðæt spere him eode þurh ūt</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Skt. i. 12, 55: Byrht. Th. 135, 53; By. 137)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Nægle oððe spere cuspide</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 21, 24)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ecg sceal on sweorde, ord spere</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. Th. 346, 14; Gn. Ex. 204)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Mid spere lancea</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Jn. Skt. 19, 34)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">accepit lanceam in manu</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē nam him spere on hand</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 2, 13; S. 517, 8)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ða speru sōðfæsðnesse veritatis jacula</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 35, 5; Swt. 245, 9; 38, 6; Swt. 277, 22)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Spera sparorum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 96, 33)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Mid sperum tōsticad confossum vulneribus</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 3, 9; Swt. 128, 14)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Spiorum (swiorum, Wrt.) contis</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 21, 57)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Speoru contos</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (104, 58)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Speru</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (14, 72 : 20, 15 : ansatas (cf. ansatas ætgāras, 3, 68), 5, 44: 88, 16)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Speru, boltas catapultas</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (18, 58: 85, 16)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hī lēton of folman feōlhearde speru fleōgan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Byrht. Th. 134, 63; By. 108)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ūt lytel spere gif hēr inne siē</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lchdm. iii. 52, 18)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ātor-spere" class="xref-target">ātor-spere</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:bār-spere" class="xref-target">bār-spere</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:deāþ-spere" class="xref-target">deāþ-spere</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:huntig-spere" class="xref-target">huntig-spere</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:pull-spere" class="xref-target">pull-spere</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:scot-spere" class="xref-target">scot-spere</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:wæl-spere" class="xref-target">wæl-spere</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:wīg-spere" class="xref-target">wīg-spere</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="rēce-leās-līce" d:title="rēce-leās-līce">
		
		<body>
			<h1>rēce-leās-līce<span class="pron"> | reː.Ke.læ͜ɑːs.liː.tʃe |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adverb</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">admonendi sunt pacifici, ne tantae actionis pondus levigent</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Sint tō manienne ðā ðe ðā sibbe sāwað, ðæt hiē swā micel weorc tō recceleāslīce and tō unwærlīce ne dōn</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 361, 6)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Swā hwilc man swā Godes weorc clǣnlīce and behogodlīce wirceð, hē bið ēcelīce gehealden. Sē þe hit rēceleāslīce and unclǣnlīce wyrceð, hē bið āwyrged intō helle</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. A. 168, 121)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
