			<h1>ferhþ-bana<span class="pron"> | ferxθ.bɑ.nɑ |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:fyrst" class="xref-target">fyrst</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="slǣting" d:title="slǣting">
		<body>
			<h1>slǣting<span class="pron"> | slæː.ting |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">wudas and slǣtinge (cf. William of Malmesbury's statement that he gave the English free leave to hunt)</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 1087; Erl. 225, 7)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:preceding word" class="xref-target">preceding word</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="hwistlian" d:title="hwistlian">
		<body>
			<h1>hwistlian<span class="pron"> | xwist.li.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Hwyslaþ exsibilat</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Germ. 398, 176)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Wistlaþ ot þām dæle þe þ̄ sār biþ</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Lch. ii. 258, 19)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Hwistliende sibilant (coluber linguis trisulcis)</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (An. Ox. 4703)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Swisliende</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (2, 370)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ā-hwistlian" class="xref-target">ā-hwistlian</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-bēnlīc" d:title="ge-bēnlīc">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-bēnlīc<span class="pron"> | je.beːn.liːK |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">prayer-like, nun-like</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. vestālis)</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="tō-scendan" d:title="tō-scendan">
		<body>
			<h1>tō-scendan<span class="pron"> | toː.ʃen.dɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">to destroy</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">contrivit idolum</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē tōscende ꝥ deōfolgyld</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Gr. D. 121, 24)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="for-hogiend" d:title="for-hogiend">
		<body>
			<h1>for-hogiend<span class="pron"> | for.xo.Gi͜ynd |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A despiser, contemner</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">cultor pauperum et contemptor sui</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Þearfena lufiend and his sylfes forhogiend</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Gr. D. 329, 13)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="myscan" d:title="myscan">
		<body>
			<h1>myscan<span class="pron"> | my.ʃɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:miscan" class="xref-target">miscan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="hǣr" d:title="hǣr">
		
		<body>
			<h1>hǣr<span class="pron"> | xæːr |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>neuter noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Hair, a hair</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hǣr capillus</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Gl. 70, 30)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hǣr pilus</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Recd. 38, 21; Wrt. Voc. 64, 30)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hǣr pili</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. Gl. 70; Som. 70, 54; Wrt. Voc. 42, 62)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Loccas vel unscoren hǣr comæ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (70, 56; Wrt. Voc. 42, 64)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">if the hair be too thick</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gif hǣr tō þicce sīe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. M. i. 87, 3; Lchdm. ii. 156, 8)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">there shall not a hair of your head be lost</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ne sceal eōw beōn forloren ān hǣr of eōwrum heāfde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. i. 236, 22)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">thou canst not make one hair of thy locks white or black</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðū ne miht wyrcan ān hǣr ðīnes feaxes hwīt oððe blacc</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (482, 19)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">his raiment was wrought of camel's hair</span>
							<span class="q-oe">His reāf wæs geworht of oluendes hǣre</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (ii. 38, 9)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">that iron come not on hair, nor on nail</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt īren ne cume on hǣre ne on nægle</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. Pen. 10; Th. ii. 280, 20)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the head perishes not when the hairs are all restored</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ne losaþ ðæt heāfod ðonne ða hǣr beōþ ealle geedstaðelodd</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. ii. 542, 35)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">for contrarious hairs, to remove them</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Wið wiðerweard hǣr onweg tō ādōnne</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lchdm. i. 362, 8)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hēras heāfdes capilli capitis</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. Kmbl. Lind. 10, 30)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">multiplicati sunt super capillos capitis mei</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hiora is mycle mā ðonne ic mē hæbbe on heāfde nū hǣra feaxes</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 68, 4)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">capillis suis</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Mid hērum oððe fæx hire</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Jn. Skt. Lind. 11, 2)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the blessed man was cheerful in aspect, with white hair</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Se eādiga wæs blīðe on andwlitan mid hwītum hǣrum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. ii. 186, 20)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">clothed with camel's hair</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Mid olfendes hǣrum gescrȳd</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (i. 330, 2 : Mt. Kmbl. 3, 4)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">I lost the hairs that I had</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic beleās hērum ðām ðe ic hæfde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 107 a; Th. 407, 36; Rä. 27, 5)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:hrycg-hǣr" class="xref-target">hrycg-hǣr</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:tægl-hǣr" class="xref-target">tægl-hǣr</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:feax" class="xref-target">feax</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ǣ-mirce" d:title="ǣ-mirce">
		<body>
			<h1>ǣ-mirce<span class="pron"> | æː.mir.Ke |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Excellent, distinguished</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. egregius)</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="-læcne" d:title="-læcne">
		<body>
			<h1>-læcne<span class="pron"> | læ.kne |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:eāþ-lǣcne" class="xref-target">eāþ-lǣcne</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="for-gifedness" d:title="for-gifedness">
		
		<body>
			<h1>for-gifedness<span class="pron"> | for.Gi.fed.ness |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">forgiveness</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">confessio peccati ueniam donat</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Andetnys synne forgyfednysse sylð</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Scint. 40, 13)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="segling" d:title="segling">
		<body>
			<h1>segling<span class="pron"> | se.ɣling |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Sailing</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">ut neque velo neque remigio quicquam proficere valeremus</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt wē ne mid seglinge ne mid rōwnesse ōwiht fremian mihte</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 5, 1 ; S. 613, 25)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē mid seglunge binnon ānum dæge com tō Antiochian</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ap. Th. 6, 27)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="set-hrægl" d:title="set-hrægl">
		<body>
			<h1>set-hrægl<span class="pron"> | set.xræɣl |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>neuter noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A cloth for covering a seat</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">tapeta</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Setrægl tapeta</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. i. 82, 19)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic gean tō Cristes weofede ānre lytlere goldenre rōde and ānes sethrægles [an altar-cloth?]</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Chart. Th. 564, 10, 18)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ān lang healwāhrift and þrīō sethrægl</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (538, 4)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:setl-hrægl" class="xref-target">setl-hrægl</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-teolod" d:title="ge-teolod">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-teolod<span class="pron"> | je.te͜o.lod |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>participle</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Gained</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. lucrifactus)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">then shall every one show to him what he has gained with the pound</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðonne sceal gehwā him æteōwian hwæt he mid ðam punde geteolod hæfþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. ii. 558, 10)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge-tilian" class="xref-target">ge-tilian</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="be-swingan" d:title="be-swingan">
		<body>
			<h1>be-swingan<span class="pron"> | be.swin.gɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Hē beswincgð mid untrumnyssum his gecore-nan</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. Th. i. 470, 25)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Hī beswingað mē</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (152, 9)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Saulus beswang þā crīstenan</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (392, 1)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Gif mon cierliscne mon unsynnigne beswinge</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Ll. Th. i. 84, 3)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Mid gierde mon bið beswungen, and mid stæfe hē bið āwreðed</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 125, 25)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Wǣre þū tō-dæg beswuncgen?</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Coll. M. 34, 7, 15)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="lār-swic" d:title="lār-swic">
		<body>
			<h1>lār-swic<span class="pron"> | lɑːr.swiK |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Deception, seduction, delusion, treachery</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Mycel is nȳdþearf manna gehwylcum, ðæt hē wið deūfles lārswice warnige symle</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wulfst. 309, 14)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ā-blǣcung" d:title="ā-blǣcung">
		<body>
			<h1>ā-blǣcung<span class="pron"> | ɑː.blæː.kung |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Pallor</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. palloribus)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">palloribus</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Āblǣcungum (ǣ-, An. Ox. 4897, q. v.)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hpt. Gl. 518, 62)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="freca" d:title="freca">
		<body>
			<h1>freca<span class="pron"> | fre.kɑ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -an</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A bold man, warrior, hero</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. bellātor, hēros = GREEK)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the Scyldings' warrior seized the belted hilt</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gefēng fetelhilt freca Scyldinga</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Beo. Th. 3131; B. 1563: Andr. Kmbl. 2328; An. 1165)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">Moses bade the bold arise</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Moyses bebeād frecan arīsan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. 154; Th. 191, 20; Exod. 217)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:hild-freca" class="xref-target">hild-freca</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:scyld-freca" class="xref-target">scyld-freca</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:sweord-freca" class="xref-target">sweord-freca</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:wīg-freca" class="xref-target">wīg-freca</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ferhþ-wērig" d:title="ferhþ-wērig">
		<body>
			<h1>ferhþ-wērig<span class="pron"> | ferxθ.weː.riG |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">soul-weary, sad</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ferþ-wērig" class="xref-target">ferþ-wērig</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:fyrhþ-wērig" class="xref-target">fyrhþ-wērig</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-bridlian" d:title="ge-bridlian">
		
		<body>
			<h1>ge-bridlian<span class="pron"> | je.brid.li.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -ode</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -od</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To bridle, restrain</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. frēnāre)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">he has now bridled the creatures</span>
							<span class="q-oe">He ða gesceafta nū gebridlod [MS. gebridlode] hæfþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 21; Fox 74, 32)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">that they bridle their mind</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt hī hira mōd gebridligen that they bridle their mind</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 33, 1; Swt. 215, 7; Hat. MS. 41 a, 8)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="emdenes" d:title="emdenes">
		<body>
			<h1>emdenes<span class="pron"> | em.de.nes |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:endemes" class="xref-target">endemes</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="snīðan" d:title="snīðan">
		<body>
			<h1>snīðan<span class="pron"> | sniː.θɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -snāð, pl: -snidon</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -sniden</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to cut, make an incision in anything</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Snāð ðæt īs ðara hāligra līchoman</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Shrn. 62, 1)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Mec snāð seaxes ecg</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. Th. 408, 2; Rä. 27, 6)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to cut as a surgeon does, to lance or to amputate</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">secuerunt praegnantes</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Mon snīð ða bearneācnan wīf</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 48, 2; Swt. 367, 14)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gif ðonne ðæt worms up stīhþ tō ðon ðæt ðē þince ðæt hit mon snīþan mǣge and ūt forlǣtan . . . ðonne hrīn ðū him mid ðȳ snidīsene and snīð listum . . . ðonne ðū hit tōstinge oððe snīþe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lchdm. ii. 208, 11-21)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Snīð oððe ceorf on ðæt hāle and ðæt cwice līc</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (84, 28: 52, 2)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gōd lǣce ðe wel cann wunda snīðan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 49; Swt. 377, 18)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic wēne ðæt hē hiene snide slāwlīcor, gif hē him ǣr sǣde ðæt hē hiene snīðan wolde . . . se lǣce, ðonne hē cymþ ðone untruman tō snīðanne</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (26; Swt. 186, 2-7)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">II a.</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">metaphorically</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">ut culpae morbos supplicio resecarent</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Ðæt mon mǣge snīþan and bærnan his unþeāwas</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 38, 7; Fox 210, 3)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">III.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to cut up or to pieces</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðone ramm ðū snīðst tō sticcon</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ex. 29, 17)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">secti sunt</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hiē wǣron snidene mid snide</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 30; Swt. 205, 13)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">IV.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to cut so as to kill, to slay an animal</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">mactavistis</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðara ēwena meolc gē brucon and ða ðe fǣtte wǣron gē snidon</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. Ecg. P. iii. 16; Th. ii. 202, 24)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ða ealdan sacerdas cealf snidon</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. ii. 210, 19)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">God hēt niman ānes geāres lamb and snīðan on Eāstertīde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (40, 11: 262, 29)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">V.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to cut stone, to hew</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðara wyrhtena ðe ðæne stān snidon and fēgdon</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Anglia xi. 4, 12)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">VI.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to cut hair</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Wið heāfodece, hundes heāfod gebærn tō ahsan and snīð ðæt heāfod; lege on</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lchdm. ii. 20, 2)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">VII.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to cut corn, to reap</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">in gaudio metent</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ða on teārum sāwaþ, hī eft gefeān snīðaþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 125, 5)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ā-snīðan" class="xref-target">ā-snīðan</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:be-snīðan" class="xref-target">be-snīðan</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge-snīðan" class="xref-target">ge-snīðan</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:of-snīðan" class="xref-target">of-snīðan</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:tō-snīðan" class="xref-target">tō-snīðan</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:ymb-snīðan" class="xref-target">ymb-snīðan</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:snǣdan" class="xref-target">snǣdan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="leāsung-spell" d:title="leāsung-spell">
		<body>
			<h1>leāsung-spell<span class="pron"> | læ͜ɑː.sung.spell |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>neuter noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A false or foolish story, a fable</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">ex quo quidam, dum non concedunt Deo potentiam, suas inanes ratiunculas conquirentes, ridiculum Phaetontis fabulam texuerunt</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðā hæfdon monige unwīse menn him tō worde and tō leāsungspelle ðæt siō hǣte nǣre for hiora synnum ac sǣdon ðæt hiō wǣre for Fetontis forscapunge</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 1, 7; Swt. 40, 8)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="þurh-borian" d:title="þurh-borian">
		<body>
			<h1>þurh-borian<span class="pron"> | θurx.bo.ri.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">to bore through, perforate</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">simulacra quae an solida essent scire ego cupiens omnia perforavi</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðā wolde ic witan hwæðer ða gelīcnissa wǣron gegotene ealle swā hē sǣde; hēt hiē ðā þurhborian</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Nar. 20, 1)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="fore-seuwenes" d:title="fore-seuwenes">
		<body>
			<h1>fore-seuwenes<span class="pron"> | fo.re.se.u.we.nes |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A despising, contempt, dishonour</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. contemptus, dedĕcus)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">on account of my unworthiness and dishonour</span>
							<span class="q-oe">On mīnre unwurþnesse and foreseuwenesse</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 5, 1; Fox 10, 23)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="samod-geflit" d:title="samod-geflit">
		<body>
			<h1>samod-geflit<span class="pron"> | sɑ.mod.Ge.flit |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>neuter noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Strife, conflict</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. concertatio)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Somodgeflit concertatio</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 24, 18)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="be-cuman" d:title="be-cuman">
		<body>
			<h1>be-cuman<span class="pron"> | be.ku.mɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to come, get</span>
					</p>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(1)</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">local, of completed movement (arrival, traverse)</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ecbyrht becuman wolde on Germaniam . . . ac hē ne mihte; ac Wihtbyrht ðyder becom . . . and eft wæs hām hweorfende on Scotland, þanon hē ǣr becom</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 5, 9; Sch. 589, 5-12)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hē lange wunode wræclāstum. . . . Syððan forð becom</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 1065; P. 194, 10)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ðæt word becom tō Nerōne</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Bl. H. 173, 35)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Siþþan eāstan hider Engle and Seaxe up becōman</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 937; P. 110, 4)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hī ofer sǣ becōmon</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (1052; P. 182, 7)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">convenerunt in unum</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Hī becōman on ān</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Spl. 2, 3)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-en">have a good journey and a happy return</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Farað gesunde and gesǣlige becumað</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. S. 6, 89)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Gif þū wǣre wegfērende and þū þonne becōme on þeōfsceole</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 14, 3; F. 46, 26)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Tōgædere becuman</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. S. 23 b, 643)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
							<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
								<li>
									<p>
										<span class="sense-label">(1 a)</span>
										<span class="sub-heading">of attack</span>
									</p>
									<ul class="quotes">
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Hiē on Ahtēne ungearwe becōman and hiē gefliēmdon</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 3, 1; S. 98, 15)</span>
										</li>
									</ul>
								</li>
								<li>
									<p>
										<span class="sense-label">(1 b)</span>
										<span class="sub-heading">of coming into the world, birth</span>
									</p>
									<ul class="quotes">
										<li>
											<span class="q-la">cum te matris ex utero natura produxit</span>
											<span class="q-oe">Þā þū ǣrest tō monnum becōme</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 7, 3; F. 20, 10)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Hē hider becom of his Fæder rīce</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Bl. H. 203, 2)</span>
										</li>
									</ul>
								</li>
							</ol>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(2)</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">temporal</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-en">he will not live till the seventh day</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Hē tō þām seofoþan dæge ne becymð</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Lch. iii. 76, 23)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-en">when Lent had got to the Sunday</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Ðā þā seō hālige tīd lenctenfæstenes becom on þone drihtenlican dæg</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. S. 23 b, 649)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(3)</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">where a state, condition, position, &amp;c. is reached, to come to power, get into trouble</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">si ad regiminis culmen eruperit</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Gif hē on rīce becymð</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 35, 12)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Gē becumað on micle yfelu</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Deut. 31, 29)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hē becom on hatunga his herges</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Bl. H. 193, 1)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hē becom tō ðǣre cynelican geðincðe</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. Th. i. 80, 34)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-en">this law fell into neglect</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Þeōs ǣ becom tō gȳmeleāste</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Angl. vii. 8, 71)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Becuman tō þǣm ēcean līfe</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Bl. H. 77, 21)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">quo desiderium innititur, illuc gressus oferis efficaciter non sequuntur</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Ne magon ðider fullīce becuman ðā stæpas ðæs weorces ðieder ðe hē wilnað</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 65, 17)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hī on his anwald becumene wǣron</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 1067; P. 201, 22)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
							<ol class="sub-senses">
								<li>
									<p>
										<span class="sub-heading">becuman tó to become</span>
									</p>
									<ul class="quotes">
										<li>
											<span class="q-en">the persecution does not become a blessing to them</span>
											<span class="q-oe">Seō ēhtnys him ne becymð tō nānre eādignysse</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. Th. i. 552, 32, 34)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Seō lease wyriung becymð þām rihtwīsum tō bletsunge</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (554, 22)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Ꝥ hit him tō forwyrde becume</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Angl. vii. 28, 261)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Þeāh þe hit ūs becōme tō ēcere ālȳsednysse</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. S. 27, 178)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Him tō gemynde þā mihton becuman</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. T. Grn. 12, 30)</span>
										</li>
									</ul>
								</li>
							</ol>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(4)</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">of acquirement, to come to, by</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ǣrþon þe hē tō his leōmum becōme</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Bl. H. 167, 2)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">vindicati sunt et restituti</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Hī him gefylstan ꝥ hiē eft tō hiora āgnum becōman</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 4, 3; S. 162, 21)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ꝥ hiē mōsten tō þǣm sāwlum becuman</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (3, 3; S. 102, 21)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
							<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
								<li>
									<p>
										<span class="sense-label">(4 a)</span>
										<span class="sub-heading">where something is received, to come to a person</span>
									</p>
									<ul class="quotes">
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Swā hwæt swā gē biddað . . . hit eōw becymð (-cymeð, L. R.)</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Mk. 11, 24)</span>
										</li>
									</ul>
								</li>
							</ol>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(5)</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">of recourse</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-en">I had recourse to these words lest any man lie</span>
									<span class="q-oe">On ðās word ic becom þe lǣs ǣnig man leōge</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Bl. H. 177, 33)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">of events, to come upon, to befall</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ꝥ wīte þe nǣnig ende ne becymeþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bl. H. 51, 31)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gif him ǣnig hearm of þām drence becymð</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. T. Grn. 21, 32, 38)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Se grama þe ofer mannum becymð</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. Th. ii. 538, 28: Wlfst. 201, 6)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Him siþþan becom on micel hungor . . . him becom on þæt Deniscæ gewin</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 6, 13; S. 268, 8-10)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Þā sorga þe on woruld becumað</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (89, 14)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðā bisgu þe on þā rīcu becōmon</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. proœm. 7)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Þāra þinga þe ūs on becwōmon</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Nar. 14, 23)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">si quis noctu oriretur pavor tumultusque aliquis novus</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gif ūs on niht uncūðes hwæt on becwōme</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (13, 2)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ūs wæs swælc geswencnis becymen</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (14, 31)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">III.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to become, behove</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">etsi oportuerit me commori tibi</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gif ic scile ł becyme mec ꝥ ic efne gesuelta ðē</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Mk. L. 14, 31)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ofer-becuman" class="xref-target">ofer-becuman</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="hearm" d:title="hearm">
		
		<body>
			<h1>hearm<span class="pron"> | xæ͜ɑrm |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Causing harm or sorrow, grievous, injurious, evil, malicious</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the malicious spirit of evil</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Herm bealowes gāst</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. 228; Th. 307, 19; Sat. 682)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">ipse liberavit me a verbo aspero</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē mē ālȳsde of hearmum worde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 90, 3)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">qui cogitaverunt malitias in corde</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ða inwit and fācen hycgeaþ on heortan þurh hearme geþoht</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (139, 2)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">went a long journey into the power of evil ones</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Tugon longne sīð in hearmra hond</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 62 a; Th. 228, 20; Ph. 441)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">ut non declines cor meum in verbum malum</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ne hyld ðū mīne heortan ðæt ic hearme word þuruh inwitstæf ūtforlǣte</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 140, 5)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="meagol-līce" d:title="meagol-līce">
		<body>
			<h1>meagol-līce<span class="pron"> | mæ͜ɑ.ɣol.liː.tʃe |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adverb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Earnestly, strenuously</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">they earnestly prayed to the living God and the holy archangel Michael</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hiē ðone lifgendan God and ðone hālgan heāhengel Michael meagollīce (cf. Homl. Th. i. 504, 7 where in the same narrative geomlīce bǣdon occurs) gebǣdon</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Blickl. Homl. 201, 13)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē hafaþ wīslīcu word, wile meagollīce mōdum tǣcan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. 169; Th. 211, 16; Exod. 527)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="bōc-hūs" d:title="bōc-hūs">
		<body>
			<h1>bōc-hūs<span class="pron"> | boːk.xuːs |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>neuter noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A BOOK-HOUSE, library</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. librarium)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Bōchūs librarium</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. Gl. 109; Som. 79, 5; Wrt. Voc. 58, 48)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="elm" d:title="elm">
		<body>
			<h1>elm<span class="pron"> | elm |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Elm ulmus</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 124, 4)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Genim elmes rind</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Lch. ii. 52, 9)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Elmes drænc a drink made with elm rind</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (66, 25)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-mearcian" d:title="ge-mearcian">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-mearcian<span class="pron"> | je.mæ͜ɑr.Ki.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:mearcian" class="xref-target">mearcian</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="un-nyt[t]" d:title="un-nyt[t]">
		<body>
			<h1>un-nyt[t]<span class="pron"> | un.nyt, t |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>neuter noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">a vain thing, vanity, frivolity</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ne gerīseþ ǣnig unnytt mid bisceopum, ne doll ne dysig</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. I. P. 9; Th. ii. 314, 30)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">odisti observantes vanitatem supervacue</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðū hātodest ða ðe beeodon īdelnesse and ða ðe unnyt worhton</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 30, 6)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Wē lǣraþ ðæt man æt ciricwæccan ǣnig unnit ne dreōge</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. Edg. C. 28; Th. ii. 250, 13: 26; Th. ii. 250, 5: 65; Th. ii. 258, 12)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðonne mæg hē ongitan ðæt yfel and ðæt unnet, ðæt hē ǣr on his mōde hæfde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 35, 1; Fox 154, 26)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hwȳ gē ymb ðæt unnet swincen?</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Met. 10, 21)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">quare meditati sunt inania</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hwī smeāgaþ hī unnytt</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 2, 1)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">vana locuti sunt unusquisque</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Unnyttu ł īdelnyssa sprǣcon ānra gehwilc</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Lamb. ii. 3)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">an evil thing, iniquity</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">loqueutur iniquitatem</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hī unnyt sæcgeaþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 93, 4)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="fiþer-feald" d:title="fiþer-feald">
		<body>
			<h1>fiþer-feald<span class="pron"> | fi.θer.fæ͜ɑld |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">four-fold</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">reddo quadruplum</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic forgeldo feoðorfald</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lk. ' R. 19, 8)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="stīge" d:title="stīge">
		<body>
			<h1>stīge<span class="pron"> | stiː.Ge |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -an</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A path</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Faestin vel ānstīgan, festin (-s, MS.) vel ānstīga termofilas</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Txts. 104, 1042)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:stīg" class="xref-target">stīg</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="smitta" d:title="smitta">
		<body>
			<h1>smitta<span class="pron"> | smit.tɑ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A smear, blot, mark, spot</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">sine macula</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Būtan smittan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (R. Ben. Interl. 4, 3)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">naevorum, notarum</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Smyttena</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hpt. Gl. 421, 56)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:smitte" class="xref-target">smitte</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="æt-īwness" d:title="æt-īwness">
		<body>
			<h1>æt-īwness<span class="pron"> | æt.iːw.ness |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">shewing, display of what may be seen or noted</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Seō æteōwnes þāra wīta ne byþ nā gelīce nyt eallum mannum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Gr. D. 317, 23)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">In þæ-re ætywnesse (-eāw-, v. l.) wundorlices foretācnes</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (19, 4)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">In æteōwnysse (-eāwnesse, v. l.) þæs īdlan gylpes</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (77, 3)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">la.</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">shewing which serves as proof</span>
								<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. per multa signorum experimenta)</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">per multa signorum experimenta</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Ðerh menigo ðæra tāceno ædeāunisse</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Jn. p, 2, 1)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">shewing, making known, manifestation</span>
					</p>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(a)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">of a circumstance</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">resurrectionis manifestatio</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Ēristes ædeāunise</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Jn. p. 8, I)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ārīse hine ðiō engelica ædeāunise (revelatione) ongēton</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Lk. p. II, 8)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(b)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">of a person, bringing into public notice</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">in diem ostensionis suae</span>
									<span class="q-oe">On dæg ædeāunise (-eōwnisse, R.) his</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Lk. L. I. 80)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">in a special sense Epiphany</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðone hālan dæg æt Drihtnes ætywnesse. . . . On ðone sextan dæg þæs mōnðes bið se mæra dæg þone Grēacas nemnað epiphania . . . ꝥ is on ūre geþeōde Drihtnes aetywnesse</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="niht-wacu" d:title="niht-wacu">
		<body>
			<h1>niht-wacu<span class="pron"> | nixt.wɑ.ku |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A night-watch</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Mec oft bigeat nearo nihtwaco æt nacan stefnan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. Th. 306, 13 ; Seef. 7)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:next word" class="xref-target">next word</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-firenian" d:title="ge-firenian">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-firenian<span class="pron"> | je.fi.re.ni.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Sē ðe willende on slǣpe gefyrenað (peccaverit)</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Ll. Th. ii. 138, 10)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="carited" d:title="carited">
		<body>
			<h1>carited<span class="pron"> | kɑ.ri.ted |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">charity</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. caritas)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">held much charity in the house</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Heōld mycel carited in ðe hūs</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 1137; Erl. 263, 6)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="under-fōnd" d:title="under-fōnd">
		<body>
			<h1>under-fōnd<span class="pron"> | un.der.foːnd |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. susceptor)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">susceptor</span>
							<span class="q-oe">under-fōnd</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Lamb. 3, 4: 53, 6: 90, 2)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="hǣlþ" d:title="hǣlþ">
		<body>
			<h1>hǣlþ<span class="pron"> | xæːlθ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">(good) health</span>
					</p>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(1)</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">of body</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hē cwæit þæt hire cild gesund beōn sceolde, and eal hire hīwisc hǣlðe brūcan</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. Th. ii. 150, 19)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Gif þū gesihst þē on wætere cealdan þw[e]ān, hǣlde līchaman (sanitatem carports) getācnaþ</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Lch. iii. 214, 14)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(2)</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">of soul, salvation</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Eallon þām tō ēcere hǣlðe þe his līchaman sēceað</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 1023 ; P. 156, 25)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">healing</span>
					</p>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(1)</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">physical</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Heō ārās andsund of þām bedde . . . þā wundrode se Þegn his wīfes hǣlðe</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. S. 22, 55)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hē sumne blindne man gehǣlde . . . and manega gelȳfdon þurh ðæs mannes hǣlðe</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (34)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(2)</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">spiritual</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">in salutare tuum</span>
									<span class="q-oe">On hālwendlican þīnum ł hǣlðe</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. L. 118, 81)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:un-hǣlþ" class="xref-target">un-hǣlþ</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:wan-hǣlþ" class="xref-target">wan-hǣlþ</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="-wrecness" d:title="-wrecness">
		<body>
			<h1>-wrecness<span class="pron"> | wre.kness |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:god-wrecness" class="xref-target">god-wrecness</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="teofrian" d:title="teofrian">
		<body>
			<h1>teofrian<span class="pron"> | te͜o.fri.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -ode</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To allot(?), appoint</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">he has appointed it to be the wall's support</span>
							<span class="q-la">lapidem quem reprobaverunt aedificantes, hic factus est in caput anguli: a Domino factum est illud</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðone sylfan stān ðe hine wyrhtan āwurpan nū se geworden is hwommona heāgost hālig Drihten tō wealles wraðe wīs teofrade</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 117, 21)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:tiber" class="xref-target">tiber</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="sundor-folgoþ" d:title="sundor-folgoþ">
		<body>
			<h1>sundor-folgoþ<span class="pron"> | sun.dor.fol.ɣoθ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">An appointment, office</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē sǣde þæt nān crīsten man ne mōste habban nǣnne his sunderfolgeþa</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 6, 31; S. 286, 5)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:sundor-notu" class="xref-target">sundor-notu</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:sundor-nytt" class="xref-target">sundor-nytt</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="Babilōnia" d:title="Babilōnia">
		<body>
			<h1>Babilōnia<span class="pron"> | bɑ.bi.loː.ni.ɑ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Babylon</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">Babylon</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Babilōnia</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (acc. Grk, Ors. 2, 4; Bos. 44, 17)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:Babilōn" class="xref-target">Babilōn</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="dēmere" d:title="dēmere">
		<body>
			<h1>dēmere<span class="pron"> | deː.me.re |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A DEEMER, judge</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. jūdex)</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ǣg-hwilc" d:title="ǣg-hwilc">
		
		<body>
			<h1>ǣg-hwilc<span class="pron"> | æːj.xwilk |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Every, all, whosoever, whatsoever, every one</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. quicunque, unusquisque, omnis)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">every day</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ǣghwylc dæg</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. Bos. 6, 34)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">every year</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ǣghwylce geāre</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 2, 16; S. 519, 23)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">here is every man true to the other</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hēr is ǣghwylc eorl ōðrum getrȳwe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Beo. Th. 2460; B. 1228)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">he gave a present to every one</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ǣghwylcum māððum gesealde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Beo. Th. 2104; B. 1050)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">unumquemque alienorum</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ǣghwylcne ellþeōdigra</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Andr. Kmbl. 51; An. 26)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">each supports the other firmly</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Wreðiaþ fæste ǣghwilc ōðer</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. Met. Fox 11, 69; Met. 11, 35)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">on every day</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ǣghwelce dæg</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. Met. Fox 14, 9; Met. 14, 5)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">every one wishes to cultivate life</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ǣghwylc wille līfes tiligan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 27a; Th. 81, 4; Cri. 1318)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">thou art knowing in every matter</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðū ǣghwylces canst</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Andr. Kmbl. 1016; An. 508)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="CITELIAN" d:title="CITELIAN">
		<body>
			<h1>CITELIAN<span class="pron"> | Ki.te.li.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -ode</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -od</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To tickle</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. titillare, Ettm.)</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="efn-ling" d:title="efn-ling">
		<body>
			<h1>efn-ling<span class="pron"> | efn.ling |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A consort, an equal, a fellow</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. consors)</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="fǣr-spel" d:title="fǣr-spel">
		
		<body>
			<h1>fǣr-spel<span class="pron"> | fæːr.spel |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>neuter noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A sudden message, sudden news, horrible message</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. imprōvīsus vel terrĭbĭlis nuncius)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">they announced to them the sudden news</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hie him fǣrspel bodedon</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Judth. 12; Thw. 25, 5; Jud. 244)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the sudden tidings came in their tent</span>
							<span class="q-oe">On fyrd hyra fǣrspell becwom</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. 148; Th. 186, 8; Exod. 135)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">he bare mental sorrow heavy at heart at the sudden news</span>
							<span class="q-oe">He ðæs fǣrspelles mōdsorge wæg hefige æt heortan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 48 a; Th. 165, 4; Gū. 1023)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">at the sudden news</span>
							<span class="q-oe">For ðam fǣrspelle</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Andr. Kmbl. 2173; An. 1088)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the damsel was chilled with terror at the horrible message</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Wæs seō fǣmne for ðam fǣrspelle egsan geaclad</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 69 b; Th. 258, 19; Jul. 267)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">this messenger announces an impious horrible message to me</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Me ðes ār bodaþ frēcne fǣrspell</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (69 b; Th. 259, 4; Jul. 277)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="bīge" d:title="bīge">
		<body>
			<h1>bīge<span class="pron"> | biː.Ge |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A bending, turning, bend, an angle, a corner</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. flexus, sinus, angulus)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">angelus ad locum angustum transivit, ubi nec ad dexteram nec ad sinistram poterat deviare</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Se engel eōde into ānum nyrwette, ðe he ne mihte forbūgan on nāðere healfe, forðamðe ðǣr nān bīge næs</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Num. 22, 26)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">fractura membri</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Bīge limes</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Fulg. 19)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:bȳge" class="xref-target">bȳge</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="spær" d:title="spær">
		<body>
			<h1>spær<span class="pron"> | spær |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Spare, frugal</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">parcus cibus</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Spær mete parcus cibus</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Scint. 52, 6)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:spær-hende" class="xref-target">spær-hende</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:spær-līc" class="xref-target">spær-līc</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:spær-ness" class="xref-target">spær-ness</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="full-gangan" d:title="full-gangan">
		<body>
			<h1>full-gangan<span class="pron"> | full.gɑn.gɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Ic ne mōt mid mīnum ðeāwum mīnra ðēnunga fulgangan</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 7, 3; F. 20, 32)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="bōc-weorc" d:title="bōc-weorc">
		<body>
			<h1>bōc-weorc<span class="pron"> | boːk.we͜ork |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>neuter noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Literary work, study</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Bisceopes dægweorc, ꝥ bið mid rihte his gebedu ǣrest, and ðonne his bōcweorc, rǣding oððon rihting, lār oððon leornung</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ll. Th. ii. 314, 19)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="rǣdfæstum" d:title="rǣdfæstum">
		<body>
			<h1>rǣdfæstum<span class="pron"> | ræːd.fæ.stum |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">rǣdfæstum mōde</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Skt. i. 18, 185)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Se rǣd wæs ǣfre on his rǣdfæstum geþance</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. T. Grn. 2, 5)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Ðæt hig māgon ārīsan, gif hig rǣdfæste beōþ</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (19, 5)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Rincas rǣdfæste</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. Th. 347, 15; Sch. 13)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:rǣd-leās" class="xref-target">rǣd-leās</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="bryne-ādl" d:title="bryne-ādl">
		<body>
			<h1>bryne-ādl<span class="pron"> | bry.ne.ɑːdl |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A burning disease, a fever</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. æstuans morbus, febris)</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="gremung" d:title="gremung">
		
		<body>
			<h1>gremung<span class="pron"> | gre.mung |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Irritation, provocation</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">in irritatione</span>
							<span class="q-oe">On græmunge</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. L. 94, 9)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">in exacerbatione</span>
							<span class="q-oe">On gremminge</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Rdr. 94. 9)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="īdel-līce" d:title="īdel-līce">
		
		<body>
			<h1>īdel-līce<span class="pron"> | iː.del.liː.tʃe |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adverb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">in vain, to no purpose</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. supervacue, vane)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Haldende īdelnisse īdel-līce (supervacue)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Srt. 30, 7)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Mon hwæðre īdellīce (vane) bið gedroefed</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (38, 7: 88, 48)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">without cause</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. vane)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Īdellīce (vane) edwīttun sāwle mīne</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (34, 7)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:īdel" class="xref-target">īdel</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="leōht" d:title="leōht">
		<body>
			<h1>leōht<span class="pron"> | le͜oːxt |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">a light</span>
					</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">light</span>
					</p>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(1)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">the medium of visual perception generally; the condition of space in which light is present</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Leōht hafað hīw and hād Hāliges Gāstes</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Sal. 408)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ǣr-fæder" d:title="ǣr-fæder">
		<body>
			<h1>ǣr-fæder<span class="pron"> | æːr.fæ.der |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -fæderes, dative sg: -fædere, nominative pl: -fæderas, accusative pl: -fæderas, genitive pl: -a, dative pl: -um</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A forefather, father</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. propator, pater)</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="land-scearu" d:title="land-scearu">
		<body>
			<h1>land-scearu<span class="pron"> | lɑnd.ʃæ͜ɑ.ru |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Swā hē on lansceare (printed -sceape, but see Nap. 41) stille stande ðǣr hine storm ne mæg āwecgan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (An. 501)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðis ys seō landscaru tō trefwurabo</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cht. E. 296, 1 : 8 : 12)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">On landscare hrycg</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cht. Crw. 3, 3)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:landgemǣro" class="xref-target">landgemǣro</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="setla" d:title="setla">
		<body>
			<h1>setla<span class="pron"> | set.lɑ |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ān-setla" class="xref-target">ān-setla</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:cot-setla" class="xref-target">cot-setla</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge-setla" class="xref-target">ge-setla</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:wēsten-setla" class="xref-target">wēsten-setla</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="widrian" d:title="widrian">
		<body>
			<h1>widrian<span class="pron"> | wi.dri.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:wederian" class="xref-target">wederian</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="linnan" d:title="linnan">
		<body>
			<h1>linnan<span class="pron"> | lin.nɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ā-linnan" class="xref-target">ā-linnan</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:of-linnan" class="xref-target">of-linnan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="sticca" d:title="sticca">
		<body>
			<h1>sticca<span class="pron"> | stik.kɑ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -an</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">a stick, peg</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Sticca gergenna (gergenna lignum teres, quo per duas ansas transmisso operculum firmatur ne excidat, Migne)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. i. 287, 38: ii. 41, 32)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Se sticca (the tent-peg him eode ūt þurh ðæt heāfod in tō ðære eorþan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Jud. 4, 21)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Styre mid sticcan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lchdm. ii. 76, 26)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Genim twegen sticcan feðerecgede and wrīt on ǣgðerne sticcan be hwælcere ecge</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (i. 386, 4-6)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Nim ǣnne sticcan and gnīd tō sumum þinge</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (iii. 274, 3)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">I a.</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">the pointer of a dial</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Se sticca on ðæm dægmǣle</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Anglia viii. 317, 20)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">a spoon</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Lǣt yrnan ðæt blōd on grēnne sticcan hæslenne, weorp ðonne ofer weg āweg</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lchdm. ii. 142, 20: 144, 7: 104, 7)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Genim fīf sticcan fulle ecedes</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (i. 110, 21: iii. 4, 18)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Wring ðæt wōs of, ānne sticcan fulne, and huniges þrȳ sticcan fulle</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (102, 14)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Nim wīfes meolce þrȳ sticcæs fulla and cyleþena ānne sticce fulne</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (96, 27)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:candel-sticca" class="xref-target">candel-sticca</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:clader-sticca" class="xref-target">clader-sticca</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:geoc-sticca" class="xref-target">geoc-sticca</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:plant-sticca" class="xref-target">plant-sticca</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:regol-sticca" class="xref-target">regol-sticca</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:seām-sticca" class="xref-target">seām-sticca</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:stōr-sticca" class="xref-target">stōr-sticca</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:tōþ-sticca" class="xref-target">tōþ-sticca</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="un-reordian" d:title="un-reordian">
		<body>
			<h1>un-reordian<span class="pron"> | un.re͜or.di.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">to speak ill of, to abuse</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Swā firenfulle fācnum wordum heora aldorðægn unreordadon (on reordadon? v. on, B. III. 5)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. Th. 269, 1; Sat. 66)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:on" class="xref-target">on</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="heāfod-stocc" d:title="heāfod-stocc">
		<body>
			<h1>heāfod-stocc<span class="pron"> | xæ͜ɑː.fod.stokk |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A stock or post on which the head of a criminal was fixed after beheading</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Heora lima man ealle tōbrǣd ǣlc fram ōðrum . . . and ðā heāfodleāsan man hēngc on ðā portweallas, and man sette heora heāfda swilce ōþra ðeōfa būton ðām portweallon on ðām heāfodstoccum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. S. 23, 71-76)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Æfter Foss tō þām heāfodstocce</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (C. D. iii. 384, 29)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Of ðǣre hylle andlang ðǣre dīc ūp tō heāfodstoccan; of heāfodstoccan andlang strǣt</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (v. 110, 34: 217, 14)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Tō weāwan hōcan; ðanon on ðā heāfodstoccas</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (207, 26)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Be gemǣre; ðæt on ðā heāfodstoccas; of ðan stoccan on ðone mǣrstān</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (iii. 439, 6)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">On gerihte on ðā heāfudstoccas; of ðan heāfodstoccum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (vi. 62, 7)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">On grēne wei on neðe hēuedstokes; of ðanne hēuedstocken</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (iii. 201, 32)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="cursumbor" d:title="cursumbor">
		<body>
			<h1>cursumbor<span class="pron"> | kur.sum.bor |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:coczumber" class="xref-target">coczumber</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="mǣgþ-hād" d:title="mǣgþ-hād">
		<body>
			<h1>mǣgþ-hād<span class="pron"> | mæːɣθ.xɑːd |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Kinship, relationship</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">'he who loveth not his brother continueth in death' ... All we are brethren that believe on God, and we all say 'our Father that art in heaven.' Let no man presume on kinship without true love.</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ealle wē sind gebrōðra ðe on God gelȳfaþ and we ealle cweþaþ 'Ūre Fæder þe eart on heofonum.' Ne gedyrstlǣce nān man be mǣgþhāde būtan sōðre lufe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. i. 54, 6-11)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="wīf-lufu" d:title="wīf-lufu">
		<body>
			<h1>wīf-lufu<span class="pron"> | wiːf.lu.fu |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -an</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Love for a woman</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Se hālga wer ðære wīflufan (the love of Herod for Herodias) wordum stȳrde, unryhtre ǣ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. Th. 260, 12; Jul. 296)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ingelde weallaþ wælnīðas, and him wīflufan cōlran weorðaþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Beo. Th. 4137; B. 2065)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:wīf-myne" class="xref-target">wīf-myne</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="hird-ness" d:title="hird-ness">
		<body>
			<h1>hird-ness<span class="pron"> | xird.ness |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">watchful care, taking charge, taking care that a thing be not damaged</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">monasterio solerti custodia praefuit</span>
							<span class="q-oe">þām mynstre fore wæs mid geornlicre heordnysse</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Gr. D. 52, 15)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">On hū mycelre Godes heordnysse (custodia) beōð þā þe cunnon hī sylfe forseōn on þysum līfe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (39, 30)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">cum in monasterio regularis vitae custodiam teneret</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Þā þā hē nam þā hyrdnysse (hiordnisse, v. l.) þæs regollican lifes in þām mynstre</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (104, 2)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">a watch, guard to prevent evil</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">posui ori meo custodiam</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic gesette mīnum mūþe heordnesse</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (R. Ben. 21, 11)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">III.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">a watch, period during which watch is kept</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="sniden-ness" d:title="sniden-ness">
