				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Wallendre hǣte and swoloðan caumate</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (An. Ox. 23, 55)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="biter-wyrde" d:title="biter-wyrde">
		<body>
			<h1>biter-wyrde<span class="pron"> | bi.ter.wyr.de |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Bitter of speech, given to bitter words</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ꝥ gē ne beōn tō biterwyrde, ne bealufulle on mōde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. A. 48, 576)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="samod-wist" d:title="samod-wist">
		<body>
			<h1>samod-wist<span class="pron"> | sɑ.mod.wist |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A being together, common existence</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">ut tanto nostris hostibus potentiores simus, quanto cum auctore omnium unum efficimur per humilitatem</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Tō þon ꝥ wē sȳn swā myccle strangran wið ūrum feōndum, swā myccle mā wē gefremede beōð under eādmōdnesse tō þǣre samodwiste þæs ordfruman eallra gesceafta</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Gr. D. 224, 4)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:sam-wist" class="xref-target">sam-wist</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="un-ālīfend-līc" d:title="un-ālīfend-līc">
		
		<body>
			<h1>un-ālīfend-līc<span class="pron"> | un.ɑː.liː.fend.liːtʃ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Unallowable, illicit</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">illecebrosis, inlicitis</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Unālȳfendlīcum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hpt. Gl. 505, 42)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">ab inlecebrarum</span>
							<span class="q-oe">From unālīfendlīcum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 2, 12: 44, 13)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="nirwett" d:title="nirwett">
		<body>
			<h1>nirwett<span class="pron"> | nir.wett |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>neuter noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Rōmāne on ungewis on ān nirewett befōran</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 3, 8; S. 120, 29)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">II a.</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">a place of confinement</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Godes Sunu wæs gelēd on nearuwre binne, tō ðī þæt hē ūs fram hellicum nyrwette (the prison (or (?) confinement) of hell) ālȳsde</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. Th. i. 34, 32)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:breōst-nirwett" class="xref-target">breōst-nirwett</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="un-gefērendlīc" d:title="un-gefērendlīc">
		<body>
			<h1>un-gefērendlīc<span class="pron"> | un.Ge.feː.rend.liːK |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Inaccessible, difficult of access</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Fōran wē þurh ða ungefērenlīcan (-fērend-?) eorþan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Nap. 17, 7)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-canc" d:title="ge-canc">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-canc<span class="pron"> | je.kɑnk |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>neuter noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A mock, gibe</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. ludibrium, vituperium)</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ang-mōd" d:title="ang-mōd">
		<body>
			<h1>ang-mōd<span class="pron"> | ɑng.moːd |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">non sit turbulentus et anxius</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Ne beō hē drēfende ne angmōd (ancg-, v. l.)</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (R. Ben. 120, 12)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Wurdon heora eāgan āfyllede mid teārum and angmōde geōmrodon ealle heora heortan</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. S. 23, 244)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-tal" d:title="ge-tal">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-tal<span class="pron"> | je.tɑl |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Quick, ready, active</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. agilis, velox, expeditus)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">their tongues were swift to every wrong and to every evil exceeding sharp</span>
							<span class="q-la">lingua eorum machæra acuta</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Wǣron hyra tungan getale teōnan gehwylcre and to yfele gehwām ungemet scearpe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 56, 5)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="gryre-meaht" d:title="gryre-meaht">
		
		<body>
			<h1>gryre-meaht<span class="pron"> | gry.re.mæ͜ɑxt |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A power that inspires terror, terrible power</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">His (Antichrist's) hlīsa and gryremiht bitf from sǣ tō sǣ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wlfst. 195, 20)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="lytig-līce" d:title="lytig-līce">
		
		<body>
			<h1>lytig-līce<span class="pron"> | ly.tiG.liː.tʃe |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adverb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Cunningly, artfully, craftily</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. callide)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">sese callide defendentis</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðe hit symle lytiglīce lādaþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 35, 3; Swt. 241, 8)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">callide</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Litelīce</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ex. 32, 12)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ða woruldsǣlþa mid swīðe manigre swētnesse swīðe</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="þeāwian" d:title="þeāwian">
		<body>
			<h1>þeāwian<span class="pron"> | θæ͜ɑː.wi.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">to make (well) mannered</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge-þeāwian" class="xref-target">ge-þeāwian</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="drǣfness" d:title="drǣfness">
		<body>
			<h1>drǣfness<span class="pron"> | dræː.fness |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:tō-drǣfness" class="xref-target">tō-drǣfness</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="fyrmest" d:title="fyrmest">
		<body>
			<h1>fyrmest<span class="pron"> | fyr.mest |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">marking order in time</span>
					</p>
					<ol class="sub-senses">
						<li>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hē tō fulluhte heora fyrmest beāh</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. S. 10, 150)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Seō bōc ys gehāten Genesis, . . . for þām þe heō ys firmest bōca</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. Gen. Thw. 2, 34)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">marking order in rank, importance</span>
					</p>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(1)</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">of persons</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Maurus wæs fyrmest muneca tō ðām mǣran Benedicte</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. S. 6, 51)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">Nemroth condendae Babyloniae auctor exstiterat</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Nembroð fyrmest wæs æt þǣre getimbrunge þǣre byrig Babilonian</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Angl. vii. 40, 380)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">On þām gefērscipe wǣran þā fyrmestan Mellitus, . . . Rufianus</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 995; P. 128, 32)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(2)</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">of things</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">On þām fyrmestum stōwum ealles his anwealdes</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Lch. iii. 440, 12)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">marking order in merit, excellent</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hū se lāreōw sceal beōn on his weorcum fyrmest (praecipuus). Se lāreōw sceal biōn on his weorcum heālic (praecipuus)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 81, 1)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="gearc" d:title="gearc">
		<body>
			<h1>gearc<span class="pron"> | Gæ͜ɑrk |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Ready, active, quick</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">On orde stōd Eādweard se langa, gearc and geornful</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (By. 274)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="GEĀ" d:title="GEĀ">
		<body>
			<h1>GEĀ<span class="pron"> | Gæ͜ɑː |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adverb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">YEA</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. ætiam)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">'Quod est, lingua Anglōrum, verbum adfirmandi et consentiendi,'</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 5, 2; S. 183, 35)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">yea, Lord, thou knowest that I love thee</span>
							<span class="q-la">ætiam, Dŏmĭne</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Geā, Drihten, ðū wāst ðæt ic ðē lufige</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Jn. Bos. 21, 15, 16; Vulg.)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">say now yea</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Cweþ [cwæþ MS.] nū geā</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 5, 2; S. 615, 9)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="for-gitelness" d:title="for-gitelness">
		<body>
			<h1>for-gitelness<span class="pron"> | for.Gi.tel.ness |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">oblivionem</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Foregytelnysse</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (R. Ben. I. 28, 15)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="heard-heāwa" d:title="heard-heāwa">
		<body>
			<h1>heard-heāwa<span class="pron"> | xæ͜ɑrd.xæ͜ɑː.wɑ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -an</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A chisel</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. scalprum)</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-bisgīan" d:title="ge-bisgīan">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-bisgīan<span class="pron"> | je.bis.Giː.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Hē mid Godes herungum his mūð gebysgað</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. Th. i. 494, 16)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="trahtnung" d:title="trahtnung">
		<body>
			<h1>trahtnung<span class="pron"> | trɑxt.nung |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:in-trahtnung" class="xref-target">in-trahtnung</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="leōd-fruma" d:title="leōd-fruma">
		<body>
			<h1>leōd-fruma<span class="pron"> | le͜oːd.fru.mɑ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -an</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">The first in time of a people, the founder of a people, a patriarch; the first in rank among a people, a prince, chieftain, king</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">one father had they, founder beloved</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Him wæs ān fæder leōf leōdfruma</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. 161; Th. 200, 9; Exod. 354)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Leōdfruma [St. Andrew]</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Andr. Kmbl. 3318; An. 1662)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Leōdfruma [Constantine]</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Elen. Kmbl. 382; El. 191)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">my lord</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Mīn leōdfruma</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 115 a; Th. 442, 5; Kl. 8)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Sethes cynn, leōfes leōdfruman</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. 63; Th. 75, 26; Gen. 1246)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">from that patriarch [Isaac] shall come nations wide-spreading</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Of ðam leōdfruman brād folc cumaþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (106; Th. 140, 24; Gen. 2332)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">if they durst follow their chief</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gif hī leōdfruman lǣstan dorsten</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. Met. Fox 1, 53; Met. 1, 27)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Cyning, leōfne leōdfruman [Hrothgar]</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 60 b; Th. 222, 7; Ph. 345: Beo. Th. 4266; B. 2130)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Cyning, leōfne leōdfruman [St. Andrew]</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Andr. Kmbl. 1977; An. 991)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="-lēpig" d:title="-lēpig">
		<body>
			<h1>-lēpig<span class="pron"> | leː.piG |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:-līpig" class="xref-target">-līpig</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="lungen-ǣder" d:title="lungen-ǣder">
		<body>
			<h1>lungen-ǣder<span class="pron"> | lun.Gen.æː.der |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A lung-vein</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Lǣt him of lungenǣdre blōd.</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lch. ii. 106, 24)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="un-dirne" d:title="un-dirne">
		
		<body>
			<h1>un-dirne<span class="pron"> | un.dir.ne |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Not hidden, discovered, revealed, manifest</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gif mon āfelle on wuda wel monega treōwa and wyrð eft undierne (-dyrne, MS. B.)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. In. 43; Th. i. 128, 20: 44; Th. i. 130, 3)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt wearð underne eorðebūendum, ðæt Meotod hæfde miht</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. Th. 265, 1; Sat. 1)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Wīde wearð wyrd undyrne</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Apstls. Kmbl. 84; Ap. 42)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðā wæs Grendles gūðcræft gumum undyrne</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Beo. Th. 255; B. 127: 4004; B. 2000)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the punishment of sin shall stand revealed before them</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Bið him synwracu andweard undyrne</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. Th. 94, 16; Cri. 1541)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Nū is undyrne werum, hū ða wihte hātne sindon</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (429, 19; Rä. 43, 15)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic wordum wemde wyrd undyrne</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Andr. Kmbl. 2959; An. 1482)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic gearwe wāt ðæt ðē (God) siendan ealle wīsan (printed wifan) undierne and cūðe dīnre ðære hālgan þrynesse</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Anglia xi. 97, 7)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="Arrius" d:title="Arrius">
		<body>
			<h1>Arrius<span class="pron"> | ɑr.ri.us |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -ii</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Arius</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:Arīus" class="xref-target">Arīus</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="be-seōn" d:title="be-seōn">
		<body>
			<h1>be-seōn<span class="pron"> | be.se͜oːn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">intrans. To look</span>
					</p>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(1)</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">absolute</span>
							</p>
							<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
								<li>
									<p>
										<span class="sense-label">(a)</span>
										<span class="sub-heading">physical</span>
									</p>
									<ul class="quotes">
										<li>
											<span class="q-la">noli respicere post tergum</span>
											<span class="q-oe">Ne beseoh þū underbæc</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Gen. 19, 17)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Mann þe hys hand āsett on hys sulh and on bæc besyhð</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Lk. 9, 62)</span>
										</li>
									</ul>
								</li>
								<li>
									<p>
										<span class="sense-label">(b)</span>
										<span class="sub-heading">mental</span>
									</p>
									<ul class="quotes">
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Beseoh (respice) and gehȳr mē</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Spl. 12, 3)</span>
										</li>
									</ul>
								</li>
							</ol>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(2)</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">with preps.</span>
							</p>
							<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
								<li>
									<p>
										<span class="sense-label">(a)</span>
										<span class="sub-heading">physical</span>
									</p>
									<ul class="quotes">
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Beseō hē upp tō þǣre nǣddran, and hē leofað, swā hē besihð on hig</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Num. 21, 8)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Swā ðā eāgan on besiōð</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 41, 4; F. 252, 13)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-la">Dominus de coelo prospexit</span>
											<span class="q-oe">Of heofenum beseah Drihten</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 52, 3)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">þæt folc beseah on Faraones here</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Ex. 14, 10)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Hē beseah tō heofenum</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. Th. i. 62, 9: Ap. Th. 11, 18)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Hē underbæc beseah wið þæs wælfylles</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Gen. 2562)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">þonne hiē besāwon on þā burg</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 2, 8 ; S. 92, 32)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Beō se canon him ætforan eāgum, beseō tō</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (LK Th. ii. 250, 24)</span>
										</li>
									</ul>
								</li>
								<li>
									<p>
										<span class="sense-label">(b)</span>
										<span class="sub-heading">mental, to look with favour, attention, expectation, &amp;c.</span>
									</p>
									<ul class="quotes">
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Hē nǣfre ne besyhð to ðǣre uplican are</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 67, 14)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Beseah Drihten tō Abele and tō his lācum</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Gen. 4, 4, 5)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Hē beseah wið mīn, and gehȳrde mīn gebed</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 39, 1)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-la">omnes declinaverunt, simul inutiles facti sunt</span>
											<span class="q-oe">Ealle heō on āne īdelnesse symle besēgan</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (52, 4)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Beseoh tō mē</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 12, 3: 21, 1)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-la">intende in adjutorium meum</span>
											<span class="q-oe">Beseoh mē tō fultume</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (37, 21)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-la">respice in auxilium meum</span>
											<span class="q-oe">Beseoh þi mē on fultun</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (70, 11)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Beseoh tō ūs</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Gen. 47, 25)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">þēh Godes bydel misdō, ne beseō man nā þǣrtō ealles tō swȳðe</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Wlfst. 178, 11)</span>
										</li>
									</ul>
								</li>
							</ol>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">reflexive</span>
					</p>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(1)</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">absolute</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">cum elevasset oculos, vidit camelos</span>
									<span class="q-oe">þā hē hyne beseah, þā geseah hē olfendas</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Gen. 24, 63: 33, 1: Hml. S. 23 b, 772)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">cum circumspexisset huc atque illuc</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Þā beseah hē hyne ymbūtan hider and þider</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Ex. 2, 12)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ne beseoh þū þe nā</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Lch. i. 202, 17)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">ꝥ hē hine underbæc ne besāwe</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 35, 6; F. 170, 9)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(2)</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">with prep.</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Beseah hē hine underbæc wiþ ðæs wīfes</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 35, 6 ; F. 170, 14)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">ꝥ hē hine ne besiō tō his ealdun yfelum</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (17)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">III.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">trans. To see about, care for, attend to, provide for</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">omnia vasa cunctamque substantiam conspiciat</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ealle fata and spēde hē sceal beseōn</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (R. Ben. 55, 1)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē wæs wel besewen on reāfe and yfele on þeāwum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. Th. i. 534, 3)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hlāf well besewen and well gesyfled</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (C. D. iv. 278, 4)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Behealde hē þæt his oflētan ne beōn yfele besewene</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ll. Th. ii. 360, 27)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">multi superna respecti gratia</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Manega mid upplicre besawene gyfe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Scint. 46, 15)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="tigele" d:title="tigele">
		
		<body>
			<h1>tigele<span class="pron"> | ti.Ge.le |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -an</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A tile, brick</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. tegula)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Tigule tegula</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Txts. 101, 1992)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Tigele figulum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 148, 79)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Tigle testula</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Germ. 391, 17)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">testa</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Spl. 21, 16)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">operibus luti et lateris</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Mid weorcum clāmes and tigelan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ex. 1, 14)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">murus coctili latere atque interfuso bitumine compactus</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Se weall is geworht of tigelan and eorðtyrewan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 2, 4; Swt. 74, 17)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Genim swealwan, gebærn under tigelan tō ahsan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lchdm. ii. 156, 9)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ða reādan tigelan gecnuwa tō duste</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (114, 24)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">sume tibi laterem, et describes in eo civitatem Jerusalem</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Nim sume tigelan (tiglan, Cott. MSS.) and wrīt on hiere ða burg Hierusalem</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 21; Swt. 161, 3, 9, 11)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Tieglan (tiglan, Cott. MSS.)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Swt. 161, 12, 20)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">whoso teacheth a fool is as one that glueth a potsherd together (Eccl. 22, 7)</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Se ðe lǣrþ stuntne swylce se ðe belīme tigelan (testam)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Scint. 96, 19)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Tigelan lateres</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 51, 41)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Tigelena gemet a tale of bricks</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ex. 5, 14)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Tiglena testularum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hpt. Gl. 499, 28)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Tighelana tegularum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (459, 40)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Tigelum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. Th. 477, 28; Ruin. 31)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hig hæfdon tygelan (lateres) for stān</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Gen. 11, 3)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:þæc-tigele" class="xref-target">þæc-tigele</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:hrōf-tigel" class="xref-target">hrōf-tigel</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="CEORL" d:title="CEORL">
		<body>
			<h1>CEORL<span class="pron"> | Ke͜orl |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">a freeman of the lowest class, CHURL, countryman, husbandman</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. homo liber, rusticus, colonus)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">a churl's close must be fenced</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ceorles weorþig sceal beōn betȳned</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. In. 40; Th. i. 126, 13)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Se ceorl</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (60; Th. i. 140, 8)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">so also we ordain for all degrees, whether to churl or earl [gentle or simple]</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Swā we eāc settaþ be eallum hādum, ge ceorle ge eorle</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. Alf. pol. 4; Th. i. 64, 3)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">a twelve hundred man's oath stands for six churls' oaths</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Twelfhyndes mannes āþ forstent vi ceorla āþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. O. 13; Th. i. 182, 19)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">of a husbandman's meadow</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Be ceorles gærstūne</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. In. 42; Th. i. 128, 4, 5)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">a land's man</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Landes [MS. londes] ceorl</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. Met. Fox 12, 54; Met. 12, 27)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">a man, husband</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. vir, maritus)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">king of the commons</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ceorla cyngc</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 1020; Erl. 160, 23)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">old men wish</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ealdan ceorlas wilniaþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 36, 5; Fox 180, 7)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">voca virum [husband] tuum</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Clypa ðīnne ceorl</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Jn. Bos. 4, 16, 17)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">thow hast had five husbands</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðū hæfdest fīf ceorlas</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (4, 18)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">III.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">a free man, as opposed to þeōw, and to þrǣl a slave; or as opposed to þegen a thane or nobleman, as we say, 'gentle or simple:'</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">we know that, by the grace of God, a slave has risen to a thane, and a ceorl [free man] has risen to an earl, a singer to a priest, and a scribe to be a bishop</span>
							<span class="q-oe">We witan ðæt, þurh Godes gyfe, þrǣl wearþ to þegene, and ceorl wearþ to eorle, sangere to sacerde, and bōcere to biscope</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. Eth. vii. 21; Th. i. 334, 7-9)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">if a free man thrived, so that he had fully five hides of his own land, church and kitchen, bell-house and a city-gate-seat, and special duty in the king's hall, then was he thenceforth worthy of thane-right</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gif ceorl geþeāh, ðæt he hæfde fullīce fīf hīda āgenes landes, cirican and cycenan [MS. Ky-cenan UNCERTAIN ], bell-hūs and burh-geat-setl, and sunder-note on cynges healle, ðonne wæs he ðonon-forþ begen-rihtes weorþe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. R. 2; Th. i. 190, 14-17)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ceorl-boren" class="xref-target">ceorl-boren</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:ceorl-folc" class="xref-target">ceorl-folc</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:ceorl-ian" class="xref-target">ceorl-ian</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:ceorl-isc" class="xref-target">ceorl-isc</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:ceorl-iscnes" class="xref-target">ceorl-iscnes</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:ceorl-līe" class="xref-target">ceorl-līe</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:ceorl-līce" class="xref-target">ceorl-līce</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:ceorl-strang" class="xref-target">ceorl-strang</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:æcer-ceorl" class="xref-target">æcer-ceorl</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:hūs-" class="xref-target">hūs-</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="eāc" d:title="eāc">
		<body>
			<h1>eāc<span class="pron"> | æ͜ɑːK |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adverb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">where there is addition of objects</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Þǣr wearð Sīulf ealdorman ofslægen ... and Eādwold, and manige eāc tō him, ... swīðe mænige eāc mid him</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 905; P. 95, 16, 20)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Þā cinges þegnas ..., ge eāc sum dǣl þæs Norð-Wealcynnes</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (894; P. 87, 18)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hȳ habbaþ eall ꝥ ðā unstyriendan habbaþ, and eāc māre tō</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 41, 5; F. 252, 26)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">where there is addition of condition or circumstance</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hēt ic ǣlcne mon hine gegerwan, and faran forð, and ꝥ eāc bebeād ðæt ...</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Nar. 9, 37)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Drihten is mid þē on þīnre heortan and on þīnum innoþe and eāc on þīnum fultome</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bl. H. 5, 12)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Salde se here him micle āþas þæt hiē of his rīce uuoldon, and him eāc gehēton þæt ...</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 878; P. 76, 14)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Be westan Sealwuda ge be eāstan, ge eāc be norþan Temese</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (894; P. 87, 17: Bl. H. 15, 4: 21, 10)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hiē beōð ūpāhafene and eāc beōð onbærnde ... ge eāc beoð besmitene</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (25, 7)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē for þon ūs gesette ꝥ wē hine biddan sceoldan, þȳ wē sceolan þonne eāc ūre heortan geclǣnsian, ... Gehȳran wē eāc ꝥ ...</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (21, 2-5)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">III.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">combined with</span>
					</p>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(1)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">swā</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Fōron micel dǣl þāra burgwara, and eāc swā ōþres folces</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 896; P. 89, 5)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Līnsǣd sāwan, wādsǣd eāc swā</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Angl. ix. 262, 11)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Beōð henna ākende ... eāc swā (preterea) beōð wildeōr ācennede</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Nar. 34, 4)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Wæs ic sāriges mōdes and þā mīne frȳnd swā eāc</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (30, 15)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(2)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">swilce</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ac eāc swylce uerum</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (An. Ox. 2917: uerum etiam, 4096)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Næs nō on gesundum þingum ānum, ac eāc swylce on wiðerweardum þingum</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Bl. H. 13, 8)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="mund-heāls" d:title="mund-heāls">
		
		<body>
			<h1>mund-heāls<span class="pron"> | mund.xæ͜ɑːls |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Safety which comes from the protection (mund) afforded by another (?)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">when Christ was born, after he had chosen a safe retreat in Mary's protecting womb</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðā se ælmihtiga ācenned wearþ siððan hē Marian mundheāls geceās</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 14a ; Th. 28, 14; Cri. 446)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="brǣding" d:title="brǣding">
		<body>
			<h1>brǣding<span class="pron"> | bræː.ding |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A spreading</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. ampliatio)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">he may be ashamed of the spreading of his fame</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Mæg hine scamian ðære brǣdinge his hlīsan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 19; Fox 68, 24)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-nugan" d:title="ge-nugan">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-nugan<span class="pron"> | je.nu.ɣɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">present: 3sg: -hit -neah</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To suffice, to be sufficient, not to be wanting</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. sufficere)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">if in our soul we be not wanting [if it is sufficient to us in our soul]</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gif us on ferðe geneah</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 93 a; Th. 348, 29; Sch. 35: 90 a; Th. 337, 26; Gn. Ex. 70)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">no human tongue is sufficient to tell the divine virtue of that begotten messenger</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Nǣnig mennisc tunge ne geneah ðæs acendan engles godcund mægen to gesecgenne</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Blickl. Homl. 165, 5)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:be-nugan" class="xref-target">be-nugan</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:nugan" class="xref-target">nugan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="wude-" d:title="wude-">
		<body>
			<h1>wude-<span class="pron"> | wu.de |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:wudu-" class="xref-target">wudu-</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-wlitig" d:title="ge-wlitig">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-wlitig<span class="pron"> | je.wli.tiG |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:un-gewlitig" class="xref-target">un-gewlitig</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="sciccing" d:title="sciccing">
		
		<body>
			<h1>sciccing<span class="pron"> | ʃik.King |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">a cloak, cape</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. cappa)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Scicing, scinccing, scicging cappa</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Txts. 50, 245)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Sciccing</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. i. 284, 64: ii. 13, 24)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:preceding word" class="xref-target">preceding word</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="pocc" d:title="pocc">
		<body>
			<h1>pocc<span class="pron"> | pokk |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Wiþ pocce on eāgum</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Lch. ii. 36, 23)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ā-stīgan" d:title="ā-stīgan">
		<body>
			<h1>ā-stīgan<span class="pron"> | ɑː.stiː.ɣɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">A.</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">intrans.</span>
							</p>
							<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
								<li>
									<p>
										<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
										<span class="meaning-en">without adv. or prep. that marks upward or downward</span>
									</p>
									<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
										<li>
											<p>
												<span class="sense-label">(1)</span>
												<span class="meaning-en">of motion lit. or fig.</span>
											</p>
											<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
												<li>
													<p>
														<span class="sense-label">(a)</span>
														<span class="meaning-en">downward</span>
													</p>
													<ul class="quotes">
														<li>
															<span class="q-oe">Heō stihð oð þæs heōfenes heānesse, and þanon āstihð</span>
															<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 18, 6)</span>
														</li>
														<li>
															<span class="q-oe">Crīst on þīnne innoþ āstīgeþ</span>
															<span class="q-cite"> (Bl. H. 5, 14)</span>
														</li>
														<li>
															<span class="q-la">qui descendant in terram</span>
															<span class="q-oe">Þā þe on eorðan āstīgað</span>
															<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 21, 27)</span>
														</li>
														<li>
															<span class="q-oe">Tō ðām munte Synay āstāh se Scyppend</span>
															<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. Th. ii. 196, 22)</span>
														</li>
														<li>
															<span class="q-la">descendit</span>
															<span class="q-oe">Of heofenum āstāh (descendit) mannes Bearn</span>
															<span class="q-cite"> (386, 2: Ps. Spl. 7, 17)</span>
														</li>
														<li>
															<span class="q-oe">Þū āstige on helle grund</span>
															<span class="q-cite"> (Bl. H. 87, 14)</span>
														</li>
														<li>
															<span class="q-oe">Of heofenum oþ eorþan āstīgan</span>
															<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 4, 3; S. 567, 40: 570, 1)</span>
														</li>
														<li>
															<span class="q-en">to land</span>
															<span class="q-oe">Tō eorþan āstīgan</span>
															<span class="q-cite"> (Bl. H. 233, 27)</span>
														</li>
														<li>
															<span class="q-la">descendentibus in lacum</span>
															<span class="q-oe">Āstīgendum in seāð</span>
															<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Srt. 27, 1)</span>
														</li>
													</ul>
												</li>
												<li>
													<p>
														<span class="sense-label">(b)</span>
														<span class="meaning-en">upward</span>
													</p>
													<ul class="quotes">
														<li>
															<span class="q-la">ascendit</span>
															<span class="q-oe">Nān mann ne āstihð (ascendit) tō heofenum</span>
															<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. Th. ii. 386, 1)</span>
														</li>
														<li>
															<span class="q-la">ascendit in montem</span>
															<span class="q-oe">Hē āstāh (-stāhg, R.) on þone munt</span>
															<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. 5, 1)</span>
														</li>
														<li>
															<span class="q-oe">'Āstīgað on mīn scip.' Hē þā āstāg on ꝥ scip mid his discipulum</span>
															<span class="q-cite"> (Bl. H. 233, 23)</span>
														</li>
													</ul>
												</li>
												<li>
													<p>
														<span class="sense-label">(c)</span>
														<span class="meaning-en">direction not strongly marked</span>
													</p>
													<ul class="quotes">
														<li>
															<span class="q-oe">Þonne āstīgeþ wolcen from norþdǣle</span>
															<span class="q-cite"> (Bl. H. 91, 32)</span>
														</li>
														<li>
															<span class="q-oe">Storm of ðǣm munte āstāg</span>
															<span class="q-cite"> (203, 8)</span>
														</li>
														<li>
															<span class="q-oe">Seōð ꝥ þā bān āne beōn lǣfed, āstīge þǣrin gelōmlīce</span>
															<span class="q-cite"> (Lch. i. 340, 26)</span>
														</li>
													</ul>
												</li>
											</ol>
										</li>
										<li>
											<p>
												<span class="sense-label">(2)</span>
												<span class="meaning-en">metaphorical</span>
											</p>
											<ul class="quotes">
												<li>
													<span class="q-oe">Ic lǣrde wlance men ꝥ hiē ne āstigan on ofermēdu</span>
													<span class="q-cite"> (Bl. H. 185, 14)</span>
												</li>
												<li>
													<span class="q-la">efferatus superbia</span>
													<span class="q-oe">Hē wæs on swā micle ofermētto āstigen</span>
													<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 6, 9; S. 264, 8)</span>
												</li>
											</ul>
										</li>
									</ol>
								</li>
								<li>
									<p>
										<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
										<span class="meaning-en">with adv. or prep.</span>
									</p>
									<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
										<li>
											<p>
												<span class="sense-label">(1)</span>
												<span class="meaning-en">of motion, lit. or fig.</span>
											</p>
											<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
												<li>
													<p>
														<span class="sense-label">(a)</span>
														<span class="meaning-en">downward</span>
													</p>
													<ul class="quotes">
														<li>
															<span class="q-oe">Se Hālga Gāst ofer hiē āstāg</span>
															<span class="q-cite"> (Bl. H. 13, 328)</span>
														</li>
														<li>
															<span class="q-oe">Āstīh ādūne</span>
															<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. Th. ii. 196, 27)</span>
														</li>
														<li>
															<span class="q-oe">Wē leornedon ꝥ se Drihtnes Gāst ofer hiene āstige on culfran onlīcnesse</span>
															<span class="q-cite"> (Bl. H. 135, 1)</span>
														</li>
														<li>
															<span class="q-oe">Þām brōþrum wæs aneāðe niþer tō āstīgenne tō þām wæterseāðe</span>
															<span class="q-cite"> (Gr. D. 112, 17)</span>
														</li>
														<li>
															<span class="q-la">condescendendo</span>
															<span class="q-oe">Of dūne āstiggende (-stīgende, v. l.)</span>
															<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 101, 14)</span>
														</li>
													</ul>
												</li>
												<li>
													<p>
														<span class="sense-label">(b)</span>
														<span class="meaning-en">upward</span>
													</p>
													<ul class="quotes">
														<li>
															<span class="q-oe">Āstīh up tō mē</span>
															<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. Th. ii. 196, 29)</span>
														</li>
														<li>
															<span class="q-oe">Āstīg up</span>
															<span class="q-cite"> (Bl. H. 87, 22)</span>
														</li>
														<li>
															<span class="q-la">emersisse</span>
															<span class="q-oe">Þæt hiē up āstigen</span>
															<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 31, 35)</span>
														</li>
													</ul>
												</li>
											</ol>
										</li>
										<li>
											<p>
												<span class="sense-label">(2)</span>
												<span class="meaning-en">of direction</span>
											</p>
											<ul class="quotes">
												<li>
													<span class="q-oe">Se munt āstīhð up ðreō mīla on heānnysse</span>
													<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. Th. ii. 164, 14)</span>
												</li>
												<li>
													<span class="q-oe">Se stīpel sceolde āstīgan upp tō heofenum</span>
													<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. T. Grn. 4, 9)</span>
												</li>
											</ul>
										</li>
										<li>
											<p>
												<span class="sense-label">(3)</span>
												<span class="meaning-en">of excess</span>
											</p>
											<ul class="quotes">
												<li>
													<span class="q-oe">Ne āstīhð nān getel ofer þæt</span>
													<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. Th. i. 188, 35)</span>
												</li>
											</ul>
										</li>
									</ol>
								</li>
							</ol>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">B.</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">trans.</span>
							</p>
							<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
								<li>
									<p>
										<span class="sense-label">(1)</span>
										<span class="meaning-en">to descend, go down into</span>
									</p>
									<ul class="quotes">
										<li>
											<span class="q-la">qui descendunt mare in navibus</span>
											<span class="q-oe">Þā ðe āstīgað sǣ on scipum</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Spl. 106, 23)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Staþu āstīgan</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Lch. iii. 210, 16)</span>
										</li>
									</ul>
								</li>
								<li>
									<p>
										<span class="sense-label">(2)</span>
										<span class="meaning-en">to ascend, mount</span>
									</p>
									<ul class="quotes">
										<li>
											<span class="q-la">ego ascendo navem</span>
											<span class="q-oe">Ic āstīge mīn scyp</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Coll. M. 26, 31)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Wē gelȳfað þæt of mancynne swā micel getel āstige þæt uplice rīce</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. Th. i. 344, 13)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Āstīgan þæt heofenlice rīce</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (ii. 82, 9)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Scyp āstīgan</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Lch. iii. 184, 13)</span>
										</li>
									</ul>
								</li>
							</ol>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-þȳdon" d:title="ge-þȳdon">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-þȳdon<span class="pron"> | je.θyː.don |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge-þeōdan" class="xref-target">ge-þeōdan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="pytt" d:title="pytt">
		<body>
			<h1>pytt<span class="pron"> | pytt |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">a pit, hole in the ground, a grave</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Pyt puteus</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. i. 84, 58)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Scrobs ys pytt oððe dīc</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. Gr. 9, 51 ; Zup. 66, 10)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">sepulcrum patens est guttur eorum</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Heora mōd ys swā deōp swā grundleās pytt</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 5, 10)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gif hwā pytt (cisternam) ādelfe and hine ne oferhelie and ðǣr fealle on oxa oððe assa, gilde ðæs pyttes hlāford ðæra nȳtena wurð</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ex. 21, 33-34)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Pytte baratrum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 11, 68)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">On fūlan pyt; of ðam pytte on dene</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cod. Dip. Kmbl. iii. 77, 20)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">On wulfputt; of ðam pytte on ða wōgan ǣc</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (449, 31-32)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Tō wulfpytte</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cod. Dip. B. i. 280, 20)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gelǣste man ā ðone sāwelsceat æt openum pytte (cf. æt openum græfe, L. Eth. v. 12 ; Th. i. 308, 5)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wulfst. 118, 7)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Uton dōn hine on ðone ealdan pytt (cisternam)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Gen. 37. 20)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">in lacum missus sum</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic wæs on pytt beworpen</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (40, 15)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">lacum aperuit</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē ādylfþ ðone pytt</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 7, 15)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hwylces eōwres assa befealþ on ānne pytt (puteum)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lk. Skt. 14, 5)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē hēt ādelfan ǣnne gehwǣdne pytt</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. ii. 02, 2)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">On hiere bryne gemulton ealle ða onlīcnessa tōgædere and on pyttas besuncan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 5, 2 ; Swt. 216, 3)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">a pit (as in pitted with small-pox)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">serpedo (cf. serpedo a mesylle, 224, 9 : a tetere, 267, 48)</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Pyt ful wyrmses</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. i. 20, 4)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:gang-pytt" class="xref-target">gang-pytt</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:hor-pytt" class="xref-target">hor-pytt</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:lām-pytt" class="xref-target">lām-pytt</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:mōr-pytt" class="xref-target">mōr-pytt</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:rysc-pytt" class="xref-target">rysc-pytt</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:wæter-pytt" class="xref-target">wæter-pytt</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="dægmǣl-sceāwere" d:title="dægmǣl-sceāwere">
		
		<body>
			<h1>dægmǣl-sceāwere<span class="pron"> | dæɣ.mæːl.ʃæ͜ɑː.we.re |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">An observer of the dial, an observer of times and seasons, an astrologer, diviner</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Dægmēlsceāwere aruspex</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. i. 17, 12)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">horoscopus</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (60, 11)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:tīd-sceāwere" class="xref-target">tīd-sceāwere</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="iōwih" d:title="iōwih">
		<body>
			<h1>iōwih<span class="pron"> | i͜oː.wix |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:eōwic" class="xref-target">eōwic</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="hundredes man" d:title="hundredes man">
		<body>
			<h1>hundredes man<span class="pron"> | xun.dre.des, mɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Cyðe hit man ðam hundredes men</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. Edg. H. 2; Th. i. 258, 7)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:hundred-mann" class="xref-target">hundred-mann</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ebba" d:title="ebba">
		<body>
			<h1>ebba<span class="pron"> | eb.bɑ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">On þīs ylcan geāre wæs swa mycel ebba ǣghwǣr ānes dæges swā nān man ǣror gemunde, and swā ꝥ man fērde rīdende and gangende ofer Tæmese be-eāstan þǣre brigge on Lunden</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 1114; P. 244, 13)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">iii.</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">ebban tȳne he must put three fences to correspond to the heights of spring, middle and neap tides (v. Seebohm Vill. Comm. p. 155)</span>
							</p>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="gefrett" d:title="gefrett">
		<body>
			<h1>gefrett<span class="pron"> | Ge.frett |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>participle</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">consumed</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. devorāvit)</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:fretan" class="xref-target">fretan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-bīwan" d:title="ge-bīwan">
		
		<body>
			<h1>ge-bīwan<span class="pron"> | je.biː.wɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To rub, polish</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">confricatus, i. lima—tus, exprimatus</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gebeōwed</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 133, 25)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:bīwan" class="xref-target">bīwan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="fæstum" d:title="fæstum">
		<body>
			<h1>fæstum<span class="pron"> | fæ.stum |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">VI.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">of established reputation (?), standard (of books) ?</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">aperto praecepit edicto, ne quis Christianus docendorum liberalium studiorum professor esset</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē forbeād openlīce þæt mon nāne fæste bōc ne leornade</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 6, 31; S. 286, 4)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="swician" d:title="swician">
		<body>
			<h1>swician<span class="pron"> | swi.Ki.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -ode</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to wander</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðaer hī swiciaþ on swīman, firenweorc beraþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. Th. 79, 33; Cri. 1300)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">spatiaretur</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Suicade, suicudae spatiaretur</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Txts. 99, 1893)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">per nota loca dispersi vagarentur</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hī ðurh cūþe stōwe swicedon and fōron</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 4. 4; S. 571, 4)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">erraverunt in solitudine</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hī swycedan geond wēsten</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 106, 3)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Swicedan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (39)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">pervagatus</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Swiciende pervagatus</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 68, 79)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to depart, turn</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">a judiciis tuis non declinavi</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Nā ic fram ðīnum dōnum dǣdum swicade</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 118, 102)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">III.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to deceive</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Mǣst ǣlc swicode and ōðrum derede wordes and dǣde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wulfst. 160, 3)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ne ǣnig ne syrwe ne ōðrum ne swicie</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (73, 12: 70, 5)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Lytelīce swician</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (55, 16)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ða men ðe ne dorstan for Godes ege swician . . . ða ðe cūðan swician and befician and mid leāsbregdum earmum mannum derian</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. I. P. 12; Th. ii. 320, 31-26)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Swiciende licceteras ārīsaþ and forlǣraþ tō manege</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wulfst. 89, 17)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">III a.</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">with prep, on, ymb, to practise deceit in relation to a matter</span>
								<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. cf. O. Sax. swīkan umbi)</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-en">he who fraudulently deceives in the matter of a monastery's possessions</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Se ðe on mynstres ǣhtum mid fācne swicaþ</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. i. 398, 26)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Annanias and Saphira swicedon on heora āgenum ǣhtum</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (33)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-en">is ever practising deceit in respect to man</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Se syrwienda deofol ā swicaþ, embe mancyn</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Wulfst. 107, 23)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Se sceaða georne swicode ymb ða sāwle</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. Th. 38, 15; Gen. 607)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">IV.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to offend; also to be offended</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. scandalizare, scandalizari)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gif ðīn hand ðē swicaþ (scandalizat)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. Kmbl. 18, 8, 9: Mk. Skt. 9, 43, 45)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">etsi omnes scandalizati fuerint serf non ego</span>
							<span class="q-oe">þeāh ðe ealle swicion ne swicige. ic ðē nā</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (14, 29)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">IV a.</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">to give offence by words, speak injuriously</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">non murmures, non blasphemes</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Nā murcna ðū nā swica ðū</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Scint. 164, 16)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ā-swician" class="xref-target">ā-swician</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:ǣ-swician" class="xref-target">ǣ-swician</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:be-swician" class="xref-target">be-swician</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:swīcan" class="xref-target">swīcan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="burg-sittende" d:title="burg-sittende">
		<body>
			<h1>burg-sittende<span class="pron"> | burɣ.sit.ten.de |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">city-dwelling, inhabiting a city</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:burh-sittende" class="xref-target">burh-sittende</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="mān-dǣd" d:title="mān-dǣd">
		<body>
			<h1>mān-dǣd<span class="pron"> | mɑːn.dæːd |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">piaculo</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Māndǣde</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (An. Ox. 2006)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">facinorum, i. criminum</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Māndǣda</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (921)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">passionum, i. uitiorum</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Māndǣda</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (1137)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-cnedan" d:title="ge-cnedan">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-cnedan<span class="pron"> | je.kne.dɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -cnæd, pl: -cnǣdon</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -cneden</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To mix, mingle, spread, knead</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. depsere)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">depse nunc tres mensuras similaginis</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gecned nū hrædlīce þrī sestras smedeman</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Gen. 18, 6)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">knead it with milk</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gecned hine mid meocle</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Th. An. 119, 5)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">donec fermentaretur totum</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ōððæt sic gecnoeden all</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lk. Skt. Lind. 13, 21)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">cataplasma</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gecneden sealf</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cot. 209)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="þǣr-bufan" d:title="þǣr-bufan">
		<body>
			<h1>þǣr-bufan<span class="pron"> | θæːr.bu.fɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adverb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Besides, over and above that</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē cwæð : 'Biscepe gedafnaþ ðæt hē siē tǣlleās.' Ðǣrbufan (v. 1 Tim. 3, 2 sqq. for the additional remarks referred to) is geteald hwelc hē beōn sceal, gif hē untǣlwierðe biþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 8; Swt. 53, 10)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="þearf" d:title="þearf">
