			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="byrg(e)an" d:title="byrg(e)an">
		<body>
			<h1>byrg(e)an<span class="pron"> | byrɣ, e, ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">to save</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:be-byrg(e)an" class="xref-target">be-byrg(e)an</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="leāse" d:title="leāse">
		<body>
			<h1>leāse<span class="pron"> | læ͜ɑː.se |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adverb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Falsely</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē leāse fleswede (leāslīce ongann)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 2, 9; Sch. 147, 1)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="hold" d:title="hold">
		<body>
			<h1>hold<span class="pron"> | xold |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A title which seems to have been introduced by the Danes</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ysopa hold and Ōscytel hold</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (905; Erl. 98, 34)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Þurcytel eorl and ða holdas ealle</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (918; Erl. 104, 22)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Þurferþ eorl and ða holdas</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (921; Erl. 107, 28)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Holdes and cyninges heāhgerēfan wergild iiii þūsend þrymsa</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. Wg. 4; Th. i. 186, 8)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-sceād" d:title="ge-sceād">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-sceād<span class="pron"> | je.ʃæ͜ɑːd |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">reasonable, discreet, prudent</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hī setton him ǣnne wīcnere getreōwne and swīðe gesceādne</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. S. 23, 217)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Þā ne beōð nā wīse ne gescāde þe Godē nellað hȳran</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ll. Th. i. 334, 5)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">calculated, fixed (? cf. ge-sceād ; XI. 2)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">ratum</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gesceād ratum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Kent. Gl. 1164)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:un-gesceād" class="xref-target">un-gesceād</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="cwealde" d:title="cwealde">
		<body>
			<h1>cwealde<span class="pron"> | kwæ͜ɑl.de |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -cwealde, pl: -cwealdon</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">slew</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:cwellan" class="xref-target">cwellan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="rǣw" d:title="rǣw">
		<body>
			<h1>rǣw<span class="pron"> | ræːw |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Andlang rǣwe on þornwīc</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (C. D. v. 220, 36)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-en">In compounds</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Tō brōce; andlang brōcrēwe</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (C. D. v. 122, 19)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">On ðā norðrǣwe</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (iii. 412, 28)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:fyrs-rǣw" class="xref-target">fyrs-rǣw</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:stæf-rǣw" class="xref-target">stæf-rǣw</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:þorn-rǣw" class="xref-target">þorn-rǣw</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:wīþig-rǣw" class="xref-target">wīþig-rǣw</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="byldan" d:title="byldan">
		<body>
			<h1>byldan<span class="pron"> | byl.dɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -bylde</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -bylded</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To make bold, to animate, instigate, exhort, encourage, confirm</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. animare, instigare, hortarī confirmare)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">he would encourage the race of the Frisians</span>
							<span class="q-oe">He Fresena cyn byldan wolde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Beo. Th. 2193; B. 1094)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">good companions should encourage a young prince</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Geongne æðeling sceolon gōde gesīðas byldan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Menol. Fox 488; Gn. C. 15)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the son of Ælfric encouraged them</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hī bylde bearn Ælfrīces</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Byrht. Th. 137, 60; By. 209)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">so Godric encouraged them all to the war</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Swā hī ealle bylde Godrīc to gūþe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Byrht. Th. 141, 11; By. 320)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">rogaverunt Sigberctum ad confirmandum militem secum venire in prælium</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Bǣdon hī Sigebyrht ðæt he mid him to ðam gefeohte fōre and hyra fultum trymede and bylde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 3, 18; S. 546, 20, col. 1)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:byld" class="xref-target">byld</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="bere-ærn" d:title="bere-ærn">
		
		<body>
			<h1>bere-ærn<span class="pron"> | be.re.ærn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>neuter noun</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">horreum</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Bereern (her-, L. ) horreum</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Lk. R. 12, 24)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Þā feōwer hyrnan þæs berenes</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Lch. iii. 290, 28)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">area</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Bernes flōr (berern, L.) area</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Lk. 3, 17)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Æt bernes dure</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Ll. Th. i. 440, 2)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">On hlāfordes berne . . . of his āganum berne</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Ll. Th. i. 434, 16, 19 : Cht. E. 377, 6, 7)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">On bærene gebringan</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Cht. Th. 144, 38)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Tō hire byrene (bern-hūs, berne, v. ll.)</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Gr. D. 68, 22 : 69, 4: 290, 20, 24)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">In berern</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. L. R. 13, 30: Lk. L. R. 3, 17)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Nabbað nig bern (beren, v. l. )</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Lk. 12, 24)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Ic tōwurpe mīne bernu (bererno. L., berern, R. )</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (18)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ān-leger" d:title="ān-leger">
		<body>
			<h1>ān-leger<span class="pron"> | ɑːn.le.Ger |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">lying with one person</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. unicubus)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">a woman with one husband</span>
							<span class="q-la">unicuba</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ānlegere wifman a woman with one husband</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (R. 8)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-yrgan" d:title="ge-yrgan">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-yrgan<span class="pron"> | je.yr.ɣɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge-irgan" class="xref-target">ge-irgan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="eæd-leǣnian" d:title="eæd-leǣnian">
		<body>
			<h1>eæd-leǣnian<span class="pron"> | e.æd.le.æː.ni.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">to reward</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. retribuere)</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge-eædleǣnian" class="xref-target">ge-eædleǣnian</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:edleǣnian" class="xref-target">edleǣnian</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="hǣmed-dreām" d:title="hǣmed-dreām">
		
		<body>
			<h1>hǣmed-dreām<span class="pron"> | xæː.med.dræ͜ɑːm |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">The pleasure of a vicious life(?), a life of pleasure</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">lenocinii (antequam Samson illecebrosis lenocinii nexibus nodaretur, Ald. 72, 15)</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hǣmedrīmes (hǣmeddrīmes), [hæmed-] scipes lenocinii</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (An. Ox. 5046)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="fore-gegān" d:title="fore-gegān">
		<body>
			<h1>fore-gegān<span class="pron"> | fo.re.Ge.ɣɑːn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">(1)</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to precede</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">stella antecedebat eos</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Stearra foregeeāde heū</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. L. 2, 9)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">(2)</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to pass away</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">hora praeteriuit</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Tīd is foregeeād ł tīd eāde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Mk. L. R. 6, 35)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="fleardere" d:title="fleardere">
		<body>
			<h1>fleardere<span class="pron"> | flæ͜ɑr.de.re |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">One who acts with (wicked) folly, wantonly</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Warnige hē eāc ꝥ hē þurh geþafunge ne wurðe þǣra fleardera gefēra</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Nap. 23)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:next word" class="xref-target">next word</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-gyrnan" d:title="ge-gyrnan">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-gyrnan<span class="pron"> | je.Gyr.nɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge-girnan" class="xref-target">ge-girnan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ofer-stǣlan" d:title="ofer-stǣlan">
		<body>
			<h1>ofer-stǣlan<span class="pron"> | o.fer.stæː.lɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">to confute, convince, convict</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic oferstǣle confuto</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. i. 34, 15)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Oberstaelid confutat</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (ii. 105, 32)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Oferstǣleþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (15, 31)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">I allow that I am very properly confuted, and I am always much more pleased when you confute me with such arguments, than I ever should be when I confuted another man</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic eom geþafa ðæt ic eom swīðe rihte oferstēled, and ic beo ealne weig micle gefegenra ðonne ðū mē myd þillīcum ofærstǣlest, ðonne ic ǣfre wēræ ðonne ic ōðerne man oferstǣlde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Shrn. 197, 32-35)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ne beō dū tō ānwille; forðam ðe is gerisenlīcre ðæt ðū sī mid rihte oferstēled, ðonne ðū oferstēle ōðerne man mid wōge</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Prov. Kmbl. 8)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt hi ðæs deōfles leāsunge mid Godes sōðfæstnysse oferstǣlan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. ii. 100, 9)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Oberstaelende convincens</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 104, 37)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">confutans</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Oferstǣlende</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (14, 60: confutans, 23, 45 : Hpt. Gl. 436, 37)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Oberstaeled convicta</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 104, 45)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">when he is convinced</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðonne hē oferstǣled biþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 6 ; Swt. 46, 16)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">he will then be convicted of being God's foe</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē biþ ðonne oferstǣled ðæt hē Godes feōnd is</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. i. 612, 24)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">if a man commit perjury on a relic, and he be convicted</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gif hwā mǣne āþ on hāligdōme swerige, and hē oferstǣled weorðe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. C. S. 36; Th. i. 398, 5 : 37 ; Th. i. 398, 12)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Oferstǣlede confutati, superati, convicli, redarguti</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hpt. Gl. 475, 19)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-mǣtan" d:title="ge-mǣtan">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-mǣtan<span class="pron"> | je.mæː.tɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -mǣtte</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -mǣted</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To dream</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. somniare, somnium videre)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">what he had dreamed</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hwæt hine gemǣtte</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. 178; Th. 223, 20; Dan. 122 : Rood. Kmbl. 3; Kr. 2.)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">as his lord had dreamed</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Swā his man-drihten gemǣted wearþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. 179; Th. 225, 21; Dan. 157.)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:mǣtan" class="xref-target">mǣtan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="bleō-fāg" d:title="bleō-fāg">
		<body>
			<h1>bleō-fāg<span class="pron"> | ble͜oː.fɑːɣ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">uersicolor</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Bleōfāh uersicolor</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (An. Ox. 521)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">in orbem</span>
						<span class="q-oe">On þysne mislecan ymbhwyrft and bleōfāgan in orbem</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 48, 59)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">multicolora</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Bleōfāge multicolora</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Germ. 390, 104)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="anhagie" d:title="anhagie">
		<body>
			<h1>anhagie<span class="pron"> | ɑn.xɑ.Gi͜y |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">III.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">without tō</span>
					</p>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(1)</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">with dat. infin.</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Seō racu ðe mē onhagað ðē tō gerihtreccenne</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Solil. H. 26, 7)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ne onhagað ūs nā swīðor be dām tō sprecenne</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. Th. i. 488, 8)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">etsi rerum tarditas foras peccatum distulit, intus hoc consensionis opere voluntas implevit</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Ðæt ðætte hine ne onhagode ūtane forð tō brenganne mid weorcum, innane hē hit geðafode</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 417. 17)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-en">what is proper for him to give, what he is to keep</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Hwæt hine anhagige tō sellanne, hwæt hē healdan scyle</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (341, 13)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(2)</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">with infinitive</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">saepe mansueti dissolutionis torpescunt taedio</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Oft ðā monðwǣran weorðað swā besolcne . . . ðæt hiē ne anhagað nāne wuht nyttwyrðes dōn</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 289, 16)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(3)</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">with clause</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Þā þe heora hlāfordas freōgean noldon, oþþe hiē ne anhagade þæt hiē mehten</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 4, 9; S. 190, 34)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="eācan" d:title="eācan">
		<body>
			<h1>eācan<span class="pron"> | æ͜ɑː.kɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -eōc, pl: -eōcon</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -eācen, past participle sg: -ēcen</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">to increase (trans.)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hī sculon ǣlce dæg eācan (ȳcan, v. l.) ꝥ mon ǣlce dæg wanaþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 26, 2; F. 94, 1)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Nō þās bebodu tō brecanne, ac mid eallum gōdum tō eācanne (īcanne, v. l.)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ll. Th. i. 56, 2)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>participle</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(1)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">increased, augmented</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Eācne egesan</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Sal. 473)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-en">wounds from the swords are increased upon me by deadly stroke day and night</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Mē ecga dolg eācen weorðað þurh deāðslege dagum and nihtum</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Rä. 6, 13)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(2)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">endowed with excellent qualities or properties, noble, excellent, great</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Higelāces þegn, gōd mid Geātum ... wæs mægenes strengest, ... æðele and eācen</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (B. 198: Rā. 34, 11)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Eācen feoh (cf. hālig feoh, 201)</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Gen. 1517)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hē eācenne gāst in sefan sende, snyttro cræftas</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Dan. 485)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Beorhtne sunu, beam eācen Godes</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Cri. 205)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Eald sweord eācen</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (B. 1663)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Eācne eardas</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (1621)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ic heāfde forcearf Grendeles mōdor eācnum ecgum</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (2140)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
							<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
								<li>
									<p>
										<span class="sense-label">(2 a)</span>
										<span class="meaning-en">endowed, inspired with something</span>
									</p>
									<ul class="quotes">
										<li>
											<span class="q-la">afflatus (praesago spiritu, Ald. 35, 13)</span>
											<span class="q-oe">Eācen</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii, 79, 48: 5, 6)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Adam wearð of Godes mūðe gāste eācen</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Gen. 1001: Rä. 10, 8)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Bið seō mōddor mægene eācen</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (81, 15)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Cræfte eācen</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (21)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Nǣron gē swā eācne mōdgeþances</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Dan. 136)</span>
										</li>
									</ul>
								</li>
							</ol>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(3)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">pregnant</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">coelesti pignore, Ald. 182, 5</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Eācene feta</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 94, 40: 37, 40)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">i. fecunda, plena, gravida</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Eācenu foeta</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Wülck. Gl. 238, 8)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">On ðone dæg S&amp;c-tilde;a Maria wæs eācen geworden</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Shrn. 67, 9: Cri. 38: Deōr. 11)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Heō wæs magotimbre be Abrahame eācen worden</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Gen. 2236: 2766)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">ex fecundo (utero)</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Of ēcnum</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Hpt. Gl. 404, 67)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Idesa wurdon eācne, eaforan brōhtan on woruld</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (2606)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">vae praegnantibus</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Wā ēknum</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. R. 24, 19)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:bearn-eācen" class="xref-target">bearn-eācen</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:feorh-eācen" class="xref-target">feorh-eācen</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:mægen-eācen" class="xref-target">mægen-eācen</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:īcan" class="xref-target">īcan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="hago-spind" d:title="hago-spind">
		
		<body>
			<h1>hago-spind<span class="pron"> | xɑ.ɣo.spind |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">The cheek</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hagospind genæ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. 64, 41)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Heagospind</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (282, 56)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hecgaspind</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. Gl. 71; Som. 70, 78; Wrt. Voc. 43, 11)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">a hart's cheek</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Heortes heagospind a hart's cheek</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lchdm. i. 336, 12)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:spind" class="xref-target">spind</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="on-drincan" d:title="on-drincan">
		<body>
			<h1>on-drincan<span class="pron"> | on.drin.kɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Ic ðæs wæteres ondranc</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. S. 23 b, 506)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">haec bestia potata aqua</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Ðis deōr mid þȳ ðe hit þæs wætres ondronc</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Nar. 15, 18)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:in-drincan" class="xref-target">in-drincan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="hwæcce" d:title="hwæcce">
		<body>
			<h1>hwæcce<span class="pron"> | xwæk.Ke |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -an</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A chest</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:hwicce" class="xref-target">hwicce</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="hlāw" d:title="hlāw">
		<body>
			<h1>hlāw<span class="pron"> | xlɑːw |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:hlǣw" class="xref-target">hlǣw</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="wōl-bryne" d:title="wōl-bryne">
		<body>
			<h1>wōl-bryne<span class="pron"> | woːl.bry.ne |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Deadly violence</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">Romae gravis pestilentia per universam civitatem violenter incanduit, ut merito praecedente prodigio coelum ardere visum sit, quando caput gentium tanto morborum igne flagravit</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Wearð micel wundor on heofonum gesewen, swelce eal se hefon birnende wæs. Ðæt tācen wearð on Rōmānum swīþe gesweotolad mid ðæm miclan wōlbryne monncwealmes, ðe him raðe ðæs æfter com</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 2, 6; Swt. 86, 24)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="for-bernan" d:title="for-bernan">
		<body>
			<h1>for-bernan<span class="pron"> | for.ber.nɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:for-bærnan" class="xref-target">for-bærnan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ā-brēgan" d:title="ā-brēgan">
		<body>
			<h1>ā-brēgan<span class="pron"> | ɑː.breː.ɣɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Ðæt nīwe wīlte ābrēgeþ (terret) ðæs mannes mōd</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Gr. D. 135, 19)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">God heora mōd ābrēgde.</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (249, 10)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">terreat</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Ābrēge terreat</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Lch. i. 69, 5)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">territus</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Āfyrhted and ābrēged territus</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Gr. D. 222, 15)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">vehetnenter exterrītus</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Swīðe ābrēged vehetnenter exterrītus</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (39, 7)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Hiē forhte and ābrēgde cwǣdon</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Bl. H. 85, 9)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Wǣron ðā fȳnd ābrēgede mid ðȳ egesan</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Shrn. 136, 15)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="wealdend" d:title="wealdend">
		
		<body>
			<h1>wealdend<span class="pron"> | wæ͜ɑl.dend |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">one who exercises power over persons or things, a controller, master</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">quod quisque potest, in eo validus: quod non potest, in hoc imbecillis esse censendus est</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ǽlc mon biþ wealdend ðæs ðe hē welt, næfþ hē nānne anweald ðæs ðe hē ne welt</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 36, 3; Fox 176, 17)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hī hine heom for god hæfdon, and hȳ sǣdon ðæt hē wǣre ealles gewinnes waldend</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 1, 6; Swt. 36, 21)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">we knew he was master of us</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Wē witon hē ūre wæs wealdend</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Blickl. Homl. 243, 18)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Se ðe ðæs weddes waldend sȳ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. Edm. B. 6; Th. i. 254, 22)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">nequam homines potenteis felicesque arbitraris</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðū wēndest ðæt steōrleāse men wǣron gesǣlige and wealdendas ðisse worulde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 8, 3; Fox 14, 1)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">ille genus humanum terrenis omnibus praestare voluit</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē wolde ðætte ealle men wǣran ealra ōþra gesceafta wealdandas</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (14, 2; Fox 44, 33)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">one who exercises dominion, a ruler, governor, sovereign</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">hic et haec praesul</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðes and ðeōs wealdend hic et haec praesul</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. Gr. 9, 10; Zup. 39, 12)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Cum mid ūs for ðon ðe ðū eart ūre wealdend</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Blickl. Homl. 239, 9)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Eādgār, Engla waldend</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 973; Erl. 124, 9)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Eādweard, hæleða wealdend</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (1065; Erl. 196, 27)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Englalandes wealdend</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cod. Dip. Kmbl. iv. 232, 3)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">non dominamur fidei vestrae</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ne sint wē nāne waldendas eōwres geleāfan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 17; Swt. 115, 24)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">non dominantes in clero</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ne sint wē nāne waldendas ðisses folces</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Swt. 119, 24)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðeōda kyningas beōð ðæs folces</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-tīdan" d:title="ge-tīdan">
		
		<body>
			<h1>ge-tīdan<span class="pron"> | je.tiː.dɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -de</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -ed</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To betide, happen</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. contingere)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">it often happens</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Getīdeþ oft it often happens</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 33, 2; Fox 124, 13)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">ne deterius tibi āliquid contingat</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðē-læs ðe ðē on sumum þingum wyrs getīde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Jn. Bos. 5, 14)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">it happened that...</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Getȳdde hit, ðæt ...</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 16, 2; Fox 52, 34)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="un-gefrætwod" d:title="un-gefrætwod">
		<body>
			<h1>un-gefrætwod<span class="pron"> | un.Ge.fræ.twod |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Unadorned</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">incompta</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ungefrætwodu</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 44, 3)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="fearh-hama" d:title="fearh-hama">
		<body>
			<h1>fearh-hama<span class="pron"> | fæ͜ɑrx.xɑ.mɑ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -an</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A little stem</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. cauliculus)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Fearh-hama cauliculus</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. Gl. 76; Som. 71, 117; Wrt. Voc. 45, 22)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="here-lof" d:title="here-lof">
		<body>
			<h1>here-lof<span class="pron"> | xe.re.lof |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">warlike glory, fame</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">hlīsa rumusculus</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Herelof</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (An. Ox. 4564)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">famosae uirginitatis rumore (comperto)</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hlīsfulles mǣg[ðhādes] herelofe (herelofa rumore, fama, Hpt. Gl. 511, 25)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (4521)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">a sign of victory, trophy</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">tropeum, i. signum uiclorie</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Herelof</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (An. Ox. 1908)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">triumphi tropeum</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Siges herelof</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (1761)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="berþor" d:title="berþor">
		<body>
			<h1>berþor<span class="pron"> | ber.θor |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:beorþor" class="xref-target">beorþor</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:hyse-beorþor" class="xref-target">hyse-beorþor</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="circan" d:title="circan">
		<body>
			<h1>circan<span class="pron"> | Kir.kɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">to roar (?)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Circinde wæter</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lch. i. 390, 11)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:cearcian" class="xref-target">cearcian</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="leāsing" d:title="leāsing">
		<body>
			<h1>leāsing<span class="pron"> | læ͜ɑː.sing |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A false person</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">never shall thou persuade me to promise tribute to false creatures, to dumb and deaf idols [or is leāsingum = with lies, falsely. v. leāsung]</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Nǣfre ðū gelǣrest ðæt ic leāsingum dumbum and deāfum deōfolgieldum gaful onhāte</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 68 a; Th. 251, 23; Jul. 149)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:leāsung" class="xref-target">leāsung</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="scīnendlīc" d:title="scīnendlīc">
		<body>
			<h1>scīnendlīc<span class="pron"> | ʃiː.nend.liːK |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Clear, bright</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Beorht ł scīnendlīc ł leōht lucidum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Lamb. 18, 9)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:þurh-scīnendlīc" class="xref-target">þurh-scīnendlīc</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="mōt-gerēfa" d:title="mōt-gerēfa">
		<body>
			<h1>mōt-gerēfa<span class="pron"> | moːt.Ge.reː.fɑ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -an</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">The gerēfa who presides at a court or mōt</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">nullus vicecomes vel praepositus</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Swā ðæt nān scȳrgerēfe oððe mōtgerēfe ðār habban ǣne sōcne oððe gemōt būton ðæs abbudes āgen hǣse</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cod. Dip. Kmbl. iv. 200, 9)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="georran" d:title="georran">
		<body>
			<h1>georran<span class="pron"> | Ge͜or.rɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:girran" class="xref-target">girran</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="weā-gesiþ" d:title="weā-gesiþ">
		<body>
			<h1>weā-gesiþ<span class="pron"> | wæ͜ɑː.Ge.siθ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">-Weāgesȳþ satelles</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (An. Ox. 46, 35)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="rusce" d:title="rusce">
		<body>
			<h1>rusce<span class="pron"> | ru.ʃe |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -an</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Rushy ground (?)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Tō ðære wulfruscan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cod. Dip. Kmbl. iii. 131, 7)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:rysc" class="xref-target">rysc</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="hēdan" d:title="hēdan">
		<body>
			<h1>hēdan<span class="pron"> | xeː.dɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to take charge or possession of (with gen.)</span>
					</p>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(1)</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">the object a person</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Gif hē næbbe mǣgburg, hēden his þā gefān</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Ll. Th. i. 148, 19)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(2)</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">the object a thing</span>
							</p>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to have a care for, take notice of (with gen.)</span>
					</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">III.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to care for, take notice of (with acc.)</span>
					</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">IV.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to take care that (with clause)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hēde sē ðe scīre healde ꝥ hē friðige and forðige ǣlce be ðām ðe hit sēlest sȳ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Angl. ix. 259, 13)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">V.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to observe, take note of (gen.)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Næs him nā þe sēl þæs þe hē georne hēdde, ne mihte hē þǣr nǣnne geseōn þe hē gecnāwan cūþe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. S. 23, 638)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gelamp hit ꝥ sume hlosniende menn ðǣr betweōnan eōdon and þisra seofona georne hēddon</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (137)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ferhþ-loca" d:title="ferhþ-loca">
		
		<body>
			<h1>ferhþ-loca<span class="pron"> | ferxθ.lo.kɑ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -an</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Soul-inclosure, bosom, body</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. mentis clausūra, pectus, corpus)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">that thy name, O Christ, be firmly established in our soul's inclosure</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt ðīn nama, Crist, in ūrum ferhþlocan sī feste gestaðelod</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hy. 6, 5, 32; Hy. Grn. ii. p. 286, 5, 32)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">dread ye not feeble bodies</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ne willaþ eōw andrǣdan fǣge ferhþlocan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. 156; Th. 194, 27; Exod. 267)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="mǣrþu" d:title="mǣrþu">
		
