			<h1>cild-claþ<span class="pron"> | Kild.klɑθ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>neuter noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A child-cloth, a swaddling-cloth</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. infantilis pannus)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">pannis eum involvit</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hine mid cildclāðum bewand</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lk. Bos. 2, 7)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="freō-man" d:title="freō-man">
		<body>
			<h1>freō-man<span class="pron"> | fre͜oː.mɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-en">what freeborn children wilt thou give me, Ruler of spirits, for my comfort? ... Thou hast not granted me a son ... My steward goes rejoicing in fair sons and daughters</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Hwæt gifest þū me, gāsta Waldend, freōmanna tō frōfre ... ne sealdest þū mē sunu ... Gǣð gerēfa mīn fægen freōbearnum</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Gen. 2175)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Eallum freōmannum (friōum monnura, v.l.) þās dagas siēn forgifene.</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Ll. Th. i. 92, 2)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="heolfor" d:title="heolfor">
		<body>
			<h1>heolfor<span class="pron"> | xe͜ol.for |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>neuter noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Blood from a wound, gore</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. cruor)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">there came not out blood or gore from my breast though the steel with stiff edge bit me</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Blōd ūt ne com heolfor of hreþre ðeāh mec bite stīðecg stȳle</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 130 a; Th. 499, 9; Rä. 88, 13)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">thirsty for gore</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Heolfres þurstge</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (99 b; Th. 373, 24; Seel. 114)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">blood and hot gore bubbled up in the water</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Flōd blōde weōl hātan heolfre</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Beo. Th. 2850; B. 1423: 1702; B. 849: 2609; B. 1302: Andr. Kmbl. 2483; An. 1243: 2555; An. 1279: Cd. 166; Th. 206, 9; Exod. 449: Th. 208, 1; Exod. 476)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="fōr-sceōtan" d:title="fōr-sceōtan">
		<body>
			<h1>fōr-sceōtan<span class="pron"> | foːr.ʃe͜oː.tɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">present: 3sg: -scȳt, pl: -sceōtaþ</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -sceāt, pl: -scuton</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -scoten</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To shoot before, anticipate, come before, prevent</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. anticipare, prævenire)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">unhappy men cannot wait till he [death] comes to them, but anticipate him beforehand</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ða ungesǣligan menn ne māgon gebidon hwonne he [deāþ] him to cume, ac fōrsceōtaþ hine fōran</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 39, 1; Fox 212, 3)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the transient punishment will prevent eternal damnation</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Fōrscȳt ðæt hwīlendlīce wīte ða ēcan geniðerunge</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. i. 576, 2)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">Deus meus præveniet me</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Mīn God fōrscȳt [MS. forscytte] oððe fōrestepþ me</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Lamb. 58, 11)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-hweled" d:title="ge-hweled">
