			<h1>wyrhta<span class="pron"> | wyrx.tɑ |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:croc-wyrhta" class="xref-target">croc-wyrhta</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:frum-wyrhta" class="xref-target">frum-wyrhta</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:gim-wyrhta" class="xref-target">gim-wyrhta</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:godweb-wyrhta" class="xref-target">godweb-wyrhta</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:īsern-wyrhta" class="xref-target">īsern-wyrhta</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:lām-wyrhta" class="xref-target">lām-wyrhta</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:lǣst-wyrhta" class="xref-target">lǣst-wyrhta</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:leōþ-wyrhta" class="xref-target">leōþ-wyrhta</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:lypen-wyrhta" class="xref-target">lypen-wyrhta</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:mēd-wyrhta" class="xref-target">mēd-wyrhta</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:morþ-wyrhta" class="xref-target">morþ-wyrhta</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:morþor-wyrhta" class="xref-target">morþor-wyrhta</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:nīd-wyrhta" class="xref-target">nīd-wyrhta</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:scild-wyrhta" class="xref-target">scild-wyrhta</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:scōh-wyrhta" class="xref-target">scōh-wyrhta</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:slecg-wyrhta" class="xref-target">slecg-wyrhta</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:sweord-wyrhta" class="xref-target">sweord-wyrhta</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="wōhness" d:title="wōhness">
		<body>
			<h1>wōhness<span class="pron"> | woː.xness |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">crookedness (lit. or fig.), a crooked place</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">dirigo</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic gerihte sume wōhnysse</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. Gr. 28, 5 ; Zup. 173, 9)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">erwni prava in directa (Is. 40, 4)</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ealle wōhnyssa beōð gerihte</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. i. 360, 33)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">wrongdoing, iniquily, perversity, depravity, wickedness</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Heora wōhnys on ðam regole his rihtwisnysse aetspearn.</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. ii. 158, 10)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">in iniquitatibus conceptus sum</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic wæs on wōnysse geeācnod</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. I. 27; S. 495, 24)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">a longa iniquitate atque infelicitate liberatam</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Fram langre wōnesse and ungesǣlignysse ālȳsde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (2, 15 ; S. 519, 10)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">iniquitales</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Wōnessa</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 5, 13; S. 633, 38: Blickl. Homl. 107, 24)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Heora wōhnyssa forgyfennys,</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Ass. 136, 668)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ǣlc ðæra wōnessa (crimes) ðe tō ǣnigre bōte gebyrie,</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cod. Dip. Kmbl. v. 143, 23)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">in iniquitatibus</span>
							<span class="q-oe">On wðnyssum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. l, 27; S. 495, 25)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gif hie on ǣnigum dǣle wōlīce libban heora līf, sȳn hiē from heora wōnessum onwende, and fram heora unrihtum oncyrran.</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Blickl. Homl. 109, 20)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="folc-āgende" d:title="folc-āgende">
		<body>
			<h1>folc-āgende<span class="pron"> | folk.ɑː.Gen.de |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>participle</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Folk-owning</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. pāpulum possīdens)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the folk-owning [man] was much irritated</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Bealg hine swīðe folcāgende</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 68a; Th. 253, 26; Jul. 186: Beo. Th. 6218; B. 3113)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the tract of earth is not easy of access to many folk-owning [men]</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Nis se foldan sceat mongum gefēre folcāgendra</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 56a; Th. 198, 4; Ph. 5)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-gān" d:title="ge-gān">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-gān<span class="pron"> | je.gɑːn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">A. III 2.</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">utrum cogitatio suggestione an delectatione acciderit</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hwæðer se geþōht geeōde þe mid scylde þe mid lustfullnesse</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 1, 27; Sch. 95, 17)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">B. II 4.</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Eall ꝥ manncynne tō ðām mǣstan gōde geeōde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. A. 154, 58)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">IV.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">the verb here might be translated to traverse, the Latin</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-wæccan" d:title="ge-wæccan">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-wæccan<span class="pron"> | je.wæk.kɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">ianitori praecipiat ut uigilet</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Hē ðǣm doruorde bebeād ꝥte gewæhte</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Mk. L. 13, 34)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="rȳne-līc" d:title="rȳne-līc">
		<body>
			<h1>rȳne-līc<span class="pron"> | ryː.ne.liːtʃ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Mystical</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. mysticus)</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge-rȳnelīc" class="xref-target">ge-rȳnelīc</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:rūn-līc" class="xref-target">rūn-līc</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="þegnian" d:title="þegnian">
		<body>
			<h1>þegnian<span class="pron"> | θe.ɣni.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -ode</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -od</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to serve a person (dat.), do a person (dat.) service, minister to, attend upon</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">quis major est,qui recumbit? an qui ministrat?</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hwæðer ys yldra ðe se ðe ðēnaþ ðe se ðe sitt</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lk. Skt. 22, 27)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">On heāhsetle siteþ self cyning (God), and ðiōs sīde gesceaft þēnaþ and þiōwaþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Met. 29, 77)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gif him ārlīce esne þēnaþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. Th. 430, 9; Rä. 44, 5: 403, 28; Rä. 22, 14)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">prosequitur</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Þēnaþ prosequitur</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hpt. Gl. 451, 57)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē (a king) bioþ swīþe anlīc ðara his þegna sumum ðe him þēniaþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 37, 1; Fox 186, 12)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gif hē nǣre sōþ God, nā him englas ne þegnodon. On ðisse bysene is gecȳþed, ðæt eallum geleāffullum mannum englas þegniaþ, ðonne hī habbaþ deōfol oferswīþed</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Blickl. Homl. 35, 1-4)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic geornlīce Gode þegnode þurh holdne hyge</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. Th. 37, 7; Gen. 585)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">mihi ministrabat</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē mē holdlīce ðegnade</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 100, 6)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">filius hominis non venit ministrari, sed ministrare (Mt. 20, 28)</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ne com ic tō ðon on eorðan ðæt mē mon ðēnōde, ac tō ðon ðæt ic wolde ðegnian</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 41; Swt. 301, 2)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Iōsep hæfde mycele gife æt his hlāforde and þēnode (ministrabat) him</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Gen. 39, 4: 40, 4)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Englas him þegnedan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Blickl. Homl. 27, 22)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Þegnedon</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (33, 34)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">ministra mihi</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Þēna me</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lk. Skt. 17, 8)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">omnis arbitretur obsequium se praestare Deo</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ǣlc wēnþ ðæt hē þenige Gode</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Jn. Skt. 16, 2)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the bishop and the priest, if they desire to serve God aright, must minister daily to God's people</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Se biscop and se mæssepreōst, gif hī mid rihte willaþ Gode þeōwian, ðonne sceolan hī þegnian dæghwamlīce Godes folce</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Blickl. Homl. 45, 30)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ne þūhte hit mē nāuht rihtlīc, gif him sceoldan þeōwe men þēnigan (þēnian, Cott. MS.)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 41, 2; Fox 244, 27)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">On ðam hūse hyra ðeāw wæs, ðæt hī ða untruman in lǣdan sceoldan, and him ætsomne ðēnigean</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 4, 24; S. 538, 29)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">I a.</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">where the instrument with which service is performed is given</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-en">I served my foes with my good sword, as was fitting</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Mec lāðgeteōnan þreātedon; ic him þēnode deōran sweorde swā hit gedēfe wæs</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Beo. Th. 1125; B. 560)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ðās bōc Leōfrīc gef Sco Petro and eallum his æftergengum intō Exancestre Gode mid tō þēnienne</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Chart. Erl. 253, 12)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to serve food, to supply wants, minister to necessities, provide</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">aqua sufficientem cunctis illo advenientibus gratiae suae coelestis copiam ministrat</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt ylce wæter eallum ðyder cumendum his heofonlīcre gife genihtsumnesse ðegnaþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 4, 28; S. 605, 32)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Seō mȳse is seō bōclīce lār, seō ðe ūs ðēnaþ līfes hlāf</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. ii. 114, 26)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Martha gearwode ðam Hǣlende ǣfengereordu ... Martha wæs geornful ðæt heō ðon Hǣlende tō gecwēmnesse þegnode (þēnode, Lk. Skt. 10, 40): heō him tō cwæþ: 'Hwȳ nelt ðū gēman ðæt mīn sweostor mē lǣt āne þegnian (þēnian, Lk. Skt.)?'</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Blickl. Homl. 67, 25-31)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Malchus, ða þēnunga ðe hē ðider brōhte, heom geornlīce þēnode, ðæt hī be dǣle hī gereordodon</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Skt. i. 23, 240)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Se him ða gerȳno ðēnode (ministrare solebat) ðæs hālgan geleāfan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 3, 23; S. 554, 17)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hwænne gesāwe wē ðē hingrigendne oððe þyrstendne ... and wē ne þēnedon ðē?</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. Kmbl. 25, 44)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Eallum Godes ðearfum man sceall weldǣda þēnian</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. i. 514, 5)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē him bigleofan ðēnian wolde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (ii. 128, 29)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē hēt hire þēnian of his ēstmetum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Ass. 110, 268)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">III.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to serve an office, administer, perform the duties of an office</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">qui cum annis multis episcopatum administraret</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðā hē ðā monig geār biscophād ðegnade</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 3, 23; S. 555, 7)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðēnade</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (4, 3; S. 566, 28, 40)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">Vilfrid annos quinque officium episcopatus exercebat</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðegnode Willferþ ða bisceopðēnunge fīf geār</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (4, 13; S. 583, 14)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">officium ministrare digne</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Medomlīce ðēnian ða ðēnunga</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 1; Swt. 27, 10)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Þe king him gon to þeinen, þæ quene bar to drinken</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Laym. 30786)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">A þusen cnihtes þeineden þan kinge ... þas beorn þa sunde from kuchene to þan kinge</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (24595)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge-þegnian" class="xref-target">ge-þegnian</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:under-þegnian" class="xref-target">under-þegnian</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="glīw-stōl" d:title="glīw-stōl">
		
		<body>
			<h1>glīw-stōl<span class="pron"> | gliːw.stoːl |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A seat of music and song (cf. þǣr (at Hrothgar's court) wæs gidd and gleō, B. 2105; cf. also seledreām), a joyous home (cf. hleōw-stōl for similar compound). The subject of the riddle is a stag's horn, which is shed and its place taken by a new one. This process is represented as the expulsion of a man from his home and country by a younger brother who takes his place.</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="folgoþ" d:title="folgoþ">
		
		<body>
			<h1>folgoþ<span class="pron"> | fol.ɣoθ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">that which follows, -- A train, retinue</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. id quod sĕquĭtur, cŏmĭtātus)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the noblest men always came to his retinue and to his service</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ā to his folgoþe and to his þēnunge ða æðelestan men cōmon</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 3, 14; S. 540, 11)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">among the train of earl Sweyn</span>
							<span class="q-oe">On Swegenes eorles folgoþe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 1048; Erl. 178, 16)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">service of a follower, -- A service, office, official dignity</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. cŏmĭtis servĭtus, ministĕrium, offĭcium, præpŏsĭtūra)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">let the bishop exact the penalty for contempt from the reeve in whose service it may be</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Se biscop amanige ða oferhȳrnesse æt ðam gerēfan ðe hit on his folgoþe sȳ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. Ath. i. 26; Th. i. 214, 3)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">he followed Julian, and in that service he avoided all foulness, living as a monk</span>
							<span class="q-oe">He folgode Iuliane, and he on ðam folgoþe ealle fūlnysse forbeāh, lybbende swā swā munuc</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. ii. 500, 12)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">in the eighteenth year [from that] in which archbishop Oswald took office</span>
							<span class="q-oe">On ðȳ eahtateōðan geāre ðe Ōswold arcebisceop to folgoþe fēng</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cod. Dipl. 620; A. D. 978; Kmbl. iii. 168, 23)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">let the reeve be without [ = deprived of] his official dignity</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Beō se gerēfa būton his folgoþe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. Ath. v. § 11; Th. i. 240, 19)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">Valentinian was chief of Julian's soldiers: he [Julian] commanded him to give up christianity or his office; then it was dearer to him to give up his office than christianity</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ualentinianus wæs Iulianuses cempena ealdorman: he him bebeād ðæt he forlēte ðone his cristendōm oððe his folgoþ; ðā wæs him leōfre ðæt he forlēte his folgoþ ðonne ðone cristendōm</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 6, 33; Bos. 129, 16-19)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">they [the angels] have the choicest of services with their King</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Habbaþ folgoþa cyst mid Cyninge</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 13b; Th. 24, 26; Cri. 390)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">III.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">condition of life</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. condĭtio vltæ)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">one is miserable, the other is fortunate . . . of which of them is the condition better?</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ōðer biþ unlǣde, ōðer biþ eādig . . . hwæðres biþ hira folgoþ betra</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Salm. Kmbl. 740; Sal. 369)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:under-folgoþ" class="xref-target">under-folgoþ</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="giefernes" d:title="giefernes">
		<body>
			<h1>giefernes<span class="pron"> | Gi͜y.fer.nes |</span>
			</h1>
