			<h1>stēpan to bereave<span class="pron"> | steː.pɑn, to, be.ræ͜ɑ.ve |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:stīpan to bereave" class="xref-target">stīpan to bereave</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="scip-wealh" d:title="scip-wealh">
		<body>
			<h1>scip-wealh<span class="pron"> | ʃip.wæ͜ɑlx |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -weales</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A servant whose service is connected with ships</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt land is sum inland, sum hit is ðān scipwealan tō gafole gesett (the land in question lies by the Severn)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cod. Dip. Kmbl. iii. 450. 19)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="morgen-gifu" d:title="morgen-gifu">
		<body>
			<h1>morgen-gifu<span class="pron"> | mor.Gen.Gi.fu |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Ic gean into Ǣlīg . . þāra þreō landa þe wit būta geheōtan Gode, ꝥ is æt rettendūne þe wes mīn morgangifu . . . ,</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (C. D. iii. 274, 16)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">concessit Ælfegus illi viduæ donum dotis suæ tantum quad ei dederat Eadricus, quando eam primum accepit uxorem</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Gewāt Eādrīc ær Ælfēh cwideleās, and Ælfēh fēng tō his lǣne. Ðā hæfde Eādrīc lāfe and nān bearn. Þā geūþe Ælfēh hire hire morgengife</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Cht. E. 212, 19)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Nabbe gē (the suitors for the speaker's daughter) nā gōdne tīman āredodne . . . ac . . . āwrītað eōwre naman on gewrite and hire morgengife, þonne āsænde ic þā gewrita mīnre dohtor ꝥ heō sylf geceōse hwilcne eōwer heō wille,</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Ap. Th. 20, 7)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-fōn" d:title="ge-fōn">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-fōn<span class="pron"> | je.foːn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">present: 1sg: -ge-fō, 2sg: -ge-fēhst, 3sg: -ge-fēhþ, pl: -ge-fōþ</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -ge-fēng, pl: -ge-fēngon</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -ge-fangen</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">imperative: sg: -ge-fōh</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To take, seize, catch</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. capere)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">ego do regi quicquid capio</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic sylle cync swā hwæt swā ic gefō</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Coll. Monast. Th. 22, 27)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">he seizes that which he tracks</span>
							<span class="q-oe">He gefēhþ ðæt ðæt he æfter spyreþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 39, 1; Fox 212, 1)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">homines eris capiens</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðū byst men gefōnde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lk. Bos. 5, 10)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">quando tu illos cepisti</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðonne ðū hīg gefangen hæbbe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Gen. 44, 4)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">quomodo capis pisces?</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hū gefēhst ðū fixas?</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="firmdig" d:title="firmdig">
		<body>
			<h1>firmdig<span class="pron"> | firm.diG |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:frimdig" class="xref-target">frimdig</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="hūsel-wer" d:title="hūsel-wer">
		<body>
			<h1>hūsel-wer<span class="pron"> | xuː.sel.wer |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">One who may take the sacrament, a communicant</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hūsulweras</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 44 a; Th. 149, 28; Gū. 768)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="under-steppan" d:title="under-steppan">
