			<h1>up-heald<span class="pron"> | up.xæ͜ɑld |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Turned upward</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="sōþ-word" d:title="sōþ-word">
		<body>
			<h1>sōþ-word<span class="pron"> | soːθ.word |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">a true word</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic Gode sealmas singe, sōðword sprece</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 56, 9: 118, 93)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="heal" d:title="heal">
		
		<body>
			<h1>heal<span class="pron"> | xæ͜ɑl |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A corner, an angle, a secret place[?]</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Heal oððe hyrne angulus</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. 80, 73)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">duplex semper est in angulis paries</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ǣlc wag biþ gebiēged twiefeald on ðæm heale</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 35, 5; Swt. 245, 13)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">he found him leaning in the corner of his church against the altar</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðā gemētte hē hine hleonian on ðam hale his cyrcan wið ðam weofode</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Guthl. 20; Gdwin. 82, 22)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">in abditis</span>
							<span class="q-oe">On halum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Spl. 16, 13)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ed-recan" d:title="ed-recan">
		<body>
			<h1>ed-recan<span class="pron"> | ed.re.kɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -te</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -ed</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To ruminate</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. ruminare)</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:eodorcan" class="xref-target">eodorcan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="hæg" d:title="hæg">
		<body>
			<h1>hæg<span class="pron"> | xæG |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">a fence; a hag, an enclosure</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Terram nominatam Haeg</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (C. D. i. 49, 23)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge-hæg" class="xref-target">ge-hæg</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:haga" class="xref-target">haga</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:hecg" class="xref-target">hecg</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:hecge" class="xref-target">hecge</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:hege" class="xref-target">hege</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="tylþ" d:title="tylþ">
		<body>
			<h1>tylþ<span class="pron"> | tylθ |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:tilþ" class="xref-target">tilþ</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="steng" d:title="steng">
		<body>
			<h1>steng<span class="pron"> | steng |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A stang (v. Halliwell's Dict.), pole, stake, staff, cudgel, bar</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Steng (stencg, stengc) vectis</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. Gr. 9, 28; Zup. 55, 10: Wrt. Voc. i. 26, 44)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Stengc</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (81, 29)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Steng clava</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (ii. 104, 11: 14, 41: claumentia, 131, 55)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Styng clava</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (i. 33, 60)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Wið slege īsernes oððe stenges (stænges, MS. H.)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lchdm. i. 132, 4)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Wið wunda som hȳ sȳn of īserne, som hȳ sȳn of stence (stæncge, MS. H.)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (166, 10)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðā hēt se dēma hī nacode gebindan tō ānum stænge</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Shrn. 115, 13)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Heāfod on steng (stipitem) āsettan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 3, 12; S. 537, 34)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Stengcum fustibus</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hpt. Gl. 487. 48)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Stencgum (stængum, Rush.)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. Kmbl. Lind. 26, 47)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Stengum sudibus</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 85, 53)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Mid stengum ðyrscan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Shrn. 55, 10)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Mid stearcum stengum beātan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. i. 428, 6)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">facies vectes de lignis sethim</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hāt wyrcean twegen stengeas (stengas, Hatt. MS.) of ðæm treōwe ðe is haten sethim</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 22, 1; Swt. 168, 22)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:wīte-steng" class="xref-target">wīte-steng</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="brǣd" d:title="brǣd">
		
		<body>
			<h1>brǣd<span class="pron"> | bræːd |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">BREADTH, width, latitude</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. latitudo, amplitudo)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the ark shall be fifty fathoms in breadth</span>
							<span class="q-la">quinquaginta cubitorum erit latitudo arcæ</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Biþ se arc fīftig fæðma on brǣde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Gen. 6, 15)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">latitudine sui status</span>
							<span class="q-oe">On brǣdo his stealles</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 1, 1; S. 474, 29)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">ambulabam in latitudine</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic on brǣdu [brǣde, Spl.] gange</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 118, 45)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">exaudivit me in latitudine Dominus</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Drihten me gehȳrde on heāre [ = heāhre, MS. hearr] brǣdu</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (117, 5)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">habet ingressum amplitudinis quasi jactus fundæ</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hī habbaþ ingang swā mycelre brǣdo swā mon mæg mid liðeran geworpan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 4, 13; S. 583, 11)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:hand-brǣd" class="xref-target">hand-brǣd</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="for-þeōn" d:title="for-þeōn">
		<body>
			<h1>for-þeōn<span class="pron"> | for.θe͜oːn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -þeōde</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -þeōd</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To oppress</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. opprīmere, subīgere)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">shadow oppressed the bright splendour</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Scīrne scīman sceadu forþeōde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Rood Kmbl. 108; Kr. 54)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-fylling" d:title="ge-fylling">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-fylling<span class="pron"> | je.fyl.ling |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Completion</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">omnis consummations vidi finem</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ealre gefyllingce ł ǣlcre geændunge ic geseah ende</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. L. 118, 96)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="riht-þeōw" d:title="riht-þeōw">
		
		<body>
			<h1>riht-þeōw<span class="pron"> | rixt.θe͜oːw |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">a lawful slave</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. servum me juris tui esse profitere)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">servum me juris tui esse profitere</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Sæge ꝥ ic þīn rihtþeōwa (-þeōw, v. l.) sȳ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Gr. D. 180, 6)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="hyge-frōfor" d:title="hyge-frōfor">
		<body>
			<h1>hyge-frōfor<span class="pron"> | xy.Ge.froː.for |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Comfort for the mind or heart</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="gāst-lic" d:title="gāst-lic">
		<body>
			<h1>gāst-lic<span class="pron"> | gɑːst.liːtʃ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">pertaining to the spirit</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">extaseos</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gāst-licre ūphefnesse</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 31, 68)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">in extasi</span>
							<span class="q-oe">On mōdes heānnesse, on gāstlicre gesiḥðe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (47, 21)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Dæg miḋ glædnise gǣstlicum (spiritali) ūē worḋia</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Rtl. 89, 26)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ealle þās þæs monnes good ge gāst-lice ge līchomlice</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 34, 6; F. 140, 31)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">spiritual as opposed to bodily, fleshly, physical</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">typicus Benjamin</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Se gāslica wulf</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (An. Ox. 1922)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Seō cwēn (the queen of Sheba) . . . seō gāstlice cwēn, Godes gelaḋung</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. Th. ii. 588)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē is se grundweall þǣre gāstlican cyrcan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (22)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hī him þā gāstlican lāc geoffriaḋ on menigfealdum gemetum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (14)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Sē forlēt his gāstlican wǣpna and fēng tō his spere and tō his sweorde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 1056; P. 186, 27)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">IIa.</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">of relationship, spiritual as opposed to natural</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Godes gelaḋung bewȳpḋ hire gāstlican cild</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. Th. i. 84, 29)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">III.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">spiritual as opposed to worldly or profane, divine, heavenly, holy, sacred</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">anagogen (cf. anagogen, i. superno sensu ūplican l̄ heofenlicum angite, An. Ox. 184)</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gāstlecum andgite</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. l, 10)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">in oromate (cf. in oromate, i. uisione superna on ūplicere gesihþe, An. Ox. 404)</span>
							<span class="q-oe">On gāstlicre gesiþe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 43, 60: 62, 62)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gǣst-licre</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (75, 65)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">tropologiam</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Æfter gāstlicre gebȳcnuncge</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (An. Ox. 8, 15 c)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">mistico officio</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gāstlicre gerȳne</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (2883)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">contemplativam (vitam)</span>
							<span class="q-oe">þ̄t gāstlice, heofenlice</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (2432)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">charismatum i. donorum (cf. gāst-gifu)</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gāstlicra sylena l̄ gyfa</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (342 : 2863)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">nequaquam spiritalia praecepta cognoscere</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Nāne wuht ongitan ḋāra gæstlecena beboda</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 27)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">mysticis (i. diuinis) commentariis</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Mid gāstlicum trahtnungum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (An. Ox. 171)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">mysticis (i. sanctis) explanationibus</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gāstlicum gerecednessun</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (1081)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">praesagis</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Mid gāstlicum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (1529)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">spiritalibus commentis</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gāslicum orþangcum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (3226)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">spiritalia praecepta</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðā gǣsḋlecan (gāstlican, v. l.) bebodu</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 29, 21)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:gāst" class="xref-target">gāst</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="un-gefyrn" d:title="un-gefyrn">
		<body>
			<h1>un-gefyrn<span class="pron"> | un.Ge.fyrn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adverb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">At no distant date, before long, soon</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðū āfindst his mihte ungefyrn on ðē sylfum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Skt. ii. 25, 153)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Eallum folce ðæs swīðe ungefyrn (very soon after that) hē geswutelian wolde hwæs gehwā gelȳfan sceolde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (i. 23, 405)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:un-fyrn" class="xref-target">un-fyrn</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="swīg-dæg" d:title="swīg-dæg">
		<body>
			<h1>swīg-dæg<span class="pron"> | swiːG.dæj |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A day on which silence was to be observed</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Circlīce þeāwas forbeōdaþ tō secgenne ǣnig spel on ðām þrȳm swīgdagum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. i. 218, 31: ii. 362, 16)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="birst" d:title="birst">
		<body>
			<h1>birst<span class="pron"> | birst |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">birst burstest, bursts; 2nd and 3rd pers. pres. of berstan</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:berstan" class="xref-target">berstan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ǣ-swind" d:title="ǣ-swind">
		<body>
			<h1>ǣ-swind<span class="pron"> | æː.swind |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">inert, sluggish</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ēsuind, āsolcen iners</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 111, 27)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ǣswind</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (45, 50)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ā-swindan" class="xref-target">ā-swindan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="in-gewinn" d:title="in-gewinn">
		<body>
			<h1>in-gewinn<span class="pron"> | in.Ge.winn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>neuter noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">An intestine struggle</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">I have now shortly related their intestine struggles</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Scortlīce is hæbbe nū gesǣd hiora ingewinn</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 2, 6 ; Swt. 88, 29)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:in-gefeoht" class="xref-target">in-gefeoht</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="gum-cynn" d:title="gum-cynn">
		<body>
			<h1>gum-cynn<span class="pron"> | gum.kynn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>neuter noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Mankind, men, a race, nation</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. humanum genus, gens, natio)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">he resolved to destroy mankind</span>
							<span class="q-oe">He þohte forgrīpan gumcynne</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. 64; Th. 77, 14; Gen. 1275)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">amongst men on the earth I am unique</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Eom ic gumcynnes ānga ofer eorþan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 129a; Th. 496, 11; Rä. 85, 12: Beo. Th. 5524; B. 2765)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">whatever matron brought forth this son amongst men</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Swā hwylc mægþa ðone magan cende æfter gumcynnum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Beo. Th. 1892; B. 944)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">we are of the race of the Gauts' people</span>
							<span class="q-oe">We synt gumcynnes Geāta leōde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (525; B. 260)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="fēr-rǣden[n]" d:title="fēr-rǣden[n]">
		<body>
			<h1>fēr-rǣden[n]<span class="pron"> | feːr.ræː.den, n |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">On ūre fǣrrǣdenne</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Vis. Lfc. 20)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="gang" d:title="gang">
		<body>
			<h1>gang<span class="pron"> | gɑng |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>participle</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">went; p. of geongan</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:geongan" class="xref-target">geongan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-styltan" d:title="ge-styltan">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-styltan<span class="pron"> | je.styl.tɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -te</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To be astonished, to be silent from astonishment</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">stupebant omnes</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gestylton ł gesuīgdon alle</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. Kmbl. Lind. 12, 23)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">populus stupefactus est</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Folc gestylte [gistylted wæs, Rush.]</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Mk. Skt. Lind. 9, 15)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">stupuerunt parentes</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gestyldon aldro</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lk. Skt. Lind. 8, 56)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge-stillan" class="xref-target">ge-stillan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="salpanra" d:title="salpanra">
		<body>
			<h1>salpanra<span class="pron"> | sɑl.pɑn.rɑ |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:sāl IV" class="xref-target">sāl IV</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-dēman" d:title="ge-dēman">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-dēman<span class="pron"> | je.deː.mɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -de</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -ed</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To deem, judge, determine, ordain, decree, doom, condemn</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. jūdicāre, decernĕre, sancīre, condemnāre)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">he will judge each deed</span>
							<span class="q-oe">He wile gedēman dǣda gehwylce</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 15 b; Th. 33, 13; Cri. 525)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">that he judge every one righteously</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt he ǣghwelcne on riht gedēmeþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. Alf. 49; Th. i. 56, 30 : Ps. Th. 57, 10)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">he condemned our Lord to death</span>
							<span class="q-oe">He gedēmde ūrne Drihten to deāþe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 6, 3; Bos. 117, 42)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">sanxērunt</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gedēmdon [MS. gedēmden]</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Mone B. 1940)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">he who shall doom unjust doom</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Se ðe undōm gedēme</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. C. S. 15; Th. i. 384, 7)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">as is ordained</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Swā gedēmed is</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 58 a; Th. 207, 26; Ph. 147)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">successōrem fore Ceoluulfum decrēvisset</span>
							<span class="q-oe">He gedēmed hæfde ðæt Ceōlwulf æfter hint cyning wǣre</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 5, 23; S. 646, 1 : Cd. 186; Th. 231, 11; Dan. 245)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">your enemies are condemned to death</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Fȳnd syndon eōwere gedēmed to deāþe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Judth. 11; Thw. 24, 19; Jud. 196)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="þennan" d:title="þennan">
		<body>
			<h1>þennan<span class="pron"> | θen.nɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">qua tenditur</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Þyder [h]is þened</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (An. Ox. 17, 53)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">I a.</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">figurative, to extend the fame of, exalt</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">figurative, to extend the fame of, exalt</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">prosequitur, i. tractat t laudat (integritatem immensis rumorum laudibus prosequitur, Ald. 26, 8)</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Þenaþ, tōbǣd</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (An. Ox. 1919)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:on-þennan" class="xref-target">on-þennan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="for-dēmednes" d:title="for-dēmednes">
		<body>
			<h1>for-dēmednes<span class="pron"> | for.deː.med.nes |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Condemnation, proscription</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. condemnātio, proscriptio)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">per dēcem annos, incendiis ecclēsiārum, proscriptiōnibus innōcentum, cædibus martyrum incessābiliter acta est</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Þurh tyn winter full Godes cyricena bærnesse, and unsceaððiendra fordēmednesse, and slege hāligra martyra unblinnendlīce dōn wæs</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 1, 6; S. 476, 25)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="god-borh" d:title="god-borh">
		<body>
			<h1>god-borh<span class="pron"> | god.borx |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A pledge confirmed by an appeal to God, one that is accompanied by the formulae of religion</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">if any one bring against another a charge in the matter of a pledge whose validity was confirmed by invoking the name of the Deity (where solemn formulae were used to give validity. Cf. the formulae pp. 178-182 beginning on þone Drihten, on Ælmihtiges Godes naman, on lifiendes Godes naman), and will accuse him that he do not carry out any of the pledges that he gave him</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Be godborgum (-borhgum, v. l.). Gif hwā ōðerne godborges oncunne and tiōn wille ꝥ hē hwelcne ne gelǣste þāra þe hē him gesealde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ll. Th. i. 82, 4-6)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="wrist" d:title="wrist">
		<body>
			<h1>wrist<span class="pron"> | wrist |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A wrist</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gif hit ānfeald tyhtle sȳ, dūfe seo, hand æfter ðam stāne ōð ða wriste; and gif hit þryfeald sȳ, ōð ðæne elbogan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. Ath. iv. 7 ; Th. i. 226, 17)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:cneōw-wyrste" class="xref-target">cneōw-wyrste</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:hand-wyrst" class="xref-target">hand-wyrst</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="on-setenness" d:title="on-setenness">
		
		<body>
			<h1>on-setenness<span class="pron"> | on.se.ten.ness |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">laying on, imposition</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. manus impositioni)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Fram þâm rihtgeleāffullum bisceope onsetnesse (manus impositioni) and sume gebede beōn getrymede</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ll. Th. ii. 232, 19)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Þurh biscopa handa onsetenesse</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Shrn. 85, 19 (in Dict.))</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">institution</span>
					</p>
					<ol class="sub-senses">
						<li />
					</ol>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ufor" d:title="ufor">
		<body>
			<h1>ufor<span class="pron"> | u.for |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adverb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">ut tanto sollicitius praecipitem ruinam metuant, quanto altius stant</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðætte hiē swā micle swīðor ðone spild ðæs hryres him ondrǣden ðonne ða ōðre, swā hī ufor stondað ðonne ðā ōðre</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 407, 21)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:uferor" class="xref-target">uferor</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:yfemest" class="xref-target">yfemest</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="cȳþig" d:title="cȳþig">
		
		<body>
			<h1>cȳþig<span class="pron"> | Kyː.θiG |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Known</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">cognitus</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Cȳðig cognitus</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Jn. p. 6, 2)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">manifestum facere</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Cȳðic dōn manifestum facere</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. L. 26, 73)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">nota</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Cȳðigo nota</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Jn. L. 15, 15)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge-cȳþig" class="xref-target">ge-cȳþig</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:un-andcȳþigness" class="xref-target">un-andcȳþigness</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="feoht-wite" d:title="feoht-wite">
		<body>
			<h1>feoht-wite<span class="pron"> | fe͜oxt.wi.te |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">a fine for fighting</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:fyht-wīte" class="xref-target">fyht-wīte</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-berst" d:title="ge-berst">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-berst<span class="pron"> | je.berst |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A bursting, eruption</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. eruptio)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">against bursting of erysipelas</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Wið ōmena geberste</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. M. 1, 39; Lchdm. ii. 100, 2)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="full-gān" d:title="full-gān">
		<body>
			<h1>full-gān<span class="pron"> | full.gɑːn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(1)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">to follow a profession, carry on an office, apply oneself to, practise a habit</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Sē ðe his woruldlustum eallum fulgǣþ</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 31, 1; F. 112, 6)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Gif hwā forlǣt ǣlc gōd and fulgǣþ þām yfele</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (36, 6; F. 182, 7)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ꝥ mon fulgā eallum his lustum</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (24, 2; F. 82, 13)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">nec totum se ad hoc, quod agit, conferat</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Ne fulgā hē eallunga ðæs līchoman wilnunga</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 395, 10)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">sic enim clarius testatiusque sapientiae tractatur officium</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Hī secgaþ ꝥ hī mægen þȳ ēþ hiora wīsdōme fulgān and hine gehealdan</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 39, 2; F. 212, 19)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hiō hyre firenluste fulgān ne mōste būtan manna bysmrunge</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 1, 2; S. 30, 33)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Þæt hiē his giongorscipe fulgān (fyligan, MS.) wolden</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Gen. 249)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(2)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">to give effect to, carry out</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Sē þe ne hwyrfð his mōd æfter īdlum geþōhtum, and him mid weorcum fulgǣð, þeāh hī him on mōd cumen</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 23, 4)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(3)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">to execute a command, task, &amp;c., do a person's will</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ǣlc wuht his rihtgesetnesse fuleōde būtan menn ānum</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 5, 3; F. 12, 9)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">fastidiose ducem in disponendo bello audientes</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Þā on ðǣm tweōn þe hiē swā ungeorne his willan fulleōdon</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 3, 11; S. 146, 24)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Fulgā nū se mete ðǣre wambe willan, and siō wamb ðæs metes</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 317, 16)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hī ðīnum willan woldon fulgān</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 3, 4; F. 6, 24)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(4)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">with the idea of help, service</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-en">the shaft did its office well, swift-winged helped on the arrow-head</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Sceaft nytte heōld, feðergearwum fūs flāne fulleōde</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (B. 3119)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">dictator homines quicunque sceleribus obnoxii essent, impunitate promissa, militiae mancipavit</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Ealle þā þe . . . hiē selfe forworht hæfdon, hiē hit eall forgeāfon wið þǣm þe hiē him æt þǣm gewinnum fuleōden</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 4, 9; S. 192, 1)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-bīgan" d:title="ge-bīgan">
		
		<body>
			<h1>ge-bīgan<span class="pron"> | je.biː.ɣɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">flectit, curvat, inclinat</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gebīgþ flectit, curvat, inclinat</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 149, 44)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gebīged curva</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (23, 47)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">to cause to move from a position or direction</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">þā þōhton hiē hiō sceoldon of þām muntum hiē gebīgan mid hiora flāna gescotum</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 6, 36 ; S. 294, 23)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">to bend, give shape or direction to an object</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">curvat (fornicem)</span>
									<span class="q-oe">pebēgð curvat (fornicem)</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Kent. Gl. 755)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">Circumflexus accentus</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Circumflexus accentus gebīged accent</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Angl. viii. 333, 26)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">adunci</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Gebēgdes adunci</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 9, 60)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">flexo tramite, inclinato</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Gebīgdre stīge flexo tramite, inclinato</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (149, 45)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">curbo (poplite)</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Gebēgde curbo (poplite)</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (83, 14)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">laganum</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Gebīge[n]dne hlāf laganum</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Ex. 29, 23)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">aduncis</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Gebēgdum aduncis</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 99, 22)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
							<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
								<li>
									<p>
										<span class="sense-label">II a.</span>
										<span class="sub-heading">reflex, of a person, to bow in reverence</span>
									</p>
									<ul class="quotes">
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Hē hine eādmōdlīce gebīgde ādūne tō his fōtum</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. S. 10, 128)</span>
										</li>
									</ul>
								</li>
							</ol>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">III.</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">to incline, turn a person to, bring to accept a faith, practice, object of worship, &amp;c.</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hē þæt hǣðene landfolc tō Crīstes geleāfan mid bodunge gebīgde</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. Th. ii. 164, 20)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hē hine tō fulluhte gebīgde . . . ðā gebrōðra ðe hē ǣr tō Gode gebīgde</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. S. 15, 26, 38)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">ad thalami copulam in—clinarent</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Tō brȳdbūres geþeōdnesse gebīgdan ad thalami copulam in—clinarent</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (An. Ox. 3201)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Gif hē mihte hī gebīgan tō his synscipe</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. Th. ii. 476, 21)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Gyf þū Godes folc gebīgean ne miht tō rihte</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Wlfst. 7, 8)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hē wolde gebīgan his leōda tō geleāfan and tō þām lifigendan Gode</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. S. 26, 46)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hine gebēgean tō beteran wege</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 1067 ; P. 201, 29)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">IV.</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">to turn, bring to a desired condition, adapt</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ūre mōd gebīg, þanc and þeāwas on þīn gewil</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Hy. 7, 77)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Se bisceop ne mihte gebīgan his spraec tō Nordhymbriscum gereorde swā hraþe</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. S. 26, 68)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">V.</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">to turn thought, attention, &amp;c. , bring to consider</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hē gebīgde his mōd tō untrumra monna diōgolnessum</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 99, 22)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">VI.</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">to bend, subdue, humiliate, subject</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">deformatio statum cordis inclinat</span>
									<span class="q-oe">-Wlǣttuncg ānrǣdnesse gebīgde deformatio statum cordis inclinat</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (An. Ox. 4469)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Englisce menn ꝥ land gebēgdan þan kyninge tō handan</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 1074; P. 209, 20)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">þæt hī mē gebȳgen oð eorðan</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 16, 10)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">conculcabis leonem et draconem</span>
									<span class="q-oe">þ ū miht leōn and dracan liste gebȳgean conculcabis leonem et draconem</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (90, 13)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">þā þeōwas uneāþe oferwunnene wurdon, and VI M ofslagen ǣr hiē mon gebīggiean mehte</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (ors. 5, 3 ; S. 222, 29)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">incurvatus sum et humiliatus</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Ic eom gebīged (-bigged, v. l.) and gehēned incurvatus sum et humiliatus</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 67, 18)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">ego ad nihilum redactus sum</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Ic tō nāwihte eom nȳde gebīged ego ad nihilum redactus sum</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 72, 17)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Burga fīfe wǣran under Norðmannum nȳde gebēgde</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 942; P. 110, 20)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To bow, bend, turn, inflect or decline a part of speech, twist, bow down, humble, bring under, subdue, crush</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. flectĕre, inflectĕre, declīnāre. humiliāre)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">he brought them to baptism</span>
							<span class="q-oe">He hī to fulluhte gebīgde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (H. R. 101, 26)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">he shall be low bowed down</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Se sceal heān wesan niðer gebīged</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 84 a; Th. 316, 28; Mōd. 55: Bd. 4, 10; S. 578, 28: Gen. 27, 29)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">omnia nōmina quinque declīnāti-ōnĭbus inflectuntur</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ealle naman beōþ gebīgede on fīf declīnungum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. Gr. 7; Som. 6, 2: 14; Som. 16, 56: Exon. 24 a; Th. 69, 26; Cri. 1126: Ors. 3, 9; Bos. 64, 15: Ælfc. T. 30, 5: Ps. Th. 106, 15)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:un-gebīged" class="xref-target">un-gebīged</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge-bȳgan" class="xref-target">ge-bȳgan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ærce-hād" d:title="ærce-hād">
