<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="-eāgede" d:title="-eāgede">
		<body>
			<h1>-eāgede<span class="pron"> | æ͜ɑː.Ge.de |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ān-eāgede" class="xref-target">ān-eāgede</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:sceolh-eāgede" class="xref-target">sceolh-eāgede</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:sūr-eāgede" class="xref-target">sūr-eāgede</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="for-standan" d:title="for-standan">
		
		<body>
			<h1>for-standan<span class="pron"> | for.stɑn.dɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">present: 3sg: -stent</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -stōd, pl: -stōdon</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -standen</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to stand up for, to defend, aid, help, benefit, avail</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. defendĕre, prodesse)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">if he will not stand up for him</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gif hine nelle forstandan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. In. 62; Th. i. 142, 6)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">a twelve hundred man's oath stands for the oath of six churls</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Twelfhyndes mannes āþ forstent vi ceorla āþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. O. 13; Th. i. 182, 19)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">that his witness avail again nothing</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt his gewitnes eft nāht ne forstande</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. Ath. i. 10; Th. i. 204, 24)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">if any one stand up for him</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gif hine hwā forstande</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. Ath. i. 1; Th. i. 198, 25)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">if any one defend him</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gif hine hwā fōrene forstande</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (v. § 1, 4; Th. i. 230, 4: v. § 8, 2; Th. i. 236, 12: L. Eth. i. 4; Th. i. 284, 3: L. C. S. 33; Th. i. 396, 17)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">he might defend the treasure</span>
							<span class="q-oe">He mihte hord forstandan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Beo. Th. 5903; B. 2955)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">protect thou me</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Forstond ðū mec</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 118 b; Th. 455, 31; Hy. 4, 58)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">who shall defend it, if thou dost not shield it</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hwā forstandeþ hie, gif ðu hie ne scyldest</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Blickl. Homl. 225, 18)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">what did it help the best men -- or what does it profit?</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hwæt forstōd ðām betestum mannum -- oððe hwæt forstent hit</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 18, 4; Fox 68, 7, 9)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the washing profits nothing</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ne forstent ðæt þweāl nāuht</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 54; Hat. MS.)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to understand</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. intelligĕre)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">I can scarcely understand thy questions</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Uneāðe ic mæg forstandan ðīne acsunga</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 5, 3; Fox 12, 15)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">they themselves understood his words [to be] perverted</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Selfe forstōdon his word onwended</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. 37; Th. 48, 2; Gen. 769)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:under-standan" class="xref-target">under-standan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-brehtnis" d:title="ge-brehtnis">
