			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ān-cenned" d:title="ān-cenned">
		
		<body>
			<h1>ān-cenned<span class="pron"> | ɑːn.Ken.ned |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>participle</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Only-begotten</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. uni-genitus)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">only-begotten Son</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Āncenned Sunu</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 14b; Th. 29, 18; Cri. 464)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the only-begotten Son</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Se āncenneda Sunu</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Jn. Bos. 1, 18: 3, 16)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="fōt-gangende" d:title="fōt-gangende">
		<body>
			<h1>fōt-gangende<span class="pron"> | foːt.gɑn.Gen.de |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Going on foot, foot (soldiers)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">peditatu</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Fōtgangendum here</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (An. Ox. 5254)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="wynsum-līc" d:title="wynsum-līc">
		<body>
			<h1>wynsum-līc<span class="pron"> | wyn.sum.liːtʃ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Pleasant, agreeable</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē bið ðām gōdum glædmōd on gesihþe, wlitig, wynsumlīc weorude ðam hālgan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. Th. 57, 1; Cri. 912)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">votivum, acceptum, desiderativum</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Wynsumlīc</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hpt. Gl. 446, 49)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Þūhte fæger and wlitig heora līf and wynsumlīc</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Blickl. Homl. 107, 30)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Eall ðæt him hēr on worlde wynsumlīc wæs</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (111, 26: 115, 11)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge-wynsumlīc" class="xref-target">ge-wynsumlīc</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ealdor" d:title="ealdor">
		
		<body>
			<h1>ealdor<span class="pron"> | æ͜ɑl.dor |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -ealdres, dative sg: -ealdre, nominative pl: -ealdras, accusative pl: -ealdras</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">an ELDER, parent, head of a family, author</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. pārens, paterfamilias, auctor)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">prīmi pārentes nastri</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ūre ealdras ða ǣrestan menn</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. I. 27; S. 493, 3)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">inīquĭtas patrum ejus</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt unriht ðe his ealdras ǣr gefremedon</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 108, 14)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">hŏmo erat paterfamĭlĭas</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Sum hīredes ealdor wæs</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. Bos. 21, 33)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">tenebrarum auctor</span>
							<span class="q-oe">þȳstra ealdor</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 2, 1; S. 501, 16)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">an elder, chief, governor, prince</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. sĕnior, præpŏsĭtus, princeps)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">senĭōres pŏpŭli</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæs folces ealdoran</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lev. 4, 15)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">centŭrio</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hundredes ealdor</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. Bos. 8, 5: Ælfc. Gl. 6; Som. 56, 58)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the chief butler</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæra byrla ealdor</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Gen. 40, 9)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">dixit Iesus ad magistrātus templi</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Cwæþ se Hǣlend to ðæs temples ealdrum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lk. Bos. 22, 52 : C. R. Ben. 25)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">that was their chief</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt wæs ealdor heora</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. 221; Th. 287, 27; Sat. 373)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the prince of the heavens</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Heofna ealdor</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. 226; Th. 300, 20; Sat. 567)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the prince of thanes</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ealdor þegna</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Beo. Th. 3293; B. 1644)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">a dreadful prince</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Egesful ealdor</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 70 b; Th. 262, 7; Jul. 329)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">he stood opposite his sovereign</span>
							<span class="q-oe">He ofer his ealdre gestōd</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (55 b; Th. 196, 1; Az. 167)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">princĭpes Zabulon</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ealdras of Zabulone</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 67, 25 : 82, 9)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-mǣdan" d:title="ge-mǣdan">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-mǣdan<span class="pron"> | je.mæː.dɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -ge-mǣd</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to make insane</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">amens (puer . . . vertitur in rabiem fraudatus mente sagaci, bacchatur . . . amens, Aid. 176, 17)</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gemǣd</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 94, 4: 5, 59)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to make foolish</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">ineptus</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gemǣdid</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. in, 70)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">vanas</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gemaeded</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (123, 13)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">vecordem (juvenem, Prov. 7, 7)</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gemǣdedne</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (87, 51)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge-mād" class="xref-target">ge-mād</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="FRAM" d:title="FRAM">
		
		<body>
			<h1>FRAM<span class="pron"> | frɑm |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>preposition (w. dative)</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">FROM</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. ab)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">deleō hōminem a fācie terræ, ab hōmine usque ad animantia, a reptili usque ad volucres cœli</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic adilige ðone mannan fram ðære eorþan ansīne, fram ðam men ōþ ða nȳtenu, fram ðam slincendum ōþ ða fugelas</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Gen. 6, 7)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">discēdite a me</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gewītaþ fram me</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 6, 7: Ps. Spl. 30, 15: Mt. Bos. 1, 17, 21, 22)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>preposition</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">with verbs of speaking, Concerning, about, of</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. cum verbis loquendi, de)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">that he, concerning Sigemund, had heard tell of valiant deeds</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt he fram Sigemunde secgan hȳrde ellendǣdum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Beo. Th. 1754; B. 875)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">never have I heard speak about thee of such hostile snares</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Nō ic fram ðe swylcra searunīða secgan hȳrde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Beo. Th. 1167; B. 581)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">III.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">fram is sometimes placed after its case</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">he banished him from mankind</span>
							<span class="q-oe">He hine forwræc mancynne fram</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Beo. Th. 221; B. 110)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="lēon-fōt" d:title="lēon-fōt">
