						<span class="meaning-en">Lion's foot, a plant</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="for-tīhan" d:title="for-tīhan">
		<body>
			<h1>for-tīhan<span class="pron"> | for.tiː.xɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">present: 3sg: -tīþ</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -tāh, pl: -tigon</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -tigen</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To draw against or over, cover over with anything, darken, obscure</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. obdūcĕre)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">covers over the mind with the mist of error</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Mid gedwol-miste fortīþ mōd</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. Met. Fox 22, 67; Met. 22, 34)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:tīhan I" class="xref-target">tīhan I</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="norþ-land" d:title="norþ-land">
		<body>
			<h1>norþ-land<span class="pron"> | norθ.lɑnd |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">land lying to the north</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hī hwemdon mid þām scypon wið þæs norðlandes</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 1052 ; P. 180, 19)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
