				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Orcus, Pluto</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="be-reāflan" d:title="be-reāflan">
		<body>
			<h1>be-reāflan<span class="pron"> | be.ræ͜ɑː.flɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">populatur</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Bereāfað populatur</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (An. Ox. 139)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">moliuntur fraudes</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Bereafiað moliuntur fraudes</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Kent. Gl. 3)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">abegerant</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Bereāuedon abegerant</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (An. Ox. 7, 263)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">grassari</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Bereāfian grassari</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (5343)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">fraudaretur</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Bereāfed fraudaretur</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (1583)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">with acc. of person (or thing) despoiled</span>
							</p>
							<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
								<li>
									<p>
										<span class="sense-label">(1)</span>
										<span class="sub-heading">alone</span>
									</p>
									<ul class="quotes">
										<li>
											<span class="q-la">se expolians</span>
											<span class="q-oe">Hē bereāfode hine sylfne se expolians</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Gr. D. 68, 8)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Hī ðæt mynster berēfodon</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 794; P. 57, 12)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">ꝥ hē God bereāfige</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Lch. iii. 444, 1)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-la">castrorum praedam percensere</span>
											<span class="q-oe">þ ā wīcstōwa and þæt wæl bereāfian castrorum praedam percensere</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 3, 9; S. 128, 9)</span>
										</li>
									</ul>
								</li>
								<li>
									<p>
										<span class="sense-label">(2)</span>
										<span class="sub-heading">with spoil</span>
									</p>
									<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
										<li>
											<p>
												<span class="sense-label">(a)</span>
												<span class="sub-heading">in gen.</span>
											</p>
											<ul class="quotes">
												<li>
													<span class="q-oe">pū þā treōwa heora leāfa bereā-fast</span>
													<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 4 ; F. 8, 6)</span>
												</li>
												<li>
													<span class="q-oe">Se mōna þā sunnan heore leōhtes bereāfaþ</span>
													<span class="q-cite"> (F. 8, 1)</span>
												</li>
												<li>
													<span class="q-oe">Hāma bereāfod</span>
													<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 975 ; P. 120, 24: 1065; P. 195, 6: Cri. 558 : El. 910)</span>
												</li>
											</ul>
										</li>
										<li>
											<p>
												<span class="sense-label">(b)</span>
												<span class="sub-heading">inst. (dat.)</span>
											</p>
											<ul class="quotes">
												<li>
													<span class="q-oe">Scæb ꝥ heāfod feaxe bereāfað</span>
													<span class="q-cite"> (Lch. i. 322, 18)</span>
												</li>
												<li>
													<span class="q-oe">Hī hine wǣdon bereāfoden</span>
													<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. Th. i. 430, 2 : 428, 5)</span>
												</li>
												<li>
													<span class="q-oe">Wæs hē lande bereāfod</span>
													<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 1065 ; P. 194, 4: Hml. S. 23 b, 207 : B. 2746: An. 1316)</span>
												</li>
												<li>
													<span class="q-la">aporiamur bonis nostris</span>
													<span class="q-oe">Wē sind bereāfod ūrum gōdum aporiamur bonis nostris</span>
													<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. i. 54, 43)</span>
												</li>
											</ul>
										</li>
										<li>
											<p>
												<span class="sense-label">(c)</span>
												<span class="sub-heading">with æt</span>
											</p>
											<ul class="quotes">
												<li>
													<span class="q-la">predati sunt Loth</span>
													<span class="q-oe">Hī bereāfodon Loth æt his ǣhton predati sunt Loth</span>
													<span class="q-cite"> (Prud. 2 b : Chr. 1043; P. 163, 34)</span>
												</li>
												<li>
													<span class="q-oe">þeāh se reāfere ūs æt ǣhtum bereāfige</span>
													<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. Th. i. 576, 10: Ll. Th. ii. 180, 21)</span>
												</li>
												<li>
													<span class="q-oe">Gif man beō æt his ǣhtum bereāfod</span>
													<span class="q-cite"> (i. 286, 16)</span>
												</li>
												<li>
													<span class="q-la">spoliaverat</span>
													<span class="q-oe">Aaron hæfde bereāfod (spoliaverat) ꝥ folc æt hira golde</span>
													<span class="q-cite"> (Ex. 32, 25)</span>
												</li>
											</ul>
										</li>
									</ol>
								</li>
							</ol>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">with acc. of spoil and on with person</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">ꝥ hē him āgeāfe þæt hē ǣr on him bereāfode (ge-, v. l. )</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 3, 11; S. 146, 30)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="un-sliten" d:title="un-sliten">
		<body>
			<h1>un-sliten<span class="pron"> | un.sli.ten |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Unrent</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the coat was unrent ... They said: Let us not rend it</span>
							<span class="q-la">scindamus</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt cyrtel wæs unslitten,... Cuoedon: Ne tōslīte (scindamus) uē hiā</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Jn. Skt. Lind. 19, 23)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="cwidol" d:title="cwidol">
		<body>
			<h1>cwidol<span class="pron"> | kwi.dol |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:cwedol" class="xref-target">cwedol</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="and-wlite" d:title="and-wlite">
		<body>
			<h1>and-wlite<span class="pron"> | ɑnd.wli.te |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>neuter noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">The face, countenance, personal appearance, forehead, form, surface</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. facies, vultus, aspectus, frons, forma, superficies)</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="wlǣta" d:title="wlǣta">
		
		<body>
			<h1>wlǣta<span class="pron"> | wlæː.tɑ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -an</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">nausea, loathing</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Wið spiwðan and wlǣttan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lchdm. i. 358, 24)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Wiþ wlǣttan, ðam men ðe hine ne lyst his metes ne līþes</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (ii. 62, 15)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Wiþ nnluste and wlǣttan ðe of magan cymð</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (184, 5)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Wlǣtan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (158, 12)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gif hwā on scipe wlǣttan þolige</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (i. 206, 9)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðone wlǣttan ðæs magan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (204, 20)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ne yrne hē, ðe læs hē mid ðæs rynes ēðgunge hwylcne wleāttan (wlǣttan, v. l.) and sogeðan on his heortan ne āstyrige</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (R. Ben. 68, 3)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">what produces nausea, an object of loathing</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">vertatur in nauseam</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ōð hit gǣð þurh eōwre næsþyrlu and sī gewend tō wlǣttan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Num. 11, 20)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Būtan hlāfe ǣlc mete tō wlǣttan byþ gehwyrfed</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Coll. Monast. Th. 28, 35)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Seō ofering ðē wurþ oþþe tō sāre oððe tō wlǣttan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 14, 1; Fox 42, 16)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">sentina</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Wlǣttan sentina</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ānglia xiii. 28, 28)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">foetidam nauseam (sentinam)</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Fūlne wlǣttan foetidam nauseam</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hpt. Gl. 475, 50)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">nausiam</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Wlǣtan nausiam</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 81, 9)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">III.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">defilement, disfigurement</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">deformatio (venusti capitis deformatio, Ald. 62)</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Wlǣtta deformatio</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hpt. Gl. 510, 6)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Þu miht mid wlate þe este bugge</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (O. and N. 1506)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:an-wlǣta" class="xref-target">an-wlǣta</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:-wlāta" class="xref-target">-wlāta</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:ā-wlǣtan" class="xref-target">ā-wlǣtan</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge-wlǣtan" class="xref-target">ge-wlǣtan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="hwearftlian" d:title="hwearftlian">
		<body>
			<h1>hwearftlian<span class="pron"> | xwæ͜ɑrft.li.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -ode</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To turn round, roll round, revolve, move about, rove</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">verso</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic hwearftlige verso</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. Gr. 37; Som. 39, 15)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the eyes that now rove through unallowed desires</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ða eāgan ðe nū þurh unālȳfedlīce gewilnunga hwearftliaþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. i. 530, 31)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the millstone that is continually turning and makes no progress, betokens worldly love, that goes round and round in errors and takes no firm step in the way of God</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Se cwyrnstān ðe tyrnþ singallīce and nǣnne færeld ne þurhtīhþ getācnaþ woruldlufe ðe on gedwyldum hwyrftlaþ and nǣnne stæpe on Godes wege gefæstnaþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (514, 21)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">great trust was revolving in Peter's heart</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Micel trūwa hwearftlode on Petres heortan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (392, 34)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="cīwung" d:title="cīwung">
		<body>
			<h1>cīwung<span class="pron"> | Kiː.wung |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Chewing</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. ruminatio)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Cīwung vel edroc ruminatio</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. i. 54, 62)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-hiwad" d:title="ge-hiwad">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-hiwad<span class="pron"> | je.xi.wɑd |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>participle</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Coloured</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. purpuratus)</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="cyfes" d:title="cyfes">
