	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="lādung" d:title="lādung">
		<body>
			<h1>lādung<span class="pron"> | lɑː.dung |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">An excusing, a clearing of or defending against a charge, an apology, excuse, a defence, exculpation</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Lādung apologia</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. Gl. 106; Som. 78, 64; Wrt. Voc. 57, 43)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">excussatio</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 146, 15)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">God allows the wicked man time, that he may, if he will, cease from his wicked deeds: that, if he will not, he may, having nothing to plead in his defence, very justly be thrust into the hands of the devil</span>
							<span class="q-oe">God lǣt him fyrst ðæt hē his māndǣda geswīce gif hē wile: gif hē nele ðæt hē beō būtan ǣlcere lādunge swīðe rihtlīce tō deōfles handa āsceofen</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. i. 270, 1)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">mentes fallaci defensione circumdatæ</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Mōd ymbtrymedu mid lytelīcre lādunge</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 35, 5; Swt. 245, 8)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">semper improbas defensiones quærunt</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hī simle sēceaþ endeleāse lādunga</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (35, 2; Swt. 239, 8)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">as a legal term, purgation, the clearing himself on the part of an accused person, by oath or by some form of ordeal, of the charge made against him</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">And stande betwux burgum ān lagu æt lādunge</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. C. S. 34; Th. i. 396, 22)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">when accusation is made, the bishop shall so order the proceedings by which the accused is to clear himself, that no man may be able to offer wrong to another in the matter of taking oath or of undergoing the ordeal</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Bisceop sceall æt tihtlan, lādunge gedihtan ðæt ǣnig man ōðrum ǣnig wōh beōdan ne mǣge āðor oððe on āþe oððe on ordāle</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. I. P. 7; Th. ii. 312, 15)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:lād" class="xref-target">lād</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:lādian" class="xref-target">lādian</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:be-lādung" class="xref-target">be-lādung</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="hrycgmearh-liþ" d:title="hrycgmearh-liþ">
		<body>
			<h1>hrycgmearh-liþ<span class="pron"> | xrydʒː.mæ͜ɑrx.liθ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>neuter noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">The spine</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hrygmergliþ spina</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. 283, 46)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="fang" d:title="fang">
		<body>
			<h1>fang<span class="pron"> | fɑng |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">what is taken, A booty</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. captūra, præda)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">they would take booty</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hī fang woldon fōn</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 1016; Th. 281, 30)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:feax-fang" class="xref-target">feax-fang</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:feoh-fang" class="xref-target">feoh-fang</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:fore-fang" class="xref-target">fore-fang</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:for-fang" class="xref-target">for-fang</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:under-fang" class="xref-target">under-fang</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="lǣþ-leās" d:title="lǣþ-leās">
		<body>
			<h1>lǣþ-leās<span class="pron"> | læːθ.læ͜ɑːs |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:lāþ-leās" class="xref-target">lāþ-leās</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="þeōn" d:title="þeōn">
		<body>
			<h1>þeōn<span class="pron"> | θe͜oːn |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:þeōwan" class="xref-target">þeōwan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="gold-smiþ" d:title="gold-smiþ">
		<body>
			<h1>gold-smiþ<span class="pron"> | gold.smiθ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A goldsmith, worker in gold</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. aurifex)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">Tubalcain was a worker both in gold and in iron</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Tubalcain wæs ēgðer ge goldsmiþ ge īsensmiþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Gen. 4, 22)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Goldsmiþ aurifex</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Coll. Monast. Th. 29, 35: Homl. Th. i. 64, 8)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">which king Edred gave by charter to his goldsmith Ælfsig</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðe Eādrēd cyng gebōcode Ælfsige his goldsmipe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cod. Dipl. Kmbl. iii. 431, 24: vi. 211, 7: Bt. Met. Fox 10, 67; Met. 10, 34)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-mǣran" d:title="ge-mǣran">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-mǣran<span class="pron"> | je.mæː.rɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -de</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -ed</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To celebrate, divulge, spread abroad</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">qua divulgata visione</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðā ðeōs gesyhþ wæs gemǣred</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 4, 25; S. 601, 25 : 3, 10; S. 535, note 2)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">divulgatum est verbum istud apud Judæos</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gemǣred wæs word ðis mið Iudeum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. Kmbl. Rush. 28, 15)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">illi diffamaverunt eum</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hiæ gemērdon hine</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (9, 31)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="god-dōhtor" d:title="god-dōhtor">
		<body>
			<h1>god-dōhtor<span class="pron"> | god.doːx.tor |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A GODDAUGHTER</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">I grant to my goddaughter the land at Stretton</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic geann mīnre goddōhtor ðæt land æt Strǣttūne</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Chart.Th. 548, 5)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-ēfstan" d:title="ge-ēfstan">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-ēfstan<span class="pron"> | je.eːf.stɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -ēfste</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -ēfsted, past participle sg: -ēfst</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">imperative: sg: -ēfst</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To hasten, make haste, be quick</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. festīnāre, accelerāre)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">accělěra ut eruas me</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Geēfst oððe hrada ðæt ðū alȳse me</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Lamb. 30, 2)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ēfstan" class="xref-target">ēfstan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ēstines" d:title="ēstines">
		<body>
			<h1>ēstines<span class="pron"> | eː.sti.nes |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Benignity, kindness, bounteousness</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. bĕnignĭtas)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">Dŏmĭnus dăbit bĕnignĭtātem</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Drihten selþ ēstinesse</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Spl. T. 84, 13: 64, 12)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="be-hīdan" d:title="be-hīdan">
		<body>
			<h1>be-hīdan<span class="pron"> | be.xiː.dɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -hīdde</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To hide</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. abscondere)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">quod nudus essem, abscondi me</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Forðamðe ic eom nacod, ic behīdde me</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Gen. 3, 10, 8)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:be-hȳdan" class="xref-target">be-hȳdan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="on-wrigenness" d:title="on-wrigenness">
		<body>
			<h1>on-wrigenness<span class="pron"> | on.wri.Gen.ness |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">An uncovering, discovery</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Onwrigenys apocalypsis</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hpt. Gl. 435, 43)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">a removal of that which obscures or conceals</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-en">a light to lighten the Gentiles</span>
									<span class="q-la">lumen ad revelationem gentium</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Leōht tō onwrigennysse þeōda</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. i. 136, 22)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">an explanation, exposition (v. on-wreōn, III)</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">ecclesiasticae traditionis, expositionis</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Circlīcere anwrigenisse</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Hpt. Gl. 410, 36)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-en">by means of an explanation (translation) in their own tongue</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Hæbben ða ungelǣredan inlendisce ðæs hālgan regules cȳððe þurh āgenes gereordes anwrigennesse</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Lchdm. iii. 442, 9)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">III.</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">an exposure of a person's real character (v. on-wreōn, V)</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-en">the vanity of your pretensions will be exposed, and the reality of our claims will be made manifest</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Nū neālǣceþ ǣgðer ge ðīn onwrigennes ge uncer gecȳðnes</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Blickl. Homl. 187, 23)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">IV.</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">a revelation, manifestation made to the eye or to the ear by divine power (v. on-wreōn, VI)</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Heō sægde ðæt heō geleornod hæfde on onwrihgennysse (MS. T. onwrignesse) ðæt hire forþfōre wǣre swīðe neāh. Sǣde heō him ðæt seō onwrihgnes ðyslīc wǣre. Cwæþ ðæt heō gesāwe micelne þreāt</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 3, 8; S. 531, 35-38)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Se Hǣlend geswutelode him ða tōweardan onwrigenysse (a revelation of the future), be ðære hē āwrāt ða bōc ðe is gehāten Apocalipsis</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. i. 60, 1)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-en">through a revelation made by Christ</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Helena hī āfunde þurh Cristes onwrigennesse</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (H. R. 99, 8)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">superna illi oracula restiterunt</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Him ða upplīcan onwrigenesse wiðstōdon</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 5, 9; S. 622, 21)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="lendenu" d:title="lendenu">
		
		<body>
			<h1>lendenu<span class="pron"> | len.de.nu |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -a</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Lendena lumbia</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. i. 283, 52 : ii. 51, 73)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Lēndnum, laendum clunis</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Txts. 48, 216)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Lāreōwas ūs secgað þ on þām lendenum is þæs līchaman gālnyss</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. A. 17, 95)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">accingere gladium luum circa femor</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Begyrd sweord ðīn ymb lendna [lendynu, Ps. Cam. : lendan ( = lendna), Ps. Srt.]</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Vos. 44, 4)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="cæg-loca" d:title="cæg-loca">
		<body>
			<h1>cæg-loca<span class="pron"> | KæG.lo.kɑ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -an</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">The action of locking up, a key-locking, any repository locked up</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. clavis et loculamentum)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">unless it has been brought under his wife's 'lock and key,' let her be clear; for it is her duty to keep the keys of them; namely, her 'hord-ern,' and her chest, and her cupboard</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Būton hit under ðæs wīfes cǣglocan [cǣglocum MS. A.] gebroht wǣre, sȳ heō clǣne, ac ðæra cǣgean heō scēal UNCERTAIN weardian; ðæt is, hire hordern, and hire cyste, and hire tege</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. C. S. 77; Th. i. 418, 19-22)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="Gota" d:title="Gota">
		<body>
			<h1>Gota<span class="pron"> | go.tɑ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">Gothus quidam pauper spiritu</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Sum Gota þearfa on gāste</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Gr. D. 113, 15)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Hū se Gota geneādod āgeaf Furtunate þā cnapan</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (79, 8)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Wisle lond, and be-eāstan þǣm sint Datia, þā þe iū wǣron Gotan</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 1, 1; S. 16, 18)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Hū Bonefatius þām Gotan gefyllde þā flaxan. Hit gelamp ꝥ him cōmon twēgen men tō of Gotena þeōde, þā sǣdon ꝥ hī tō Rauennan faran woldon</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Gr. D. 66, 3-7)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="mæst-land" d:title="mæst-land">
		<body>
			<h1>mæst-land<span class="pron"> | mæst.lɑnd |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>neuter noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Land on which mast is produced</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Eall ðæt wudu—lond ðæt Æþelbald gesealde tō mæstlonde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Chart. Th. 140, 2)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="friþ-her[e]paþ" d:title="friþ-her[e]paþ">
		<body>
			<h1>friþ-her[e]paþ<span class="pron"> | friθ.xer, e, pɑθ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">The king's highway, a public road which was under the king's friþ</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">On Wifeles ford; ðonne andlang ðæs friðherpadcs (Icknield Way ?)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (C. D. v. 214, 35)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="wiþ-sacung" d:title="wiþ-sacung">
		<body>
			<h1>wiþ-sacung<span class="pron"> | wiθ.sɑ.kung |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Renunciation</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. abrenuntiatio)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Nāht ūs framaþ wiðsacing (abrenuntiatio) līchaman būtan wiðsacinge geþances</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Scint. 60, 14)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="mæþel-friþ" d:title="mæþel-friþ">
		<body>
			<h1>mæþel-friþ<span class="pron"> | mæ.θel.friθ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>neuter noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Peace secured by law at a public assembly, the violation of which had to be compensated twofold</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ciricfriþ II. gylde; mæthlfriþ II. gylde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ll. Lbmn, 3, 6)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="sulh-æcer" d:title="sulh-æcer">
