			<h1>þrum<span class="pron"> | θrum |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:tunge-þrum" class="xref-target">tunge-þrum</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="cylcende" d:title="cylcende">
		
		<body>
			<h1>cylcende<span class="pron"> | Kyl.Ken.de |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>participle</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">ructans</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:bealcan" class="xref-target">bealcan</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:bealcettan" class="xref-target">bealcettan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="be-fician" d:title="be-fician">
		<body>
			<h1>be-fician<span class="pron"> | be.fi.Ki.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">to deceive, to go round</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. decipere)</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="winter-tīd" d:title="winter-tīd">
		<body>
			<h1>winter-tīd<span class="pron"> | win.ter.tiːd |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Winter-time, winter</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hit is wintertīd nū, and ic wundrie þearle hwanon þes wyrtbrǣð þus wynsumlīce stēme</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Skt. i. 4, 35)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">brumali tempore</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Swā gelīc swā ðū æt swǣsendum sette mid ðīnum ðegnum on wintertīde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 2, 13; S. 516, 16)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðās wyrte ðū scealt niman on wintertīde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lchdm. i. 148, 2)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-teōn" d:title="ge-teōn">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-teōn<span class="pron"> | je.te͜oːn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">present: 1sg: -teō, 2sg: -tȳhst, 3sg: -tȳhþ, pl: -teōþ</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -teāh, sg: -teāg, sg: -tēh, pl: -tugon</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -togen</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to draw, lead, incite, excite, constrain, restrain, bring up, instruct, bring to an end, complete, draw or bind together, string a musical instrument</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. trahere, ducere, perducere, stringere, evaginare, excitare, constringere, educare, instituere, ad finem perducere, complere, nervis aptare vel instruere)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">would draw him into despair</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Woldon hine geteōn in orwēnnysse</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 41 a; Th. 136, 24; Gū. 546)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">has mulieres consuetudo constringit</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðās wīf wuna getēþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 1, 7; S. 494, 11)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">consummabis summitatem ejus</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðū getīhst his heāhnisse</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Gen. 6, 16)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">he drew Adam from hell</span>
							<span class="q-oe">He Adam fram helle getēh</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Nicod. 30; Thw. 17, 31)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">multos ad Catholicam Dominici Paschæ celebrationem perduxit</span>
							<span class="q-oe">He monige to rihtre weorþunge ðǣre Drihtenlīcan Eāstrana geteāh and gelǣdde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 5, 18; S. 636, 4)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">when they had drawn all the people of Greece to the wars</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðā hī hæfdon getogen eall Creāca folc to ðǣm gewinnum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 1, 14; Bos. 37, 14, 35)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">he drew an ancient relic [i. e. a sword]</span>
							<span class="q-oe">He geteāg ealde lāfe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. 162; Th. 203, 22; Exod. 407)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">evaginata sica</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Getogene ðȳ wǣpne</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 2, 9; S. 511, 21)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">excitatum ad scelera vulgus</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Folc to mānum getogen</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (2, 5; S. 507, 42)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">he has restrained all creatures</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hæfþ ealle gesceafta getogen</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. Met. Fox 11, 48; Met. 11, 24)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">those who were rightly instructed in the art of numbers</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ða ðe wǣron on rīm-cræfte rihte getogene</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 975; Th. 226, 31; Edg. 27)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">a man so well instructed</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Swā getogen mann</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. ii. 122, 13: Th. Ap. 17, 18)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">hoc bellum quarto imperii sui anno complevit</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðeōs fyrd wæs getogen ðȳ feorþan geāre his rīces</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 1, 3; S. 475, 15)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">illa erat multo dolore constricta</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Wæs heō mid micle sāre getogen</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (5, 3; S. 616, 22)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">alvus constricta</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Wamb getogen</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Med. ex Quadr. 6, 11; Lchdm. i. 352, 24)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">a harp strung with ten strings</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Mid tyn strengum getogen hearpe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 143, 10)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the organs were played</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ða organa wǣron getogene</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Th. Ap. 25, 15)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to bring as an offering or gift, contribute, bestow, give</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. conferre)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">gave possession of war-horses and weapons</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Onweald geteāh wicga and wǣpna</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Beo. Th. 2093; B. 1044: 4337; B. 2165)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">do not give them a denial</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Nō ðū him wearne geteōh</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (738; B. 366)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="beād" d:title="beād">
		<body>
			<h1>beād<span class="pron"> | bæ͜ɑːd |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">a prayer</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. oratio)</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:gebēd" class="xref-target">gebēd</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:beāda" class="xref-target">beāda</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="for-myltan" d:title="for-myltan">
		<body>
			<h1>for-myltan<span class="pron"> | for.myl.tɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">to melt</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. līquor)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">līquor</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic formylte</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. Gr. 29; Som. 33, 44)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:for-meltan" class="xref-target">for-meltan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="-hlēþa" d:title="-hlēþa">
