			<h1>māh<span class="pron"> | mɑːx |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Wicked, wanton</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge-māh" class="xref-target">ge-māh</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="fæstn" d:title="fæstn">
		<body>
			<h1>fæstn<span class="pron"> | fæstn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">a fortification</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. mūnīmentum)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">of those fortifcations</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðara fæstna</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. 209; Th. 259, 15; Dan. 692)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:fæsten II" class="xref-target">fæsten II</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="mynster-þegnung" d:title="mynster-þegnung">
		<body>
			<h1>mynster-þegnung<span class="pron"> | myn.ster.θe.ɣnung |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Minster-service, service in a minster</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="wītu" d:title="wītu">
		<body>
			<h1>wītu<span class="pron"> | wiː.tu |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">the pains that we inflict</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">wītu ne ondrǣde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (85, 15: Cd. Th. 289, 3; Sat. 392)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:blōd-wīte" class="xref-target">blōd-wīte</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:dol-wīte" class="xref-target">dol-wīte</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:fiht-wīte" class="xref-target">fiht-wīte</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:fyht-wīte" class="xref-target">fyht-wīte</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:fyrd-wīte" class="xref-target">fyrd-wīte</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:ferd-wīte" class="xref-target">ferd-wīte</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:helle-wīte" class="xref-target">helle-wīte</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:leger-wīte" class="xref-target">leger-wīte</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:weard-wīte" class="xref-target">weard-wīte</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:weorold-wīte" class="xref-target">weorold-wīte</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:wræc-wīte" class="xref-target">wræc-wīte</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="dǣl-leās" d:title="dǣl-leās">
		<body>
			<h1>dǣl-leās<span class="pron"> | dæːl.læ͜ɑːs |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Without a part, portionless, deficient</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. expers)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">expers, indoctus</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Dǣlleās vel cræftleās</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. Gl. 18; Som. 58, 123; Wrt. Voc. 22, 36: 90; Som. 75, 2; Wrt. Voc. 51, 47)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="crēd" d:title="crēd">
		<body>
			<h1>crēd<span class="pron"> | kreːd |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:han-crēd" class="xref-target">han-crēd</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ofer-gitness" d:title="ofer-gitness">
		<body>
			<h1>ofer-gitness<span class="pron"> | o.fer.Git.ness |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Forgetfulness, oblivion</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">in terra oblivionis, v. 12</span>
							<span class="q-oe">On ðam lande ðe ofer—gytnes on eardige</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 87, 11)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">in oblivione</span>
							<span class="q-oe">On ofergetnisse</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lk. Skt. Rush. 12, 6)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="hridder" d:title="hridder">
		
		<body>
			<h1>hridder<span class="pron"> | xrid.der |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Hrīder glebulum</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 98, 12)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Hridder capisterium</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (92, 3: 19, 38)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Hū hē geedstaðelode, ꝥ tōbrokene hridder (capisterium) . . . hē genam þā sticcu þæs tōbrocenan hriddres (hridderes, v. l.) . . . and hire āgæf ꝥ hriddern (hridder, v. l.) . . . þā landleōde āhēngon ꝥ ilce hriddern (hridder) in þǣre cyrcan ingange</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Gr. D. 96, 30-97, 34)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="steall" d:title="steall">
		<body>
			<h1>steall<span class="pron"> | stæ͜ɑll |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">a standing position</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Setl gedafenaþ dēman, and steall fylstendum</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Stephanus hine (Christ) geseah standende, forðan ðe hē wæs his gefylsta</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. i. 48, 29)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">give him the medicine hot to drink in a standing position; let him stand a good while</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Syle hāt drincan in stalle stonde gōde hwīle</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lchdm. iii. 28, 5)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">the way matters stand, position of affairs, state, condition</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">status ecclesiae</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Se steall cyricean</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 2, 4; S. 505, 10)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">in periculum sui status</span>
							<span class="q-oe">On frǣcenesse heora stealles</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (4, 25; S. 601, 18)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">de cujus statu vitae</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Be ðisses biscopes līfes stealle</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (5, 19; S. 637, 2)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Be ðam stalle cyrican</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (3, 19, S. 561, 7)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">priscum in statum</span>
							<span class="q-oe">On ðone ǣrran steall</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (5, 20; S. 642, 10: 5, 24; S. 646, 38)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">regni statum</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðone stal ðæs rīces</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (4, 26; S. 603, 8)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">III.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">position, place</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">carceres (the starting-place in the circus), scridwīsa auriga</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Horsa steal</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. i. 39, 37)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">latitudine sui status</span>
							<span class="q-oe">On brǣdo his stealles</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd, 1, 1; S. 474, 29)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt se sȳ furþor forlǣten on stealle and on setle (cf. on stele and on setle, 13, 1), se ðe furðor on geearnunge sȳ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (R. Ben. 12, 19)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">ultimus omnium stet aut in loco quem talibus negligentibus seorsum constituerit abbas</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Stande hē ealra ȳtemest, oðþe on ðam stede ðe se abbod swā gēmeleāsum monnum tō stealle on sundrum betǣht hæfþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (68, 11)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt hī nǣfre ne beōn on stede ne on stealle, ðǣr ǣfre undōn worðe ðæt ūre forgengles geūðen</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Chart. Th. 348, 30)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">IV.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">place, stead</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Brihtwald gehālgode Tobian on his steall</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 693; Erl. 43, 19)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Steal</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (780; Erl. 57, 1: 803; Erl. 61, 23)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Stall</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (779; Erl. 55, 38)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Stal</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (678; Erl. 41, 7: 727; Erl. 47, 2: 796; Erl. 59, 39)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">V.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">a place for cattle, a stall</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">stabulum</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Stal</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 121, 11)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Steal</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (i. 15, 23)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæra tamra nȳtena steall</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Boutr. Scrd. 21, 9)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">VI.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">a place for catching fish</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">laxa retia in capturam (captura locus piscosus, ubi capiuntur pisces)</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Lēt ða netto on stællo</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lk. Skt. Lind. 5, 4)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:æt-steall" class="xref-target">æt-steall</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:bōd-steall" class="xref-target">bōd-steall</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:burg-steall" class="xref-target">burg-steall</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:fore-steall" class="xref-target">fore-steall</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge-steall" class="xref-target">ge-steall</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:geard-steall" class="xref-target">geard-steall</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:hege-steall" class="xref-target">hege-steall</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:mylen-steall" class="xref-target">mylen-steall</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:ofer-steall" class="xref-target">ofer-steall</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:on-steall" class="xref-target">on-steall</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:scip-steall" class="xref-target">scip-steall</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:treōw-steall" class="xref-target">treōw-steall</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:wæter-steall" class="xref-target">wæter-steall</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:weal-steall" class="xref-target">weal-steall</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:weard-steall" class="xref-target">weard-steall</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:weofod-steall" class="xref-target">weofod-steall</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:weoh-steall" class="xref-target">weoh-steall</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:wīc-steall" class="xref-target">wīc-steall</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:wīg-steall" class="xref-target">wīg-steall</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:wið-steall" class="xref-target">wið-steall</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:wiðer-steall" class="xref-target">wiðer-steall</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:wiðer-steal" class="xref-target">wiðer-steal</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:fæst-steall" class="xref-target">fæst-steall</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:stæl" class="xref-target">stæl</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:stede" class="xref-target">stede</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="on-galness" d:title="on-galness">
		<body>
			<h1>on-galness<span class="pron"> | on.gɑl.ness |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A constant singing or song</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">[tu es] decantatio mea semper</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ongalnis ł sang mīn symle</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Rdr. 70, 6)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="gelimplǣcan" d:title="gelimplǣcan">
		<body>
			<h1>gelimplǣcan<span class="pron"> | Ge.lim.plæː.kɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">to become fitted</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. coaptari)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">coaptari</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gelimplǣcan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (An. Ox. 80)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="weg-farende" d:title="weg-farende">
		<body>
			<h1>weg-farende<span class="pron"> | wej.fɑ.ren.de |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A wayfarer</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ūre dagas gewītað swā swā wegfarende menn</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. S. 28, 154)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hī begunnon tō āxienne æt ōþrum wegfarendum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (31, 992)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="hwīl-stycce" d:title="hwīl-stycce">
		<body>
			<h1>hwīl-stycce<span class="pron"> | xwiːl.styk.Ke |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>neuter noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A fragment or short portion of time</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">all that they can earn in any of their fragments of time</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ǣghwæðæs ðe hie on ǣnegum hiora hwīlsticcum geearnian mǣgen</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. Alf. pol. 43; Th. i. 92, 12)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="Benesing-tūn" d:title="Benesing-tūn">
		<body>
			<h1>Benesing-tūn<span class="pron"> | be.ne.sing.tuːn |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:Bensingtūn" class="xref-target">Bensingtūn</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="fær" d:title="fær">
		<body>
			<h1>fær<span class="pron"> | fær |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>neuter noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">nominative sg: -nom. acc:, genitive sg: -færes, dative sg: -fære, nominative pl: -faru, genitive pl: -fara, dative pl: -farum</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">a going, journey, way, journeying, expedition</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. iter, expeditio bellica)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">iter diei</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ānes dæges fær</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lk. Bos. 2, 44)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">facilitate the people's journeying</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gōdige folces fær</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. Pen. 15; Th. ii. 282, 9)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">that was a great expedition</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt wæs fær micel</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Invent. Crs. Recd. 1295; El. 646)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">that in which a journey or voyage is made,-a vehicle, vessel, ship</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. vehiculum, navis)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">make thou that vessel</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðū ðær [Th. Grn. ðæt that] fær gewyrc</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. 65; Th. 79, 6; Gen. 1307)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">Noah's ark</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Fær Noes</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. 66; Th. 80, 4; Gen. 1323)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ād-fær" class="xref-target">ād-fær</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge-fær" class="xref-target">ge-fær</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:in-fær" class="xref-target">in-fær</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:ofer-fær" class="xref-target">ofer-fær</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:ongeān-fær" class="xref-target">ongeān-fær</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:ūt-fær" class="xref-target">ūt-fær</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:þurh-fær" class="xref-target">þurh-fær</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="-rǣde" d:title="-rǣde">
		<body>
			<h1>-rǣde<span class="pron"> | ræː.de |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge-rǣde" class="xref-target">ge-rǣde</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-feallan" d:title="ge-feallan">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-feallan<span class="pron"> | je.fæ͜ɑl.lɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">intrans.</span>
					</p>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(1)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">to fall from a higher to a lower position</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">super quem ceciderit</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Ofer þæne þe hē gefylþ</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (An. Ox. 61, 28)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">descendant usque ad abyssos</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Þā tō heofenum āstīgað, nyðer gefeallað under neowulne grund</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 106, 25: Cri. 1532)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hiē hine forlētan and hē gefeōl on þone stocc</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Bl. H. 189, 12)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">descendit pluvia</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Gefeāll regn</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. L. 7, 25)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ealle þā yldestan witan gefeōllan of ānre ūpflōran, būtan se hālga Dūnstān āna ætstōd uppon ānum beāme</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 978; P. 123, 2)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Se heoton biþ gefeallen æt þǣm feōwer endum middangeardes</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Bl. H. 93, 5)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Gefeallen snāw</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 148, 8)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(2)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">to fall from an erect position</span>
							</p>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(2)(a)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">of living things</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">labat</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Āslād and gefiōll</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 50, 62)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">procumberet</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Gefeoll</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (66, 9)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hē gefeāll onufa suira his</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Lk. L. 15, 20)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Gefeōl se rīca on his reste middan</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Jud. 67)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hē gefeōll tō foldan</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (280)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(2)(a α)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">to stumble, fall into or over</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ēghuoelc sē ðe gefalleð onufa ðæm stāne</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Lk. L. R. 20, 18)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Gif gefallas scīp in seāð</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. L. 12, 11)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hī on ðone seāð gefeōllan</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 56, 8)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(2)(a β)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">to fall in reverence</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ꝥ wif forhtade ... and gifeōl (gefeall, L.) bifora him</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Mk. R. 5, 33)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ꝥ wīf gīfeōll bifora fōtum his</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Lk. R. 8, 47)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hē gifeōll on onsiōne</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (17, 16)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(2)(a γ)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">to fall dead or wounded, fall in battle</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Gefallas hiā in mūðe suordes</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Lk. L. 21, 24)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Micel wæl gefeōl</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 943; P. 111, 12: 1004; P. 135, 36)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Þǣr on greōt gefeōll se hȳhsta dǣl</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Jud. 308)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hwæt wæs on manrīme ... dareðlācendra deādra gefeallen</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (El. 651)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(2)(b)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">of material objects, buildings, &amp;c.</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Þonne gefeallaþ ealle deōfolgyld</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Bl. H. 93, 16)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Þæt hūs nō gefeōll (-feāll, L.)</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. R. 7, 25, 27: Lk. L. 6, 49)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(3)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">to fall</span>
							</p>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(3)(a)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">of persons, to perish, be ruined</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Se līchoma lǣne gedreōseð, fǣge gefealleð</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (B. 1755)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">vos moriemini ..., sicut unus de principibus cadetis</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Gē sweltað ..., swā ealdormann ān gefealleð</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 81, 7)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Leāf fēalewiað, feallað on eorðan, ... swā gefeallað þā þe firena lǣstað</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Sal. 315)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(3)(b)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">of things, to decline, decay, fail</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Mycel yfel weaxeþ on þīnum rīce, gif þū lǣtest leng þysne drȳ rīxian, ... and þīn rīce for his lārum gefealleþ</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Bl. H. 181, 34)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Eāðor is ... ðon ān merce gefalla</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Lk. L. 16, 17)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(4)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">to fall to doing something, to fall ādoing, busy one's self at something, apply with energy to</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">concitus descendit, atque in ejusdem rustici amplexum ruit</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Hē ofdūne āstāh and gefeōll on þæs ceorles clyppinge</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Gr. D. 47, 1 [: Ap. Th. 16, 23. v. Dict.])</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(5)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">of that which (violently) affects the mind</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">timor irruit super eum</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Ondo gefeōll (gifeōl, R.) ofer hine</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Lk. L. 1, 12)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hē fond his mondryhten ādlwērigne; him þæt in gefeōl hefig æt heortan</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Gū. 981)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">trans.</span>
					</p>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(1)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">to reach by falling, to fall and reach, fall to</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hē meregrund gefeōll</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (B. 2100)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hē hreās on hrūsan ... hē eorðan gefeōll</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (2834)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Lagu land gefeōl (of the water of the Red Sea when it fell upon the Egyptians trying to follow in the track of the Israelites)</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Exod. 482: 491)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(2)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">to cause by falling</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">quantam reipublicae orbitatem occasu suo intulerit Fabiorum familia</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Hit is on leōðum gesungen hwelcne demm hie Rōmānum gefeōllan</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 2, 4; S. 72, 11)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="stān-fāh" d:title="stān-fāh">
		<body>
			<h1>stān-fāh<span class="pron"> | stɑːn.fɑːx |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Many-coloured with stones, epithet of a road</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="sulh-geteōh" d:title="sulh-geteōh">
		<body>
			<h1>sulh-geteōh<span class="pron"> | sulx.Ge.te͜oːx |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>neuter noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -teōges</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">An implement belonging to a plough</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">let him collect together all the apparatus of his plough</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gegaderie hē ealle his sulhgeteōgo tōgædere</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lchdm. i. 400, 19)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ganet" d:title="ganet">
		<body>
			<h1>ganet<span class="pron"> | gɑ.net |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A gannet, sea-fowl, water-fowl, swan</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. fŭlĭca, cygnus)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ganet cygnus</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Glos. Prudent. Recd. 144, 32)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">over the sea-fowl's bath</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ofer ganetes bæþ [MS. baþ]</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 975; Erl. 125, 21)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the gannet's cry</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ganetes hleōðor</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 81 b; Th. 307, 8; Seef. 20)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">sea fowls came flying from the ocean</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Cōmon of gārsecge ganetas fleōgan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 104, 35)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ganot" class="xref-target">ganot</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="hell-rūna" d:title="hell-rūna">
		<body>
			<h1>hell-rūna<span class="pron"> | xell.ruː.nɑ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -an</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">One skilled in the mysteries of hell, a sorcerer, necromancer</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:helle-rūne" class="xref-target">helle-rūne</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="tweōnigend-līc" d:title="tweōnigend-līc">
		<body>
			<h1>tweōnigend-līc<span class="pron"> | twe͜oː.ni.Gend.liːtʃ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Expressing doubt</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Sume syndon dubitativa, ðæt synd twȳnigendlīce (tweōniend-, MS. H.)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. Gr. 38; Zup. 228, 16)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Twȳniendlīce</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (44; Zup. 261, 2)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="wǣpn" d:title="wǣpn">
