<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="eal-niwe" d:title="eal-niwe">
		<body>
			<h1>eal-niwe<span class="pron"> | æ͜ɑl.ni.we |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">all-new, quite new</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:eall-niwe" class="xref-target">eall-niwe</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="hold-scipe" d:title="hold-scipe">
		<body>
			<h1>hold-scipe<span class="pron"> | xold.ʃi.pe |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Loyalty, fealty, allegiance</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">they destroyed the lands of all those men that were in allegiance to the king</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Eallra ðæra manna land hī fordydon ðe wǣron innan ðæs cynges holdscipe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 1087; Erl. 224, 15)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">said that they did it on account of the loyalty of the monastery</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Sægdon ðæt hī hit dyden for ðes mynstres holdscipe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (1070; Erl. 209, 15)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-grētan" d:title="ge-grētan">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-grētan<span class="pron"> | je.greː.tɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">present: 3sg: -grēt, pl: -grētaþ</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -grētte, pl: -grētton</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -grēted</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To approach, come to, address, greet, welcome</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. adire, alloqui, salutare)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">the wife shall the nobles' chief first greet</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Wīf sceal eodor æþelinga [MS. e] ǣrest gegrētan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 90 a; Th. 339, 7; Gn. Ex. 90)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">he addressed his faithful friend in powerful words</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Holdne gegrētte meaglum wordum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Beo. Th, 3964; B. 1980)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">he then addressed them</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hie ðā gegrētte</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Andr. Kmbl. 507; An. 254)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">that we may see our friends and greet our kinsmen</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt we māgon ūre frȳnd geseōn and ūre siblingas gegrētan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. ii. 526, 33)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">men blame and insult those that love right</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Man tǣleþ and mid yfle gegrēteþ ða ðe riht lufiaþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Swt. A. S. Rdr. 110, 164)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:grētan" class="xref-target">grētan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-līfed" d:title="ge-līfed">
		
		<body>
			<h1>ge-līfed<span class="pron"> | je.liː.fed |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">endowed with belief, believing</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Se gelȳfeda ætwint ðām frecednyssum ðǣra deōflicra costnunga</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. Th. i. 368, 32)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">men of little faith</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hwōnlīce gelȳfede menn</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (566, 28)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">¶</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">believing on</span>
							</p>
							<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
								<li>
									<p>
										<span class="sense-label">(1)</span>
										<span class="meaning-en">with acc., cf. ge-līfan; II. 1 a α</span>
									</p>
									<ul class="quotes">
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Sum man . . . swīðe gelȳfed on þone lyfiendan God</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Ælfc. T. Grn. 11, 5)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Sum mǣden . . . on ðone Hǣlend gelȳfed</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. S. 7, 7)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Cōmon his āgene landleōde gelȳfede (-leōf-, v. l.) on God</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (14, 172)</span>
										</li>
									</ul>
								</li>
								<li>
									<p>
										<span class="sense-label">(2)</span>
										<span class="meaning-en">with dat., cf. ge-līfan; II. 1 a β</span>
									</p>
									<ul class="quotes">
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Sume sǣdon ꝥ hī wǣran on Crīste gelȳfede</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. S. 2, 303)</span>
										</li>
									</ul>
								</li>
							</ol>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:riht-gelīfed" class="xref-target">riht-gelīfed</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:un-gelīfed" class="xref-target">un-gelīfed</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:be-līfed" class="xref-target">be-līfed</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="malscrung" d:title="malscrung">
		<body>
			<h1>malscrung<span class="pron"> | mɑl.ʃrung |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Malscrung pressicium (for prestigium?)</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Hpt. 33, 246, 83)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="æfesa" d:title="æfesa">
		<body>
			<h1>æfesa<span class="pron"> | æ.fe.sɑ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -an</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Produce of woods on which swine might be fed</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">cum porcorum esca et cum fructibus . . . quoaue dono tertiam sarcinam iumentariam fructuum qui nascuntur in sylua proxime ad kyngesbyrig sita</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Mid mæste and mid æuesan . . . and ic ann þæt þridde swun (?) of æuesan þæs nēxtan wudes þe līþ tō kyngesbyrig</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (C. D. iv. 202, 2-12)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:æfesn" class="xref-target">æfesn</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:æfes-weorc" class="xref-target">æfes-weorc</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="on-geflogen" d:title="on-geflogen">
		<body>
			<h1>on-geflogen<span class="pron"> | on.Ge.flo.Gen |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>participle</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Attacked with disease</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gif men his leoþu acen oððe [hē] ongeflogen sȳ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lchdm. i. 86, 21)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:on-flyge" class="xref-target">on-flyge</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="burg-waru" d:title="burg-waru">
		<body>
			<h1>burg-waru<span class="pron"> | burɣ.wɑ.ru |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">populus civitatis</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Eall seō buruhwaru</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Deut. 21, 21)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Gyf hit binnan byrig gedōn bið, fare seō buruhwaru sylf tō and begyte þā banan</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Ll. Th. i. 286, 21)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Seō burhwaru gelæhton hine</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Ap Th. 26, 23)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Seō burhwaru, þæt sind Turonisce ..., and Pictauienscisce ... būtū ðā burhwara (-waru, -waræ, Hml. S. 31, 1469) besǣton ðone hālgan</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. Th. ii. 518, 18-24)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">civile bellum</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Burware gefeoht</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt Voc. i. 35, 17)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">clamor Gomorrhae</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Hreām þǣre burhware of Gomorra</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Gen. 18, 20)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">in scelere civitatis</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Mid þisre scildigre burhware</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (19, 15)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Com se cyning mid þǣre burhware tō ðām temple</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. Th. i. 462, 6)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Hē þā twā burhwara, Sodomam and Gomorram, forbærnde</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (246, 25)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Hiē þā burgware (here? or under preceding word ?), Beneuentius and Sepontanus hātton þā twā leōde, hiē þā ongunnon ānwigges biddan (cf. Neapolite cwǣdon gefeoht tōgeānes þǣre burhware Sepontiniscre ceastre and tōgeānes Beneuentanos, Hml. Th. i. 504, 12-15)</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Bl. H. 201, 21)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:next word" class="xref-target">next word</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="treōwþ" d:title="treōwþ">
		<body>
			<h1>treōwþ<span class="pron"> | tre͜oːwθ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">diaconum in suam suscepit fidem</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē nam þone deācon in his treōwþe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Gr. D. 253, 16)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="tō-slūping" d:title="tō-slūping">
		<body>
			<h1>tō-slūping<span class="pron"> | toː.sluː.ping |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Dissolution</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. dissolulio vitae)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">dissolulio vitae</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Tōslūpincg līfes</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Scint. 68, 8)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="god-gesprǣce" d:title="god-gesprǣce">
		<body>
			<h1>god-gesprǣce<span class="pron"> | god.Ge.spræː.Ke |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>neuter noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">An oracle</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">erat oraculum huiusmodi</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Wæs þis godgesprǣce (-sprec, -spræcen, -sprecen, v. ll.) þisses gemetes</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 2, 12; Sch. 152, 12)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">iuxta oraculum</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Æfter þām godgesprǣce (-sprece, þǣre gōdan sprǣce, þām gōdgesprece [the MS. has the accent], v. ll.)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Sch. 161, 15)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:godcund" class="xref-target">godcund</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:god-sprǣce" class="xref-target">god-sprǣce</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="þyrelian" d:title="þyrelian">
		<body>
			<h1>þyrelian<span class="pron"> | θy.re.li.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Þyrlie obunco</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (An. Ox. 18 b, 66)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="clǣþ" d:title="clǣþ">
		<body>
			<h1>clǣþ<span class="pron"> | klæːθ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">a cloth</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">put on a cloth</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Dō on clǣþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. M. 2, 47; Lchdm. ii. 260, 28)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:clāþ" class="xref-target">clāþ</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="nāgan" d:title="nāgan">
		<body>
			<h1>nāgan<span class="pron"> | nɑː.ɣɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē nāh æfter forðsīðe crīstenra manna gemānan.</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ll. Th. i. 372, 34)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Nāh man on ǣnigne tīman dæges ne nihtes æt Godes hūse unnyt tō dōnne,</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wlfst. 278, 18: 39, 16)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Be þām magon Godes þeōwas gecnāwan ꝥ hī nāgon mid worldcampe tō farene, ac mid gāstlican wǣpnan campian,</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ll. Th. ii. 388, 4)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">III.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">not to be obliged or bound to do</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">he was not bound to do it</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðā ðā Landfranc cræfede fæstnunge his gehērnesse mid āðswerunge, þā forsōc hē and sǣde ꝥ hē hit nāhte tō dōnne</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 1070; P. 206, 2)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="efen-esne" d:title="efen-esne">
		<body>
			<h1>efen-esne<span class="pron"> | e.fen.e.sne |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A fellow-servant</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. conservus)</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:efne-esne" class="xref-target">efne-esne</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="cist-beām" d:title="cist-beām">
		<body>
			<h1>cist-beām<span class="pron"> | Kist.bæ͜ɑːm |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:cyst-beām" class="xref-target">cyst-beām</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="frōfernis" d:title="frōfernis">
		<body>
			<h1>frōfernis<span class="pron"> | froː.fer.nis |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:frēfer-ness" class="xref-target">frēfer-ness</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ǣwe" d:title="ǣwe">
		<body>
			<h1>ǣwe<span class="pron"> | æː.we |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A married woman; in pl. married people</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">uxor</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gif hē cyfesan hæbbe and nāne rihtǣwe . . . beō hit cyfes beō hit ǣwe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ll. Th. ii. 186, 2-5: 270, 6)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ciric is sācerdes ǣwe; nāh hē mid rihte ænige ōþre</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (334, 24: 340, 5)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Oð þæt hē on rihtre ǣwe gewīfige, and hæbbe þā syþþan and nāne ōþre þā hwīle þe seō libbe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wlfst. 304, 21)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ūre Drihten forbeād twǣmincge betwux twām ǣwum ðus; 'Swā hwā swā his ǣwe forlǣt and ōðer genimd.</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. Th. 323, 31-3)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē gehǣlde sum wīf, ānes ealdormannes ǣwe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (150, 3)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Forlicgan wið ōðres ǣwe oþþe wið gehādode</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ll. Th. i. 404, 22)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">uxorem; muliere</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Be þām men þe his ǣwe forlǣt and be þām wīfe þe hire wer forlǣt</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (ii. 180, 13, 15)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Healde gehwā his ǣwe þā hwīle þe heō libbe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (300, 26)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:riht-ǣwe" class="xref-target">riht-ǣwe</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="woel" d:title="woel">
		<body>
			<h1>woel<span class="pron"> | wo.el |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:wǣl" class="xref-target">wǣl</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="here-spell" d:title="here-spell">
		<body>
			<h1>here-spell<span class="pron"> | xe.re.spell |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>neuter noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A story of praise, panegyric, eulogy</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gehȳr nū þis herespel (the story of creation)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Sch. 37)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:here-word" class="xref-target">here-word</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="for-sliet" d:title="for-sliet">
		<body>
			<h1>for-sliet<span class="pron"> | for.sli͜yt |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Slaughter, massacre</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. internecio)</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="astīðian" d:title="astīðian">
		<body>
			<h1>astīðian<span class="pron"> | ɑ.stiː.θi.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -ode, sg: -ude</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -od, past participle sg: -ud</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To become hard, dry, dry up, wither</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. indurare, arescere)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">my strength dried up as a tile</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Astīðude swā swā tigle miht mīn</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Spl. 21, 14)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">induret et arescat</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hit astiðaþ and drugaþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (89, 6)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="burg-weall" d:title="burg-weall">
		<body>
			<h1>burg-weall<span class="pron"> | burɣ.wæ͜ɑll |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">juxta urbis muros</span>
						<span class="q-oe">In Lucan þǣre cæstre ... seō eā flōweþ be þām burhwealle</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Gr. D. 192, 16)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">On ðā burhwalles; of ðām burhwallan ... cn suðwardne ðone burhwal</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (C.D. iii. 394, 28-30)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Pharao hēt hī wyrcan his burhweallas (cf. hig getimbrodun Pharaones eardungburga urbes tabernaculorum, Ex. 1, 11)</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. Th. ii. 190, 34)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="unfriþ-scip" d:title="unfriþ-scip">
		<body>
			<h1>unfriþ-scip<span class="pron"> | un.friθ.ʃip |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>neuter noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">a ship which is carrying on hostilities</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðam cynge com word ðæt unnfriðscipa lǣgen be westan and hergodon</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 1046; Erl. 173, 5)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">a ship belonging to a hostile country</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">omnis ceapscip, i.e. navis institoris, pacem habeat, quae in portum veniet, licet navis sit inimicorum, si non sit abacta tempestatibus (Lat. vers.)</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ǣlc ceāpscip frið hæbbe ðe binnan mūðan cuman(-e?), þēh hit unfriðscyp sȳ, gyf hit undrifen bið</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. Eth. ii. 2; Th. i. 286, 21)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="freōls-bryce" d:title="freōls-bryce">
		<body>
			<h1>freōls-bryce<span class="pron"> | fre͜oːls.bry.Ke |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Syndan freōlsbrycas(-bricas, v.l.) and fæsten-brycas wīde geworhte oft and gelōme.</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Wulfst. 164, 9)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-þynge" d:title="ge-þynge">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-þynge<span class="pron"> | je.θyn.Ge |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>neuter noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Growth, increase, advancement, honour</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">that he may have advancement and honour</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðætte he hæbbe forþgeong and geþyngo</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Jn. Skt. p. 188, 11)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">provectum</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Giþynge</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Rtl. 50, 21)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge-þungen" class="xref-target">ge-þungen</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="swēge" d:title="swēge">
		<body>
			<h1>swēge<span class="pron"> | sweː.Ge |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:hās-swēge" class="xref-target">hās-swēge</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="fird-leās" d:title="fird-leās">
		<body>
			<h1>fird-leās<span class="pron"> | fird.læ͜ɑːs |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:fyrd-leās" class="xref-target">fyrd-leās</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-cypsed" d:title="ge-cypsed">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-cypsed<span class="pron"> | je.Kyp.sed |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>participle</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Fettered</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. compēditus)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">introeat in conspectu tuo gĕmĭtus compĕdītōrum</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ingā on gesyhþe ðīne geōmrunga gecypsedra</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Spl. 78, 11)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">Dŏmĭnus solvit compĕdītos</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Driht tolȳseþ gecypsede</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Spl. 145, 6)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="un-wērig" d:title="un-wērig">
		<body>
			<h1>un-wērig<span class="pron"> | un.weː.riG |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Not weary, fresh</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Æt nīxtan wurdon hī ealle geteorode, and hē āna unwērig him æfter fyligde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Skt. ii. 30, 34)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gif mon on mycelre rāde weorðe geteorad, nime betonican...; ðonne bið hē sōna unwērig</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lchdm. i. 76, 8)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">cum alias aliis legiones dies noctesque succedere sine requie cogeret</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē hēt ðæt mon ðæt fæsten brǣce and on fuhte dæges and nihtes, simle ān legie after ōþerre unwērig</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 5, 11; Swt. 238, 9)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-ortrīwan" d:title="ge-ortrīwan">
		
		<body>
			<h1>ge-ortrīwan<span class="pron"> | je.or.triː.wɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -de</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to despair of</span>
					</p>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(1)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">with gen. Cf. I a</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">spemque fugato nes dolor adsit</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Ne þū tō wāclīce geortreōwe ǣniges gōdes</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Met. 5, 35)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(2)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">with prep.</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">de Dei misericordia nunquam desperare</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Hē nǣfre ne geortreōwe be Godes mildse</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (R. Ben. 19, 2)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">quae nec praesentis solamen temporis abesse patiantur</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Þā ðē ne lǣtað geortrēwan (-treōwan, v. l.) be þȳs andweardan līfe</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 10; S. 23, 7)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ne sceolon wē nǣfre geortrȳwan be Godes mildheortnesse</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Ll. Th. ii. 400, 1)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(3)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">with clause</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">calore desperato</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Sē ðe tō lange wunað on ðǣm wlacum treōwum, hē geortreōwð ðæt hē ǣfre mæge on welme weorðan</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 447, 9)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(4)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">absolute, to despair</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">in desperatione est</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Hē geortriēwð</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 447, 11)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I a.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">reflex. to cause (oneself) to despair. Cf. I. 1</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Þæt ðū þē ne geortrȳwe nānes gōdes</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 6; F. 14, 35)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to doubt, distrust</span>
					</p>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(1)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">to doubt the possibility of, be uncertain about something</span>
							</p>
							<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
								<li>
									<p>
										<span class="sense-label">(1)(a)</span>
										<span class="meaning-en">with acc.</span>
									</p>
									<ul class="quotes">
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Þonne bið ūs gesewen þæt ūs ǣr gesǣd wæs, þeāh þe wē hit nū geortrȳwan (-trūwian, v. l.), for ðȳ wē hit geseōn ne magon</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Wlfst. 3, 18)</span>
										</li>
									</ul>
									<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
										<li>
											<p>
												<span class="sense-label">(aa)</span>
												<span class="meaning-en">with acc. and clause in apposition</span>
											</p>
											<ul class="quotes">
												<li>
													<span class="q-la">nec diffidendum est nostra aetate fieri potuisse</span>
													<span class="q-oe">Nis ꝥ tō geortrȳwanne (-enne, v. l.), ꝥ on ūre yldo ꝥ beōn mihte</span>
													<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 4, 19; Sch. 441, 7)</span>
												</li>
											</ul>
										</li>
									</ol>
								</li>
								<li>
									<p>
										<span class="sense-label">(1)(b)</span>
										<span class="meaning-en">with clause</span>
									</p>
									<ul class="quotes">
										<li>
											<span class="q-la">quia per experimentum non novit, veraciter esse diffidat . . . diffidunt an vera sint</span>
											<span class="q-oe">Hē geortreōweð hweþer hī sōðe sȳn, for þon þe hē nǣfre ne cūþe þurh gewisse āfandunge . . . hī geortreōwdon hwæðer hī sōðe wǣron þe nǣron</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Gr. D. 261, 18-22)</span>
										</li>
									</ul>
								</li>
							</ol>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(2)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">not to trust in something</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Sȳ þū nǣfre swā synful þæt þū ǣfre geortrȳwe on Godes mildheortnysse</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Angl. xii. 517, 26)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(3)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">not to trust to a person (dat.) for doing something (clause)</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-en">I trust to God that he can preserve us</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Ne geortriēwe (-trūwige, Bos. 48, 45) ic nā Gode þæt hē ūs ne mæge gescildan</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 2, 5; S. 86, 4)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge-ortrēwan" class="xref-target">ge-ortrēwan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="cyn-recen" d:title="cyn-recen">
