	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="fōt-lǣst" d:title="fōt-lǣst">
		
		<body>
			<h1>fōt-lǣst<span class="pron"> | foːt.læːst |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:lǣs-hosum" class="xref-target">lǣs-hosum</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="æt-gemman" d:title="æt-gemman">
		<body>
			<h1>æt-gemman<span class="pron"> | æt.Gem.mɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -genam, pl: -genāmon</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -genufnen</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To take away by force, to pluck out, withdraw, deliver, rescue</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. eripere)</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="biscop-seðel" d:title="biscop-seðel">
		<body>
			<h1>biscop-seðel<span class="pron"> | bi.ʃop.se.θel |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>neuter noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -seðles</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A bishop's seat or residence</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. sedes episcopalis)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">Mellitus succeeded to the episcopal residence of Canterbury church</span>
							<span class="q-la">Mellitus sedem Doruvernensis ecclesiæ suscepit</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Mellitus fēng to ðam biscopseðle Contwara burge cirican</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 2, 7; S. 509, 8)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="rabbian" d:title="rabbian">
		<body>
			<h1>rabbian<span class="pron"> | rɑb.bi.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -ode</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To rage</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">God lǣt ðone deōfol Antecrist rabbian and wēdan sume hwīle</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wulfst. 84, 11)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="emetig" d:title="emetig">
		<body>
			<h1>emetig<span class="pron"> | e.me.tiG |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Empty, vacant</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. vacuus, vacans)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">invēnit eam [domum] vacantem</span>
							<span class="q-oe">He gemēteþ hit [hūs] emetig</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. Kmbl. Rush. 12, 44)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:æmtig" class="xref-target">æmtig</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="et-felgan" d:title="et-felgan">
		<body>
			<h1>et-felgan<span class="pron"> | et.fel.ɣɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -fealh, pl: -fulgon</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -folgen</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To cleave or stick to, adhere</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. adhærēre)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">a wicked heart cleaves not to me</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Nā etfilgþ me heorte þweor</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Spl. T. 100, 4)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:æt-felgan" class="xref-target">æt-felgan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="mis-dōn" d:title="mis-dōn">
		<body>
			<h1>mis-dōn<span class="pron"> | mis.doːn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">to act wrongly, offend, transgress</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gif hit geweorðeþ ðæt man unwilles ǣnig þing misdēþ, nā biþ ðæt nā gelīc ðam ðe sylfwilles misdēþ, and eāc se ðe nȳdwyrhta biþ ðæs ðe hē misdēþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. Eth. vi. 52; Th. i. 328, 21: L. Edg. C. 4; Th. ii. 262, 6)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">qui male agit</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Se ðe misðōeþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Jn. Skt. Lind. 3, 20)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Se ðe misdyde, hē hit gebēte</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. I. P. 19; Th. ii. 328, 15)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Tō fela is ðæra ðe misdydan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wulfst. 270, 30)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-blīþe" d:title="ge-blīþe">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-blīþe<span class="pron"> | je.bliː.θe |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Blithe (or blithely)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē swȳþe geblīþe hine hēt gyrwan tō þām ingange þæs heofonlican rices</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Guth. 80, 1)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="hafe-leāst" d:title="hafe-leāst">
		<body>
			<h1>hafe-leāst<span class="pron"> | xɑ.fe.læ͜ɑːst |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Want of means, indigence</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">from lack of means</span>
							<span class="q-oe">For hauelēste</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 675; Erl. 38, 12)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:hafen-leāst" class="xref-target">hafen-leāst</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="fandere" d:title="fandere">
		<body>
			<h1>fandere<span class="pron"> | fɑn.de.re |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">One who tries, tests, &amp;c.</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Nā swylce leornungcniht ac swylce fandere (temptator)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Scint. 206, 4)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:fandian" class="xref-target">fandian</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="āwārnian" d:title="āwārnian">
		<body>
			<h1>āwārnian<span class="pron"> | ɑː.wɑːr.ni.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -ode</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -od</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To be confounded</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. confundi)</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:āswārnian" class="xref-target">āswārnian</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="dwild" d:title="dwild">
		<body>
			<h1>dwild<span class="pron"> | dwild |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Mikell hæþenndom and hefig dwilde</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Orm. 9736)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="MIS-FĒRAN" d:title="MIS-FĒRAN">
		<body>
			<h1>MIS-FĒRAN<span class="pron"> | mis.feː.rɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To go wrong, to go astray</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="wirsa" d:title="wirsa">
		
		<body>
			<h1>wirsa<span class="pron"> | wir.sɑ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Worse, worst</span>
					</p>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(1)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">in a moral sense</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">For hwam lifaþ se wyrsa leng?</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Salm. Kmbl. 716; Sal. 357)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ne wearð nān wærsa dǣd gedōn ðonne ðeōs wæs</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 979; Erl. 129, 4)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Gif wē ðæt ne dōþ, ðonne wyrce wē ūs myccle synne; and ūs is get wyrse ðæt wē ūrne ceāp teōþian, gif wē willaþ syllan ðæt wyrste Gode</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Blickl. Homl. 41, 7)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hī for nānum ermþum ne byōð nō ðȳ betran, ac ðȳ wyrsan</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 39, 11; Fox 230, 17)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ðā gǣð hē and him tō genymð seofun ōðre gāstas wyrsan (nequiores) ðonne hē . . . and wurðaþ ðæs mannes ȳtemestan wyrsan (pejora) ðonne ða ǣrran</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. Kmbl. 12, 45: Wrt. Voc. ii. 72, 59)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ðes wyrresta cyning Neron</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. i. 384, 3)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Se wyresta sceaþa (Judas)</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Blickl. Homl. 69, 10)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ðis is manna se wyrresta</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (185, 2)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Se eallra wyrresta mon</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 14, 3; Fox 46, 20)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ðē þūhte ðæt eallra ðinga wyrrest</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (38, 4; Fox 204, 9)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ðæs wyrrestan eorðcyninga</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. Th. 235, 13; Dan. 305)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">in actione pessima</span>
									<span class="q-oe">On werrestre dǣde</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Confess. Peccat.)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Swā byð ðisse wyrrestan (wyrsesta, Lind., pessimae) cneōrysse</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. Kmbl. 12, 45)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Wirestan</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Deut. 1, 35)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ða wyrstan (pessimam) ingewitnesse mē ic geseō</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 5, 13; S. 632, 32)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ða wyrrestan, fā folcsceaðan</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Andr. Kmbl. 3183; An. 1594)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ðām wyrrestum wītes þegnum</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. Th. 251, 28; Jul. 152)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">in rebus pessimis</span>
									<span class="q-oe">On werstum ðingum</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Kent. Gl. 23)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
							<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
								<li>
									<p>
										<span class="sense-label">(1 a)</span>
										<span class="meaning-en">of an unfitting condition of things</span>
									</p>
									<ul class="quotes">
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">And ðæt git wyrse is, ðæt wē witon manige foremǣre weras forþgewitene ðe swiþe feāwa manna ā ongit</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 19; Fox 70, 11: Met. 10, 57)</span>
										</li>
									</ul>
								</li>
							</ol>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(2)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">of the physical condition of persons or things</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hē tōbrycð hys stede on ðam reāfe, and se slite byð ðe wyrsa</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. Kmbl. 9, 16)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Siō wund bið ðæs ðe wierse</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 17; Swt. 123, 18)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">deterius habebat</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Heō wæs ðe wyrse</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Mk. Skt. 5, 26)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Seō frecednes dæghwamlīce wæs wyrse and wyrse</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 4, 32; S. 611, 24)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
							<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
								<li>
									<p>
										<span class="sense-label">(2 a)</span>
										<span class="meaning-en">where injury is done to a person in respect to his well-being</span>
									</p>
									<ul class="quotes">
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Se ðe ōðerne mid wō forsecgan wille, ðæt hē āðer oþþe feō oþþe freme ðā wyrse sȳ</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (L. C. S. 16; Th. i. 384, 24)</span>
										</li>
										<li>
											<span class="q-oe">Hī dydan mycelne hearm ābūtan Hāmtūne . . . swā ðæt seō scīr and ða ōðra scīra, ðæ ðǣr neāh sindon, wurdon fela wintra ðe wyrsan</span>
											<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 1065; Erl. 197, 11)</span>
										</li>
									</ul>
								</li>
							</ol>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(3)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">of the condition of affairs, of an (unfavourable) circumstance or event</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Mē ðǣr wyrse gelamp, ðonne ic tō hyhte āgan mōste</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. Th. 275, 22; Sat. 175)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hit him wyrse gelomp</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (272, 26; Sat. 125)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Wæs ǣfre heora æftra sȳð wyrse ðonne se ǣrra</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 1001; Erl. 137, 14)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Swā wearð hit fram dæge tō dæge lætre and wyrre</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (1066; Erl. 202, 17)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ne wearð wyrse dǣd (more disastrous act) monnum gemearcod</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. Th. 37, 24; Gen. 594)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hē āwende hit him tō wyrsan þinge</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (17, 13; Gen. 259)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hē tǣhte Absalone ōðerne rǣd wyrsan tō his willan</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Skt. i. 19, 206)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Wēne ic tō ðē wyrsan þinga, gif ðū Grendles dearst bīdan</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Beo. Th. 1055; B. 525)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(4)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">of that which is harmful, painful, etc.</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-en">they never met with harder fighting in England</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Hī nǣfre wyrsan handplegan on Angelcynne ne gemitton</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 1004; Erl. 138, note 7)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ðȳ læs God ūs sende on wyrsan tintrego</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Blickl. Homl. 243, 20)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ðæra synfullena deāþ byð se wyrsta (wyrresta, Ps. Surt.: wyrst, Ps. Spl., pessima)</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 33, 21)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Wilddeōra ðæt wyrreste (grimmeste, Exon. Th. 371, 29) . . . wyrmcynna ðæt grimmeste (wyrreste, Exon. Th. 371, 32)</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Soul Kmbl. 164-167; Seel. 82-84)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Se deōfol slōh lōb mid ðære wyrstan wunde (with the most grievous disorder)</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. ii. 452, 26)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-en">with the most virulent poison</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Mid ðȳ werrestan āttre</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Shrn. 84, 28)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-en">to the most cruel death</span>
									<span class="q-oe">On ðone wyrrestan deāð</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Andr. Kmbl. 172; An. 86)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">saevissimis afflictionibus</span>
									<span class="q-oe">We[r]stum gedrecenyssum</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Hpt. Gl. 409, 59)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Getogen tō ðǣm wyrstan tintregum</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Blickl. Homl. 245, 1)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ða werrestan tintrega</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (229, 25)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Wyrrestan</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. Th. 257, 20; Jul. 250: Elen. Kmbl. 1860; El. 932)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(5)</span>
								<span class="meaning-en">marking inferiority</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hē bið swīðe gelīc sumum ðara gumena ðe him þringaþ ymbe ūtan; gif hē wyrsa ne bið, ne wēne ic his nā beteran</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Met. 25, 20)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ǣlc man sylþ ǣrest gōd wīn, and ðonne hig druncene beōð ðæt ðe wyrse (wyrest, Rush.: wurresta, Lind., deterius) byð</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Jn. Skt. 2, 10)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hē ðæt betere geceās, and ðam wyrsan wiðsōc</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Elen. Kmbl. 2078; El. 1040)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">On ðone wyrsan dǣl scyrede</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. Th. 75, 24; Cri. 1226)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">On ða wyrsan hand</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Salm. Kmbl. 998; Sal. 500)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Onwendan heora wuldor on ðæne wyrsan hād styrces</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 105, 17)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Wyrsan wīgfrecan</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Beo. Th. 4985; B. 2496)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Buccena flǣsc is wyrrest</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Lchdm. ii. 196, 17)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Gif wē willaþ syllan ūre ðæt wyrste Gode</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Blickl. Homl. 41, 8)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:weorr" class="xref-target">weorr</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="mistel-lām" d:title="mistel-lām">
		<body>
			<h1>mistel-lām<span class="pron"> | mi.stel.lɑːm |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>neuter noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Bird-lime made from the berries of the mistletoe</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. viscus)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Mistellām viscus</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. i. 289, 65)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="be-heōfian" d:title="be-heōfian">
		<body>
			<h1>be-heōfian<span class="pron"> | be.xe͜oː.fi.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To lament evils</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. mala plangere)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">mala plangere</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Yfelu beheōfian</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Scint. 44, 5)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="under-gitan" d:title="under-gitan">
		<body>
			<h1>under-gitan<span class="pron"> | un.der.Gi.tɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Þeān ðe se Hālga Gāst ne beō swutollīce genemned tō ðām Fæder and tō ðām Suna, swā ðeāh hē byð symle ðǣrtō undergyten</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. ii. 56, 30)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-notian" d:title="ge-notian">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-notian<span class="pron"> | je.no.ti.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">functus, usus</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Genotad</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 152, 19)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="of-smorian" d:title="of-smorian">
		<body>
			<h1>of-smorian<span class="pron"> | of.smo.ri.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">to choke, strangle, suffocate</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">dolo comitis sui strangulatus</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hiene ofsmorode his ealdor—mon</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 6, 36; Swt. 294, 9)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">suffocatus</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Mid ðæm brǣþe ofsmorod</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (6, 32 ; Swt. 288, 2)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ēren" d:title="ēren">
		<body>
			<h1>ēren<span class="pron"> | eː.ren |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Brazen</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. æreus)</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ǣren" class="xref-target">ǣren</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="hīru" d:title="hīru">
		<body>
			<h1>hīru<span class="pron"> | xiː.ru |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:huru" class="xref-target">huru</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="gedwol-sprǣc" d:title="gedwol-sprǣc">
		<body>
			<h1>gedwol-sprǣc<span class="pron"> | Ge.dwol.spræːK |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Heretical speech, heresy</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Twēgen ðsēr wǣron bisceophādes men þe ǣlces yfeles heāfodhebban wǣron . . . hī Godes gelaðunge drehton and mid heora gedwolsprǣce eall folc āmyrdon</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. S. 23, 369)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="rihte" d:title="rihte">
		<body>
			<h1>rihte<span class="pron"> | rix.te |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adverb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">of direction, right, due, directly, straight</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">runs straight on in its course</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Swā oft ǣspringc ūt āwealleþ of clife hārum, and gereclīce, rihte flōweþ, irneþ wið his eardes</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Met. 5, 14)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">due east of them</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ryhte beeāstan him</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 1, 1; Swt. 16, 3)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">of time, directly, straightway</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">mitte jam nunc</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Send nū rihte</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ex. 9, 19)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">jam nunc videbis</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Nū rihte ðū gesihst</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Num. 11, 23)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gif ic on helle gedō hwyrft ǣnigne, ðū mē æt byst efne rihte</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 138, 6)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">III.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">in accordance with justice or equity, justly</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">judicabit orbem terræ in justitia</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē ymbhwyrft eorþan dēmeþ sōðe and rihte</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 97, 9 : in aequitate, 95, 13)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">IV.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">rightly, well, in a manner suited to the circumstances of a case, fittingly, properly, duly</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Rihte ys hē genemned Jacob; nu hē beswāc mē</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Gen. 27, 36 : Exon. Th. 9, 7; Cri. 139)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">recte</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Wæs swīðe ryhte tō ðæm wītgan gecweden</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 21; Swt. 153, 16)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ne ǣnig wið ōðerne getrȳwlīce ne þohte swā rihte swā hē scolde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wulfst. 160, 2 : Cd. Th. 127, 32; Gen. 2119)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">quam bonus Deus his, qui recto sunt corde</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hū gōd is God ðām ðe mid heortan rihte hycgeaþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Th. 72, 1 : 62, 6)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">habitabunt recti cum vultu tuo</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Scylan eard niman on ðīnre ansȳne ða mid rǣde hēr rihte lifigeaþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (139, 13)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">V.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">correctly, in the proper manner, exactly, accurately, truly</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">to speak Latin correctly</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Wē biddaþ ðē, Lāreōw, ðæt ðū tǣce ūs sprecan rihte</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Coll. Monast. Th. 18, 8)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Bæd ðæt hē hyra randan rihte heōldon</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Byrht. Th. 132, 23; By. 20)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">correctly</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Swā wæs on ðǣm scennum þurh rūnstafas rihte gemearcod, hwam ðæt sweord geworht ǣrest wǣre</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Beo. Th. 3395; B. 1695)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">they were exactly such then as they are now</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Swylce hȳ wǣron rihte ... swilce hī nū sindon</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 7, 2; Fox 18, 1)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">it (Babylon) is very accurately quadrangular</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Heō is swīðe ryhte feōwerscȳte</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 2, 4; Swt. 74, 13)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">to say with greater accuracy</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ryhtor cweþan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (5, 1; Swt. 214, 9)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:eāst-rihte" class="xref-target">eāst-rihte</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:norþ-rihte" class="xref-target">norþ-rihte</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:ðǣr-rihte" class="xref-target">ðǣr-rihte</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="fadian" d:title="fadian">
		<body>
			<h1>fadian<span class="pron"> | fɑ.di.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">digessit</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Fadode digessit</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (An. Ox. 56, 326)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(1)</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">absolute</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-en">that in the matter of just judgement his ordering be the same for friends and for strangers</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Seofon þing gedafenað rihtwīsum cyninge . . . seofoðe, ꝥ hē be freōndan and be fremdan fadige gelīce on rihtlican dōme</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Ll. Th. ii. 306, 29)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(2)</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">with acc.</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">praepositus omnia disponens</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Se prāfast þæt fadaþ and gegearewaþ</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (R. Ben. 137, 22)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-en">he orders not his life wisely</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Hē wīslīce his līf ne fadað</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Wlfst. 52, 28)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Fadode</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (159, 18)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">domui Dei dignum constituant dispensatorem</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Gesette man þæne þe Godes hūs wel fadige</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (R. Ben. 119, 12)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Gif hē his līf rihtlice fadige</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Ll. Th. i. 346, 18)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-en">to order their conversation aright</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Heora āgene wīsan rihtlīce fadian</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (ii. 318, 13 : Wlfst. 143, 22 : 144, 22)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-fara" d:title="ge-fara">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-fara<span class="pron"> | je.fɑ.rɑ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -an</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A companion</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. sōcius)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">I am a soldier's companion</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic eom fyrdrinces gefara</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 127 a; Th. 489, 3; Rä 78, 2)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">in sōcios arma vertere incipiunt</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hī heora wǣpen hwyrfdon wið heora gefaran</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 1, 15; S. 483, 5)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge-fēra" class="xref-target">ge-fēra</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="eald-dagas" d:title="eald-dagas">
		<body>
			<h1>eald-dagas<span class="pron"> | æ͜ɑld.dɑ.ɣɑs |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Ancient days, days of old</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. prisci dies)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">In eald-dagum</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 12a; Th. 19, 19; Cri. 303: Ors. 3, 7; Bos. 61, 44: Bd. 4, 27; S. 604, 41, MS. B.)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="heofon-þrym" d:title="heofon-þrym">
		<body>
			<h1>heofon-þrym<span class="pron"> | xe͜o.fon.θrym |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -mes</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Heavenly glory or majesty</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="æfen-lic" d:title="æfen-lic">
		<body>
			<h1>æfen-lic<span class="pron"> | æ.fen.liːtʃ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-la">vespertinis horis</span>
						<span class="q-oe">Æfernlicum tīdum</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Rtl. 174, 37)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ēwe" d:title="ēwe">
		<body>
			<h1>ēwe<span class="pron"> | eː.we |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A sheep, generally as ōvis</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. ōvis)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">of a sheep's worth</span>
							<span class="q-la">de ōvis prētio</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Be ēwes weorþe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. In. 55; Th. i. 138, 6)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:eōwu" class="xref-target">eōwu</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="hunig-swǣs" d:title="hunig-swǣs">
		<body>
			<h1>hunig-swǣs<span class="pron"> | xu.niG.swæːs |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adjective</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Like honey</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. melleus)</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="fealgian" d:title="fealgian">
		<body>
			<h1>fealgian<span class="pron"> | fæ͜ɑl.Gi.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -ode</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To fallow, break-up land</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Me mæig on sumera fealgian, myxendincgan UNCERTAIN ūt dragan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Angl. ix. 261, 8)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:next word" class="xref-target">next word</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="for-gīmeleāsian" d:title="for-gīmeleāsian">
		<body>
			<h1>for-gīmeleāsian<span class="pron"> | for.Giː.me.læ͜ɑː.si.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Excesserit, i. culpaverit, fregerit vel forgēmeleāsaþ</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 145, 70)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Sī forlǣten, forgȳmeleāsod excipiatur</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (An. Ox. 4571)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="for-gȳman" d:title="for-gȳman">
		
		<body>
			<h1>for-gȳman<span class="pron"> | for.Gyː.mɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -de</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -ed</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To neglect, pass by, transgress</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. negligere, præterire, transgredi)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">he forgets and neglects the future state</span>
							<span class="q-oe">He ða forþgesceaft forgyteþ and forgȳmeþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Beo. Th. 3506; B. 1751)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">quare discipuli tui transgrediuntur traditionem seniorum?</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hwī forgȳmāþ ðīne leorningcnihtas ūre yldrena lage</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. Bos. 15, 2)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">quare vos transgredimini mandatum Dei propter traditionem vestram?</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hwī forgȳme gē Godes bebod for eōwre lage</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (15, 3)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">qui neglexit sermonem Domini, dimisit servos suos et jumenta in agris</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Se ðe Drihtnes word forgīmde, he forlēt his men and nȳtenu ūte</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ex. 9, 21)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">nunquam mandatum tuum prætерivi</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic nǣfre ðīn bebod ne forgȳmde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lk. Bos. 15, 29)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">they neglected the service of God</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hie þegnscipe Godes forgȳmdon</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Cd. 18; Th. 21, 20; Gen. 327)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">illi neglexerunt</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Forgȳmdon hig ðæt</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. Bos. 22, 5)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">be not heedless of thy Lord's correction</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ne forgȳm ðū ðīnes Drihtnes steōre</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. ii. 328, 21)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-munan" d:title="ge-munan">
		
		<body>
			<h1>ge-munan<span class="pron"> | je.mu.nɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">present: 2sg: -Þū ge-manst, 2sg: -munst, 3sg: -hē ge-manþ, 3sg: -muneþ, 3sg: -myneþ, pl: -ge-munon</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -ge-mȳste</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">either the verb is taken to be passive or gemunende should be read</span>
							<span class="q-la">non recordentur</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ne sint gemunene</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Kent. Gl. 1131)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to retain in mind, recall to mind, recollect, bear in mind</span>
					</p>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(1)</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">with acc.</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ic geman mīn āgen dysig</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 35, 2; F. 156, 27)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Hiē gemunan (-on, v. l.) ðone tōhopan, and forgietað hira demm</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 345, l)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ic ðis eall gemunde</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (5, 8)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ðār þū nū gemundest dā word þe ic þē sǣde</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 35, 2 ; F. 156, 21)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">recordatus est Petrus verbi Jesu</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Þā gemunde (-mȳste, L.) Petrus word þas Hǣlend</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. R. 26, 75)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(2)</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">with gen.</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ic ne gemune nānre his synna</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. S. 12, 156)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ðæs bismeres ðū ne gemansð</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 207, 12)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">non meminit pressurae</span>
									<span class="q-oe">Wīf. . . ne gemynes ðæs hefignise</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Jn. L. 16, 21)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ne gē eft gemynas fīf hlāfana</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Mt. L. 16, 9)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ðīnra synna ne weorðe ic gemunende, ac gemun ðū hiora</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 413, 22)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(3)</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">with clause</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Gif þū gemanst þæt brōþor þīn hæfð ǣnig þincg ongeān þē</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Scint. 23, 14)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Gemunst</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Bt. 36, 3; F. 176, 22)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Gemunst (-manst, v.l.) ðū ꝥ wit ǣr sprǣcon</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (38, 3; F. 200, ii)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Mīn mōd gemanð hū (gemyneð hwilc, v. l.) hit ǣr wæs</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Gr. D. 4, 11 ; 6, 8)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Swā mycel swā nān man ne gemunet ꝥ hit ǣfre ǣror dyde</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 1099; P. 235, 7)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Gemunde ic hū ic geseah . . . hū ðā ciricean stōdon bōca gefyldæ</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 5, 8)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ðætte ðæt mōd . . . gemyne of ðǣm suingum tō hwǣm eal monncynn gesceapen is</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (255, 18)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Ðæt hī gemunen ðæt hiē . . . biōð gesomnode</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (397, 8)</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Seldon hiē willað gemunan hū micel hiē nimað</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (343, 16)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(4)</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">where (1) and (3) are combined</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-en">the earliest thing that I can remember is that my father was a captain</span>
									<span class="q-oe">ꝥ is ꝥ ic gefyrnost gemunan mæg, ꝥ mīn fæder wæs cempena ealdorman</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. S. 30, 322)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I a.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to bear in mind, not to forget to do</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gefēra, gemyne ꝥ ðū ūre gecwedrǣdenne tō longe ne oferbrec</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ors. 5, 12 ; S. 242, 7)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gemunon wē symle ꝥ wē þā gōd dōn þe ūs Godes bēc lǣraþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bl. H. 73, 26)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">ꝥ hē oft hæbbe on gemynde ꝥ mannum is mǣst þearf tō gemunenne, ꝥ is ꝥ hī rihtne geleāfan habban, and ꝥ hī rihtne crīstendōm healdan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ll. Th. i. 326)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to remember (and pray for)</span>
					</p>
					<ol class="sub-senses labeled">
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(1)</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">the living</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-oe">Gemune þū mē earminge on þīnum gebedum</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. A. 178, 311)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>
								<span class="sense-label">(2)</span>
								<span class="sub-heading">the dead</span>
							</p>
							<ul class="quotes">
								<li>
									<span class="q-la">ea ratione ut memores sint ejus et animae Osmodi ad anniversarium ejus</span>
									<span class="q-oe">On ðā gerāð ðe hī gemunen hī and Osmōdes sāulæ tō his gemunde dege</span>
									<span class="q-cite"> (Cht. Th. 493, 10)</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">III.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to bear in mind as worth considering, mind, think of</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðā cwǣdon hī ꝥ hī þæs ne gemundon þonne mā þe heora gefēran</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 755; P. 49, 23)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">IV.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to record, make mention of</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">memoratur, i. dicitur</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hē gemanþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (An. Ox. 1598)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">memorant</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gemunað</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 55, 34)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Nū ic þyses Alexandres gemyndgade, ic wille þæs māran Alexandres gemunende beōn</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ox. 3, 7 ; S. 110, II)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">memoratur</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Is gemunen, gesǣd</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (An. Ox. 1514: 2814)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gereht, gemunen</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (2206)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">V.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">absolute, to exercise the faculty of memory</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Seō sāwul þurh þæt gemynd gemanð</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. Th. i. 288, 28)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Seō sāwul is memoria, þæt is gemynd, þonne heō gemanð</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. S. I. 186)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gemynen (remini-scentur) alle gemǣru eorðan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Srt. 21, 28)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">VI.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to exercise the mind (?), meditate, consider</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">comminiscuntur (cf. comminiscuntur, pro tractabantur ł meditabuntur, An. Ox. 7, 209)</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Rǣswodan, spǣcan, wǣran gemunende</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 24, 2)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">VII.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">to put in mind, remind a person of something, charge with</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic gemunde þē fācnes, þǣr nān næs</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. A. 135, 641)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:munan" class="xref-target">munan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="þeōd-sceaþa" d:title="þeōd-sceaþa">
		<body>
			<h1>þeōd-sceaþa<span class="pron"> | θe͜oːd.ʃæ͜ɑ.θɑ |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -an</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A criminal against the community, a spoiler of the community, a great criminal or spoiler</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Wāc biþ se hyrde, ðe nele ða heorde bewerian, gyf ðǣr hwylc þeōdsceaða sceaðian onginneþ. Nis nān swā yfel sceaða swā is deōfol sylf. Ðonne mōton ða hyrdas beōn swīðe wacore, ðe wið ðone þeōdsceaðan folce sceolon scyldan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. C. E. 26; Th. i, 374, 22-28: Wulfst. 191, 6-13)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Þeōdsceada, fȳrdraca</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Beo. Th. 5369; B. 2688: 4545; B. 2278)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Se þeōdsceaða (famine)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Andr. Kmbl. 2232; An. 1117)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gyf God ne gescyrte ðæs þeōdscaðan (Antichrist) līfdagas</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wulfst. 86, 17)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">God biddan, ðæt hē ūs gescylde wið ðone þeōdscaðan (Antichrist)</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (80, 6)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðider (to hell) sculon þeōfas and deōdscaðan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (26, 18: 165, 36: Exon. Th. 98, 20; Cri. 1610)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Lācende lēg lāðwende men þreāð, þeōdsceaþan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (97, 25; Cri. 1596)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:folc-sceaþa" class="xref-target">folc-sceaþa</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:leōd-sceaþa" class="xref-target">leōd-sceaþa</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="sīd-wyrm" d:title="sīd-wyrm">
		<body>
			<h1>sīd-wyrm<span class="pron"> | siːd.wyrm |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A silk-worm</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Siolucwyrm oððe sīdwyrm bombix</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Wrt. Voc. ii. 12, 22)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Sȳdwyrm</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (i. 24, 6)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="for-sōc" d:title="for-sōc">
		<body>
			<h1>for-sōc<span class="pron"> | for.soːk |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -for-sōc, pl: -sōcon</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">refused; p. of for-sacan</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:for-sacan" class="xref-target">for-sacan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ā-mānsumung" d:title="ā-mānsumung">
		<body>
			<h1>ā-mānsumung<span class="pron"> | ɑː.mɑːn.su.mung |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Þone cwyde þǣre āmānsumunge (-mǣn-, v. l.)</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Gr. D. 152, 11)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Þǣre āmānsumunge gemet</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (R. Ben. 48, 15)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Hē āmǣnsumenge (-mānsumunge, v. l.) underhnīge</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (48, 10)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:next word" class="xref-target">next word</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-þwǣrnes" d:title="ge-þwǣrnes">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-þwǣrnes<span class="pron"> | je.θwæːr.nes |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="labeled">
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">I.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">concord, peace</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">omnes, qui per discordiam separantur a viriditate dilectionis, arefiunt</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ǣlc ðāra ðe hine āscādan wille from ðǣre geðwǣrnesse, hē wile forlǣtan ðǣre lufan grēnnisse and forseārian on ðǣre ungeðwǣrnesse</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Past. 359, 14)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gesibsumnesse and geþwǣrnesse ūs betweōnan healdan</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ll. Th. i. 246, 22)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Hiē him eāþmēdo budon and geþuǣrnesse</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 827; P. 60, 34)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="sense-label">II.</span>
						<span class="meaning-en">gentleness</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">cum omni mansuetudine et obedientia</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Underfō hē þā geboda his tǣcendes mid ealre geþwǣrnesse and mid micelre eāðmōdnesse</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (R. Ben. 128, 12)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Of irsunge wyxt seofung, and of ðǣre geþwǣrnesse lufu</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Prov. K. 23)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:un-geþwǣrness" class="xref-target">un-geþwǣrness</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-hlinung" d:title="ge-hlinung">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-hlinung<span class="pron"> | je.xli.nung |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>feminine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -e</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Resting, reclining</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Gihlionunga</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lk. R. 17, 7)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="stǣlan" d:title="stǣlan">
		<body>
			<h1>stǣlan<span class="pron"> | stæː.lɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Men him eallinga ne ondrǣdaþ, hū ꝥ diōful him on stǣleð ealle þā unrihtan weorc þe hēr worhte biōð</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Verc. Först. 89, 11)</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Þæt mē ne mōtan þā dreōrgan deōfla æt mīnum ende ne on dōmdæge mīne synna on stǣlan (cf. þæt mē nǣfre deōfel nāht on ne mæge bestǣlan, 101, 52)</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Angl. xi. 100, 94: Verc. Först. 147, 29)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="forþfēran" d:title="forþfēran">
		<body>
			<h1>forþfēran<span class="pron"> | forθ.feː.rɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">to die</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">here, A. D. 860, king Æthelbald died</span>
							<span class="q-oe">A.D. 860, hēr, Æðelbald cyning forþfērde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 860; Erl. 71, 3)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="eærfoðian" d:title="eærfoðian">
		<body>
			<h1>eærfoðian<span class="pron"> | e.ær.fo.θi.ɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">to trouble</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. tribulare)</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="forþ-beran" d:title="forþ-beran">
		<body>
			<h1>forþ-beran<span class="pron"> | forθ.be.rɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">present: 3sg: -bereþ, 3sg: -bireþ</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -bær, pl: -bǣron</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -boren</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To bear or carry forth, bring forth, bring forward, produce</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. proferre, perhĭbēre)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">Albānum egrĕgium fēcunda Britannia profert</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðone æðelan Albanum seō wæstmberende Bryton forþbereþ</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Bd. 1, 7; S. 476, 34)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">ut omnes pălam quæ gessĕrant confĭtendo proferrent</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðætte ealle openlīce be heora dǣde þurh andetnesse forþbǣron</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (4, 27; S. 604, 23: Blickl. Homl. 25, 2; 101, 30)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">ut testĭmōnium perhĭbēret de lūmĭne</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt he gewitnesse forþbǣre be ðam leōhte</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Jn. Bos. 1. 8)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ge-welhwǣr" d:title="ge-welhwǣr">
		<body>
			<h1>ge-welhwǣr<span class="pron"> | je.wel.xwæːr |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>adverb</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">Everywhere</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:welhwǣr" class="xref-target">welhwǣr</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="wiþer-sprecend" d:title="wiþer-sprecend">
		<body>
			<h1>wiþer-sprecend<span class="pron"> | wi.θer.spre.Kend |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">One who contradicts</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. contradictor)</span>
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="riht-sinscipe" d:title="riht-sinscipe">
		<body>
			<h1>riht-sinscipe<span class="pron"> | rixt.sin.ʃi.pe |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">lawful matrimony</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðrȳ hādas sindon þe cȳðdon gecȳðnesse be Crīste; þæt is mæigdhād, and wudewanhād, and rihtsinscipe</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Hml. Th. i. 148, 7)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:riht-gesinscipe" class="xref-target">riht-gesinscipe</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="fīc-wyrm" d:title="fīc-wyrm">
		<body>
			<h1>fīc-wyrm<span class="pron"> | fiːK.wyrm |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">A FIG-WORM, a worm originating from the fig-disease</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. vermis ex fīco morbo ōriens)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">dēcident fīet morbi vermes in balneo</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Feallaþ ða fīcwyrmas on ða beðinge</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (L. M. 3, 48; Lchdm. ii. 340. 8)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="ēfstan" d:title="ēfstan">
		
		<body>
			<h1>ēfstan<span class="pron"> | eːf.stɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -ēfstte, sg: -ēfste, pl: -ēfston, pl: -ēfstun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -ēfsted, past participle sg: -ēfst</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">imperative: sg: -ēfst, sg: -ēfste, pl: -ēfstaþ</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To hasten, draw near, approach, make haste, be quick</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. festīnāre, properāre, concurrere, appropinquāre, accelerāre)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">let us now hasten to see the wonders</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Uton nū ēfstan seōn wundur</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Beo. Th. 6193; B. 3101: Rood Kmbl. 67; Kr. 34)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">he hastened northward</span>
							<span class="q-oe">He ēfste [ēfstte, Th. 278, 23, col. 2] norþweard</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Chr. 1016; Th. 278, 22, col. 1)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">festīnāvit Abraham in tabernāculum</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Abraham ēfste in to ðam getelde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Gen. 18, 6: Lk. Bos. 19, 6; Beo. Th. 2990; B. 1493: Cd. 139; Th. 174, 2; Gen. 2872)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">appropinquāvērunt usque ad portas mortis</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hī ēfston ōþ to gatum deāþes</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Spl. 106, 18: Byrht. Th. 137, 55; By. 206)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">accelerāvērunt</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Hī geneālǣhton oððe ēfstun [ēfston, Ps. Spl. 15, 3]</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Lamb. 15, 4)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">festīna ibi</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ēfst ardlīce ðyder</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Gen. 19, 22: Lk. Bos. 19, 5)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">accelera ut ēruas me</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ēfst [Th. ēfste] oððe neālǣce ðæt ðū generige me</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Ps. Spl. 30, 2)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">festīnāte et addūcite eum ad me</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ēfstaþ and lǣdaþ hine to me</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Gen. 45, 13: Boutr. Scrd. 22, 42: Homl. Th. ii. 88, 32)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">hasten that ye go through the narrow gate</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ēfstaþ ðæt ge gangon þurh ðæt nearwe geat</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Lk. Bos. 13, 24)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">that we may hasten to thee with all our heart</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ðæt we to ðē mid ealre heortan ēfston</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Homl. Th. ii. 600, 3)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-la">ad quam festīnātum erat</span>
							<span class="q-oe">To ðam ðe hit ēfst wæs</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Prov. 20)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:ge-ēfstan" class="xref-target">ge-ēfstan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="trahtung" d:title="trahtung">
		<body>
			<h1>trahtung<span class="pron"> | trɑx.tung |</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:of-trahtung" class="xref-target">of-trahtung</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="fellan" d:title="fellan">
		
		<body>
			<h1>fellan<span class="pron"> | fel.lɑn |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>verb</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">present: 1sg: -felle, 2sg: -felest, 2sg: -felst, 3sg: -feleþ, 3sg: -felþ, pl: -fellaþ</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">past: sg: -felde, pl: -feldon</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">participle: past participle sg: -felled</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">To cause to fall, to fell, cut or throw down, strip off, destroy</span>
						<span class="meaning-la"> (Lat. cædĕre, sternĕre, projĭcĕre, abjĭcĕre, dejĭcĕre, destruĕre)</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">borne where it was thrown down</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Gefered ðǣr hit felde</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. 109 b; Th. 419, 11; Rä. 38, 4)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:āfellan" class="xref-target">āfellan</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:be-fellan" class="xref-target">be-fellan</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:fyllan" class="xref-target">fyllan</a>, <a href="x-dictionary:r:feallan" class="xref-target">feallan</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="solor" d:title="solor">
		
		<body>
			<h1>solor<span class="pron"> | so.lor |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>masculine noun</b>
				</p>
				<p>
					<b class="ending">genitive sg: -es</b>
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol>
				<li>
					<p>
						<span class="meaning-en">An upper chamber, a soler</span>
					</p>
					<ul class="quotes">
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">until it stand firmly in the upper chamber of the mind</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Ic wilnige ðætte ðeōs sprǣc stigge on ðæt ingeþonc ðæs leorneres suǣ suǣ on sume hlǣdre ōððæt hiō fæstlīce gestonde on ðæm solore ðæs mōdes</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Past. proem.; Swt. 23, 18)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="q-en">in that upper chamber (its nest)</span>
							<span class="q-oe">Se fugel ofer heānne beām hūs getimbreþ, and gewīcaþ ðǣr sylf in ðam solere</span>
							<span class="q-cite"> (Exon. Th. 212, 2; Ph. 204)</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="feor-land" d:title="feor-land">
		
		<body>
			<h1>feor-land<span class="pron"> | fe͜or.lɑnd |</span>
			</h1>
			<div>
				<p>
					<b>noun</b>
				</p>
				<ul class="quotes">
					<li>
						<span class="q-oe">Geācsode se foresprecena wræcca on feorlandum þæs hālgan weres forðfōre</span>
						<span class="q-cite"> (Guth. 94, 2)</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
			<p class="xref">See also: <a href="x-dictionary:r:feor" class="xref-target">feor</a>
			</p>
		</body>
	</d:entry>
<d:entry xmlns:d="http://www.apple.com/DTDs/DictionaryService-1.0.rng" id="firr" d:title="firr">
